 (337,289,67,3,NULL,'Abraham was not a jew or a christian;'),
 (338,289,46,4,NULL,'Of the jews there are those who displace words from their places and say..'),
 (339,289,160,4,NULL,'we forbade the jews certain foods that had been lawful to them for their wrongdoing,and for hindering many from the way of Allah '),
 (340,289,18,5,NULL,'(Both) the jews and the christian said:"we are sons of Allah and His beloved."'),
 (341,290,41,5,NULL,'or it be among the jews men who will listen to any lie will listen even to others who have never so much as come to you.'),
 (342,290,44,5,NULL,'By its standard have been judged the jews,by the prophets who bowed(as in islam) to Allah''s will,..'),
 (343,290,51,5,NULL,'O you who believe! Take not the jews or the christians for your friends and protectors.'),
 (344,290,64,5,NULL,'The jews say:"Allah''s hand is tied up."'),
 (345,290,82,5,NULL,'Strongest among men in enmity to the believers will you find the jews and the pagans'),
 (346,290,30,9,NULL,'The jews call Uzayr a son of God,and the christian all christ the son of God.'),
 (347,290,118,16,NULL,'To the jews who prohibited such things as we have mentioned to you before'),
 (348,290,17,22,NULL,'Those who believe those who foloow the jewish and the sabians,christians,Magians,and polytheists'),
 (349,291,100,6,NULL,'yet they make the jinns equal with Allah,though Allah did create the jinns.'),
 (350,291,112,6,NULL,'Satans among men and jinns,inspiring each other with flowery discourses by way of deception.'),
 (351,291,128,6,NULL,'O you assembly of jinns!Much (toll) did you take of men'),
 (352,291,130,6,NULL,' O you assembly of jinns and men came there not unto you messengers from amongst you'),
 (353,291,38,7,NULL,'He will say enter you in the company of the peoples who passed away before you men and jinns into the fire'),
 (354,291,179,7,NULL,'Many are the jinns and men we have made for Hell'),
 (355,291,119,11,NULL,'and the word of your Lord shall be fulfilled i will fill hell with jinns and men altogether'),
 (356,291,27,15,NULL,'And the jinn race,we had created before from the fire of a scorching wind.'),
 (357,291,50,18,NULL,'He was one of the jinns,and he broke the command of his Lord.'),
 (358,291,17,22,NULL,'And before solomon were marshelled his hosts of jinns and men and birds,and they were all kept in order and ranks'),
 (359,291,39,27,NULL,'said an ifrit of the jinns i will bring it to you before you rise from your council'),
 (360,291,13,32,NULL,'But the words of me will come true,i will fillHell with jinns and men altogether'),
 (361,291,12,34,NULL,'and there were jinns that worked in front of him,by the leaves of his Lord'),
 (362,291,41,34,NULL,'No,but they worshipped the jinns most of them believed in them'),
 (363,291,158,37,NULL,'And they have invented a blood relationship between Him and jinns'),
 (364,291,158,37,NULL,'but the jinns know that they have indeed to appear (before his judgemental seat)'),
 (365,291,29,41,NULL,'And the unbelievers will say our Lord! show us those,among jinns and men,who misled us.'),
 (366,291,29,46,NULL,'Behold,we turned towards you a company of jinns(quietly) listening to quran'),
 (367,291,56,51,NULL,'i have only created jinns and men,that they may serve me'),
 (368,291,15,55,NULL,'And He created jinns from fire free of smoke'),
 (369,291,33,55,NULL,'O you assembly of jinns and men if it be you can pass beyond the zones of the heavens and the earth,pass you.'),
 (370,291,39,55,NULL,'On that Day no question will be asked of man or jinn as to his sin'),
 (371,291,56,55,NULL,'in them will be (Maidens), chaste,restraining their glances,whom no man or jinn before them has touched'),
 (372,291,74,55,NULL,'whom no man or jinn before them has touched'),
 (373,291,1,72,NULL,'say:it has been revealed to me that a company of jinns listened(to the quran).'),
 (374,291,6,72,NULL,'True there were persons among mankind who took shelter with persons among jinns,but they increased them in folly'),
 (375,291,6,114,NULL,'Among jinns and among men'),
 (376,292,29,9,NULL,'nor acknowledge the religion of truth,(even if they are)of the people of the Book,until they pay the jizyah with willing submission,and feel themselves subdued'),
 (377,293,6,4,NULL,'if then you find sound judgement in them,release their property to them.'),
 (378,293,60,4,NULL,'their(real)wish is to resort together for judgement to satan,though they were ordered to reject him.'),
 (379,293,50,5,NULL,'But who for a people whose faith is assured cant give better judgment than Allah?'),
 (380,293,50,5,NULL,'Do they then seek after a judgement of (the Days of) ignorance.'),
 (381,293,96,6,NULL,'such is the judgement and ordering of (Him), the the Exalted to power,the omniscient'),
 (382,293,150,7,NULL,'did you make haste to bring on the judgement of your Lord?'),
 (383,293,37,13,NULL,'Thus have we revealed it to be a judgement of authority in Arabic'),
 (384,293,74,21,NULL,'And to Lut,too,we gave judgement and knowledge'),
 (385,293,78,21,NULL,'we did witness their judgement'),
 (386,293,46,40,NULL,'and (the sentence will be) on the day that judgement will be established'),
 (387,294,193,2,NULL,'And fight them on until..there prevail justice and faith in Allah.'),
 (388,294,18,3,NULL,'That is the witness of Allah ,His angels and those endued with knowledge,standing firm on justice'),
 (389,294,8,4,NULL,'and speak to them words of kindness and justice'),
 (390,294,49,4,NULL,'But never will they fail to receive justice in the least little things'),
 (391,294,58,4,NULL,'And who you judge between man and man ,to judge with justice'),
 (392,294,127,4,NULL,'that you stand firm to justice orphans'),
 (393,294,151,6,NULL,'Take not life which Allah has made scared,except by way of justice and Law'),
 (394,294,152,6,NULL,'give measure and weight with (full) justice'),
 (395,294,90,16,NULL,'Allah commands justice, the doing of good,and liberality to kith and kin'),
 (396,295,184,2,NULL,'but if any of you is ill,or on a journey,..'),
 (397,295,185,2,NULL,'but if anyone is ill,or on a journey'),
 (398,295,43,4,NULL,'if you are ill,or on a journey,or one of you comes from offices of nature'),
 (399,295,6,5,NULL,'But if you are ill,or on a journey,or one of you comes from offices of nature'),
 (400,295,106,5,NULL,'two just men of your own'),
 (401,296,71,39,NULL,'And it keepers will say, Did not messangers come to you from among yourselves.'),
 (402,296,73,39,NULL,'its gate will be opened and its keeper will say'),
 (403,296,49,40,NULL,'Those in the fire will say to the keepers of Hell:"pray to your Lord to lighten us the penalty for a day(at least)!"'),
 (404,296,8,67,NULL,'Almost bursting with fury every time a group is cast therein,its keeper will ask Did no warner come to you?'),
 (405,296,33,83,NULL,'But they had not been sent as keepers over them!'),
 (406,297,59,6,NULL,'With him are the keys of the unseen,that treasures that none knows but He'),
 (407,297,61,24,NULL,'that you should eat in your own houses or in houses of which the keys are in your possession or in house of a sincere friend of yours'),
 (408,297,76,28,NULL,'such were the treasures we had'),
 (409,298,83,2,NULL,'Treat with kindness your parents and kindred and orphans and those in need'),
 (410,298,143,2,NULL,'For Allah is to all people most surely full of kindness,Most merciful'),
 (411,298,207,2,NULL,'And Allah is full of kindness to (His) devotees'),
 (412,298,229,2,NULL,'...after that the parties should either hold together on equitable terms,or separate with kindness.'),
 (413,298,30,3,NULL,'And Allah is full of kindness for those that serve Him.'),
 (414,298,5,4,NULL,'But feed and clothe them therewith, and speak to them words of kindness and justice.'),
 (415,298,8,4,NULL,'and speak to them words of kindness and justice'),
 (416,298,19,4,NULL,'On the contary live with them on a footing of kindness and equity'),
 (417,298,47,16,NULL,'Or that He may not call them to account by a process of slow wastage for your Lord is indeed full of kindness and mercy'),
 (418,298,24,17,NULL,'And out of kindness lower to them the wing of humility and say '),
 (419,298,28,17,NULL,'And even if you have to turn away from them in pursuit of the mercy from your Lord which you do expect,yet speak to them a word of easy kindness.'),
 (420,299,95,5,NULL,'if any of you does so intentionally,the compensation is an offering brought to the kabah of a domestic animal'),
 (421,299,97,5,NULL,'Allah made the kabah the sacred House an asylum of security for men'),
 (422,300,5,76,NULL,'As to the Righteous,they shall drink of a cup(of wine) mixed with kafur.'),
 (423,301,177,2,NULL,'But it is Righteous to spend of your substance for your kin'),
 (424,301,180,2,NULL,'It is prescribed,when death approaches any of you,if he leave any goods,that he make a bequest to parents and next of kin'),
 (425,301,68,3,NULL,'Without doubt,among men, the nearest of kin to Abraham,are those who follow him'),
 (426,301,135,4,NULL,'Stand out firmly for justice,as witness to Allah,even as against yourselves,or your parents or your kin'),
 (427,301,113,9,NULL,'it is not fitting for the prophet and those who believe,that they should pray for forgiveness for pagans,even though they be of kin'),
 (428,301,23,42,NULL,'say:"No reward do i ask of you for this except the love of those near of kin"'),
 (429,302,13,5,NULL,'for Allah loves those who are kind.'),
 (430,302,117,9,NULL,'but He turned to them(also):for He is unto them Most Kind,Most Merciful.'),
 (431,302,128,9,NULL,'it grieves him that you should perish ardently anxious is he over you to the believers is he most kind and merciful'),
 (432,302,7,16,NULL,'for your Lord is indeed Most kind,Most Merciful'),
 (433,302,23,17,NULL,'your Lord has decreed that you worship none but Him,and that you be kind to parents.'),
 (434,302,14,19,NULL,'And kind to his parents,and he was not overbearing or rebellious.'),
 (435,303,29,4,NULL,'Nor kill or destroy yourselves for verily Allah has been to you Most Merciful'),
 (436,303,92,4,NULL,'if one (so) kills a believer,it is ordained that he should free a believing slave'),
 (437,303,92,4,NULL,'Never should a believer kill a Believer;but (if it so happens) by mistake,(compensation is due)'),
 (438,303,93,4,NULL,' if a man kills a believer intentionally,his recompense is Hell,to abide therein(for ever):'),
 (439,303,157,4,NULL,'for of a surety they killed him not'),
 (440,303,157,4,NULL,'But they killed him not,nor crucified him,but so it was made to appear to them,..'),
 (441,303,3,5,NULL,'that which has been killed by strangling,or by a violent blow, or by a headlong fall,or by being gored to death;'),
 (442,303,95,5,NULL,'a domestic animal equivalent to that one he killed,an adjudged by two just men among you;'),
 (443,303,95,5,NULL,'O you who believer kill not game while in the sacred precints or in pilgrim grab'),
 (444,303,151,6,NULL,'kill not your children on a plea of want we provide sustenanace for you and for them'),
 (445,303,31,17,NULL,'kill not your children for fear of want we shall provide'),
 (446,304,8,29,NULL,'we have enjoined on man kindness to parents'),
 (447,304,15,46,NULL,'we have enjoined on man kindness to his parents'),
 (448,304,10,59,NULL,'Our Lord! you are indeed full of kindness,Most Merciful'),
 (449,304,13,71,NULL,'what is the matter with you,that you place not your hope for kindness and long-suffering in Allah'),
 (450,304,17,90,NULL,'and enjoin deeds of kindness and compassion.'),
 (451,304,83,2,NULL,'Treat with kindness your parents and kindred and orphans and those in need'),
 (452,304,215,2,NULL,'say:whatever you spend that is good, is for parents and kindred and orphans and..'),
 (453,304,57,8,NULL,'But kindred by blood have prior rights against each other in the Book of Allah'),
 (454,304,24,9,NULL,'say:if it be that your fathers,your sons,your brothers,your mates,your kindred.'),
 (455,304,26,17,NULL,'And render to the kindred their due rights,as (also) to those in want,and the wayfarer.'),
 (456,304,22,58,NULL,'loving those who resist Allah and his messanger,even though they were their fathers or their sons, or their brohers,or their kindred.'),
