 (9641,2,'Seest thou? If We do let them enjoy (this life) for a few years,',NULL,26,205),
 (9642,3,'Hast thou then seen, if We content them for (long) years,',NULL,26,205),
 (9643,1,'Then there comes to them that with which they are threatened,',NULL,26,206),
 (9644,2,'Yet there comes to them at length the (Punishment) which they were promised!',NULL,26,206),
 (9645,3,'And then cometh that which they were promised,',NULL,26,206),
 (9646,1,'That which they were made to enjoy shall not avail them?',NULL,26,207),
 (9647,2,'It will profit them not that they enjoyed (this life)!',NULL,26,207),
 (9648,3,'(How) that wherewith they were contented naught availeth them?',NULL,26,207),
 (9649,1,'And We did not destroy any town but it had (its) warners,',NULL,26,208),
 (9650,2,'Never did We destroy a population, but had its warners -',NULL,26,208),
 (9651,3,'And We destroyed no township but it had its warners',NULL,26,208),
 (9652,1,'To remind, and We are never unjust.',NULL,26,209),
 (9653,2,'By way of reminder; and We never are unjust.',NULL,26,209),
 (9654,3,'For reminder, for We never were oppressors.',NULL,26,209),
 (9655,1,'And the Shaitans have not come down with it.',NULL,26,210),
 (9656,2,'No evil ones have brought down this (Revelation):',NULL,26,210),
 (9657,3,'The devils did not bring it down.',NULL,26,210),
 (9658,1,'And it behoves them not, and they have not the power to do (it).',NULL,26,211),
 (9659,2,'It would neither suit them nor would they be able (to produce it).',NULL,26,211),
 (9660,3,'It is not meet for them, nor is it in their power,',NULL,26,211),
 (9661,1,'Most surely they are far removed from the hearing of it.',NULL,26,212),
 (9662,2,'Indeed they have been removed far from even (a chance of) hearing it.',NULL,26,212),
 (9663,3,'Lo! verily they are banished from the hearing.',NULL,26,212),
 (9664,1,'So call not upon another god with Allah, lest you be of those who are punished.',NULL,26,213),
 (9665,2,'So call not on any other god with Allah, or thou wilt be among those under the Penalty.',NULL,26,213),
 (9666,3,'Therefor invoke not with Allah another god, lest thou be one of the doomed.',NULL,26,213),
 (9667,1,'And warn your nearest relations,',NULL,26,214),
 (9668,2,'And admonish thy nearest kinsmen,',NULL,26,214),
 (9669,3,'And warn thy tribe of near kindred,',NULL,26,214),
 (9670,1,'And be kind to him who follows you of the believers.',NULL,26,215),
 (9671,2,'And lower thy wing to the Believers who follow thee.',NULL,26,215),
 (9672,3,'And lower thy wing (in kindness) unto those believers who follow thee.',NULL,26,215),
 (9673,1,'But if they disobey you, then say: Surely I am clear of what you do.',NULL,26,216),
 (9674,2,'Then if they disobey thee, say: "I am free (of responsibility) for what ye do!"',NULL,26,216),
 (9675,3,'And if they (thy kinsfolk) disobey thee, say: Lo! I am innocent of what they do.',NULL,26,216),
 (9676,1,'And rely on the Mighty, the Merciful,',NULL,26,217),
 (9677,2,'And put thy trust on the Exalted in Might, the Merciful,-',NULL,26,217),
 (9678,3,'And put thy trust in the Mighty, the Merciful.',NULL,26,217),
 (9679,1,'Who sees you when you stand up.',NULL,26,218),
 (9680,2,'Who seeth thee standing forth (in prayer),',NULL,26,218),
 (9681,3,'Who seeth thee when thou standest up (to pray)',NULL,26,218),
 (9682,1,'And your turning over and over among those who prostrate themselves before Allah.',NULL,26,219),
 (9683,2,'And thy movements among those who prostrate themselves,',NULL,26,219),
 (9684,3,'And (seeth) thine abasement among those who fall prostrate (in worship).',NULL,26,219),
 (9685,1,'Surely He is the Hearing, the Knowing.',NULL,26,220),
 (9686,2,'For it is He Who heareth and knoweth all things.',NULL,26,220),
 (9687,3,'Lo! He, only He, is the Hearer, the Knower.',NULL,26,220),
 (9688,1,'Shall I inform you (of him) upon whom the Shaitans descend?',NULL,26,221),
 (9689,2,'Shall I inform you, (O people!), on whom it is that the evil ones descend?',NULL,26,221),
 (9690,3,'Shall I inform you upon whom the devils descend?',NULL,26,221),
 (9691,1,'They descend upon every lying, sinful one,',NULL,26,222),
 (9692,2,'They descend on every lying, wicked person,',NULL,26,222),
 (9693,3,'They descend on every sinful, false one.',NULL,26,222),
 (9694,1,'They incline their ears, and most of them are liars.',NULL,26,223),
 (9695,2,'(Into whose ears) they pour hearsay vanities, and most of them are liars.',NULL,26,223),
 (9696,3,'They listen eagerly, but most of them are liars.',NULL,26,223),
 (9697,1,'And as to the poets, those who go astray follow them.',NULL,26,224),
 (9698,2,'And the Poets,- It is those straying in Evil, who follow them:',NULL,26,224),
 (9699,3,'As for poets, the erring follow them.',NULL,26,224),
 (9700,1,'Do you not see that they wander about bewildered in every valley?',NULL,26,225),
 (9701,2,'Seest thou not that they wander distracted in every valley?-',NULL,26,225),
 (9702,3,'Hast thou not seen how they stray in every valley,',NULL,26,225),
 (9703,1,'And that they say that which they do not do,',NULL,26,226),
 (9704,2,'And that they say what they practise not?-',NULL,26,226),
 (9705,3,'And how they say that which they do not?',NULL,26,226),
 (9706,1,'Except those who believe and do good and remember Allah much, and defend themselves after they are oppressed; and they who act unjustly shall know to what final place of turning they shall turn back.',NULL,26,227),
 (9707,2,'Except those who believe, work righteousness, engage much in the remembrance of Allah, and defend themselves only after they are unjustly attacked. And soon will the unjust assailants know what vicissitudes their affairs will take!',NULL,26,227),
 (9708,3,'Save those who believe and do good works, and remember Allah much, and vindicate themselves after they have been wronged. Those who do wrong will come to know by what a (great) reverse they will be overturned!',NULL,26,227),
 (9709,1,'Ta Sin! These are the verses of the Quran and the Book that makes (things) clear',NULL,27,1),
 (9710,2,'These are verses of the Qur''an,-a book that makes (things) clear;',NULL,27,1),
 (9711,3,'Ta. Sin. These are revelations of the Qur''an and a Scripture that maketh plain;',NULL,27,1),
 (9712,1,'A guidance and good news for the believers,',NULL,27,2),
 (9713,2,'A guide: and glad tidings for the believers,-',NULL,27,2),
 (9714,3,'A guidance and good tidings for believers',NULL,27,2),
 (9715,1,'Who keep up prayer and pay the poor-rate, and of the hereafter, they are sure.',NULL,27,3),
 (9716,2,'Those who establish regular prayers and give in regular charity, and also have (full) assurance of the hereafter.',NULL,27,3),
 (9717,3,'Who establish worship and pay the poor-due and are sure of the Hereafter.',NULL,27,3),
 (9718,1,'As to those who do not believe in the hereafter, We have surely made their deeds fair-seeming to them, but they blindly wander on.',NULL,27,4),
 (9719,2,'As to those who believe not in the Hereafter, We have made their deeds pleasing in their eyes; and so they wander about in distraction.',NULL,27,4),
 (9720,3,'Lo! as for those who believe not in the Hereafter, We have made their works fairseeming unto them so that they are all astray.',NULL,27,4),
 (9721,1,'These are they who shall have an evil punishment, and in the hereafter they shall be the greatest losers.',NULL,27,5),
 (9722,2,'Such are they for whom a grievous Penalty is (waiting); and in the Hereafter theirs will be the greatest loss.',NULL,27,5),
 (9723,3,'Those are they for whom is the worst of punishment, and in the Hereafter they will be the greatest losers.',NULL,27,5),
 (9724,1,'And most surely you are made to receive the Quran from the Wise, the Knowing Allah.',NULL,27,6),
 (9725,2,'As to thee, the Qur''an is bestowed upon thee from the presence of one who is wise and all-knowing.',NULL,27,6),
 (9726,3,'Lo! as for thee (Muhammad), thou verily receivest the Qur''an from the presence of One Wise, Aware.',NULL,27,6),
 (9727,1,'When Musa said to his family: Surely I see fire; I will bring to you from it some news, or I will bring to you therefrom a burning firebrand so that you may warm yourselves.',NULL,27,7),
 (9728,2,'Behold! Moses said to his family: "I perceive a fire; soon will I bring you from there some information, or I will bring you a burning brand to light our fuel, that ye may warn yourselves.',NULL,27,7),
 (9729,3,'(Remember) when Moses said unto his household: Lo! I spy afar off a fire; I will bring you tidings thence, or bring to you a borrowed flame that ye may warm yourselves.',NULL,27,7),
 (9730,1,'So when he came to it a voice was uttered saying: Blessed is Whoever is in the fire and whatever is about it; and glory be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds;',NULL,27,8),
 (9731,2,'But when he came to the (fire), a voice was heard: "Blessed are those in the fire and those around: and glory to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,27,8),
 (9732,3,'But when he reached it, he was called, saying: Blessed is Whosoever is in the fire and Whosoever is round about it! And Glorified be Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,27,8),
 (9733,1,'O Musa! surely I am Allah, the Mighty, the Wise;',NULL,27,9),
 (9734,2,'"O Moses! verily, I am Allah, the exalted in might, the wise!....',NULL,27,9),
 (9735,3,'O Moses! Lo! it is I, Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,27,9),
 (9736,1,'And cast down your staff. So when he saw it in motion as if it were a serpent, he turned back retreating and did not return: O Musa! fear not; surely the messengers shall not fear in My presence;',NULL,27,10),
 (9737,2,'"Now do thou throw thy rod!" But when he saw it moving (of its own accord)as if it had been a snake, he turned back in retreat, and retraced not his steps: "O Moses!" (it was said), "Fear not: truly, in My presence, those called as messengers have no fear,-',NULL,27,10),
 (9738,3,'And throw down thy staff! But when he saw it writhing as it were a demon, he turned to flee headlong; (but it was said unto him): O Moses! Fear not! the emissaries fear not in My presence,',NULL,27,10),
 (9739,1,'Neither he who has been unjust, then he does good instead after evil, for surely I am the Forgiving, the Merciful:',NULL,27,11),
 (9740,2,'"But if any have done wrong and have thereafter substituted good to take the place of evil, truly, I am Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,27,11),
 (9741,3,'Save him who hath done wrong and afterward hath changed evil for good. And lo! I am Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,27,11),
 (9742,1,'And enter your hand into the opening of your bosom, it shall come forth white without evil; among nine signs to Firon and his people, surely they are a transgressing people.',NULL,27,12),
 (9743,2,'"Now put thy hand into thy bosom, and it will come forth white without stain (or harm): (these are) among the nine Signs (thou wilt take) to Pharaoh and his people: for they are a people rebellious in transgression."',NULL,27,12),
 (9744,3,'And put thy hand into the bosom of thy robe, it will come forth white but unhurt. (This will be one) among nine tokens unto Pharaoh and his people Lo! they were ever evil-living folk.',NULL,27,12),
 (9745,1,'So when Our clear signs came to them, they said: This is clear enchantment.',NULL,27,13),
 (9746,2,'But when Our Signs came to them, that should have opened their eyes, they said: "This is sorcery manifest!"',NULL,27,13),
 (9747,3,'But when Our tokens came unto them, plain to see, they said: This is mere magic,',NULL,27,13),
 (9748,1,'And they denied them unjustly and proudly while their soul had been convinced of them; consider, then how was the end of the mischief-makers.',NULL,27,14),
 (9749,2,'And they rejected those Signs in iniquity and arrogance, though their souls were convinced thereof: so see what was the end of those who acted corruptly!',NULL,27,14),
 (9750,3,'And they denied them, though their souls acknowledged them, for spite and arrogance. Then see the nature of the consequence for the wrong-doers!',NULL,27,14),
 (9751,1,'And certainly We gave knowledge to Dawood and Sulaiman, and they both said: Praise be to Allah, Who has made us to excel many of His believing servants.',NULL,27,15),
 (9752,2,'We gave (in the past) knowledge to David and Solomon: And they both said: "Praise be to Allah, Who has favoured us above many of his servants who believe!"',NULL,27,15),
 (9753,3,'And We verily gave knowledge unto David and Solomon, and they said: Praise be to Allah, Who hath preferred us above many of His believing slaves!',NULL,27,15),
 (9754,1,'And Sulaiman was Dawood''s heir, and he said: O men! we have been taught the language of birds, and we have been given all things; most surely this is manifest grace.',NULL,27,16),
 (9755,2,'And Solomon was David''s heir. He said: "O ye people! We have been taught the speech of birds, and on us has been bestowed (a little) of all things: this is indeed Grace manifest (from Allah.)"',NULL,27,16),
 (9756,3,'And Solomon was David''s heir. And he said: O mankind! Lo! we have been taught the language of birds, and have been given (abundance) of all things. This surely is evident favour.',NULL,27,16),
 (9757,1,'And his hosts of the jinn and the men and the birds were gathered to him, and they were formed into groups.',NULL,27,17),
 (9758,2,'And before Solomon were marshalled his hosts,- of Jinns and men and birds, and they were all kept in order and ranks.',NULL,27,17),
 (9759,3,'And there were gathered together unto Solomon his armies of the jinn and humankind, and of the birds, and they were set in battle order;',NULL,27,17),
 (9760,1,'Until when they came to the valley of the Naml, a Namlite said: O Naml! enter your houses, (that) Sulaiman and his hosts may not crush you while they do not know.',NULL,27,18),
 (9761,2,'At length, when they came to a (lowly) valley of ants, one of the ants said: "O ye ants, get into your habitations, lest Solomon and his hosts crush you (under foot) without knowing it."',NULL,27,18),
 (9762,3,'Till, when they reached the Valley of the Ants, an ant exclaimed: O ants! Enter your dwellings lest Solomon and his armies crush you, unperceiving.',NULL,27,18),
 (9763,1,'So he smiled, wondering at her word, and said: My Lord! grant me that I should be grateful for Thy favor which Thou hast bestowed on me and on my parents, and that I should do good such as Thou art pleased with, and make me enter, by Thy mercy, into Thy servants, the good ones.',NULL,27,19),
 (9764,2,'So he smiled, amused at her speech; and he said: "O my Lord! so order me that I may be grateful for Thy favours, which thou hast bestowed on me and on my parents, and that I may work the righteousness that will please Thee: And admit me, by Thy Grace, to the ranks of Thy righteous Servants."',NULL,27,19),
 (9765,3,'And (Solomon) smiled, laughing at her speech, and said: My Lord, arouse me to be thankful for Thy favour wherewith Thou hast favoured me and my parents, and to do good that shall be pleasing unto Thee, and include me in (the number of) Thy righteous slaves.',NULL,27,19),
 (9766,1,'And he reviewed the birds, then said: How is it I see not the hoopoe or is it that he is of the absentees?',NULL,27,20),
 (9767,2,'And he took a muster of the Birds; and he said: "Why is it I see not the Hoopoe? Or is he among the absentees?',NULL,27,20),
 (9768,3,'And he sought among the birds and said: How is it that I see not the hoopoe, or is he among the absent?',NULL,27,20),
 (9769,1,'I will most certainly punish him with a severe punishment, or kill him, or he shall bring to me a clear plea.',NULL,27,21),
 (9770,2,'"I will certainly punish him with a severe penalty, or execute him, unless he bring me a clear reason (for absence)."',NULL,27,21),
 (9771,3,'I verily will punish him with hard punishment or I verily will slay him, or he verily shall bring me a plain excuse.',NULL,27,21),
 (9772,1,'And he tarried not long, then said: I comprehend that which you do not comprehend and I have brought to you a sure information from Sheba.',NULL,27,22),
 (9773,2,'But the Hoopoe tarried not far: he (came up and) said: "I have compassed (territory) which thou hast not compassed, and I have come to thee from Saba with tidings true.',NULL,27,22),
 (9774,3,'But he was not long in coming, and he said: I have found out (a thing) that thou apprehendest not, and I come unto thee from Sheba with sure tidings.',NULL,27,22),
 (9775,1,'Surely I found a woman ruling over them, and she has been given abundance and she has a mighty throne:',NULL,27,23),
 (9776,2,'"I found (there) a woman ruling over them and provided with every requisite; and she has a magnificent throne.',NULL,27,23),
 (9777,3,'Lo! I found a woman ruling over them, and she hath been given (abundance) of all things, and hers is a mighty throne.',NULL,27,23),
 (9778,1,'I found her and her people adoring the sun instead of Allah, and the Shaitan has made their deeds fair-seeming to them and thus turned them from the way, so they do not go aright',NULL,27,24),
 (9779,2,'"I found her and her people worshipping the sun besides Allah: Satan has made their deeds seem pleasing in their eyes, and has kept them away from the Path,- so they receive no guidance,-',NULL,27,24),
 (9780,3,'I found her and her people worshipping the sun instead of Allah; and Satan maketh their works fairseeming unto them, and debarreth them from the way (of Truth), so that they go not aright;',NULL,27,24),
 (9781,1,'That they do not make obeisance to Allah, Who brings forth what is hidden in the heavens and the earth and knows what you hide and what you make manifest:',NULL,27,25),
 (9782,2,'"(Kept them away from the Path), that they should not worship Allah, Who brings to light what is hidden in the heavens and the earth, and knows what ye hide and what ye reveal.',NULL,27,25),
 (9783,3,'So that they worship not Allah, Who bringeth forth the hidden in the heavens and the earth, and knoweth what ye hide and what ye proclaim,',NULL,27,25),
 (9784,1,'Allah, there is no god but He: He is the Lord of mighty power.',NULL,27,26),
 (9785,2,'"Allah!- there is no god but He!- Lord of the Throne Supreme!"',NULL,27,26),
 (9786,3,'Allah; there is no Allah save Him, the Lord of the Tremendous Throne.',NULL,27,26),
 (9787,1,'He said: We will see whether you have told the truth or whether you are of the liars:',NULL,27,27),
 (9788,2,'(Solomon) said: "Soon shall we see whether thou hast told the truth or lied!',NULL,27,27),
 (9789,3,'(Solomon) said: We shall see whether thou speakest truth or whether thou art of the liars.',NULL,27,27),
 (9790,1,'Take this my letter and hand it over to them, then turn away from them and see what (answer) they return.',NULL,27,28),
 (9791,2,'"Go thou, with this letter of mine, and deliver it to them: then draw back from them, and (wait to) see what answer they return"...',NULL,27,28),
 (9792,3,'Go with this my letter and throw it down unto them; then turn away and see what (answer) they return,',NULL,27,28),
 (9793,1,'She said: O chief! surely an honorable letter has been delivered to me',NULL,27,29),
 (9794,2,'(The queen) said: "Ye chiefs! here is delivered to me - a letter worthy of respect.',NULL,27,29),
 (9795,3,'(The Queen of Sheba) said (when she received the letter): O chieftains! Lo! there hath been thrown unto me a noble letter.',NULL,27,29),
 (9796,1,'Surely it is from Sulaiman, and surely it is in the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful;',NULL,27,30),
 (9797,2,'"It is from Solomon, and is (as follows): ''In the name of Allah, Most Gracious, Most Merciful:',NULL,27,30),
 (9798,3,'Lo! it is from Solomon, and lo! it is: In the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful;',NULL,27,30),
 (9799,1,'Saying: exalt not yourselves against me and come to me in submission.',NULL,27,31),
 (9800,2,'"''Be ye not arrogant against me, but come to me in submission (to the true Religion).''"',NULL,27,31),
 (9801,3,'Exalt not yourselves against me, but come unto me as those who surrender.',NULL,27,31),
 (9802,1,'She said: O chiefs! give me advice respecting my affair: I never decide an affair until you are in my presence.',NULL,27,32),
 (9803,2,'She said: "Ye chiefs! advise me in (this) my affair: no affair have I decided except in your presence."',NULL,27,32),
 (9804,3,'She said: O chieftains! Pronounce for me in my case. I decide no case till ye are present with me.',NULL,27,32),
 (9805,1,'They said: We are possessors of strength and possessors of mighty prowess, and the command is yours, therefore see what you will command.',NULL,27,33),
 (9806,2,'They said: "We are endued with strength, and given to vehement war: but the command is with thee; so consider what thou wilt command."',NULL,27,33),
 (9807,3,'They said: We are lords of might and lords of great prowess, but it is for thee to command; so consider what thou wilt command.',NULL,27,33),
 (9808,1,'She said: Surely the kings, when they enter a town, ruin it and make the noblest of its people to be low, and thus they (always) do;',NULL,27,34),
 (9809,2,'She said: "Kings, when they enter a country, despoil it, and make the noblest of its people its meanest thus do they behave.',NULL,27,34),
 (9810,3,'She said: Lo! kings, when they enter a township, ruin it and make the honour of its people shame. Thus will they do.',NULL,27,34),
 (9811,1,'And surely I am going to send a present to them, and shall wait to see what (answer) do the messengers bring back.',NULL,27,35),
 (9812,2,'"But I am going to send him a present, and (wait) to see with what (answer) return (my) ambassadors."',NULL,27,35),
 (9813,3,'But lo! I am going to send a present unto them, and to see with what (answer) the messengers return.',NULL,27,35),
 (9814,1,'So when he came to Sulaiman, he said: What! will you help me with wealth? But what Allah has given me is better than what He has given you. Nay, you are exultant because of your present;',NULL,27,36),
 (9815,2,'Now when (the embassy) came to Solomon, he said: "Will ye give me abundance in wealth? But that which Allah has given me is better than that which He has given you! Nay it is ye who rejoice in your gift!',NULL,27,36),
 (9816,3,'So when (the envoy) came unto Solomon, (the King) said: What! Would ye help me with wealth? But that which Allah hath given me is better than that which He hath given you. Nay it is ye (and not I) who exult in your gift.',NULL,27,36),
 (9817,1,'Go back to them, so we will most certainly come to them with hosts which they shall have no power to oppose, and we will most certainly expel them therefrom in abasement, and they shall be in a state of ignominy.',NULL,27,37),
 (9818,2,'"Go back to them, and be sure we shall come to them with such hosts as they will never be able to meet: We shall expel them from there in disgrace, and they will feel humbled (indeed)."',NULL,27,37),
 (9819,3,'Return unto them. We verily shall come unto them with hosts that they cannot resist, and we shall drive them out from thence with shame, and they will be abased.',NULL,27,37),
 (9820,1,'He said: O chiefs! which of you can bring to me her throne before they come to me in submission?',NULL,27,38),
 (9821,2,'He said (to his own men): "Ye chiefs! which of you can bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?"',NULL,27,38),
 (9822,3,'He said: O chiefs! Which of you will bring me her throne before they come unto me, surrendering?',NULL,27,38),
 (9823,1,'One audacious among the jinn said: I will bring it to you before you rise up from your place; and most surely I am strong (and) trusty for it.',NULL,27,39),
 (9824,2,'Said an ''Ifrit, of the Jinns: "I will bring it to thee before thou rise from thy council: indeed I have full strength for the purpose, and may be trusted."',NULL,27,39),
 (9825,3,'A stalwart of the jinn said: I will bring it thee before thou canst rise from thy place. Lo! I verily am strong and trusty for such work.',NULL,27,39),
 (9826,1,'One who had the knowledge of the Book said: I will bring it to you in the twinkling of an eye. Then when he saw it settled beside him, he said: This is of the grace of my Lord that He may try me whether I am grateful or ungrateful; and whoever is grateful, he is grateful only for his own soul, and whoever is ungrateful, then surely my Lord is Self-sufficient, Honored.',NULL,27,40),
 (9827,2,'Said one who had knowledge of the Book: "I will bring it to thee within the twinkling of an eye!" Then when (Solomon) saw it placed firmly before him, he said: "This is by the Grace of my Lord!- to test me whether I am grateful or ungrateful! and if any is grateful, truly his gratitude is (a gain) for his own soul; but if any is ungrateful, truly my Lord is Free of all Needs, Supreme in Honour !"',NULL,27,40),
 (9828,3,'One with whom was knowledge of the Scripture said: I will bring it thee before thy gaze returneth unto thee. And when he saw it set in his presence, (Solomon) said: This is of the bounty of my Lord, that He may try me whether I give thanks or am ungrateful. Whosoever giveth thanks he only giveth thanks for (the good of) his own soul; and whosoever is ungrateful (is ungrateful only to his own soul''s hurt). For lo! my Lord is Absolute in independence, Bountiful.',NULL,27,40),
 (9829,1,'He said: Alter her throne for her, we will see whether she follows the right way or is of those who do not go aright.',NULL,27,41),
 (9830,2,'He said: "Transform her throne out of all recognition by her: let us see whether she is guided (to the truth) or is one of those who receive no guidance."',NULL,27,41),
 (9831,3,'He said: Disguise her throne for her that we may see whether she will go aright or be of those not rightly guided.',NULL,27,41),
 (9832,1,'So when she came, it was said: Is your throne like this? She said: It is as it were the same, and we were given the knowledge before it, and we were submissive.',NULL,27,42),
 (9833,2,'So when she arrived, she was asked, "Is this thy throne?" She said, "It was just like this; and knowledge was bestowed on us in advance of this, and we have submitted to Allah (in Islam)."',NULL,27,42),
 (9834,3,'So, when she came, it was said (unto her): Is thy throne like this? She said: (It is) as though it were the very one. And (Solomon said): We were given the knowledge before her and we had surrendered (to Allah).',NULL,27,42),
 (9835,1,'And what she worshipped besides Allah prevented her, surely she was of an unbelieving people.',NULL,27,43),
 (9836,2,'And he diverted her from the worship of others besides Allah: for she was (sprung) of a people that had no faith.',NULL,27,43),
 (9837,3,'And (all) that she was wont to worship instead of Allah hindered her, for she came of disbelieving folk.',NULL,27,43),
 (9838,1,'It was said to her: Enter the palace; but when she saw it she deemed it to be a great expanse of water, and bared her legs. He said: Surely it is a palace made smooth with glass. She said: My Lord! surely I have been unjust to myself, and I submit with Sulaiman to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,27,44),
 (9839,2,'She was asked to enter the lofty Palace: but when she saw it, she thought it was a lake of water, and she (tucked up her skirts), uncovering her legs. He said: "This is but a palace paved smooth with slabs of glass." She said: "O my Lord! I have indeed wronged my soul: I do (now) submit (in Islam), with Solomon, to the Lord of the Worlds."',NULL,27,44),
 (9840,3,'It was said unto her: Enter the hall. And when she saw it she deemed it a pool and bared her legs. (Solomon) said: Lo! it is a hall, made smooth, of glass. She said: My Lord! Lo! I have wronged myself, and I surrender with Solomon unto Allah, the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,27,44),
 (9841,1,'And certainly We sent to Samood their brother Salih, saying: Serve Allah; and lo! they became two sects quarrelling with each other.',NULL,27,45),
 (9842,2,'We sent (aforetime), to the Thamud, their brother Salih, saying, "Serve Allah": But behold, they became two factions quarrelling with each other.',NULL,27,45),
 (9843,3,'And We verily sent unto Thamud their brother Salih, saying: Worship Allah. And lo! they (then became two parties quarrelling.',NULL,27,45),
 (9844,1,'He said: O my people! why do you seek to hasten on the evil before the good? Why do you not ask forgiveness of Allah so that you may be dealt with mercifully?',NULL,27,46),
 (9845,2,'He said: "O my people! why ask ye to hasten on the evil in preference to the good? If only ye ask Allah for forgiveness, ye may hope to receive mercy.',NULL,27,46),
 (9846,3,'He said: O my people! Why will ye hasten on the evil rather than the good? Why will ye not ask pardon of Allah, that ye may receive mercy.',NULL,27,46),
 (9847,1,'They said: We have met with ill luck on account of you and on account of those with you. He said: The cause of your evil fortune is with Allah; nay, you are a people who are tried.',NULL,27,47),
 (9848,2,'They said: "Ill omen do we augur from thee and those that are with thee". He said: "Your ill omen is with Allah; yea, ye are a people under trial."',NULL,27,47),
 (9849,3,'They said: We augur evil of thee and those with thee. He said: Your evil augury is with Allah. Nay, but ye are folk that are being tested.',NULL,27,47),
 (9850,1,'And there were in the city nine persons who made mischief in the land and did not act aright.',NULL,27,48),
 (9851,2,'There were in the city nine men of a family, who made mischief in the land, and would not reform.',NULL,27,48),
 (9852,3,'And there were in the city nine persons who made mischief in the land and reformed not.',NULL,27,48),
 (9853,1,'They said: Swear to each other by Allah that we will certainly make a sudden attack on him and his family by night, then we will say to his heir: We did not witness the destruction of his family, and we are most surely truthful.',NULL,27,49),
 (9854,2,'They said: "Swear a mutual oath by Allah that we shall make a secret night attack on him and his people, and that we shall then say to his heir (when he seeks vengeance): ''We were not present at the slaughter of his people, and we are positively telling the truth.''"',NULL,27,49),
 (9855,3,'They said: Swear one to another by Allah that we verily will attack him and his household by night, and afterward we will surely say unto his friend: We witnessed not the destruction of his household. And lo! we are truthtellers.',NULL,27,49),
 (9856,1,'And they planned a plan, and We planned a plan while they perceived not.',NULL,27,50),
 (9857,2,'They plotted and planned, but We too planned, even while they perceived it not.',NULL,27,50),
 (9858,3,'So they plotted a plot: and We plotted a plot, while they perceived not.',NULL,27,50),
 (9859,1,'See, then, how was the end of their plan that We destroyed them and their people, all (of them).',NULL,27,51),
 (9860,2,'Then see what was the end of their plot!- this, that We destroyed them and their people, all (of them).',NULL,27,51),
 (9861,3,'Then see the nature of the consequence of their plotting, for lo! We destroyed them and their people, every one.',NULL,27,51),
 (9862,1,'So those are their houses fallen down because they were unjust, most surely there is a sign in this for a people who know.',NULL,27,52),
 (9863,2,'Now such were their houses, - in utter ruin, - because they practised wrong-doing. Verily in this is a Sign for people of knowledge.',NULL,27,52),
 (9864,3,'See, yonder are their dwellings empty and in ruins because they did wrong. Lo! herein is indeed a portent for a people who have knowledge.',NULL,27,52),
 (9865,1,'.And We delivered those who believed and who guarded (against evil).',NULL,27,53),
 (9866,2,'And We saved those who believed and practised righteousness.',NULL,27,53),
 (9867,3,'And we saved those who believed and used to ward off (evil).',NULL,27,53),
 (9868,1,'And (We sent) Lut, when he said to his people: What! do you commit indecency while you see?',NULL,27,54),
 (9869,2,'(We also sent) Lut (as a messenger): behold, He said to his people, "Do ye do what is shameful though ye see (its iniquity)?',NULL,27,54),
 (9870,3,'And Lot! when he said unto his folk: Will ye commit abomination knowingly?',NULL,27,54),
 (9871,1,'What! do you indeed approach men lustfully rather than women? Nay, you are a people who act ignorantly.',NULL,27,55),
 (9872,2,'Would ye really approach men in your lusts rather than women? Nay, ye are a people (grossly) ignorant!',NULL,27,55),
 (9873,3,'Must ye needs lust after men instead of women? Nay, but ye are folk who act senselessly.',NULL,27,55),
 (9874,1,'But the answer of his people was no other except that they ~s said: Turn out Lut''s followers from your town; surely they are a people who would keep pure!',NULL,27,56),
 (9875,2,'But his people gave no other answer but this: they said, "Drive out the followers of Lut from your city: these are indeed men who want to be clean and pure!"',NULL,27,56),
 (9876,3,'But the answer of his folk was naught save that they said: Expel the household of Lot from your township, for they (forsooth) are folk who would keep clean!',NULL,27,56),
 (9877,1,'But We delivered him and his followers except his wife; We ordained her to be of those who remained behind.',NULL,27,57),
 (9878,2,'But We saved him and his family, except his wife; her We destined to be of those who lagged behind.',NULL,27,57),
 (9879,3,'Then We saved him and his household save his wife; We destined her to be of those who stayed behind.',NULL,27,57),
 (9880,1,'And We rained on them a rain, and evil was the rain of those who had been warned.',NULL,27,58),
 (9881,2,'And We rained down on them a shower (of brimstone): and evil was the shower on those who were admonished (but heeded not)!',NULL,27,58),
 (9882,3,'And We rained a rain upon them. Dreadful is the rain of those who have been warned.',NULL,27,58),
 (9883,1,'Say: Praise be to Allah and peace on His servants whom He has chosen: is Allah better, or what they associate (with Him)?',NULL,27,59),
 (9884,2,'Say: Praise be to Allah, and Peace on his servants whom He has chosen (for his Message). (Who) is better?- Allah or the false gods they associate (with Him)?',NULL,27,59),
 (9885,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Praise be to Allah, and peace be on His slaves whom He hath chosen! Is Allah best, or (all) that ye ascribe as partners (unto Him)?',NULL,27,59),
 (9886,1,'Nay, He Who created the heavens and the earth, and sent down for you water from the cloud; then We cause to grow thereby beautiful gardens; it is not possible for you that you should make the trees thereof to grow. Is there a god with Allah? Nay! they are people who deviate.',NULL,27,60),
 (9887,2,'Or, Who has created the heavens and the earth, and Who sends you down rain from the sky? Yea, with it We cause to grow well-planted orchards full of beauty of delight: it is not in your power to cause the growth of the trees in them. (Can there be another) god besides Allah? Nay, they are a people who swerve from justice.',NULL,27,60),
 (9888,3,'Is not He (best) Who created the heavens and the earth, and sendeth down for you water from the sky wherewith We cause to spring forth joyous orchards, whose trees it never hath been yours to cause to grow. Is there any Allah beside Allah? Nay, but they are folk who ascribe equals (unto Him)!',NULL,27,60),
 (9889,1,'Or, Who made the earth a restingplace, and made in it rivers, and raised on it mountains and placed between the two seas a barrier. Is there a god with Allah? Nay! most of them do not know!',NULL,27,61),
 (9890,2,'Or, Who has made the earth firm to live in; made rivers in its midst; set thereon mountains immovable; and made a separating bar between the two bodies of flowing water? (can there be another) god besides Allah? Nay, most of them know not.',NULL,27,61),
 (9891,3,'Is not He (best) Who made the earth a fixed abode, and placed rivers in the folds thereof, and placed firm hills therein, and hath set a barrier between the two seas? Is there any Allah beside Allah? Nay, but most of them know not!',NULL,27,61),
 (9892,1,'Or, Who answers the distressed one when he calls upon Him and removes the evil, and He will make you successors in the earth. Is there a god with Allah? Little is it that you mind!',NULL,27,62),
 (9893,2,'Or, Who listens to the (soul) distressed when it calls on Him, and Who relieves its suffering, and makes you (mankind) inheritors of the earth? (Can there be another) god besides Allah? Little it is that ye heed!',NULL,27,62),
 (9894,3,'Is not He (best) Who answereth the wronged one when he crieth unto Him and removeth the evil, and hath made you viceroys of the earth? Is there any Allah beside Allah? Little do they reflect!',NULL,27,62),
 (9895,1,'Or, Who guides you in utter darkness of the land and the sea, and Who sends the winds as good news before His mercy. Is there a god with Allah? Exalted by Allah above what they associate (with Him).',NULL,27,63),
 (9896,2,'Or, Who guides you through the depths of darkness on land and sea, and Who sends the winds as heralds of glad tidings, going before His Mercy? (Can there be another) god besides Allah?- High is Allah above what they associate with Him!',NULL,27,63),
 (9897,3,'Is not He (best) Who guideth you in the darkness of the land and the sea, He Who sendeth the winds as heralds of His mercy? Is there any Allah beside Allah? High Exalted be Allah from all that they ascribe as partner (unto Him)!',NULL,27,63),
 (9898,1,'Or, Who originates the creation, then reproduces it and Who gives you sustenance from the heaven and the earth. Is there a god With Allah? Say: Bring your proof if you are truthful.',NULL,27,64),
 (9899,2,'Or, Who originates creation, then repeats it, and who gives you sustenance from heaven and earth? (Can there be another) god besides Allah? Say, "Bring forth your argument, if ye are telling the truth!"',NULL,27,64),
 (9900,3,'Is not He (best) Who produceth creation, then reproduceth it, and Who provideth for you from the heaven and the earth? Is there any Allah beside Allah? Say: Bring your proof, if ye are truthful!',NULL,27,64),
 (9901,1,'Say: No one in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen but Allah; and they do not know when they shall be raised.',NULL,27,65),
 (9902,2,'Say: None in the heavens or on earth, except Allah, knows what is hidden: nor can they perceive when they shall be raised up (for Judgment).',NULL,27,65),
 (9903,3,'Say (O Muhammad): None in the heavens and the earth knoweth the Unseen save Allah; and they know not when they will be raised (again).',NULL,27,65),
 (9904,1,'Nay, their knowledge respecting the hereafter is slight and hasty; nay, they are in doubt about it; nay, they are quite blind to it',NULL,27,66),
 (9905,2,'Still less can their knowledge comprehend the Hereafter: Nay, they are in doubt and uncertainty thereanent; nay, they are blind thereunto!',NULL,27,66),
 (9906,3,'Nay, but doth their knowledge reach to the Hereafter? Nay, for they are in doubt concerning it. Nay, for they cannot see it.',NULL,27,66),
 (9907,1,'And those who disbelieve say: What! when we have become dust and our fathers (too), shall we certainly be brought forth?',NULL,27,67),
 (9908,2,'The Unbelievers say: "What! when we become dust,- we and our fathers,- shall we really be raised (from the dead)?',NULL,27,67),
 (9909,3,'Yet those who disbelieve say: When we have become dust like our fathers, shall we verily be brought forth (again)?',NULL,27,67),
 (9910,1,'We have certainly been promised this, we and our fathers before; these are naught but stories of the ancients',NULL,27,68),
 (9911,2,'"It is true we were promised this,- we and our fathers before (us): these are nothing but tales of the ancients."',NULL,27,68),
 (9912,3,'We were promised this, forsooth, we and our fathers. (All) this is naught but fables of the men of old.',NULL,27,68),
 (9913,1,'Say: Travel in the earth, then see how was the end of the guilty.',NULL,27,69),
 (9914,2,'Say: "Go ye through the earth and see what has been the end of those guilty (of sin)."',NULL,27,69),
 (9915,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Travel in the land and see the nature of the sequel for the guilty!',NULL,27,69),
 (9916,1,'And grieve not for them and be not distressed because of what they plan.',NULL,27,70),
 (9917,2,'But grieve not over them, nor distress thyself because of their plots.',NULL,27,70),
 (9918,3,'And grieve thou not for them, nor be in distress because of what they plot (against thee).',NULL,27,70),
 (9919,1,'And they say: When will this threat come to pass, if you are truthful?',NULL,27,71),
 (9920,2,'They also say: "When will this promise (come to pass)? (Say) if ye are truthful."',NULL,27,71),
 (9921,3,'And they say: When (will) this promise (be fulfilled), if ye are truthful?',NULL,27,71),
 (9922,1,'Say: Maybe there may have drawn near to you somewhat of that which you seek to hasten on.',NULL,27,72),
 (9923,2,'Say: "It may be that some of the events which ye wish to hasten on may be (close) in your pursuit!"',NULL,27,72),
 (9924,3,'Say: It may be that a part of that which ye would hasten on is close behind you.',NULL,27,72),
 (9925,1,'And surely your Lord is the Lord of grace to men, but most of them are not grateful.',NULL,27,73),
 (9926,2,'But verily thy Lord is full of grace to mankind: Yet most of them are ungrateful.',NULL,27,73),
 (9927,3,'Lo! thy Lord is full of bounty for mankind, but most of them do not give thanks.',NULL,27,73),
 (9928,1,'And most surely your Lord knows what their breasts conceal and what they manifest.',NULL,27,74),
 (9929,2,'And verily thy Lord knoweth all that their hearts do hide. As well as all that they reveal.',NULL,27,74),
 (9930,3,'Lo! thy Lord knoweth surely all that their bosoms hide, and all that they proclaim.',NULL,27,74),
 (9931,1,'And there is nothing concealed in the heaven and the earth but it is in a clear book.',NULL,27,75),
 (9932,2,'Nor is there aught of the unseen, in heaven or earth, but is (recorded) in a clear record.',NULL,27,75),
 (9933,3,'And there is nothing hidden in the heaven or the earth but it is in a clear Record.',NULL,27,75),
 (9934,1,'Surely this Quran declares to the children of Israel most of what they differ in.',NULL,27,76),
 (9935,2,'Verily this Qur''an doth explain to the Children of Israel most of the matters in which they disagree.',NULL,27,76),
 (9936,3,'Lo! this Qur''an narrateth unto the Children of Israel most of that concerning which they differ.',NULL,27,76),
 (9937,1,'And most surely it is a guidance and a mercy for the believers.',NULL,27,77),
 (9938,2,'And it certainly is a Guide and a Mercy to those who believe.',NULL,27,77),
 (9939,3,'And lo! it is a guidance and a mercy for believers.',NULL,27,77),
 (9940,1,'Surely your Lord will judge between them by his judgment, and He is the Mighty, the knowing.',NULL,27,78),
 (9941,2,'Verily thy Lord will decide between them by His Decree: and He is Exalted in Might, All-Knowing.',NULL,27,78),
 (9942,3,'Lo! thy Lord will judge between them of His wisdom, and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,27,78),
 (9943,1,'Therefore rely on Allah; surely you are on the clear truth.',NULL,27,79),
 (9944,2,'So put thy trust in Allah: for thou art on (the path of) manifest Truth.',NULL,27,79),
 (9945,3,'Therefor (O Muhammad) put thy trust in Allah, for thou (standest) on the plain Truth.',NULL,27,79),
 (9946,1,'Surely you do not make the dead to hear, and you do not make the deaf to hear the call when they go back retreating.',NULL,27,80),
 (9947,2,'Truly thou canst not cause the dead to listen, nor canst thou cause the deaf to hear the call, (especially) when they turn back in retreat.',NULL,27,80),
 (9948,3,'Lo! thou canst not make the dead to hear, nor canst thou make the deaf to hear the call when they have turned to flee;',NULL,27,80),
 (9949,1,'Nor can you be a guide to the blind out of their error; you cannot make to bear (any one) except those who believe in Our communications, so they submit.',NULL,27,81),
 (9950,2,'Nor canst thou be a guide to the blind, (to prevent them) from straying: only those wilt thou get to listen who believe in Our Signs, and they will bow in Islam.',NULL,27,81),
 (9951,3,'Nor canst thou lead the blind out of their error. Thou canst make none to hear, save those who believe Our revelations and who have surrendered.',NULL,27,81),
 (9952,1,'And when the word shall come to pass against them, We shall bring forth for them a creature from the earth that shall i wound them, because people did not believe in Our communications.',NULL,27,82),
 (9953,2,'And when the Word is fulfilled against them (the unjust), we shall produce from the earth a beast to (face) them: He will speak to them, for that mankind did not believe with assurance in Our Signs.',NULL,27,82),
 (9954,3,'And when the word is fulfilled concerning them, We shall bring forth a beast of the earth to speak unto them because mankind had not faith in Our revelations.',NULL,27,82),
 (9955,1,'And on the day when We will gather from every nation a party from among those who rejected Our communications, then they shall be formed into groups.',NULL,27,83),
 (9956,2,'One day We shall gather together from every people a troop of those who reject our Signs, and they shall be kept in ranks,-',NULL,27,83),
 (9957,3,'And (remind them of) the Day when We shall gather out of every nation a host of those who denied Our revelations, and they will be set in array;',NULL,27,83),
 (9958,1,'Until when they come, He will say: Did you reject My communications while you had no comprehensive knowledge of them? Or what was it that you did?',NULL,27,84),
 (9959,2,'Until, when they come (before the Judgment-seat), (Allah) will say: "Did ye reject My Signs, though ye comprehended them not in knowledge, or what was it ye did?"',NULL,27,84),
 (9960,3,'Till, when they come (before their Lord), He will say: Did ye deny My revelations when ye could not compass them in knowledge, or what was it that ye did?',NULL,27,84),
 (9961,1,'And the word shall come to pass against them because they were unjust, so they shall not speak.',NULL,27,85),
 (9962,2,'And the Word will be fulfilled against them, because of their wrong-doing, and they will be unable to speak (in plea).',NULL,27,85),
 (9963,3,'And the Word will be fulfilled concerning them because they have done wrong, and they will not speak.',NULL,27,85),
 (9964,1,'Do they not consider that We have made the night that. they may rest therein, and the day to give light? Most surely there are signs in this for a people who believe.',NULL,27,86),
 (9965,2,'See they not that We have made the Night for them to rest in and the Day to give them light? Verily in this are Signs for any people that believe!',NULL,27,86),
 (9966,3,'Have they not seen how We have appointed the night that they may rest therein, and the day sight-giving? Lo! therein verily are portents for a people who believe.',NULL,27,86),
 (9967,1,'And on the day when the trumpet shall be blown, then those who are in the heavens and those who are in the earth shall be terrified except such as Allah please, and all shall come to him abased.',NULL,27,87),
 (9968,2,'And the Day that the Trumpet will be sounded - then will be smitten with terror those who are in the heavens, and those who are on earth, except such as Allah will please (to exempt): and all shall come to His (Presence) as beings conscious of their lowliness.',NULL,27,87),
 (9969,3,'And (remind them of) the Day when the Trumpet will be blown, and all who are in the heavens and the earth will start in fear, save him whom Allah willeth. And all come unto Him, humbled.',NULL,27,87),
 (9970,1,'And you see the mountains, you think them to be solid, and they shall pass away as the passing away of the cloud-- the handiwork of Allah Who has made every thing thoroughly; surely He is Aware of what you do.',NULL,27,88),
 (9971,2,'Thou seest the mountains and thinkest them firmly fixed: but they shall pass away as the clouds pass away: (such is) the artistry of Allah, who disposes of all things in perfect order: for he is well acquainted with all that ye do.',NULL,27,88),
 (9972,3,'And thou seest the hills thou deemest solid flying with the flight of clouds: the doing of Allah Who perfecteth all things. Lo! He is Informed of what ye do.',NULL,27,88),
 (9973,1,'Whoever brings good, he shall have better than it; and they shall be secure from terror on the day.',NULL,27,89),
 (9974,2,'If any do good, good will (accrue) to them therefrom; and they will be secure from terror that Day.',NULL,27,89),
 (9975,3,'Whoso bringeth a good deed will have better than its worth; and such are safe from fear that Day.',NULL,27,89),
 (9976,1,'And whoever brings evil, these shall be thrown down on their faces into the fire; shall you be rewarded (for) aught except what you did?',NULL,27,90),
 (9977,2,'And if any do evil, their faces will be thrown headlong into the Fire: "Do ye receive a reward other than that which ye have earned by your deeds?"',NULL,27,90),
 (9978,3,'And whoso bringeth an ill-deed, such will be flung down on their faces in the Fire. Are ye rewarded aught save what ye did?',NULL,27,90),
 (9979,1,'I am commanded only that I should serve the Lord of this city, Who has made it sacred, and His are all things; and I am commanded that I should be of these who submit;',NULL,27,91),
 (9980,2,'For me, I have been commanded to serve the Lord of this city, Him Who has sanctified it and to Whom (belong) all things: and I am commanded to be of those who bow in Islam to Allah''s Will,-',NULL,27,91),
 (9981,3,'(Say): I (Muhammad) am commanded only to serve the Lord of this land which He hath hallowed, and unto Whom all things belong. And I am commanded to be of those who surrender (unto Him),',NULL,27,91),
 (9982,1,'And that I should recite the Quran. Therefore whoever goes aright, he goes aright for his own soul, and whoever goes '' astray, then say: I am only one of the warners.',NULL,27,92),
 (9983,2,'And to rehearse the Qur''an: and if any accept guidance, they do it for the good of their own souls, and if any stray, say: "I am only a Warner".',NULL,27,92),
 (9984,3,'And to recite the Qur''an. And whoso goeth right, goeth right only for (the good of) his own soul; and as for him who goeth astray - (Unto him) say: Lo! I am only a warner.',NULL,27,92),
 (9985,1,'And say: Praise be to Allah, He will show you His signs so that you shall recognize them; nor is your Lord heedless of what you do.',NULL,27,93),
 (9986,2,'And say: "Praise be to Allah, Who will soon show you His Signs, so that ye shall know them"; and thy Lord is not unmindful of all that ye do.',NULL,27,93),
 (9987,3,'And say: Praise be to Allah Who will show you His portents so that ye shall know them. And thy Lord is not unaware of what ye (mortals) do.',NULL,27,93),
 (9988,1,'Ta sin Mim.',NULL,28,1),
 (9989,2,'Ta. Sin. Mim.',NULL,28,1),
 (9990,3,'Ta. Sin. Mim.',NULL,28,1),
 (9991,1,'These are the verses of the Book that makes (things) clear.',NULL,28,2),
 (9992,2,'These are Verses of the Book that makes (things) clear.',NULL,28,2),
 (9993,3,'These are revelations of the Scripture that maketh plain.',NULL,28,2),
 (9994,1,'We recite to you from the account of Musa and Firon with truth for people who believe.',NULL,28,3),
 (9995,2,'We rehearse to thee some of the story of Moses and Pharaoh in Truth, for people who believe.',NULL,28,3),
 (9996,3,'We narrate unto thee (somewhat) of the story of Moses and Pharaoh with truth, for folk who believe.',NULL,28,3),
 (9997,1,'Surely Firon exalted himself in the land and made its people into parties, weakening one party from among them; he slaughtered their sons and let their women live; surely he was one of the mischiefmakers.',NULL,28,4),
 (9998,2,'Truly Pharaoh elated himself in the land and broke up its people into sections, depressing a small group among them: their sons he slew, but he kept alive their females: for he was indeed a maker of mischief.',NULL,28,4),
 (9999,3,'Lo! Pharaoh exalted himself in the earth and made its people castes. A tribe among them he oppressed, killing their sons and sparing their women. Lo! he was of those who work corruption.',NULL,28,4),
 (10000,1,'And We desired to bestow a favor upon those who were deemed weak in the land, and to make them the Imams, and to make them the heirs,',NULL,28,5),
 (10001,2,'And We wished to be Gracious to those who were being depressed in the land, to make them leaders (in Faith) and make them heirs,',NULL,28,5),
 (10002,3,'And We desired to show favour unto those who were oppressed in the earth, and to make them examples and to make them the inheritors,',NULL,28,5),
 (10003,1,'And to grant them power in the land, and to make Firon and Haman and their hosts see from them what they feared.',NULL,28,6),
 (10004,2,'To establish a firm place for them in the land, and to show Pharaoh, Haman, and their hosts, at their hands, the very things against which they were taking precautions.',NULL,28,6),
 (10005,3,'And to establish them in the earth, and to show Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts that which they feared from them.',NULL,28,6),
 (10006,1,'And We revealed to Musa''s mothers, saying: Give him suck, then when you fear for him, cast him into the river and do not fear nor grieve; surely We wi!l bring him back to you and make him one of the messengers.',NULL,28,7),
 (10007,2,'So We sent this inspiration to the mother of Moses: "Suckle (thy child), but when thou hast fears about him, cast him into the river, but fear not nor grieve: for We shall restore him to thee, and We shall make him one of Our messengers."',NULL,28,7),
 (10008,3,'And We inspired the mother of Moses, saying: Suckle him and, when thou fearest for him, then cast him into the river and fear not nor grieve. Lo! We shall bring him back unto thee and shall make him (one) of Our messengers.',NULL,28,7),
 (10009,1,'And Firon''s family took him up that he might be an enemy and a grief for them; surely Firon and Haman and their hosts were wrongdoers.',NULL,28,8),
 (10010,2,'Then the people of Pharaoh picked him up (from the river): (It was intended) that (Moses) should be to them an adversary and a cause of sorrow: for Pharaoh and Haman and (all) their hosts were men of sin.',NULL,28,8),
 (10011,3,'And the family of Pharaoh took him up, that he might become for them an enemy and a sorrow, Lo! Pharaoh and Haman and their hosts were ever sinning.',NULL,28,8),
 (10012,1,'And Firon''s wife said: A refreshment of the eye to me and to you; do not slay him; maybe he will be useful to us, or we may take him for a son; and they did not perceive.',NULL,28,9),
 (10013,2,'The wife of Pharaoh said: "(Here is) joy of the eye, for me and for thee: slay him not. It may be that he will be use to us, or we may adopt him as a son." And they perceived not (what they were doing)!',NULL,28,9),
 (10014,3,'And the wife of Pharaoh said: (He will be) a consolation for me and for thee. Kill him not. Peradventure he may be of use to us, or we may choose him for a son. And they perceived not.',NULL,28,9),
 (10015,1,'And the heart of Musa''s mother was free (from anxiety) she would have almost disclosed it had We not strengthened her heart so that she might be of the believers.',NULL,28,10),
 (10016,2,'But there came to be a void in the heart of the mother of Moses: She was going almost to disclose his (case), had We not strengthened her heart (with faith), so that she might remain a (firm) believer.',NULL,28,10),
 (10017,3,'And the heart of the mother of Moses became void, and she would have betrayed him if We had not fortified her heart, that she might be of the believers.',NULL,28,10),
 (10018,1,'And she said to his sister: Follow him up. So she watched him from a distance while they did not perceive,',NULL,28,11),
 (10019,2,'And she said to the sister of (Moses), "Follow him" so she (the sister) watched him in the character of a stranger. And they knew not.',NULL,28,11),
 (10020,3,'And she said unto his sister: Trace him. So she observed him from afar, and they perceived not.',NULL,28,11),
 (10021,1,'And We ordained that he refused to suck any foster mother before, so she said: Shall I point out to you the people of a house who will take care of him for you, and they will be benevolent to him?',NULL,28,12),
 (10022,2,'And we ordained that he refused suck at first, until (His sister came up and) said: "Shall I point out to you the people of a house that will nourish and bring him up for you and be sincerely attached to him?"...',NULL,28,12),
 (10023,3,'And We had before forbidden foster-mothers for him, so she said: Shall I show you a household who will rear him for you and take care of him?',NULL,28,12),
 (10024,1,'So We gave him back to his mother that her eye might be refreshed, and that she might no grieve, and that she might know that the promise of Allah is true, but most of them do not know.',NULL,28,13),
 (10025,2,'Thus did We restore him to his mother, that her eye might be comforted, that she might not grieve, and that she might know that the promise of Allah is true: but most of them do not understand.',NULL,28,13),
 (10026,3,'So We restored him to his mother that she might be comforted and not grieve, and that she might know that the promise of Allah is true. But most of them know not.',NULL,28,13),
 (10027,1,'And when he attained his maturity and became full grown, We granted him wisdom and knowledge; and thus do We reward those who do good (to others).',NULL,28,14),
 (10028,2,'When he reached full age, and was firmly established (in life), We bestowed on him wisdom and knowledge: for thus do We reward those who do good.',NULL,28,14),
 (10029,3,'And when he reached his full strength and was ripe, We gave him wisdom and knowledge. Thus do We reward the good.',NULL,28,14),
 (10030,1,'And he went into the city at a time of unvigilance on the part of its people, so he found therein two men fighting, one being of his party and the other of his foes, and he who was of his party cried out to him for help against him who was of his enemies, so Musa struck him with his fist and killed him. He said: This is on account of the Shaitan''s doing; surely he is an enemy, openly leading astray.',NULL,28,15),
 (10031,2,'And he entered the city at a time when its people were not watching: and he found there two men fighting,- one of his own religion, and the other, of his foes. Now the man of his own religion appealed to him against his foe, and Moses struck him with his fist and made an end of him. He said: "This is a work of Evil (Satan): for he is an enemy that manifestly misleads!"',NULL,28,15),
 (10032,3,'And he entered the city at a time of carelessness of its folk, and he found therein two men fighting, one of his own caste, and the other of his enemies; and he who was of his caste asked him for help against him who was of his enemies. So Moses struck him with his fist and killed him. He said: This is of the devil''s doing. Lo! he is an enemy, a mere misleader.',NULL,28,15),
 (10033,1,'He said: My Lord! surely I have done harm to myself, so do Thou protect me. So He protected him; surely He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,28,16),
 (10034,2,'He prayed: "O my Lord! I have indeed wronged my soul! Do Thou then forgive me!" So (Allah) forgave him: for He is the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,28,16),
 (10035,3,'He said: My Lord! Lo! I have wronged my soul, so forgive me. Then He forgave him. Lo! He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,28,16),
 (10036,1,'He said: My Lord! because Thou hast bestowed a favor on me, I shall never be a backer of the guilty.',NULL,28,17),
 (10037,2,'He said: "O my Lord! For that Thou hast bestowed Thy Grace on me, never shall I be a help to those who sin!"',NULL,28,17),
 (10038,3,'He said: My Lord! Forasmuch as Thou hast favoured me, I will nevermore be a supporter of the guilty.',NULL,28,17),
 (10039,1,'And he was in the city, fearing, awaiting, when lo! he who had asked his assistance the day before was crying out to him for aid. Musa said to him: You are most surely one erring manifestly.',NULL,28,18),
 (10040,2,'So he saw the morning in the city, looking about, in a state of fear, when behold, the man who had, the day before, sought his help called aloud for his help (again). Moses said to him: "Thou art truly, it is clear, a quarrelsome fellow!"',NULL,28,18),
 (10041,3,'And morning found him in the city, fearing, vigilant, when behold! he who had appealed to him the day before cried out to him for help. Moses said unto him: Lo! thou art indeed a mere hothead.',NULL,28,18),
 (10042,1,'So when he desired to seize him who was an enemy to them both, he said: O Musa! do you intend to kill me as you killed a person yesterday? You desire nothing but that you should be a tyrant in the land, and you do not desire to be of those who act aright.',NULL,28,19),
 (10043,2,'Then, when he decided to lay hold of the man who was an enemy to both of them, that man said: "O Moses! Is it thy intention to slay me as thou slewest a man yesterday? Thy intention is none other than to become a powerful violent man in the land, and not to be one who sets things right!"',NULL,28,19),
 (10044,3,'And when he would have fallen upon the man who was an enemy unto them both, he said: O Moses! Wouldst thou kill me as thou didst kill a person yesterday. Thou wouldst be nothing but a tyrant in the land, thou wouldst not be of the reformers.',NULL,28,19),
 (10045,1,'And a man came running from the remotest part of the city. He said: O Musa! surely the chiefs are consulting together to slay you, therefore depart (at once); surely I am of those who wish well to you.',NULL,28,20),
 (10046,2,'And there came a man, running, from the furthest end of the City. He said: "O Moses! the Chiefs are taking counsel together about thee, to slay thee: so get thee away, for I do give thee sincere advice."',NULL,28,20),
 (10047,3,'And a man came from the uttermost part of the city, running. He said: O Moses! Lo! the chiefs take counsel against thee to slay thee; therefor escape. Lo! I am of those who give thee good advice.',NULL,28,20),
 (10048,1,'So he went forth therefrom, fearing, awaiting, (and) he said: My Lord! deliver me from the unjust people.',NULL,28,21),
 (10049,2,'He therefore got away therefrom, looking about, in a state of fear. He prayed "O my Lord! save me from people given to wrong-doing."',NULL,28,21),
 (10050,3,'So he escaped from thence, fearing, vigilant. He said: My Lord! Deliver me from the wrongdoing folk.',NULL,28,21),
 (10051,1,'And when he turned his face towards Madyan, he said: Maybe my Lord will guide me in the right path.',NULL,28,22),
 (10052,2,'Then, when he turned his face towards (the land of) Madyan, he said: "I do hope that my Lord will show me the smooth and straight Path."',NULL,28,22),
 (10053,3,'And when he turned his face toward Midian, he said: Peradventure my Lord will guide me in the right road.',NULL,28,22),
 (10054,1,'And when he came to the water of Madyan, he found on it a group of men watering, and he found besides them two women keeping back (their flocks). He said: What is the matter with you? They said: We cannot water until the shepherds take away (their sheep) from the water, and our father is a very old man.',NULL,28,23),
 (10055,2,'And when he arrived at the watering (place) in Madyan, he found there a group of men watering (their flocks), and besides them he found two women who were keeping back (their flocks). He said: "What is the matter with you?" They said: "We cannot water (our flocks) until the shepherds take back (their flocks): And our father is a very old man."',NULL,28,23),
 (10056,3,'And when he came unto the water of Midian he found there a whole tribe of men, watering. And he found apart from them two women keeping back (their flocks). He said: What aileth you? The two said: We cannot give (our flocks) to drink till the shepherds return from the water; and our father is a very old man.',NULL,28,23),
 (10057,1,'So he watered (their sheep) for them, then went back to the shade and said: My Lord! surely I stand in need of whatever good Thou mayest send down to me.',NULL,28,24),
 (10058,2,'So he watered (their flocks) for them; then he turned back to the shade, and said:"O my Lord! truly am I in (desperate) need of any good that Thou dost send me!"',NULL,28,24),
 (10059,3,'So he watered (their flock) for them. Then he turned aside into the shade, and said: My Lord! I am needy of whatever good Thou sendest down for me.',NULL,28,24),
 (10060,1,'Then one of the two women came to him walking bashfully. She said: My father invites you that he may give you the reward of your having watered for us. So when he came to him and gave to him the account, he said: Fear not, you are secure from the unjust people.',NULL,28,25),
 (10061,2,'Afterwards one of the (damsels) came (back) to him, walking bashfully. She said: "My father invites thee that he may reward thee for having watered (our flocks) for us." So when he came to him and narrated the story, he said: "Fear thou not: (well) hast thou escaped from unjust people."',NULL,28,25),
 (10062,3,'Then there came unto him one of the two women, walking shyly. She said: Lo! my father biddeth thee, that he may reward thee with a payment for that thou didst water (the flock) for us. Then, when he came unto him and told him the (whole) story, he said: Fear not! Thou hast escaped from the wrongdoing folk.',NULL,28,25),
 (10063,1,'Said one of them: O my father! employ him, surely the best of those that you can employ is the strong man, the faithful one.',NULL,28,26),
 (10064,2,'Said one of the (damsels): "O my (dear) father! engage him on wages: truly the best of men for thee to employ is the (man) who is strong and trusty"....',NULL,28,26),
 (10065,3,'One of the two women said: O my father! Hire him! For the best (man) that thou canst hire in the strong, the trustworthy.',NULL,28,26),
 (10066,1,'He said: I desire to marry one of these two daughters of mine to you on condition that you should serve me for eight years; but if you complete ten, it will be of your own free will, and I do not wish to be hard to you; if Allah please, you will find me one of the good.',NULL,28,27),
 (10067,2,'He said: "I intend to wed one of these my daughters to thee, on condition that thou serve me for eight years; but if thou complete ten years, it will be (grace) from thee. But I intend not to place thee under a difficulty: thou wilt find me, indeed, if Allah wills, one of the righteous."',NULL,28,27),
 (10068,3,'He said: Lo! I fain would marry thee to one of these two daughters of mine on condition that thou hirest thyself to me for (the term of) eight pilgrimages. Then if thou completest ten it will be of thine own accord, for I would not make it hard for thee. Allah willing, thou wilt find me of the righteous.',NULL,28,27),
 (10069,1,'He said: This shall be (an agreement) between me and you; whichever of the two terms I fulfill, there shall be no wrongdoing to me; and Allah is a witness of what we say.',NULL,28,28),
 (10070,2,'He said: "Be that (the agreement) between me and thee: whichever of the two terms I fulfil, let there be no ill-will to me. Be Allah a witness to what we say."',NULL,28,28),
 (10071,3,'He said: That (is settled) between thee and me. Whichever of the two terms I fulfil, there will be no injustice to me, and Allah is Surety over what we say.',NULL,28,28),
 (10072,1,'So when Musa had fulfilled the term, and he journeyed with his family, he perceived on this side of the mountain a fire. He said to his family: Wait, I have seen a fire, maybe I will bring to you from it some news or a brand of fire, so that you may warm yourselves.',NULL,28,29),
 (10073,2,'Now when Moses had fulfilled the term, and was travelling with his family, he perceived a fire in the direction of Mount Tur. He said to his family: "Tarry ye; I perceive a fire; I hope to bring you from there some information, or a burning firebrand, that ye may warm yourselves."',NULL,28,29),
 (10074,3,'Then, when Moses had fulfilled the term, and was travelling with his housefolk, he saw in the distance a fire and said unto his housefolk: Bide ye (here). Lo! I see in the distance a fire; peradventure I shall bring you tidings thence, or a brand from the fire that ye may warm yourselves.',NULL,28,29),
 (10075,1,'And when he came to it, a voice was uttered from the right side of the valley in the blessed spot of the bush, saying: O Musa! surely I am Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,28,30),
 (10076,2,'But when he came to the (fire), a voice was heard from the right bank of the valley, from a tree in hallowed ground: "O Moses! Verily I am Allah, the Lord of the Worlds....',NULL,28,30),
 (10077,3,'And when he reached it, he was called from the right side of the valley in the blessed field, from the tree: O Moses! Lo! I, even I, am Allah, the Lord of the Worlds;',NULL,28,30),
 (10078,1,'And saying: Cast down you staff. So when he saw it in motion as if it were a serpent, he turned back retreating, and did not return. O Musa! come forward and fear not; surely you are of those who are secure;',NULL,28,31),
 (10079,2,'"Now do thou throw thy rod!" but when he saw it moving (of its own accord) as if it had been a snake, he turned back in retreat, and retraced not his steps: O Moses!" (It was said), "Draw near, and fear not: for thou art of those who are secure.',NULL,28,31),
 (10080,3,'Throw down thy staff. And when he saw it writhing as it had been a demon, he turned to flee headlong, (and it was said unto him): O Moses! Draw nigh and fear not. Lo! thou art of those who are secure.',NULL,28,31),
 (10081,1,'Enter your hand into the opening of your bosom, it will come forth white without evil, and draw your hand to yourself to ward off fear: so these two shall be two arguments from your Lord to Firon and his chiefs, surely they are a transgressing people.',NULL,28,32),
 (10082,2,'"Move thy hand into thy bosom, and it will come forth white without stain (or harm), and draw thy hand close to thy side (to guard) against fear. Those are the two credentials from thy Lord to Pharaoh and his Chiefs: for truly they are a people rebellious and wicked."',NULL,28,32),
 (10083,3,'Thrust thy hand into the bosom of thy robe it will come forth white without hurt. And guard thy heart from fear. Then these shall be two proofs from your Lord unto Pharaoh and his chiefs. Lo! they are evil-living folk.',NULL,28,32),
 (10084,1,'He said: My Lord! surely I killed one of them, so I fear lest they should slay me;',NULL,28,33),
 (10085,2,'He said: "O my Lord! I have slain a man among them, and I fear lest they slay me.',NULL,28,33),
 (10086,3,'He said: My Lord! Lo! I killed a man among them and I fear that they will kill me.',NULL,28,33),
 (10087,1,'And my brother, Haroun, he is more eloquent of tongue than I, therefore send him with me as an aider, verifying me: surely I fear that they would reject me.',NULL,28,34),
 (10088,2,'"And my brother Aaron - He is more eloquent in speech than I: so send him with me as a helper, to confirm (and strengthen) me: for I fear that they may accuse me of falsehood."',NULL,28,34),
 (10089,3,'My brother Aaron is more eloquent than me in speech. Therefor send him with me as a helper to confirm me. Lo! I fear that they will give the lie to me.',NULL,28,34),
 (10090,1,'He said: We will strengthen your arm with your brother, and We will give you both an authority, so that they shall not reach you; (go) with Our signs; you two and those who follow you shall be uppermost.',NULL,28,35),
 (10091,2,'He said: "We will certainly strengthen thy arm through thy brother, and invest you both with authority, so they shall not be able to touch you: with Our Sign shall ye triumph,- you two as well as those who follow you."',NULL,28,35),
 (10092,3,'He said: We will strengthen thine arm with thy brother, and We will give unto you both power so that they cannot reach you for Our portents. Ye twain, and those who follow you, will be the winners.',NULL,28,35),
 (10093,1,'So when Musa came to them with Our clear signs, they said: This is nothing but forged enchantment, and we never heard of it amongst our fathers of old.',NULL,28,36),
 (10094,2,'When Moses came to them with Our clear signs, they said: "This is nothing but sorcery faked up: never did we head the like among our fathers of old!"',NULL,28,36),
 (10095,3,'But when Moses came unto them with Our clear tokens, they said: This is naught but invented magic. We never heard of this among our fathers of old.',NULL,28,36),
 (10096,1,'And Musa said: My Lord knows best who comes with guidance from Him, and whose shall be the good end of the abode; surely the unjust shall not be successful.',NULL,28,37),
 (10097,2,'Moses said: "My Lord knows best who it is that comes with guidance from Him and whose end will be best in the Hereafter: certain it is that the wrong-doers will not prosper."',NULL,28,37),
 (10098,3,'And Moses said: My Lord is Best Aware of him who bringeth guidance from His presence, and whose will be the sequel of the Home (of bliss). Lo! wrong-doers will not be successful.',NULL,28,37),
 (10099,1,'And Firon said: O chiefs! I do not know of any god for you besides myself; therefore kindle a fire for me, O Haman, for brick, then prepare for me a lofty building so that I may obtain knowledge of Musa''s god, and most surely I think him to be one of the liars.',NULL,28,38),
 (10100,2,'Pharaoh said: "O Chiefs! no god do I know for you but myself: therefore, O Haman! light me a (kiln to bake bricks) out of clay, and build me a lofty palace, that I may mount up to the god of Moses: but as far as I am concerned, I think (Moses) is a liar!"',NULL,28,38),
 (10101,3,'And Pharaoh said: O chiefs! I know not that ye have a god other than me, so kindle for me (a fire), O Haman, to bake the mud; and set up for me a lofty tower in order that I may survey the god of Moses; and lo! I deem him of the liars.',NULL,28,38),
 (10102,1,'And he was unjustly proud in the land, he and his hosts, and they deemed that they would not be brought back to Us.',NULL,28,39),
 (10103,2,'And he was arrogant and insolent in the land, beyond reason,- He and his hosts: they thought that they would not have to return to Us!',NULL,28,39),
 (10104,3,'And he and his hosts were haughty in the land without right, and deemed that they would never be brought back to Us.',NULL,28,39),
 (10105,1,'So We caught hold of him and his hosts, then We cast them into the sea, and see how was the end of the unjust.',NULL,28,40),
 (10106,2,'So We seized him and his hosts, and We flung them into the sea: Now behold what was the end of those who did wrong!',NULL,28,40),
 (10107,3,'Therefor We seized him and his hosts, and abandoned them unto the sea. Behold the nature of the consequence for evil-doers!',NULL,28,40),
 (10108,1,'And We made them Imams who call to the fire, and on the day of resurrection they shall not be assisted.',NULL,28,41),
 (10109,2,'And we made them (but) leaders inviting to the Fire; and on the Day of Judgment no help shall they find.',NULL,28,41),
 (10110,3,'And We made them patterns that invite unto the Fire, and on the Day of Resurrection they will not be helped.',NULL,28,41),
 (10111,1,'And We caused a curse to follow them in this world, and on the day of resurrection they shall be of those made to appear hideous.',NULL,28,42),
 (10112,2,'in this world We made a curse to follow them and on the Day of Judgment they will be among the loathed (and despised).',NULL,28,42),
 (10113,3,'And We made a curse to follow them in this world, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be among the hateful.',NULL,28,42),
 (10114,1,'And certainly We gave Musa the Book after We had destroyed the former generations, clear arguments for men and a guidance and a mercy, that they may be mindful.',NULL,28,43),
 (10115,2,'We did reveal to Moses the Book after We had destroyed the earlier generations, (to give) Insight to men, and guidance and Mercy, that they might receive admonition.',NULL,28,43),
 (10116,3,'And We verily gave the Scripture unto Moses after We had destroyed the generations of old: clear testimonies for mankind, and a guidance and a mercy, that haply they might reflect.',NULL,28,43),
 (10117,1,'And you were not on the western side when We revealed to Musa the commandment, and you were not among the witnesses;',NULL,28,44),
 (10118,2,'Thou wast not on the Western side when We decreed the Commission to Moses, nor wast thou a witness (of those events).',NULL,28,44),
 (10119,3,'And thou (Muhammad) wast not on the western side (of the Mount) when We expounded unto Moses the commandment, and thou wast not among those present;',NULL,28,44),
 (10120,1,'But We raised up generations, then life became prolonged to them; and you were not dwelling among the people of Madyan, reciting to them Our communications, but We were the senders.',NULL,28,45),
 (10121,2,'But We raised up (new) generations, and long were the ages that passed over them; but thou wast not a dweller among the people of Madyan, rehearsing Our Signs to them; but it is We Who send messengers (with inspiration).',NULL,28,45),
 (10122,3,'But We brought forth generations, and their lives dragged on for them. And thou wast not a dweller in Midian, reciting unto them Our revelations, but We kept sending (messengers to men).',NULL,28,45),
 (10123,1,'And you were not on this side of the mountain when We called, but a mercy from your Lord that you may warn a people to whom no warner came before you, that they may be mindful.',NULL,28,46),
 (10124,2,'Nor wast thou at the side of (the Mountain of) Tur when we called (to Moses). Yet (art thou sent) as Mercy from thy Lord, to give warning to a people to whom no warner had come before thee: in order that they may receive admonition.',NULL,28,46),
 (10125,3,'And thou was not beside the Mount when We did call; but (the knowledge of it is) a mercy from thy Lord that thou mayst warn a folk unto whom no warner came before thee, that haply they may give heed.',NULL,28,46),
 (10126,1,'And were it not that there should befall them a disaster for what their hands have sent before, then they should say: Our Lord! why didst Thou not send to us a messenger so that we should have followed Thy communications and been of the believers !',NULL,28,47),
 (10127,2,'If (We had) not (sent thee to the Quraish),- in case a calamity should seize them for (the deeds) that their hands have sent forth, they might say: "Our Lord! why didst Thou not sent us a messenger? We should then have followed Thy Signs and been amongst those who believe!"',NULL,28,47),
 (10128,3,'Otherwise, if disaster should afflict them because of that which their own hands have sent before (them), they might say: Our Lord! Why sentest Thou no messenger unto us, that we might have followed Thy revelations and been of the believers?',NULL,28,47),
 (10129,1,'But (now) when the truth has come to them from Us, they say: Why is he not given the like of what was given to Musa? What! did they not disbelieve in what Musa was given before? They say: Two magicians backing up each other; and they say: Surely we are unbelievers in all.',NULL,28,48),
 (10130,2,'But (now), when the Truth has come to them from Ourselves, they say, "Why are not (Signs) sent to him, like those which were sent to Moses?" Do they not then reject (the Signs) which were formerly sent to Moses? They say: "Two kinds of sorcery, each assisting the other!" And they say: "For us, we reject all (such things)!"',NULL,28,48),
 (10131,3,'But when there came unto them the Truth from Our presence, they said: Why is he not given the like of what was given unto Moses? Did they not disbelieve in that which was given unto Moses of old? They say: Two magics that support each other; and they say: Lo! in both we are disbelievers.',NULL,28,48),
 (10132,1,'Say: Then bring some (other) book from Allah which is a better guide than both of them, (that) I may follow it, if you are truthful.',NULL,28,49),
 (10133,2,'Say: "Then bring ye a Book from Allah, which is a better guide than either of them, that I may follow it! (do), if ye are truthful!"',NULL,28,49),
 (10134,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Then bring a scripture from the presence of Allah that giveth clearer guidance than these two (that) I may follow it, if ye are truthful.',NULL,28,49),
 (10135,1,'But if they do not answer you, then know that they only follow their low desires; and who is more erring than he who follows his low desires without any guidance from Allah? Surely Allah does not guide the unjust people.',NULL,28,50),
 (10136,2,'But if they hearken not to thee, know that they only follow their own lusts: and who is more astray than one who follow his own lusts, devoid of guidance from Allah? for Allah guides not people given to wrong-doing.',NULL,28,50),
 (10137,3,'And if they answer thee not, then know that what they follow is their lusts. And who goeth farther astray than he who followeth his lust without guidance from Allah. Lo! Allah guideth not wrongdoing folk.',NULL,28,50),
 (10138,1,'And certainly We have made the word to reach them so that they may be mindful.',NULL,28,51),
 (10139,2,'Now have We caused the Word to reach them themselves, in order that they may receive admonition.',NULL,28,51),
 (10140,3,'And now verily We have caused the Word to reach them, that haply they may give heed.',NULL,28,51),
 (10141,1,'(As to) those whom We gave the Book before it, they are believers in it.',NULL,28,52),
 (10142,2,'Those to whom We sent the Book before this,- they do believe in this (revelation):',NULL,28,52),
 (10143,3,'Those unto whom We gave the Scripture before it, they believe in it,',NULL,28,52),
 (10144,1,'And when it is recited to them they say: We believe in it surely it is the truth from our Lord; surely we were submitters before this.',NULL,28,53),
 (10145,2,'And when it is recited to them, they say: "We believe therein, for it is the Truth from our Lord: indeed we have been Muslims (bowing to Allah''s Will) from before this.',NULL,28,53),
 (10146,3,'And when it is recited unto them, they say: We believe in it. Lo! it is the Truth from our Lord. Lo! even before it we were of those who surrender (unto Him).',NULL,28,53),
 (10147,1,'These shall be granted their reward twice, because they are steadfast and they repel evil with good and spend out of what We have given them.',NULL,28,54),
 (10148,2,'Twice will they be given their reward, for that they have persevered, that they avert Evil with Good, and that they spend (in charity) out of what We have given them.',NULL,28,54),
 (10149,3,'These will be given their reward twice over, because they are steadfast and repel evil with good, and spend of that wherewith We have provided them,',NULL,28,54),
 (10150,1,'And when they hear idle talk they turn aside from it and say: We shall have our deeds and you shall have your deeds; peace be on you, we do not desire the ignorant.',NULL,28,55),
 (10151,2,'And when they hear vain talk, they turn away therefrom and say: "To us our deeds, and to you yours; peace be to you: we seek not the ignorant."',NULL,28,55),
 (10152,3,'And when they hear vanity they withdraw from it and say: Unto us our works and unto you your works. Peace be unto you! We desire not the ignorant.',NULL,28,55),
 (10153,1,'Surely you cannot guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He pleases, and He knows best the followers of the right way.',NULL,28,56),
 (10154,2,'It is true thou wilt not be able to guide every one, whom thou lovest; but Allah guides those whom He will and He knows best those who receive guidance.',NULL,28,56),
 (10155,3,'Lo! thou (O Muhammad) guidest not whom thou lovest, but Allah guideth whom He will. And He is Best Aware of those who walk aright.',NULL,28,56),
 (10156,1,'And they say: If we follow the guidance with you, we shall be carried off from our country. What ! have We not settled them in a safe, sacred territory to which fruits of every kind shall be drawn?-- a sustenance from Us; but most of them do not know.',NULL,28,57),
 (10157,2,'They say: "If we were to follow the guidance with thee, we should be snatched away from our land." Have We not established for them a secure sanctuary, to which are brought as tribute fruits of all kinds,- a provision from Ourselves? but most of them understand not.',NULL,28,57),
 (10158,3,'And they say: If we were to follow the Guidance with thee we should be torn out of our land. Have We not established for them a sure sanctuary, whereunto the produce of all things is brought (in trade), a provision from Our presence? But most of them know not.',NULL,28,57),
 (10159,1,'And how many a town have We destroyed which exulted in its means of subsistence, so these are their abodes, they have not been dwelt in after them except a little, and We are the inheritors,',NULL,28,58),
 (10160,2,'And how many populations We destroyed, which exulted in their life (of ease and plenty)! now those habitations of theirs, after them, are deserted,- All but a (miserable) few! and We are their heirs!',NULL,28,58),
 (10161,3,'And how many a community have We destroyed that was thankless for its means of livelihood! And yonder are their dwellings, which have not been inhabited after them save a little. And We, even We, were the inheritors.',NULL,28,58),
 (10162,1,'And your Lord never destroyed the towns until He raised in their metropolis a messenger, reciting to them Our communications, and We never destroyed the towns except when their people were unjust.',NULL,28,59),
 (10163,2,'Nor was thy Lord the one to destroy a population until He had sent to its centre a messenger, rehearsing to them Our Signs; nor are We going to destroy a population except when its members practise iniquity.',NULL,28,59),
 (10164,3,'And never did thy Lord destroy the townships, till He had raised up in their mother(-town) a messenger reciting unto them Our revelations. And never did We destroy the townships unless the folk thereof were evil-doers.',NULL,28,59),
 (10165,1,'And whatever things you have been given are only a provision of this world''s life and its adornment, and whatever is with Allah is better and more lasting; do you not then understand?',NULL,28,60),
 (10166,2,'The (material) things which ye are given are but the conveniences of this life and the glitter thereof; but that which is with Allah is better and more enduring: will ye not then be wise?',NULL,28,60),
 (10167,3,'And whatsoever ye have been given is a comfort of the life of the world and an ornament thereof; and that which Allah hath is better and more lasting. Have ye then no sense?',NULL,28,60),
 (10168,1,'Is he to whom We have promised a goodly promise which he shall meet with like him whom We have provided with the provisions of this world''s life, then on the day of resurrection he shall be of those who are brought up?',NULL,28,61),
 (10169,2,'Are (these two) alike?- one to whom We have made a goodly promise, and who is going to reach its (fulfilment), and one to whom We have given the good things of this life, but who, on the Day of Judgment, is to be among those brought up (for punishment)?',NULL,28,61),
 (10170,3,'Is he whom We have promised a fair promise which he will find (true) like him whom We suffer to enjoy awhile the comfort of the life of the world, then on the Day of Resurrection he will be of those arraigned?',NULL,28,61),
 (10171,1,'And on the day when He will call them and say: Where are those whom you deemed to be My associates?',NULL,28,62),
 (10172,2,'That Day (Allah) will call to them, and say "Where are my ''partners''?- whom ye imagined (to be such)?"',NULL,28,62),
 (10173,3,'On the day when He will call unto them and say: Where are My partners whom ye imagined?',NULL,28,62),
 (10174,1,'Those against whom the sentence has become confirmed will say: Our Lord! these are they whom we caused to err; we caused them to err as we ourselves did err; to Thee we declare ourselves to be clear (of them); they never served Us.',NULL,28,63),
 (10175,2,'Those against whom the charge will be proved, will say: "Our Lord! These are the ones whom we led astray: we led them astray, as we were astray ourselves: we free ourselves (from them) in Thy presence: it was not us they worshipped."',NULL,28,63),
 (10176,3,'Those concerning whom the Word will have come true will say: Our Lord! These are they whom we led astray. We led them astray even as we ourselves were astray. We declare our innocence before Thee: us they never worshipped.',NULL,28,63),
 (10177,1,'And it will be said: Call your associate-gods. So they will call upon them, but they will not answer them, and they shall see the punishment; would that they had followed the right way!',NULL,28,64),
 (10178,2,'It will be said (to them): "Call upon your ''partners'' (for help)" :they will call upon them, but they will not listen to them; and they will see the Penalty (before them); (how they will wish) ''if only they had been open to guidance!''',NULL,28,64),
 (10179,3,'And it will be said: Cry unto your (so-called) partners (of Allah). And they will cry unto them, and they will give no answer unto them, and they will see the Doom. Ah, if they had but been guided!',NULL,28,64),
 (10180,1,'And on the day when He shall call them and say: What was the answer you gave to the messengers?',NULL,28,65),
 (10181,2,'That Day (Allah) will call to them, and say: "What was the answer ye gave to the messengers?"',NULL,28,65),
 (10182,3,'And on the Day when He will call unto them and say: What answer gave ye to the messengers?',NULL,28,65),
 (10183,1,'Then the pleas shall become obscure to them on that day, so they shall not ask each other.',NULL,28,66),
 (10184,2,'Then the (whole) story that Day will seem obscure to them (like light to the blind) and they will not be able (even) to question each other.',NULL,28,66),
 (10185,3,'On that day (all) tidings will be dimmed for them, nor will they ask one of another,',NULL,28,66),
 (10186,1,'But as to him who repents and believes and does good, maybe he will be among the successful:',NULL,28,67),
 (10187,2,'But any that (in this life) had repented, believed, and worked righteousness, will have hopes to be among those who achieve salvation.',NULL,28,67),
 (10188,3,'But as for him who shall repent and believe and do right, he haply may be one of the successful.',NULL,28,67),
 (10189,1,'And your Lord creates and chooses whom He pleases; to choose is not theirs; glory be to Allah, and exalted be He above what they associate (with Him).',NULL,28,68),
 (10190,2,'Thy Lord does create and choose as He pleases: no choice have they (in the matter): Glory to Allah! and far is He above the partners they ascribe (to Him)!',NULL,28,68),
 (10191,3,'Thy Lord bringeth to pass what He willeth and chooseth. They have never any choice. Glorified be Allah and Exalted above all that they associate (with Him)!',NULL,28,68),
 (10192,1,'And your Lord knows what their breasts conceal and what they manifest.',NULL,28,69),
 (10193,2,'And thy Lord knows all that their hearts conceal and all that they reveal.',NULL,28,69),
 (10194,3,'And thy Lord knoweth what their breasts conceal, and what they publish.',NULL,28,69),
 (10195,1,'And He is Allah, there is no god but He! All praise is due to Him in this (life) and the hereafter, and His is the judgment, and to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,28,70),
 (10196,2,'And He is Allah: There is no god but He. To Him be praise, at the first and at the last: for Him is the Command, and to Him shall ye (all) be brought back.',NULL,28,70),
 (10197,3,'And He is Allah; there is no Allah save Him. His is all praise in the former and the latter (state), and His is the command, and unto Him ye will be brought back.',NULL,28,70),
 (10198,1,'Say: Tell me, if Allah were to make the night to continue incessantly on you till the day of resurrection, who is the god besides Allah that could bring you light? Do you not then hear?',NULL,28,71),
 (10199,2,'Say: See ye? If Allah were to make the night perpetual over you to the Day of Judgment, what god is there other than Allah, who can give you enlightenment? Will ye not then hearken?',NULL,28,71),
 (10200,3,'Say: Have ye thought, if Allah made night everlasting for you till the Day of Resurrection, who is a god beside Allah who could bring you light? Will ye not then hear?',NULL,28,71),
 (10201,1,'Say: Tell me, if Allah were to make the day to continue incessantly on you till the day of resurrection, who is the god besides Allah that could bring you the night in which you take rest? Do you not then see?',NULL,28,72),
 (10202,2,'Say: See ye? If Allah were to make the day perpetual over you to the Day of Judgment, what god is there other than Allah, who can give you a night in which ye can rest? Will ye not then see?',NULL,28,72),
 (10203,3,'Say: Have ye thought, if Allah made day everlasting for you till the Day of Resurrection, who is a god beside Allah who could bring you night wherein ye rest? Will ye not then see?',NULL,28,72),
 (10204,1,'And out of His mercy He has made for you the night and the day, that you may rest therein, and that you may seek of His grace, and that you may give thanks.',NULL,28,73),
 (10205,2,'It is out of His Mercy that He has made for you Night and Day,- that ye may rest therein, and that ye may seek of his Grace;- and in order that ye may be grateful.',NULL,28,73),
 (10206,3,'Of His mercy hath He appointed for you night and day, that therein ye may rest, and that ye may seek His bounty, and that haply ye may be thankful.',NULL,28,73),
 (10207,1,'And on the day when He shall call them and say: Where are those whom you deemed to be My associates?',NULL,28,74),
 (10208,2,'The Day that He will call on them, He will say: "Where are my ''partners''? whom ye imagined (to be such)?"',NULL,28,74),
 (10209,3,'And on the Day when He shall call unto them and say: Where are My partners whom ye pretended?',NULL,28,74),
 (10210,1,'And We will draw forth from among every nation a witness and say: Bring your proof; then shall they know that the truth is Allah''s, and that which they forged shall depart from them.',NULL,28,75),
 (10211,2,'And from each people shall We draw a witness, and We shall say: "Produce your Proof": then shall they know that the Truth is in Allah (alone), and the (lies) which they invented will leave them in lurch.',NULL,28,75),
 (10212,3,'And We shall take out from every nation a witness and We shall say: Bring your proof. Then they will know that Allah hath the Truth, and all that they invented will have failed them.',NULL,28,75),
 (10213,1,'Surely Qaroun was of the people of Musa, but he rebelled against them, and We had given him of the treasures, so much so that his hoards of wealth would certainly weigh down a company of men possessed of great strength. When his people said to him: Do not exult, surely Allah does not love the exultant;',NULL,28,76),
 (10214,2,'Qarun was doubtless, of the people of Moses; but he acted insolently towards them: such were the treasures We had bestowed on him that their very keys would have been a burden to a body of strong men, behold, his people said to him: "Exult not, for Allah loveth not those who exult (in riches).',NULL,28,76),
 (10215,3,'Now Korah was of Moses'' folk, but he oppressed them; and We gave him so much treasure that the stores thereof would verily have been a burden for a troop of mighty men. When his own folk said unto him: Exult not; lo! Allah loveth not the exultant;',NULL,28,76),
 (10216,1,'And seek by means of what Allah has given you the future abode, and do not neglect your portion of this world, and do good (to others) as Allah has done good to you, and do not seek to make mischief in the land, surely Allah does not love the mischief-makers.',NULL,28,77),
 (10217,2,'"But seek, with the (wealth) which Allah has bestowed on thee, the Home of the Hereafter, nor forget thy portion in this world: but do thou good, as Allah has been good to thee, and seek not (occasions for) mischief in the land: for Allah loves not those who do mischief."',NULL,28,77),
 (10218,3,'But seek the abode of the Hereafter in that which Allah hath given thee and neglect not thy portion of the world, and be thou kind even as Allah hath been kind to thee, and seek not corruption in the earth; lo! Allah loveth not corrupters,',NULL,28,77),
 (10219,1,'He said: I have been given this only on account of the knowledge I have. Did he not know that Allah had destroyed before him of the generations those who were mightier in strength than he and greater in assemblage? And the guilty shall not be asked about their faults.',NULL,28,78),
 (10220,2,'He said: "This has been given to me because of a certain knowledge which I have." Did he not know that Allah had destroyed, before him, (whole) generations,- which were superior to him in strength and greater in the amount (of riches) they had collected? but the wicked are not called (immediately) to account for their sins.',NULL,28,78),
 (10221,3,'He said: I have been given it only on account of knowledge I possess. Knew he not that Allah had destroyed already of the generations before him men who were mightier than him in strength and greater in respect of following? The guilty are not questioned of their sins.',NULL,28,78),
 (10222,1,'So he went forth to his people in his finery. Those who desire this world''s life said: O would that we had the like of what Qaroun is given; most surely he is possessed of mighty good fortune.',NULL,28,79),
 (10223,2,'So he went forth among his people in the (pride of his wordly) glitter. Said those whose aim is the Life of this World: "Oh! that we had the like of what Qarun has got! for he is truly a lord of mighty good fortune!"',NULL,28,79),
 (10224,3,'Then went he forth before his people in his pomp. Those who were desirous of the life of the world said: Ah, would that we had the like of what hath been given unto Korah! Lo! he is lord of rare good fortune.',NULL,28,79),
 (10225,1,'And those who were given the knowledge said: Woe to you! Allah''s reward is better for him who believes and does good, and none is made to receive this except the patient.',NULL,28,80),
 (10226,2,'But those who had been granted (true) knowledge said: "Alas for you! The reward of Allah (in the Hereafter) is best for those who believe and work righteousness: but this none shall attain, save those who steadfastly persevere (in good)."',NULL,28,80),
 (10227,3,'But those who had been given knowledge said: Woe unto you! The reward of Allah for him who believeth and doeth right is better, and only the steadfast will obtain it.',NULL,28,80),
 (10228,1,'Thus We made the earth to swallow up him and his abode; so he had no body of helpers to assist him against Allah nor was he of those who can defend themselves.',NULL,28,81),
 (10229,2,'Then We caused the earth to swallow up him and his house; and he had not (the least little) party to help him against Allah, nor could he defend himself.',NULL,28,81),
 (10230,3,'So We caused the earth to swallow him and his dwelling-place. Then he had no host to help him against Allah, nor was he of those who can save themselves.',NULL,28,81),
 (10231,1,'And those who yearned for his place only the day before began to say: Ah! (know) that Allah amplifies and straitens the means of subsistence for whom He pleases of His servants; had not Allah been gracious to us, He would most surely have abased us; ah! (know) that the ungrateful are never successful.',NULL,28,82),
 (10232,2,'And those who had envied his position the day before began to say on the morrow: "Ah! it is indeed Allah Who enlarges the provision or restricts it, to any of His servants He pleases! had it not been that Allah was gracious to us, He could have caused the earth to swallow us up! Ah! those who reject Allah will assuredly never prosper."',NULL,28,82),
 (10233,3,'And morning found those who had coveted his place but yesterday crying: Ah, welladay! Allah enlargeth the provision for whom He will of His slaves and straiteneth it (for whom He will). If Allah had not been gracious unto us He would have caused it to swallow us (also). Ah, welladay! the disbelievers never prosper.',NULL,28,82),
 (10234,1,'(As for) that future abode, We assign it to those who have no desire to exalt themselves in the earth nor to make mischief and the good end is for those who guard (against evil)',NULL,28,83),
 (10235,2,'That Home of the Hereafter We shall give to those who intend not high-handedness or mischief on earth: and the end is (best) for the righteous.',NULL,28,83),
 (10236,3,'As for that Abode of the Hereafter We assign it unto those who seek not oppression in the earth, nor yet corruption. The sequel is for those who ward off (evil).',NULL,28,83),
 (10237,1,'Whoever brings good, he shall have better than it, and whoever brings evil, those who do evil shall not be rewarded (for) aught except what they did.',NULL,28,84),
 (10238,2,'If any does good, the reward to him is better than his deed; but if any does evil, the doers of evil are only punished (to the extent) of their deeds.',NULL,28,84),
 (10239,3,'Whoso bringeth a good deed, he will have better than the same; while as for him who bringeth an ill-deed, those who do ill-deeds will be requited only what they did.',NULL,28,84),
 (10240,1,'Most surely He Who has made the Quran binding on you will bring you back to the destination. Say: My Lord knows best him who has brought the guidance and him who is in manifest error.',NULL,28,85),
 (10241,2,'Verily He Who ordained the Qur''an for thee, will bring thee back to the Place of Return. Say: "My Lord knows best who it is that brings true guidance, and who is in manifest error."',NULL,28,85),
 (10242,3,'Lo! He Who hath given thee the Qur''an for a law will surely bring thee home again. Say: My Lord is Best Aware of him who bringeth guidance and him who is in error manifest.',NULL,28,85),
 (10243,1,'And you did not expect that the Book would be inspired to you, but it is a mercy from your Lord, therefore be not a backer-up of the unbelievers.',NULL,28,86),
 (10244,2,'And thou hadst not expected that the Book would be sent to thee except as a Mercy from thy Lord: Therefore lend not thou support in any way to those who reject (Allah''s Message).',NULL,28,86),
 (10245,3,'Thou hadst no hope that the Scripture would be inspired in thee; but it is a mercy from thy Lord, so never be a helper to the disbelievers.',NULL,28,86),
 (10246,1,'And let them not turn you aside from the communications of Allah after they have been revealed to you, and call (men) to your Lord and be not of the polytheists.',NULL,28,87),
 (10247,2,'And let nothing keep thee back from the Signs of Allah after they have been revealed to thee: and invite (men) to thy Lord, and be not of the company of those who join gods with Allah.',NULL,28,87),
 (10248,3,'And let them not divert thee from the revelations of Allah after they have been sent down unto thee; but call (mankind) unto thy Lord, and be not of those who ascribe partners (unto Him).',NULL,28,87),
 (10249,1,'And call not with Allah any other god; there is no god but He, every thing is perishable but He; His is the judgment, and to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,28,88),
 (10250,2,'And call not, besides Allah, on another god. There is no god but He. Everything (that exists) will perish except His own Face. To Him belongs the Command, and to Him will ye (all) be brought back.',NULL,28,88),
 (10251,3,'And cry not unto any other god along with Allah. There is no Allah save Him. Everything will perish save His countenance. His is the command, and unto Him ye will be brought back.',NULL,28,88),
 (10252,1,'Alif Lam Mim.',NULL,29,1),
 (10253,2,'A.L.M.',NULL,29,1),
 (10254,3,'Alif. Lam. Mim.',NULL,29,1),
 (10255,1,'Do men think that they will be left alone on saying, We believe, and not be tried?',NULL,29,2),
 (10256,2,'Do men think that they will be left alone on saying, "We believe", and that they will not be tested?',NULL,29,2),
 (10257,3,'Do men imagine that they will be left (at ease) because they say, We believe, and will not be tested with affliction?',NULL,29,2),
 (10258,1,'And certainly We tried those before them, so Allah will certainly know those who are true and He will certainly know the liars.',NULL,29,3),
 (10259,2,'We did test those before them, and Allah will certainly know those who are true from those who are false.',NULL,29,3),
 (10260,3,'Lo! We tested those who were before you. Thus Allah knoweth those who are sincere, and knoweth those who feign.',NULL,29,3),
 (10261,1,'Or do they who work evil think that they will escape Us? Evil is it that they judge!',NULL,29,4),
 (10262,2,'Do those who practise evil think that they will get the better of Us? Evil is their judgment!',NULL,29,4),
 (10263,3,'Or do those who do ill-deeds imagine that they can outstrip Us? Evil (for them) is that which they decide.',NULL,29,4),
 (10264,1,'Whoever hopes to meet Allah, the term appointed by Allah will then most surely come; and He is the Hearing, the Knowing.',NULL,29,5),
 (10265,2,'For those whose hopes are in the meeting with Allah (in the Hereafter, let them strive); for the term (appointed) by Allah is surely coming and He hears and knows (all things).',NULL,29,5),
 (10266,3,'Whoso looketh forward to the meeting with Allah (let him know that) Allah''s reckoning is surely nigh, and He is the Hearer, the Knower.',NULL,29,5),
 (10267,1,'And whoever strives hard, he strives only for his own soul; most surely Allah is Self-sufficient, above (need of) the worlds.',NULL,29,6),
 (10268,2,'And if any strive (with might and main), they do so for their own souls: for Allah is free of all needs from all creation.',NULL,29,6),
 (10269,3,'And whosoever striveth, striveth only for himself, for lo! Allah is altogether Independent of (His) creatures.',NULL,29,6),
 (10270,1,'And (as for) those who believe and do good, We will most certainly do away with their evil deeds and We will most certainly reward them the best of what they did.',NULL,29,7),
 (10271,2,'Those who believe and work righteous deeds,- from them shall We blot out all evil (that may be) in them, and We shall reward them according to the best of their deeds.',NULL,29,7),
 (10272,3,'And as for those who believe and do good works, We shall remit from them their evil deeds and shall repay them the best that they did.',NULL,29,7),
 (10273,1,'And We have enjoined on man goodness to his parents, and if they contend with you that you should associate (others) with Me, of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them, to Me is your return, so I will inform you of what you did.',NULL,29,8),
 (10274,2,'We have enjoined on man kindness to parents: but if they (either of them) strive (to force) thee to join with Me (in worship) anything of which thou hast no knowledge, obey them not. Ye have (all) to return to me, and I will tell you (the truth) of all that ye did.',NULL,29,8),
 (10275,3,'We have enjoined on man kindness to parents; but if they strive to make thee join with Me that of which thou hast no knowledge, then obey them not. Unto Me is your return and I shall tell you what ye used to do.',NULL,29,8),
 (10276,1,'And (as for) those who believe and do good, We will most surely cause them to enter among the good.',NULL,29,9),
 (10277,2,'And those who believe and work righteous deeds,- them shall We admit to the company of the Righteous.',NULL,29,9),
 (10278,3,'And as for those who believe and do good works, We verily shall make them enter in among the righteous.',NULL,29,9),
 (10279,1,'And among men is he who says: We believe in Allah; but when he is persecuted in (the way of) Allah he thinks the persecution of men to be as the chastisement of Allah; and if there come assistance from your Lord, they would most certainly say: Surely we were with you. What! is not Allah the best knower of what is in the breasts of mankind.',NULL,29,10),
 (10280,2,'Then there are among men such as say, "We believe in Allah"; but when they suffer affliction in (the cause of) Allah, they treat men''s oppression as if it were the Wrath of Allah! And if help comes (to thee) from thy Lord, they are sure to say, "We have (always) been with you!" Does not Allah know best all that is in the hearts of all creation?',NULL,29,10),
 (10281,3,'Of mankind is he who saith: We believe in Allah, but, if he be made to suffer for the sake of Allah, he mistaketh the persecution of mankind for Allah''s punishment; and then, if victory cometh from thy Lord, will say: Lo! we were with you (all the while). Is not Allah Best Aware of what is in the bosoms of (His) creatures?',NULL,29,10),
 (10282,1,'And most certainly Allah will know those who believe and most certainly He will know the hypocrites.',NULL,29,11),
 (10283,2,'And Allah most certainly knows those who believe, and as certainly those who are Hypocrites.',NULL,29,11),
 (10284,3,'Verily Allah knoweth those who believe, and verily He knoweth the hypocrites.',NULL,29,11),
 (10285,1,'And those who disbelieve say to those who believe: Follow our path and we will bear your wrongs. And never shall they be the bearers of any of their wrongs; most surely they are liars.',NULL,29,12),
 (10286,2,'And the Unbelievers say to those who believe: "Follow our path, and we will bear (the consequences) of your faults." Never in the least will they bear their faults: in fact they are liars!',NULL,29,12),
 (10287,3,'Those who disbelieve say unto those who believe: Follow our way (of religion) and we verily will bear your sins (for you). They cannot bear aught of their sins. Lo! they verily are liars.',NULL,29,12),
 (10288,1,'And most certainly they shall carry their own burdens, and other burdens with their own burdens, and most certainly they shall be questioned on the resurrection day as to what they forged.',NULL,29,13),
 (10289,2,'They will bear their own burdens, and (other) burdens along with their own, and on the Day of Judgments they will be called to account for their falsehoods.',NULL,29,13),
 (10290,3,'But they verily will bear their own loads and other loads beside their own, and they verily will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection concerning that which they invented.',NULL,29,13),
 (10291,1,'And certainly We sent Nuh to his people, so he remained among them a thousand years save fifty years. And the deluge overtook them, while they were unjust.',NULL,29,14),
 (10292,2,'We (once) sent Noah to his people, and he tarried among them a thousand years less fifty: but the Deluge overwhelmed them while they (persisted in) sin.',NULL,29,14),
 (10293,3,'And verily we sent Noah (as Our messenger) unto his folk, and he continued with them for a thousand years save fifty years; and the flood engulfed them, for they were wrong-doers.',NULL,29,14),
 (10294,1,'So We delivered him and the inmates of the ark, and made it a sign to the nations.',NULL,29,15),
 (10295,2,'But We saved him and the companions of the Ark, and We made the (Ark) a Sign for all peoples!',NULL,29,15),
 (10296,3,'And We rescued him and those with him in the ship, and made of it a portent for the peoples.',NULL,29,15),
 (10297,1,'And (We sent) Ibrahim, when he said to his people: Serve Allah and be careful of (your duty to) Him; this is best for you, if you did but know:',NULL,29,16),
 (10298,2,'And (We also saved) Abraham: behold, he said to his people, "Serve Allah and fear Him: that will be best for you- If ye understand!',NULL,29,16),
 (10299,3,'And Abraham! (Remember) when he said unto his folk: Serve Allah, and keep your duty unto Him; that is better for you if ye did but know.',NULL,29,16),
 (10300,1,'You only worship idols besides Allah and you create a lie surely they whom you serve besides Allah do not control for you any sustenance, therefore seek the sustenance from Allah and serve Him and be grateful to Him; to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,29,17),
 (10301,2,'"For ye do worship idols besides Allah, and ye invent falsehood. The things that ye worship besides Allah have no power to give you sustenance: then seek ye sustenance from Allah, serve Him, and be grateful to Him: to Him will be your return.',NULL,29,17),
 (10302,3,'Ye serve instead of Allah only idols, and ye only invent a lie. Lo! those whom ye serve instead of Allah own no provision for you. So seek your provision from Allah, and serve Him, and give thanks unto Him, (for) unto Him ye will be brought back.',NULL,29,17),
 (10303,1,'And if you reject (the truth), nations before you did indeed reject (the truth); and nothing is incumbent on the messenger but a plain delivering (of the message).',NULL,29,18),
 (10304,2,'"And if ye reject (the Message), so did generations before you: and the duty of the messenger is only to preach publicly (and clearly)."',NULL,29,18),
 (10305,3,'But if ye deny, then nations have denied before you. The messenger is only to convey (the message) plainly.',NULL,29,18),
 (10306,1,'What! do they not consider how Allah originates the creation, then reproduces it? Surely that is easy to Allah.',NULL,29,19),
 (10307,2,'See they not how Allah originates creation, then repeats it: truly that is easy for Allah.',NULL,29,19),
 (10308,3,'See they not how Allah produceth creation, then reproduceth it? Lo! for Allah that is easy.',NULL,29,19),
 (10309,1,'Say: Travel in the earth and see how He makes the first creation, then Allah creates the latter creation; surely Allah has power over all things.',NULL,29,20),
 (10310,2,'Say: "Travel through the earth and see how Allah did originate creation; so will Allah produce a later creation: for Allah has power over all things.',NULL,29,20),
 (10311,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Travel in the land and see how He originated creation, then Allah bringeth forth the later growth. Lo! Allah is Able to do all things.',NULL,29,20),
 (10312,1,'He punishes whom He pleases and has mercy on whom He pleases, and to Him you shall be turned back.',NULL,29,21),
 (10313,2,'"He punishes whom He pleases, and He grants Mercy to whom He pleases, and towards Him are ye turned.',NULL,29,21),
 (10314,3,'He punisheth whom He will and showeth mercy unto whom He will, and unto Him ye will be turned.',NULL,29,21),
 (10315,1,'And you shall not escape in the earth nor in the heaven, and you have neither a protector nor a helper besides Allah.',NULL,29,22),
 (10316,2,'"Not on earth nor in heaven will ye be able (fleeing) to frustrate (his Plan), nor have ye, besides Allah, any protector or helper."',NULL,29,22),
 (10317,3,'Ye cannot escape (from Him) in the earth or in the sky, and beside Allah there is for you no friend or helper.',NULL,29,22),
 (10318,1,'And (as to) those who disbelieve in the communications of Allah and His meeting, they have despaired of My mercy, and these it is that shall have a painful punishment.',NULL,29,23),
 (10319,2,'Those who reject the Signs of Allah and the Meeting with Him (in the Hereafter),- it is they who shall despair of My Mercy: it is they who will (suffer) a most grievous Penalty.',NULL,29,23),
 (10320,3,'Those who disbelieve in the revelations of Allah and in (their) Meeting with Him, such have no hope of My mercy. For such there is a painful doom.',NULL,29,23),
 (10321,1,'So naught was the answer of his people except that they said: Slay him or burn him; then Allah delivered him from the fire; most surely there are signs in this for a people who believe.',NULL,29,24),
 (10322,2,'So naught was the answer of (Abraham''s) people except that they said: "Slay him or burn him." But Allah did save him from the Fire. Verily in this are Signs for people who believe.',NULL,29,24),
 (10323,3,'But the answer of his folk was only that they said: "Kill him" or "Burn him." Then Allah saved him from the Fire. Lo! herein verily are portents for folk who believe.',NULL,29,24),
 (10324,1,'And he said: You have only taken for yourselves idols besides Allah by way of friendship between you in this world''s life, then on the resurrection day some of you shall deny others, and some of you shall curse others, and your abode is the fire, and you shall not have any helpers.',NULL,29,25),
 (10325,2,'And he said: "For you, ye have taken (for worship) idols besides Allah, out of mutual love and regard between yourselves in this life; but on the Day of Judgment ye shall disown each other and curse each other: and your abode will be the Fire, and ye shall have none to help."',NULL,29,25),
 (10326,3,'He said: Ye have chosen only idols instead of Allah. The love between you is only in the life of the world. Then on the Day of Resurrection ye will deny each other and curse each other, and your abode will be the Fire, and ye will have no helpers.',NULL,29,25),
 (10327,1,'And Lut believed in Him, and he said: I am fleeing to my Lord, surely He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,29,26),
 (10328,2,'But Lut had faith in Him: He said: "I will leave home for the sake of my Lord: for He is Exalted in Might, and Wise."',NULL,29,26),
 (10329,3,'And Lot believed him, and said: Lo! I am a fugitive unto my Lord. Lo! He, only He, is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,29,26),
 (10330,1,'And We granted him Ishaq and Yaqoub, and caused the t prophethood and the book to remain in his seed, and We gave him his reward in this world, and in the hereafter he will most surely be among the good.',NULL,29,27),
 (10331,2,'And We gave (Abraham) Isaac and Jacob, and ordained among his progeny Prophethood and Revelation, and We granted him his reward in this life; and he was in the Hereafter (of the company) of the Righteous.',NULL,29,27),
 (10332,3,'And We bestowed on him Isaac and Jacob, and We established the prophethood and the Scripture among his seed, and We gave him his reward in the world, and lo! in the Hereafter he verily is among the righteous.',NULL,29,27),
 (10333,1,'And (We sent) Lut when he said to his people: Most surely you are guilty of an indecency which none of the nations has ever done before you;',NULL,29,28),
 (10334,2,'And (remember) Lut: behold, he said to his people: "Ye do commit lewdness, such as no people in Creation (ever) committed before you.',NULL,29,28),
 (10335,3,'And Lot! (Remember) when he said unto his folk: Lo! ye commit lewdness such as no creature did before you.',NULL,29,28),
 (10336,1,'What! do you come to the males and commit robbery on the highway, and you commit evil deeds in your assemblies? But nothing was the answer of his people except that they said: Bring on us Allah''s punishment, if you are one of the truthful.',NULL,29,29),
 (10337,2,'"Do ye indeed approach men, and cut off the highway?- and practise wickedness (even) in your councils?" But his people gave no answer but this: they said: "Bring us the Wrath of Allah if thou tellest the truth."',NULL,29,29),
 (10338,3,'For come ye not in unto males, and cut ye not the road (for travellers), and commit ye not abomination in your meetings? But the answer of his folk was only that they said: Bring Allah''s doom upon us if thou art a truthteller!',NULL,29,29),
 (10339,1,'He said: My Lord! help me against the mischievous people.',NULL,29,30),
 (10340,2,'He said: "O my Lord! help Thou me against people who do mischief!"',NULL,29,30),
 (10341,3,'He said: My Lord! Give me victory over folk who work corruption.',NULL,29,30),
 (10342,1,'And when Our messengers came to Ibrahim with the good news, they said: Surely we are going to destroy the people of this town, for its people are unjust.',NULL,29,31),
 (10343,2,'When Our Messengers came to Abraham with the good news, they said: "We are indeed going to destroy the people of this township: for truly they are (addicted to) crime."',NULL,29,31),
 (10344,3,'And when Our messengers brought Abraham the good news, they said: Lo! we are about to destroy the people of that township, for its people are wrong-doers.',NULL,29,31),
 (10345,1,'He said: Surely in it is Lut. They said: We know well who is in it; we shall certainly deliver him and his followers, except his wife; she shall be of those who remain behind.',NULL,29,32),
 (10346,2,'He said: "But there is Lut there." They said: "Well do we know who is there : we will certainly save him and his following,- except his wife: she is of those who lag behind!"',NULL,29,32),
 (10347,3,'He said: Lo! Lot is there. They said: We are best aware of who is there. We are to deliver him and his household, all save his wife, who is of those who stay behind.',NULL,29,32),
 (10348,1,'And when Our messengers came to Lut he was grieved on account of them, and he felt powerless (to protect) them; and they said: Fear not, nor grieve; surely we will deliver you and your followers, except your wife; she shall be of those who remain behind.',NULL,29,33),
 (10349,2,'And when Our Messengers came to Lut, he was grieved on their account, and felt himself powerless (to protect) them: but they said: "Fear thou not, nor grieve: we are (here) to save thee and thy following, except thy wife: she is of those who lag behind.',NULL,29,33),
 (10350,3,'And when Our messengers came unto Lot, he was troubled upon their account, for he could not protect them; but they said: Fear not, nor grieve! Lo! we are to deliver thee and thy household, (all) save thy wife, who is of those who stay behind.',NULL,29,33),
 (10351,1,'Surely We will cause to come down upon the people of this town a punishment from heaven, because they transgressed.',NULL,29,34),
 (10352,2,'"For we are going to bring down on the people of this township a Punishment from heaven, because they have been wickedly rebellious."',NULL,29,34),
 (10353,3,'Lo! We are about to bring down upon the folk of this township a fury from the sky because they are evil-livers.',NULL,29,34),
 (10354,1,'And certainly We have left a clear sign of it for a people who understand.',NULL,29,35),
 (10355,2,'And We have left thereof an evident Sign, for any people who (care to) understand.',NULL,29,35),
 (10356,3,'And verily of that We have left a clear sign for people who have sense.',NULL,29,35),
 (10357,1,'And to Madyan (We sent) their brother Shuaib, so he said: O my people! serve Allah and fear the latter day and do not act corruptly in the land, making mischief.',NULL,29,36),
 (10358,2,'To the Madyan (people) (We sent) their brother Shu''aib. Then he said: "O my people! serve Allah, and fear the Last Day: nor commit evil on the earth, with intent to do mischief."',NULL,29,36),
 (10359,3,'And unto Midian We sent Shu''eyb, their brother. He said: O my people! Serve Allah, and look forward to the Last Day, and do not evil, making mischief, in the earth.',NULL,29,36),
 (10360,1,'But they rejected him, so a severe earthquake overtook them, and they became motionless bodies in their abode.',NULL,29,37),
 (10361,2,'But they rejected him: Then the mighty Blast seized them, and they lay prostrate in their homes by the morning.',NULL,29,37),
 (10362,3,'But they denied him, and the dreadful earthquake took them, and morning found them prostrate in their dwelling place.',NULL,29,37),
 (10363,1,'And (We destroyed) Ad and Samood, and from their dwellings (this) is apparent to you indeed; and the Shaitan made their deeds fair-seeming to them, so he kept them back from the path, though they were endowed with intelligence and skill,',NULL,29,38),
 (10364,2,'(Remember also) the ''Ad and the Thamud (people): clearly will appear to you from (the traces) of their buildings (their fate): the Evil One made their deeds alluring to them, and kept them back from the Path, though they were gifted with intelligence and skill.',NULL,29,38),
 (10365,3,'And (the tribes of) A''ad and Thamud! (Their fate) is manifest unto you from their (ruined and deserted) dwellings. Satan made their deeds seem fair unto them and so debarred them from the Way, though they were keen observers.',NULL,29,38),
 (10366,1,'And (We destroyed) Qaroun and Firon and Haman; and certainly Musa came to them with clear arguments, but they behaved haughtily in the land; yet they could not outstrip (Us).',NULL,29,39),
 (10367,2,'(Remember also) Qarun, Pharaoh, and Haman: there came to them Moses with Clear Signs, but they behaved with insolence on the earth; yet they could not overreach (Us).',NULL,29,39),
 (10368,3,'And Korah, Pharaoh and Haman! Moses came unto them with clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty), but they were boastful in the land. And they were not winners (in the race).',NULL,29,39),
 (10369,1,'So each We punished for his sin; of them was he on whom We sent down a violent storm, and of them was he whom the rumbling overtook, and of them was he whom We made to be swallowed up by the earth, and of them was he whom We drowned; and it did not beseem Allah that He should be unjust to them, but they were unjust to their own souls.',NULL,29,40),
 (10370,2,'Each one of them We seized for his crime: of them, against some We sent a violent tornado (with showers of stones); some were caught by a (mighty) Blast; some We caused the earth to swallow up; and some We drowned (in the waters): It was not Allah Who injured (or oppressed) them:" They injured (and oppressed) their own souls.',NULL,29,40),
 (10371,3,'So We took each one in his sin; of them was he on whom We sent a hurricane, and of them was he who was overtaken by the (Awful) Cry, and of them was he whom We caused the earth to swallow, and of them was he whom We drowned. It was not for Allah to wrong them, but they wronged themselves.',NULL,29,40),
 (10372,1,'The parable of those who take guardians besides Allah is as the parable of the spider that makes for itself a house; and most surely the frailest of the houses is the spider''s house did they but know.',NULL,29,41),
 (10373,2,'The parable of those who take protectors other than Allah is that of the spider, who builds (to itself) a house; but truly the flimsiest of houses is the spider''s house;- if they but knew.',NULL,29,41),
 (10374,3,'The likeness of those who choose other patrons than Allah is as the likeness of the spider when she taketh unto herself a house, and lo! the frailest of all houses is the spider''s house, if they but knew.',NULL,29,41),
 (10375,1,'Surely Allah knows whatever thing they call upon besides Him; and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,29,42),
 (10376,2,'Verily Allah doth know of (every thing) whatever that they call upon besides Him: and He is Exalted (in power), Wise.',NULL,29,42),
 (10377,3,'Lo! Allah knoweth what thing they invoke instead of Him. He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,29,42),
 (10378,1,'And (as for) these examples, We set them forth for men, and none understand them but the learned.',NULL,29,43),
 (10379,2,'And such are the Parables We set forth for mankind, but only those understand them who have knowledge.',NULL,29,43),
 (10380,3,'As for these similitudes, We coin them for mankind, but none will grasp their meaning save the wise.',NULL,29,43),
 (10381,1,'Allah created the heavens and the earth with truth; most surely there is a sign in this for the believers.',NULL,29,44),
 (10382,2,'Allah created the heavens and the earth in true (proportions): verily in that is a Sign for those who believe.',NULL,29,44),
 (10383,3,'Allah created the heavens and the earth with truth. Lo! therein is indeed a portent for believers.',NULL,29,44),
 (10384,1,'Recite that which has been revealed to you of the Book and keep up prayer; surely prayer keeps (one) away from indecency and evil, and certainly the remembrance of Allah is the greatest, and Allah knows what you do.',NULL,29,45),
 (10385,2,'Recite what is sent of the Book by inspiration to thee, and establish regular Prayer: for Prayer restrains from shameful and unjust deeds; and remembrance of Allah is the greatest (thing in life) without doubt. And Allah knows the (deeds) that ye do.',NULL,29,45),
 (10386,3,'Recite that which hath been inspired in thee of the Scripture, and establish worship. Lo! worship preserveth from lewdness and iniquity, but verily remembrance of Allah is more important. And Allah knoweth what ye do.',NULL,29,45),
 (10387,1,'And do not dispute with the followers of the Book except by what is best, except those of them who act unjustly, and say: We believe in that which has been revealed to us and revealed to you, and our Allah and your Allah is One, and to Him do we submit.',NULL,29,46),
 (10388,2,'And dispute ye not with the People of the Book, except with means better (than mere disputation), unless it be with those of them who inflict wrong (and injury): but say, "We believe in the revelation which has come down to us and in that which came down to you; Our Allah and your Allah is one; and it is to Him we bow (in Islam)."',NULL,29,46),
 (10389,3,'And argue not with the People of the Scripture unless it be in (a way) that is better, save with such of them as do wrong; and say: We believe in that which hath been revealed unto us and revealed unto you; our Allah and your Allah is One, and unto Him we surrender.',NULL,29,46),
 (10390,1,'And thus have We revealed the Book to you. So those whom We have given the Book believe in it, and of these there are those who believe in it, and none deny Our communications except the unbelievers.',NULL,29,47),
 (10391,2,'And thus (it is) that We have sent down the Book to thee. So the People of the Book believe therein, as also do some of these (pagan Arabs): and none but Unbelievers reject our signs.',NULL,29,47),
 (10392,3,'In like manner We have revealed unto thee the Scripture, and those unto whom We gave the Scripture aforetime will believe therein; and of these (also) there are some who believe therein. And none deny Our revelations save the disbelievers.',NULL,29,47),
 (10393,1,'And you did not recite before it any book, nor did you transcribe one with your right hand, for then could those who say untrue things have doubted.',NULL,29,48),
 (10394,2,'And thou wast not (able) to recite a Book before this (Book came), nor art thou (able) to transcribe it with thy right hand: In that case, indeed, would the talkers of vanities have doubted.',NULL,29,48),
 (10395,3,'And thou (O Muhammad) wast not a reader of any scripture before it, nor didst thou write it with thy right hand, for then might those have doubted, who follow falsehood.',NULL,29,48),
 (10396,1,'Nay! these are clear communications in the breasts of those who are granted knowledge; and none deny Our communications except the unjust.',NULL,29,49),
 (10397,2,'Nay, here are Signs self-evident in the hearts of those endowed with knowledge: and none but the unjust reject Our Signs.',NULL,29,49),
 (10398,3,'But it is clear revelations in the hearts of those who have been given knowledge, and none deny Our revelations save wrong-doers.',NULL,29,49),
 (10399,1,'And they say: Why are not signs sent down upon him from his Lord? Say: The signs are only with Allah, and I am only a plain warner.',NULL,29,50),
 (10400,2,'Ye they say: "Why are not Signs sent down to him from his Lord?" Say: "The signs are indeed with Allah: and I am indeed a clear Warner."',NULL,29,50),
 (10401,3,'And they say: Why are not portents sent down upon him from his Lord? Say: Portents are with Allah only, and I am but a plain warner.',NULL,29,50),
 (10402,1,'Is it not enough for them that We have revealed to you the Book which is recited to them? Most surely there is mercy in this and a reminder for a people who believe.',NULL,29,51),
 (10403,2,'And is it not enough for them that we have sent down to thee the Book which is rehearsed to them? Verily, in it is Mercy and a Reminder to those who believe.',NULL,29,51),
 (10404,3,'Is it not enough for them that We have sent down unto thee the Scripture which is read unto them? Lo! herein verily is mercy, and a reminder for folk who believe.',NULL,29,51),
 (10405,1,'Say: Allah is sufficient as a witness between me and you; He knows what is in the heavens and the earth. And (as for) those who believe in the falsehood and disbelieve in Allah, these it is that are the losers.',NULL,29,52),
 (10406,2,'Say: "Enough is Allah for a witness between me and you: He knows what is in the heavens and on earth. And it is those who believe in vanities and reject Allah, that will perish (in the end).',NULL,29,52),
 (10407,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Allah sufficeth for witness between me and you. He knoweth whatsoever is in the heavens and the earth. And those who believe in vanity and disbelieve in Allah, they it is who are the losers.',NULL,29,52),
 (10408,1,'And they ask you to hasten on the chastisement; and had not a term been appointed, the chastisement would certainly have come to them; and most certainly it will come to them all of a sudden while they will not perceive.',NULL,29,53),
 (10409,2,'They ask thee to hasten on the Punishment (for them): had it not been for a term (of respite) appointed, the Punishment would certainly have come to them: and it will certainly reach them,- of a sudden, while they perceive not!',NULL,29,53),
 (10410,3,'They bid thee hasten on the doom (of Allah). And if a term had not been appointed, the doom would assuredly have come unto them (ere now). And verily it will come upon them suddenly when they perceive not.',NULL,29,53),
 (10411,1,'They ask you to hasten on the chastisement, and most surely hell encompasses the unbelievers;',NULL,29,54),
 (10412,2,'They ask thee to hasten on the Punishment: but, of a surety, Hell will encompass the Rejecters of Faith!-',NULL,29,54),
 (10413,3,'They bid thee hasten on the doom, when lo! hell verily will encompass the disbelievers',NULL,29,54),
 (10414,1,'On the day when the chastisement shall cover them from above them, and from beneath their feet; and He shall say: Taste what you did.',NULL,29,55),
 (10415,2,'On the Day that the Punishment shall cover them from above them and from below them, and (a Voice) shall say: "Taste ye (the fruits) of your deeds!"',NULL,29,55),
 (10416,3,'On the day when the doom will overwhelm them from above them and from underneath their feet, and He will say: Taste what ye used to do!',NULL,29,55),
 (10417,1,'O My servants who believe! surely My earth is vast, therefore Me alone should you serve.',NULL,29,56),
 (10418,2,'O My servants who believe! truly, spacious is My Earth: therefore serve ye Me - (and Me alone)!',NULL,29,56),
 (10419,3,'O my bondmen who believe! Lo! My earth is spacious. Therefor serve Me only.',NULL,29,56),
 (10420,1,'Every soul must taste of death, then to Us you shall be brought back.',NULL,29,57),
 (10421,2,'Every soul shall have a taste of death in the end to Us shall ye be brought back.',NULL,29,57),
 (10422,3,'Every soul will taste of death. Then unto Us ye will be returned.',NULL,29,57),
 (10423,1,'And (as for) those who believe and do good, We will certainly give them abode in the high places in gardens beneath which rivers flow, abiding therein; how good the reward of the workers:',NULL,29,58),
 (10424,2,'But those who believe and work deeds of righteousness - to them shall We give a Home in Heaven,- lofty mansions beneath which flow rivers,- to dwell therein for aye;- an excellent reward for those who do (good)!-',NULL,29,58),
 (10425,3,'Those who believe and do good works, them verily We shall house in lofty dwellings of the Garden underneath which rivers flow. There they will dwell secure. How sweet the guerdon of the toilers,',NULL,29,58),
 (10426,1,'Those who are patient, and on their Lord do they rely.',NULL,29,59),
 (10427,2,'Those who persevere in patience, and put their trust, in their Lord and Cherisher.',NULL,29,59),
 (10428,3,'Who persevere, and put their trust in their Lord!',NULL,29,59),
 (10429,1,'And how many a living creature that does not carry its sustenance: Allah sustains it and yourselves; and He is the Hearing, the Knowing.',NULL,29,60),
 (10430,2,'How many are the creatures that carry not their own sustenance? It is Allah who feeds (both) them and you: for He hears and knows (all things).',NULL,29,60),
 (10431,3,'And how many an animal there is that beareth not its own provision! Allah provideth for it and for you. He is the Hearer, the Knower.',NULL,29,60),
 (10432,1,'And if you ask them, Who created the heavens and the earth and made the sun and the moon subservient, they will certainly say, Allah. Whence are they then turned away?',NULL,29,61),
 (10433,2,'If indeed thou ask them who has created the heavens and the earth and subjected the sun and the moon (to his Law), they will certainly reply, "Allah". How are they then deluded away (from the truth)?',NULL,29,61),
 (10434,3,'And if thou wert to ask them: Who created the heavens and the earth, and constrained the sun and the moon (to their appointed work)? they would say: Allah. How then are they turned away?',NULL,29,61),
 (10435,1,'Allah makes abundant the means of subsistence for whom He pleases of His servants, and straitens them for whom (He pleases) surely Allah is Cognizant of all things.',NULL,29,62),
 (10436,2,'Allah enlarges the sustenance (which He gives) to whichever of His servants He pleases; and He (similarly) grants by (strict) measure, (as He pleases): for Allah has full knowledge of all things.',NULL,29,62),
 (10437,3,'Allah maketh the provision wide for whom He will of His bondmen, and straiteneth it for whom (He will). Lo! Allah is Aware of all things.',NULL,29,62),
 (10438,1,'And if you ask them Who is it that sends down water from the clouds, then gives life to the earth with it after its death, they will certainly say, Allah. Say: All praise is due to Allah. Nay, most of them do not understand.',NULL,29,63),
 (10439,2,'And if indeed thou ask them who it is that sends down rain from the sky, and gives life therewith to the earth after its death, they will certainly reply, "Allah!" Say, "Praise be to Allah!" But most of them understand not.',NULL,29,63),
 (10440,3,'And if thou wert to ask them: Who causeth water to come down from the sky, and therewith reviveth the earth after its death? they verily would say: Allah. Say: Praise be to Allah! But most of them have no sense.',NULL,29,63),
 (10441,1,'And this life of the world is nothing but a sport and a play; and as for the next abode, that most surely is the life-- did they but know!',NULL,29,64),
 (10442,2,'What is the life of this world but amusement and play? but verily the Home in the Hereafter,- that is life indeed, if they but knew.',NULL,29,64),
 (10443,3,'This life of the world is but a pastime and a game. Lo! the home of the Hereafter - that is Life, if they but knew.',NULL,29,64),
 (10444,1,'So when they ride in the ships they call upon Allah, being sincerely obedient to Him, but when He brings them safe to the land, lo! they associate others (with Him);',NULL,29,65),
 (10445,2,'Now, if they embark on a boat, they call on Allah, making their devotion sincerely (and exclusively) to Him; but when He has delivered them safely to (dry) land, behold, they give a share (of their worship to others)!-',NULL,29,65),
 (10446,3,'And when they mount upon the ships they pray to Allah, making their faith pure for Him only, but when He bringeth them safe to land, behold! they ascribe partners (unto Him),',NULL,29,65),
 (10447,1,'Thus they become ungrateful for what We have given them, so that they may enjoy; but they shall soon know.',NULL,29,66),
 (10448,2,'Disdaining ungratefully Our gifts, and giving themselves up to (worldly) enjoyment! But soon will they know.',NULL,29,66),
 (10449,3,'That they may disbelieve in that which We have given them, and that they may take their ease. But they will come to know.',NULL,29,66),
 (10450,1,'Do they not see that We have made a sacred territory secure, while men are carried off by force from around them? Will they still believe in the falsehood and disbelieve in the favour of Allah?',NULL,29,67),
 (10451,2,'Do they not then see that We have made a sanctuary secure, and that men are being snatched away from all around them? Then, do they believe in that which is vain, and reject the Grace of Allah?',NULL,29,67),
 (10452,3,'Have they not seen that We have appointed a sanctuary immune (from violence), while mankind are ravaged all around them? Do they then believe in falsehood and disbelieve in the bounty of Allah?',NULL,29,67),
 (10453,1,'And who is more unjust than one who forges a lie against Allah, or gives the lie to the truth when it has come to him? Will not in hell be the abode of the unbelievers?',NULL,29,68),
 (10454,2,'And who does more wrong than he who invents a lie against Allah or rejects the Truth when it reaches him? Is there not a home in Hell for those who reject Faith?',NULL,29,68),
 (10455,3,'Who doeth greater wrong than he who inventeth a lie concerning Allah, or denieth the truth when it cometh unto him? Is not there a home in hell for disbelievers?',NULL,29,68),
 (10456,1,'And (as for) those who strive hard for Us, We will most certainly guide them in Our ways; and Allah is most surely with the doers of good.',NULL,29,69),
 (10457,2,'And those who strive in Our (cause),- We will certainly guide them to our Paths: For verily Allah is with those who do right.',NULL,29,69),
 (10458,3,'As for those who strive in Us, We surely guide them to Our paths, and lo! Allah is with the good.',NULL,29,69),
 (10459,1,'Alif Lam Mim.',NULL,30,1),
 (10460,2,'A. L. M.',NULL,30,1),
 (10461,3,'Alif. Lam. Mim.',NULL,30,1),
 (10462,1,'The Romans are vanquished,',NULL,30,2),
 (10463,2,'The Roman Empire has been defeated-',NULL,30,2),
 (10464,3,'The Romans have been defeated',NULL,30,2),
 (10465,1,'In a near land, and they, after being vanquished, shall overcome,',NULL,30,3),
 (10466,2,'In a land close by; but they, (even) after (this) defeat of theirs, will soon be victorious-',NULL,30,3),
 (10467,3,'In the nearer land, and they, after their defeat will be victorious',NULL,30,3),
 (10468,1,'Within a few years. Allah''s is the command before and after; and on that day the believers shall rejoice,',NULL,30,4),
 (10469,2,'Within a few years. With Allah is the Decision, in the past and in the Future: on that Day shall the Believers rejoice-',NULL,30,4),
 (10470,3,'Within ten years - Allah''s is the command in the former case and in the latter - and in that day believers will rejoice',NULL,30,4),
 (10471,1,'With the help of Allah; He helps whom He pleases; and He is the Mighty, the Merciful;',NULL,30,5),
 (10472,2,'With the help of Allah. He helps whom He will, and He is exalted in might, most merciful.',NULL,30,5),
 (10473,3,'In Allah''s help to victory. He helpeth to victory whom He will. He is the Mighty, the Merciful.',NULL,30,5),
 (10474,1,'(This is) Allah''s promise! Allah will not fail His promise, but most people do not know.',NULL,30,6),
 (10475,2,'(It is) the promise of Allah. Never does Allah depart from His promise: but most men understand not.',NULL,30,6),
 (10476,3,'It is a promise of Allah. Allah faileth not His promise, but most of mankind know not.',NULL,30,6),
 (10477,1,'They know the outward of this world''s life, but of the hereafter they are absolutely heedless.',NULL,30,7),
 (10478,2,'They know but the outer (things) in the life of this world: but of the End of things they are heedless.',NULL,30,7),
 (10479,3,'They know only some appearance of the life of the world, and are heedless of the Hereafter.',NULL,30,7),
 (10480,1,'Do they not reflect within themselves: Allah did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them two but with truth, and (for) an appointed term? And most surely most of the people are deniers of the meeting of their Lord.',NULL,30,8),
 (10481,2,'Do they not reflect in their own minds? Not but for just ends and for a term appointed, did Allah create the heavens and the earth, and all between them: yet are there truly many among men who deny the meeting with their Lord (at the Resurrection)!',NULL,30,8),
 (10482,3,'Have they not pondered upon themselves? Allah created not the heavens and the earth, and that which is between them, save with truth and for a destined end. But truly many of mankind are disbelievers in the meeting with their Lord.',NULL,30,8),
 (10483,1,'Have they not travelled in the earth and seen how was the end of those before them? They were stronger than these in prowess, and dug up the earth, and built on it in greater abundance than these have built on it, and there came to them their messengers with clear arguments; so it was not beseeming for Allah that He should deal with them unjustly, but they dealt unjustly with their own souls.',NULL,30,9),
 (10484,2,'Do they not travel through the earth, and see what was the end of those before them? They were superior to them in strength: they tilled the soil and populated it in greater numbers than these have done: there came to them their messengers with Clear (Signs). (Which they rejected, to their own destruction): It was not Allah Who wronged them, but they wronged their own souls.',NULL,30,9),
 (10485,3,'Have they not travelled in the land and seen the nature of the consequence for those who were before them? They were stronger than these in power, and they dug the earth and built upon it more than these have built. Messengers of their own came unto them with clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty). Surely Allah wronged them not, but they did wrong themselves.',NULL,30,9),
 (10486,1,'Then evil was the end of those who did evil, because they | rejected the communications of Allah and used to mock them.',NULL,30,10),
 (10487,2,'In the long run evil in the extreme will be the End of those who do evil; for that they rejected the Signs of Allah, and held them up to ridicule.',NULL,30,10),
 (10488,3,'Then evil was the consequence to those who dealt in evil, because they denied the revelations of Allah and made a mock of them.',NULL,30,10),
 (10489,1,'Allah originates the creation, then reproduces it, then to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,30,11),
 (10490,2,'It is Allah Who begins (the process of) creation; then repeats it; then shall ye be brought back to Him.',NULL,30,11),
 (10491,3,'Allah produceth creation, then He reproduceth it, then unto Him ye will be returned.',NULL,30,11),
 (10492,1,'And at the time when the hour shall come the guilty shall be in despair.',NULL,30,12),
 (10493,2,'On the Day that the Hour will be established, the guilty will be struck dumb with despair.',NULL,30,12),
 (10494,3,'And in the day when the Hour riseth the unrighteous will despair.',NULL,30,12),
 (10495,1,'And they shall not have any intercessors from among their gods they have joined with Allah, and they shall be deniers of their associate-gods.',NULL,30,13),
 (10496,2,'No intercessor will they have among their "Partners" and they will (themselves) reject their "Partners".',NULL,30,13),
 (10497,3,'There will be none to intercede for them of those whom they made equal with Allah. And they will reject their partners (whom they ascribed unto Him).',NULL,30,13),
 (10498,1,'And at the time when the hour shall come, at that time they shall become separated one from the other.',NULL,30,14),
 (10499,2,'On the Day that the Hour will be established,- that Day shall (all men) be sorted out.',NULL,30,14),
 (10500,3,'In the day when the Hour cometh, in that day they will be sundered.',NULL,30,14),
 (10501,1,'Then as to those who believed and did good, they shall be made happy in a garden.',NULL,30,15),
 (10502,2,'Then those who have believed and worked righteous deeds, shall be made happy in a Mead of Delight.',NULL,30,15),
 (10503,3,'As for those who believed and did good works, they will be made happy in a Garden.',NULL,30,15),
 (10504,1,'And as to those who disbelieved and rejected Our communications and the meeting of the hereafter, these shall be brought over to the chastisement.',NULL,30,16),
 (10505,2,'And those who have rejected Faith and falsely denied our Signs and the meeting of the Hereafter,- such shall be brought forth to Punishment.',NULL,30,16),
 (10506,3,'But as for those who disbelieved and denied Our revelations, and denied the meeting of the Hereafter, such will be brought to doom.',NULL,30,16),
 (10507,1,'Therefore glory be to Allah when you enter upon the time of the evening and when you enter upon the time of the morning.',NULL,30,17),
 (10508,2,'So (give) glory to Allah, when ye reach eventide and when ye rise in the morning;',NULL,30,17),
 (10509,3,'So glory be to Allah when ye enter the night and when ye enter the morning -',NULL,30,17),
 (10510,1,'And to Him belongs praise in the heavens and the earth, and at nightfall and when you are at midday.',NULL,30,18),
 (10511,2,'Yea, to Him be praise, in the heavens and on earth; and in the late afternoon and when the day begins to decline.',NULL,30,18),
 (10512,3,'Unto Him be praise in the heavens and the earth! - and at the sun''s decline and in the noonday.',NULL,30,18),
 (10513,1,'He brings forth the living from the dead and brings forth the dead from the living, and gives life to the earth after its death, and thus shall you be brought forth.',NULL,30,19),
 (10514,2,'It is He Who brings out the living from the dead, and brings out the dead from the living, and Who gives life to the earth after it is dead: and thus shall ye be brought out (from the dead).',NULL,30,19),
 (10515,3,'He bringeth forth the living from the dead, and He bringeth forth the dead from the living, and He reviveth the earth after her death. And even so will ye be brought forth.',NULL,30,19),
 (10516,1,'And one of His signs is that He created you from dust, then lo! you are mortals (who) scatter.',NULL,30,20),
 (10517,2,'Among His Signs in this, that He created you from dust; and then,- behold, ye are men scattered (far and wide)!',NULL,30,20),
 (10518,3,'And of His signs is this: He created you of dust, and behold you human beings, ranging widely!',NULL,30,20),
 (10519,1,'And one of His signs is that He created mates for you from yourselves that you may find rest in them, and He put between you love and compassion; most surely there are signs in this for a people who reflect.',NULL,30,21),
 (10520,2,'And among His Signs is this, that He created for you mates from among yourselves, that ye may dwell in tranquillity with them, and He has put love and mercy between your (hearts): verily in that are Signs for those who reflect.',NULL,30,21),
 (10521,3,'And of His signs is this: He created for you helpmeets from yourselves that ye might find rest in them, and He ordained between you love and mercy. Lo! herein indeed are portents for folk who reflect.',NULL,30,21),
 (10522,1,'And one of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and the diversity of your tongues and colors; most surely there are signs in this for the learned.',NULL,30,22),
 (10523,2,'And among His Signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the variations in your languages and your colours: verily in that are Signs for those who know.',NULL,30,22),
 (10524,3,'And of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the difference of your languages and colours. Lo! herein indeed are portents for men of knowledge.',NULL,30,22),
 (10525,1,'And one of His signs is your sleeping and your seeking of His grace by night and (by) day; most surely there are signs in this for a people who would hear.',NULL,30,23),
 (10526,2,'And among His Signs is the sleep that ye take by night and by day, and the quest that ye (make for livelihood) out of His Bounty: verily in that are signs for those who hearken.',NULL,30,23),
 (10527,3,'And of His signs is your slumber by night and by day, and your seeking of His bounty. Lo! herein indeed are portents for folk who heed.',NULL,30,23),
 (10528,1,'And one of His signs is that He shows you the lightning for fear and for hope, and sends down water from the clouds then gives life therewith to the earth after its death; most surely there are signs in this for a people who understand',NULL,30,24),
 (10529,2,'And among His Signs, He shows you the lightning, by way both of fear and of hope, and He sends down rain from the sky and with it gives life to the earth after it is dead: verily in that are Signs for those who are wise.',NULL,30,24),
 (10530,3,'And of His signs is this: He showeth you the lightning for a fear and for a hope, and sendeth down water from the sky, and thereby quickeneth the earth after her death. Lo! herein indeed are portents for folk who understand.',NULL,30,24),
 (10531,1,'And one of His signs is that the heaven and the earth subsist by His command, then when He calls you with a (single) call from out of the earth, lo! you come forth.',NULL,30,25),
 (10532,2,'And among His Signs is this, that heaven and earth stand by His Command: then when He calls you, by a single call, from the earth, behold, ye (straightway) come forth.',NULL,30,25),
 (10533,3,'And of His signs is this: The heavens and the earth stand fast by His command, and afterward, when He calleth you, lo! from the earth ye will emerge.',NULL,30,25),
 (10534,1,'And His is whosoever is in the heavens and the earth; all are obedient to Him.',NULL,30,26),
 (10535,2,'To Him belongs every being that is in the heavens and on earth: all are devoutly obedient to Him.',NULL,30,26),
 (10536,3,'Unto Him belongeth whosoever is in the heavens and the earth. All are obedient unto Him.',NULL,30,26),
 (10537,1,'And He it is Who originates the creation, then reproduces it, and it is easy to Him; and His are the most exalted attributes in the heavens and the earth, and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,30,27),
 (10538,2,'It is He Who begins (the process of) creation; then repeats it; and for Him it is most easy. To Him belongs the loftiest similitude (we can think of) in the heavens and the earth: for He is Exalted in Might, full of wisdom.',NULL,30,27),
 (10539,3,'He it is Who produceth creation, then reproduceth it, and it is easier for Him. His is the Sublime Similitude in the heavens and the earth. He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,30,27),
 (10540,1,'He sets forth to you a parable relating to yourselves: Have you among those whom your right hands possess partners in what We have given you for sustenance, so that with respect to it you are alike; you fear them as you fear each other? Thus do We make the communications distinct for a people who understand.',NULL,30,28),
 (10541,2,'He does propound to you a similitude from your own (experience): do ye have partners among those whom your right hands possess, to share as equals in the wealth We have bestowed on you? Do ye fear them as ye fear each other? Thus do we explain the Signs in detail to a people that understand.',NULL,30,28),
 (10542,3,'He coineth for you a similitude of yourselves. Have ye, from among those whom your right hands possess, partners in the wealth We have bestowed upon you, equal with you in respect thereof, so that ye fear them as ye fear each other (that ye ascribe unto Us partners out of that which We created)? Thus We display the revelations for people who have sense.',NULL,30,28),
 (10543,1,'Nay! those who are unjust follow their low desires without any knowledge; so who can guide him whom Allah makes err? And they shall have no helpers.',NULL,30,29),
 (10544,2,'Nay, the wrong-doers (merely) follow their own lusts, being devoid of knowledge. But who will guide those whom Allah leaves astray? To them there will be no helpers.',NULL,30,29),
 (10545,3,'Nay, but those who do wrong follow their own lusts without knowledge. Who is able to guide him whom Allah hath sent astray? For such there are no helpers.',NULL,30,29),
 (10546,1,'Then set your face upright for religion in the right state-- the nature made by Allah in which He has made men; there is no altering of Allah''s creation; that is the right religion, but most people do not know--',NULL,30,30),
 (10547,2,'So set thou thy face steadily and truly to the Faith: (establish) Allah''s handiwork according to the pattern on which He has made mankind: no change (let there be) in the work (wrought) by Allah: that is the standard Religion: but most among mankind understand not.',NULL,30,30),
 (10548,3,'So set thy purpose (O Muhammad) for religion as a man by nature upright - the nature (framed) of Allah, in which He hath created man. There is no altering (the laws of) Allah''s creation. That is the right religion, but most men know not -',NULL,30,30),
 (10549,1,'Turning to Him, and be careful of (your duty to) Him and keep up prayer and be not of the polytheists',NULL,30,31),
 (10550,2,'Turn ye back in repentance to Him, and fear Him: establish regular prayers, and be not ye among those who join gods with Allah,-',NULL,30,31),
 (10551,3,'Turning unto Him (only); and be careful of your duty unto Him and establish worship, and be not of those who ascribe partners (unto Him);',NULL,30,31),
 (10552,1,'Of those who divided their religion and became seas every sect rejoicing in what they had with them',NULL,30,32),
 (10553,2,'Those who split up their Religion, and become (mere) Sects,- each party rejoicing in that which is with itself!',NULL,30,32),
 (10554,3,'Of those who split up their religion and became schismatics, each sect exulting in its tenets.',NULL,30,32),
 (10555,1,'And when harm afflicts men, they call upon their Lord, turning to Him, then when He makes them taste of mercy from Him, lo! some of them begin to associate (others) with their Lord,',NULL,30,33),
 (10556,2,'When trouble touches men, they cry to their Lord, turning back to Him in repentance: but when He gives them a taste of Mercy as from Himself, behold, some of them pay part-worship to other god''s besides their Lord,-',NULL,30,33),
 (10557,3,'And when harm toucheth men they cry unto their Lord, turning to Him in repentance; then, when they have tasted of His mercy, behold! some of them attribute partners to their Lord',NULL,30,33),
 (10558,1,'So as to be ungrateful for what We have given them; but enjoy yourselves (for a while), for you shall soon come to know.',NULL,30,34),
 (10559,2,'(As if) to show their ingratitude for the (favours) We have bestowed on them! Then enjoy (your brief day); but soon will ye know (your folly).',NULL,30,34),
 (10560,3,'So as to disbelieve in that which We have given them. (Unto such it is said): Enjoy yourselves awhile, but ye will come to know.',NULL,30,34),
 (10561,1,'Or, have We sent down upon them an authority so that it speaks of that which they associate with Him?',NULL,30,35),
 (10562,2,'Or have We sent down authority to them, which points out to them the things to which they pay part-worship?',NULL,30,35),
 (10563,3,'Or have We revealed unto them any warrant which speaketh of that which they associate with Him?',NULL,30,35),
 (10564,1,'And when We make people taste of mercy they rejoice in it, and if an evil befall them for what their hands have already wrought, lo! they are in despair.',NULL,30,36),
 (10565,2,'When We give men a taste of Mercy, they exult thereat: and when some evil afflicts them because of what their (own) hands have sent forth, behold, they are in despair!',NULL,30,36),
 (10566,3,'And when We cause mankind to taste of mercy they rejoice therein; but if an evil thing befall them as the consequence of their own deeds, lo! they are in despair!',NULL,30,36),
 (10567,1,'Do they not see that Allah makes ample provision for whom He pleases, or straitens? Most surely there are signs in this for a people who believe.',NULL,30,37),
 (10568,2,'See they not that Allah enlarges the provision and restricts it, to whomsoever He pleases? Verily in that are Signs for those who believe.',NULL,30,37),
 (10569,3,'See they not that Allah enlargeth the provision for whom He will, and straiteneth (it for whom He will). Lo! herein indeed are portents for folk who believe.',NULL,30,37),
 (10570,1,'Then give to the near of kin his due, and to the needy and the wayfarer; this is best for those who desire Allah''s pleasure, and these it is who are successful.',NULL,30,38),
 (10571,2,'So give what is due to kindred, the needy, and the wayfarer. That is best for those who seek the Countenance, of Allah, and it is they who will prosper.',NULL,30,38),
 (10572,3,'So give to the kinsman his due, and to the needy, and to the wayfarer. That is best for those who seek Allah''s Countenance. And such are they who are successful.',NULL,30,38),
 (10573,1,'And whatever you lay out as usury, so that it may increase in the property of men, it shall not increase with Allah; and whatever you give in charity, desiring Allah''s pleasure-- it is these (persons) that shall get manifold.',NULL,30,39),
 (10574,2,'That which ye lay out for increase through the property of (other) people, will have no increase with Allah: but that which ye lay out for charity, seeking the Countenance of Allah, (will increase): it is these who will get a recompense multiplied.',NULL,30,39),
 (10575,3,'That which ye give in usury in order that it may increase on (other) people''s property hath no increase with Allah; but that which ye give in charity, seeking Allah''s Countenance, hath increase manifold.',NULL,30,39),
 (10576,1,'Allah is He Who created you, then gave you sustenance, then He causes you to die, then brings you to life. Is there any of your associate-gods who does aught of it? Glory be to Him, and exalted be He above what they associate (with Him).',NULL,30,40),
 (10577,2,'It is Allah Who has created you: further, He has provided for your sustenance; then He will cause you to die; and again He will give you life. Are there any of your (false) "Partners" who can do any single one of these things? Glory to Him! and high is He above the partners they attribute (to him)!',NULL,30,40),
 (10578,3,'Allah is He Who created you and then sustained you, then causeth you to die, then giveth life to you again. Is there any of your (so-called) partners (of Allah) that doeth aught of that? Praised and Exalted be He above what they associate (with Him)!',NULL,30,40),
 (10579,1,'Corruption has appeared in the land and the sea on account of what the hands of men have wrought, that He may make them taste a part of that which they have done, so that they may return.',NULL,30,41),
 (10580,2,'Mischief has appeared on land and sea because of (the meed) that the hands of men have earned, that (Allah) may give them a taste of some of their deeds: in order that they may turn back (from Evil).',NULL,30,41),
 (10581,3,'Corruption doth appear on land and sea because of (the evil) which men''s hands have done, that He may make them taste a part of that which they have done, in order that they may return.',NULL,30,41),
 (10582,1,'Say: Travel in the land, then see how was the end of those before; most of them were polytheists.',NULL,30,42),
 (10583,2,'Say: "Travel through the earth and see what was the end of those before (you): Most of them worshipped others besides Allah."',NULL,30,42),
 (10584,3,'Say (O Muhammad, to the disbelievers): Travel in the land, and see the nature of the consequence for those who were before you! Most of them were idolaters.',NULL,30,42),
 (10585,1,'Then turn thy face straight to the right religion before there come from Allah the day which cannot be averted; on that day they shall become separated.',NULL,30,43),
 (10586,2,'But set thou thy face to the right Religion before there come from Allah the Day which there is no chance of averting: on that Day shall men be divided (in two).',NULL,30,43),
 (10587,3,'So set thy purpose resolutely for the right religion, before the inevitable day cometh from Allah. On that day mankind will be sundered-',NULL,30,43),
 (10588,1,'Whoever disbelieves, he shall be responsible for his disbelief, and whoever does good, they prepare (good) for their own souls,',NULL,30,44),
 (10589,2,'Those who reject Faith will suffer from that rejection: and those who work righteousness will spread their couch (of repose) for themselves (in heaven):',NULL,30,44),
 (10590,3,'Whoso disbelieveth must (then) bear the consequences of his disbelief, while those who do right make provision for themselves -',NULL,30,44),
 (10591,1,'That He may reward those who believe and do good out of His grace; surely He does not love the unbelievers.',NULL,30,45),
 (10592,2,'That He may reward those who believe and work righteous deeds, out of his Bounty. For He loves not those who reject Faith.',NULL,30,45),
 (10593,3,'That He may reward out of His bounty those who believe and do good works. Lo! He loveth not the disbelievers (in His guidance).',NULL,30,45),
 (10594,1,'And one of His signs is that He sends forth the winds bearing good news, and that He may make your taste of His mercy, and that the ships may run by His command, and that you may seek of His grace, and that you may be grateful.',NULL,30,46),
 (10595,2,'Among His Signs is this, that He sends the Winds, as heralds of Glad Tidings, giving you a taste of His (Grace and) Mercy,- that the ships may sail (majestically) by His Command and that ye may seek of His Bounty: in order that ye may be grateful.',NULL,30,46),
 (10596,3,'And of His signs is this: He sendeth herald winds to make you taste His mercy, and that the ships may sail at His command, and that ye may seek his favour, and that haply ye may be thankful.',NULL,30,46),
 (10597,1,'And certainly We sent before you messengers to their people, so they came to them with clear arguments, then We gave the punishment to those who were guilty; and helping the believers is ever incumbent on Us.',NULL,30,47),
 (10598,2,'We did indeed send, before thee, messengers to their (respective) peoples, and they came to them with Clear Signs: then, to those who transgressed, We meted out Retribution: and it was due from Us to aid those who believed.',NULL,30,47),
 (10599,3,'Verily We sent before thee (Muhammad) messengers to their own folk. Then we took vengeance upon those who were guilty (in regard to them). To help believers is ever incumbent upon Us.',NULL,30,47),
 (10600,1,'Allah is he Who sends forth the winds so they raise a cloud, then He spreads it forth in the sky as He pleases, and He breaks it up so that you see the rain coming forth from inside it; then when He causes it to fall upon whom He pleases of His servants, lo! they are joyful',NULL,30,48),
 (10601,2,'It is Allah Who sends the Winds, and they raise the Clouds: then does He spread them in the sky as He wills, and break them into fragments, until thou seest rain-drops issue from the midst thereof: then when He has made them reach such of his servants as He wills behold, they do rejoice!-',NULL,30,48),
 (10602,3,'Allah is He Who sendeth the winds so that they raise clouds, and spreadeth them along the sky as pleaseth Him, and causeth them to break and thou seest the rain downpouring from within them. And when He maketh it to fall on whom He will of His bondmen, lo! they rejoice;',NULL,30,48),
 (10603,1,'Though they were before this, before it was sent down upon them, confounded in sure despair.',NULL,30,49),
 (10604,2,'Even though, before they received (the rain) - just before this - they were dumb with despair!',NULL,30,49),
 (10605,3,'Though before that, even before it was sent down upon them, they were in despair.',NULL,30,49),
 (10606,1,'Look then at the signs of Allah''s mercy, how He gives life to the earth after its death, most surely He will raise the dead to life; and He has power over all things.',NULL,30,50),
 (10607,2,'Then contemplate (O man!) the memorials of Allah''s Mercy!- how He gives life to the earth after its death: verily the same will give life to the men who are dead: for He has power over all things.',NULL,30,50),
 (10608,3,'Look, therefore, at the prints of Allah''s mercy (in creation): how He quickeneth the earth after her death. Lo! He verily is the Quickener of the Dead, and He is Able to do all things.',NULL,30,50),
 (10609,1,'And if We send a wind and they see it to be yellow, they would after that certainly continue to disbelieve',NULL,30,51),
 (10610,2,'And if We (but) send a Wind from which they see (their tilth) turn yellow,- behold, they become, thereafter, Ungrateful (Unbelievers)!',NULL,30,51),
 (10611,3,'And if We sent a wind and they beheld it yellow, they verily would still continue in their disbelief.',NULL,30,51),
 (10612,1,'For surely you cannot, make the dead to hear and you cannot make the deaf to hear the call, when they turn back and',NULL,30,52),
 (10613,2,'So verily thou canst not make the dead to hear, nor canst thou make the deaf to hear the call, when they show their backs and turn away.',NULL,30,52),
 (10614,3,'For verily thou (Muhammad) canst not make the dead to hear, nor canst thou make the deaf to hear the call when they have turned to flee.',NULL,30,52),
 (10615,1,'Nor can you lead away the blind out of their error. You cannot make to hear any but those who believe in Our communications so they shall submit.',NULL,30,53),
 (10616,2,'Nor canst thou lead back the blind from their straying: only those wilt thou make to hear, who believe in Our signs and submit (their wills in Islam).',NULL,30,53),
 (10617,3,'Nor canst thou guide the blind out of their error. Thou canst make none to hear save those who believe in Our revelations so that they surrender (unto Him).',NULL,30,53),
 (10618,1,'Allah is He Who created you from a state of weakness then He gave strength after weakness, then ordained weakness and hoary hair after strength; He creates what He pleases, and He is the Knowing, the Powerful.',NULL,30,54),
 (10619,2,'It is Allah Who created you in a state of (helpless) weakness, then gave (you) strength after weakness, then, after strength, gave (you weakness and a hoary head: He creates as He wills, and it is He Who has all knowledge and power.',NULL,30,54),
 (10620,3,'Allah is He Who shaped you out of weakness, then appointed after weakness strength, then, after strength, appointed weakness and grey hair. He createth what He will. He is the Knower, the Mighty.',NULL,30,54),
 (10621,1,'And at the time when the hour shall come, the guilty shall swear (that) they did not tarry but an hour; thus are they ever turned away.',NULL,30,55),
 (10622,2,'On the Day that the Hour (of Reckoning) will be established, the transgressors will swear that they tarried not but an hour: thus were they used to being deluded!',NULL,30,55),
 (10623,3,'And on the day when the Hour riseth the guilty will vow that they did tarry but an hour - thus were they ever deceived.',NULL,30,55),
 (10624,1,'And those who are given knowledge and faith will say: Certainly you tarried according to the ordinance of Allah till the day of resurrection, so this is the day of resurrection, but you did not know.',NULL,30,56),
 (10625,2,'But those endued with knowledge and faith will say: "Indeed ye did tarry, within Allah''s Decree, to the Day of Resurrection, and this is the Day of Resurrection: but ye - ye were not aware!"',NULL,30,56),
 (10626,3,'But those to whom knowledge and faith are given will say: The truth is, ye have tarried, by Allah''s decree, until the Day of Resurrection. This is the Day of Resurrection, but ye used not to know.',NULL,30,56),
 (10627,1,'But on that day their excuse shall not profit those who were unjust, nor shall they be regarded with goodwill.',NULL,30,57),
 (10628,2,'So on that Day no excuse of theirs will avail the transgressors, nor will they be invited (then) to seek grace (by repentance).',NULL,30,57),
 (10629,3,'In that day their excuses will not profit those who did injustice, nor will they be allowed to make amends.',NULL,30,57),
 (10630,1,'And certainly We have set forth for men every kind of example in this Quran; and if you should bring them a communication, those who disbelieve would certainly say: You are naught but false claimants.',NULL,30,58),
 (10631,2,'verily We have propounded for men, in this Qur''an every kind of Parable: But if thou bring to them any Sign, the Unbelievers are sure to say, "Ye do nothing but talk vanities."',NULL,30,58),
 (10632,3,'Verily We have coined for mankind in this Qur''an all kinds of similitudes; and indeed if thou camest unto them with a miracle, those who disbelieve would verily exclaim: Ye are but tricksters!',NULL,30,58),
 (10633,1,'Thus does Allah set a seal on the hearts of those who do not know.',NULL,30,59),
 (10634,2,'Thus does Allah seal up the hearts of those who understand not.',NULL,30,59),
 (10635,3,'Thus doth Allah seal the hearts of those who know not.',NULL,30,59),
 (10636,1,'Therefore be patient; surely the promise of Allah is true and let not those who have no certainty hold you in light estimation.',NULL,30,60),
 (10637,2,'So patiently persevere: for verily the promise of Allah is true: nor let those shake thy firmness, who have (themselves) no certainty of faith.',NULL,30,60),
 (10638,3,'So have patience (O Muhammad)! Allah''s promise is the very truth, and let not those who have no certainty make thee impatient.',NULL,30,60),
 (10639,1,'Alif Lam Mim.',NULL,31,1),
 (10640,2,'A. L. M.',NULL,31,1),
 (10641,3,'Alif. Lam. Mim.',NULL,31,1),
 (10642,1,'These are verses of the Book of Wisdom',NULL,31,2),
 (10643,2,'These are Verses of the Wise Book,-',NULL,31,2),
 (10644,3,'These are revelations of the wise Scripture,',NULL,31,2),
 (10645,1,'A guidance and a mercy for the doers of goodness,',NULL,31,3),
 (10646,2,'A Guide and a Mercy to the Doers of Good,-',NULL,31,3),
 (10647,3,'A guidance and a mercy for the good,',NULL,31,3),
 (10648,1,'Those who keep up prayer and pay the poor-rate and they are certain of the hereafter.',NULL,31,4),
 (10649,2,'Those who establish regular Prayer, and give regular Charity, and have (in their hearts) the assurance of the Hereafter.',NULL,31,4),
 (10650,3,'Those who establish worship and pay the poor-due and have sure faith in the Hereafter.',NULL,31,4),
 (10651,1,'These are on a guidance from their Lord, and these are they who are successful:',NULL,31,5),
 (10652,2,'These are on (true) guidance from their Lord: and these are the ones who will prosper.',NULL,31,5),
 (10653,3,'Such have guidance from their Lord. Such are the successful.',NULL,31,5),
 (10654,1,'And of men is he who takes instead frivolous discourse to lead astray from Allah''s path without knowledge, and to take it for a mockery; these shall have an abasing chastisement.',NULL,31,6),
 (10655,2,'But there are, among men, those who purchase idle tales, without knowledge (or meaning), to mislead (men) from the Path of Allah and throw ridicule (on the Path): for such there will be a Humiliating Penalty.',NULL,31,6),
 (10656,3,'And of mankind is he who payeth for mere pastime of discourse, that he may mislead from Allah''s way without knowledge, and maketh it the butt of mockery. For such there is a shameful doom.',NULL,31,6),
 (10657,1,'And when Our communications are recited to him, he turns back proudly, as if he had not heard them, as though in his ears were a heaviness, therefore announce to him a painful chastisement.',NULL,31,7),
 (10658,2,'When Our Signs are rehearsed to such a one, he turns away in arrogance, as if he heard them not, as if there were deafness in both his ears: announce to him a grievous Penalty.',NULL,31,7),
 (10659,3,'And when Our revelations are recited unto him he turneth away in pride as if he heard them not, as if there were a deafness in his ears. So give him tidings of a painful doom.',NULL,31,7),
 (10660,1,'(As for) those who believe and do good, they shall surely have gardens of bliss,',NULL,31,8),
 (10661,2,'For those who believe and work righteous deeds, there will be Gardens of Bliss,-',NULL,31,8),
 (10662,3,'Lo! those who believe and do good works, for them are the gardens of delight,',NULL,31,8),
 (10663,1,'Abiding in them; the promise of Allah; (a) true (promise), and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,31,9),
 (10664,2,'To dwell therein. The promise of Allah is true: and He is Exalted in Power, Wise.',NULL,31,9),
 (10665,3,'Wherein they will abide. It is a promise of Allah in truth. He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,31,9),
 (10666,1,'He created the heavens without pillars as you see them, and put mountains upon the earth lest it might convulse with you, and He spread in it animals of every kind; and We sent down water from the cloud, then caused to grow therein (vegetation) of every noble kind.',NULL,31,10),
 (10667,2,'He created the heavens without any pillars that ye can see; He set on the earth mountains standing firm, lest it should shake with you; and He scattered through it beasts of all kinds. We send down rain from the sky, and produce on the earth every kind of noble creature, in pairs.',NULL,31,10),
 (10668,3,'He hath created the heavens without supports that ye can see, and hath cast into the earth firm hills, so that it quake not with you; and He hath dispersed therein all kinds of beasts. And We send down water from the sky and We cause (plants) of every goodly kind to grow therein.',NULL,31,10),
 (10669,1,'This is Allah''s creation, but show Me what those besides Him have created. Nay, the unjust are in manifest error',NULL,31,11),
 (10670,2,'Such is the Creation of Allah: now show Me what is there that others besides Him have created: nay, but the Transgressors are in manifest error.',NULL,31,11),
 (10671,3,'This is the Creation of Allah. Now show me that which those (ye worship) beside Him have created. Nay, but the wrong-doers are in error manifest!',NULL,31,11),
 (10672,1,'And certainly We gave wisdom to Luqman, saying: Be grateful to Allah. And whoever is grateful, he is on!y grateful for his own soul; and whoever is ungrateful, then surely Allah is Self-sufficient, Praised.',NULL,31,12),
 (10673,2,'we bestowed (in the past) Wisdom on Luqman: "Show (thy) gratitude to Allah." Any who is (so) grateful does so to the profit of his own soul: but if any is ungrateful, verily Allah is free of all wants, Worthy of all praise.',NULL,31,12),
 (10674,3,'And verily We gave Luqman wisdom, saying: Give thanks unto Allah; and whosoever giveth thanks, he giveth thanks for (the good of) his soul. And whosoever refuseth - Lo! Allah is Absolute, Owner of Praise.',NULL,31,12),
 (10675,1,'And when Luqman said to his son while he admonished him: O my son! do not associate aught with Allah; most surely polytheism is a grievous iniquity--',NULL,31,13),
 (10676,2,'Behold, Luqman said to his son by way of instruction: "O my son! join not in worship (others) with Allah: for false worship is indeed the highest wrong-doing."',NULL,31,13),
 (10677,3,'And (remember) when Luqman said unto his son, when he was exhorting him: O my dear son! Ascribe no partners unto Allah. Lo! to ascribe partners (unto Him) is a tremendous wrong -',NULL,31,13),
 (10678,1,'And We have enjoined man in respect of his parents-- his mother bears him with faintings upon faintings and his weaning takes two years-- saying: Be grateful to Me and to both your parents; to Me is the eventual coming.',NULL,31,14),
 (10679,2,'And We have enjoined on man (to be good) to his parents: in travail upon travail did his mother bear him, and in years twain was his weaning: (hear the command), "Show gratitude to Me and to thy parents: to Me is (thy final) Goal.',NULL,31,14),
 (10680,3,'And We have enjoined upon man concerning his partners - His mother beareth him in weakness upon weakness, and his weaning is in two years - Give thanks unto Me and unto thy parents. Unto Me is the journeying.',NULL,31,14),
 (10681,1,'And if they contend with you that you should associate with Me what you have no knowledge of, do not obey them, and keep company with them in this world kindly, and follow the way of him who turns to Me, then to Me is your return, then will I inform you of what you did--',NULL,31,15),
 (10682,2,'"But if they strive to make thee join in worship with Me things of which thou hast no knowledge, obey them not; yet bear them company in this life with justice (and consideration), and follow the way of those who turn to me (in love): in the end the return of you all is to Me, and I will tell you the truth (and meaning) of all that ye did."',NULL,31,15),
 (10683,3,'But if they strive with thee to make thee ascribe unto Me as partner that of which thou hast no knowledge, then obey them not. Consort with them in the world kindly, and follow the path of him who repenteth unto Me. Then unto Me will be your return, and I shall tell you what ye used to do -',NULL,31,15),
 (10684,1,'O my son! surely if it is the very weight of the grain of a mustard-seed, even though it is in (the heart of) rock, or (high above) in the heaven or (deep down) in the earth, Allah will bring it (to light); surely Allah is Knower of subtleties, Aware;',NULL,31,16),
 (10685,2,'"O my son!" (said Luqman), "If there be (but) the weight of a mustard-seed and it were (hidden) in a rock, or (anywhere) in the heavens or on earth, Allah will bring it forth: for Allah understands the finest mysteries, (and) is well-acquainted (with them).',NULL,31,16),
 (10686,3,'O my dear son! Lo! though it be but the weight of a grain of mustard-seed, and though it be in a rock, or in the heavens, or in the earth, Allah will bring it forth. Lo! Allah is Subtile, Aware.',NULL,31,16),
 (10687,1,'O my son! keep up prayer and enjoin the good and forbid the evil, and bear patiently that which befalls you; surely these acts require courage;',NULL,31,17),
 (10688,2,'"O my son! establish regular prayer, enjoin what is just, and forbid what is wrong: and bear with patient constancy whatever betide thee; for this is firmness (of purpose) in (the conduct of) affairs.',NULL,31,17),
 (10689,3,'O my dear son! Establish worship and enjoin kindness and forbid iniquity, and persevere whatever may befall thee. Lo! that is of the steadfast heart of things.',NULL,31,17),
 (10690,1,'And do not turn your face away from people in contempt, nor go about in the land exulting overmuch; surely Allah does not love any self-conceited boaster;',NULL,31,18),
 (10691,2,'"And swell not thy cheek (for pride) at men, nor walk in insolence through the earth; for Allah loveth not any arrogant boaster.',NULL,31,18),
 (10692,3,'Turn not thy cheek in scorn toward folk, nor walk with pertness in the land. Lo! Allah loveth not each braggart boaster.',NULL,31,18),
 (10693,1,'And pursue the right course in your going about and lower your voice; surely the most hateful of voices is braying of the asses.',NULL,31,19),
 (10694,2,'"And be moderate in thy pace, and lower thy voice; for the harshest of sounds without doubt is the braying of the ass."',NULL,31,19),
 (10695,3,'Be modest in thy bearing and subdue thy voice. Lo! the harshest of all voices is the voice of the ass.',NULL,31,19),
 (10696,1,'Do you not see that Allah has made what is in the heavens and what is in the earth subservient to you, and made complete to you His favors outwardly and inwardly? And among men is he who disputes in respect of Allah though having no knowledge nor guidance, nor a book giving light.',NULL,31,20),
 (10697,2,'Do ye not see that Allah has subjected to your (use) all things in the heavens and on earth, and has made his bounties flow to you in exceeding measure, (both) seen and unseen? Yet there are among men those who dispute about Allah, without knowledge and without guidance, and without a Book to enlighten them!',NULL,31,20),
 (10698,3,'See ye not how Allah hath made serviceable unto you whatsoever is in the skies and whatsoever is in the earth and hath loaded you with His favours both without and within? Yet of mankind is he who disputeth concerning Allah, without knowledge or guidance or a scripture giving light.',NULL,31,20),
 (10699,1,'And when it is said to them: Follow what Allah has revealed, they say: Nay, we follow that on which we found our fathers. What! though the Shaitan calls them to the chastisement of the burning fire!',NULL,31,21),
 (10700,2,'When they are told to follow the (Revelation) that Allah has sent down, they say: "Nay, we shall follow the ways that we found our fathers (following). "What! even if it is Satan beckoning them to the Penalty of the (Blazing) Fire?',NULL,31,21),
 (10701,3,'And if it be said unto them: Follow that which Allah hath revealed, they say: Nay, but we follow that wherein we found our fathers. What! Even though the devil were inviting them unto the doom of flame?',NULL,31,21),
 (10702,1,'And whoever submits himself wholly to Allah and he is the doer of good (to others), he indeed has taken hold of the firmest thing upon which one can lay hold; and Allah''s is the end of affairs.',NULL,31,22),
 (10703,2,'Whoever submits his whole self to Allah, and is a doer of good, has grasped indeed the most trustworthy hand-hold: and with Allah rests the End and Decision of (all) affairs.',NULL,31,22),
 (10704,3,'Whosoever surrendereth his purpose to Allah while doing good, he verily hath grasped the firm hand-hold. Unto Allah belongeth the sequel of all things.',NULL,31,22),
 (10705,1,'And whoever disbelieves, let not his disbelief grieve you; to Us is their return, then will We inform them of what they did surely Allah is the Knower of what is in the breasts.',NULL,31,23),
 (10706,2,'But if any reject Faith, let not his rejection grieve thee: to Us is their return, and We shall tell them the truth of their deeds: for Allah knows well all that is in (men''s) hearts.',NULL,31,23),
 (10707,3,'And whosoever disbelieveth, let not his disbelief afflict thee (O Muhammad). Unto Us is their return, and We shall tell them what they did. Lo! Allah is Aware of what is in the breasts (of men).',NULL,31,23),
 (10708,1,'We give them to enjoy a little, then will We drive them to a severe chastisement.',NULL,31,24),
 (10709,2,'We grant them their pleasure for a little while: in the end shall We drive them to a chastisement unrelenting.',NULL,31,24),
 (10710,3,'We give them comfort for a little, and then We drive them to a heavy doom.',NULL,31,24),
 (10711,1,'And if you ask them who created the heavens and the earth, they will certainly say: Allah. Say: (All) praise is due to Allah; nay! most of them do not know.',NULL,31,25),
 (10712,2,'If thou ask them, who it is that created the heavens and the earth. They will certainly say, "Allah". Say: "Praise be to Allah!" But most of them understand not.',NULL,31,25),
 (10713,3,'If thou shouldst ask them: Who created the heavens and the earth? they would answer: Allah. Say: Praise be to Allah! But most of them know not.',NULL,31,25),
 (10714,1,'What is in the heavens and the earth is Allah''s; surely Allah is the Self-sufficient, the Praised.',NULL,31,26),
 (10715,2,'To Allah belong all things in heaven and earth: verily Allah is He (that is) free of all wants, worthy of all praise.',NULL,31,26),
 (10716,3,'Unto Allah belongeth whatsoever is in the heavens and the earth. Lo! Allah, He is the Absolute, the Owner of Praise.',NULL,31,26),
 (10717,1,'And were every tree that is in the earth (made into) pens and the sea (to supply it with ink), with seven more seas to increase it, the words of Allah would not come to an end; surely Allah is Mighty, Wise.',NULL,31,27),
 (10718,2,'And if all the trees on earth were pens and the ocean (were ink), with seven oceans behind it to add to its (supply), yet would not the words of Allah be exhausted (in the writing): for Allah is Exalted in Power, full of Wisdom.',NULL,31,27),
 (10719,3,'And if all the trees in the earth were pens, and the sea, with seven more seas to help it, (were ink), the words of Allah could not be exhausted. Lo! Allah is Mighty, Wise.',NULL,31,27),
 (10720,1,'Neither your creation nor your raising is anything but as a single soul; surely Allah is Hearing, Seeing.',NULL,31,28),
 (10721,2,'And your creation or your resurrection is in no wise but as an individual soul: for Allah is He Who hears and sees (all things).',NULL,31,28),
 (10722,3,'Your creation and your raising (from the dead) are only as (the creation and the raising of) a single soul. Lo! Allah is Hearer, Knower.',NULL,31,28),
 (10723,1,'Do you not see that Allah makes the night to enter into the day, and He makes the day to enter into the night, and He has made the sun and the moon subservient (to you); each pursues its course till an appointed time; and that Allah is Aware of what you do?',NULL,31,29),
 (10724,2,'Seest thou not that Allah merges Night into Day and he merges Day into Night; that He has subjected the sun, and the moon (to his Law), each running its course for a term appointed; and that Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do?',NULL,31,29),
 (10725,3,'Hast thou not seen how Allah causeth the night to pass into the day and causeth the day to pass into the night, and hath subdued the sun and the moon (to do their work), each running unto an appointed term; and that Allah is Informed of what ye do?',NULL,31,29),
 (10726,1,'This is because Allah is the Truth, and that which they call upon besides Him is the falsehood, and that Allah is the High, the Great.',NULL,31,30),
 (10727,2,'That is because Allah is the (only) Reality, and because whatever else they invoke besides Him is Falsehood; and because Allah,- He is the Most High, Most Great.',NULL,31,30),
 (10728,3,'That (is so) because Allah, He is the True, and that which they invoke beside Him is the False, and because Allah, He is the Sublime, the Great.',NULL,31,30),
 (10729,1,'Do you not see that the ships run on in the sea by Allah''s favor that He may show you of His signs? Most surely there are signs in this for every patient endurer, grateful one.',NULL,31,31),
 (10730,2,'Seest thou not that the ships sail through the ocean by the Grace of Allah?- that He may show you of His Signs? Verily in this are Signs for all who constantly persevere and give thanks.',NULL,31,31),
 (10731,3,'Hast thou not seen how the ships glide on the sea by Allah''s grace, that He may show you of His wonders? Lo! therein indeed are portents for every steadfast, grateful (heart).',NULL,31,31),
 (10732,1,'And when a wave like mountains covers them they call upon Allah, being sincere to Him in obedience, but when He brings them safe to the land, some of them follow the middle course; and none denies Our signs but every perfidious, ungrateful one.',NULL,31,32),
 (10733,2,'When a wave covers them like the canopy (of clouds), they call to Allah, offering Him sincere devotion. But when He has delivered them safely to land, there are among them those that halt between (right and wrong). But none reject Our Signs except only a perfidious ungrateful (wretch)!',NULL,31,32),
 (10734,3,'And if a wave enshroudeth them like awnings, they cry unto Allah, making their faith pure for Him only. But when He bringeth them safe to land, some of them compromise. None denieth Our signs save every traitor ingrate.',NULL,31,32),
 (10735,1,'O people! guard against (the punishment of) your Lord and dread the day when a father shall not make any satisfaction for his son, nor shall the child be the maker of any satisfaction for his father; surely the promise of Allah is true, therefore let not this world''s life deceive you, nor let the archdeceiver deceive you in respect of Allah.',NULL,31,33),
 (10736,2,'O mankind! do your duty to your Lord, and fear (the coming of) a Day when no father can avail aught for his son, nor a son avail aught for his father. Verily, the promise of Allah is true: let not then this present life deceive you, nor let the chief Deceiver deceive you about Allah.',NULL,31,33),
 (10737,3,'O mankind! Keep your duty to your Lord and fear a Day when the parent will not be able to avail the child in aught, nor the child to avail the parent. Lo! Allah''s promise is the very truth. Let not the life of the world beguile you, nor let the deceiver beguile you, in regard to Allah.',NULL,31,33),
 (10738,1,'Surely Allah is He with Whom is the knowledge of the hour, and He sends down the rain and He knows what is in the wombs; and no one knows what he shall earn on the morrow; and no one knows in what land he shall die; surely Allah is Knowing, Aware.',NULL,31,34),
 (10739,2,'Verily the knowledge of the Hour is with Allah (alone). It is He Who sends down rain, and He Who knows what is in the wombs. Nor does any one know what it is that he will earn on the morrow: Nor does any one know in what land he is to die. Verily with Allah is full knowledge and He is acquainted (with all things).',NULL,31,34),
 (10740,3,'Lo! Allah! With Him is knowledge of the Hour. He sendeth down the rain, and knoweth that which is in the wombs. No soul knoweth what it will earn to-morrow, and no soul knoweth in what land it will die. Lo! Allah is Knower, Aware.',NULL,31,34),
 (10741,1,'Alif Lam Mim.',NULL,32,1),
 (10742,2,'A. L. M.',NULL,32,1),
 (10743,3,'Alif. Lam. Mim',NULL,32,1),
 (10744,1,'The revelation of the Book, there is no doubt in it, is from the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,32,2),
 (10745,2,'(This is) the Revelation of the Book in which there is no doubt,- from the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,32,2),
 (10746,3,'The revelation of the Scripture whereof there is no doubt is from the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,32,2),
 (10747,1,'Or do they say: He has forged it? Nay! it is the truth from your Lord that you may warn a people to whom no warner has come before you, that they may follow the right direction.',NULL,32,3),
 (10748,2,'Or do they say, "He has forged it"? Nay, it is the Truth from thy Lord, that thou mayest admonish a people to whom no warner has come before thee: in order that they may receive guidance.',NULL,32,3),
 (10749,3,'Or say they: He hath invented it? Nay, but it is the Truth from thy Lord, that thou mayst warn a folk to whom no warner came before thee, that haply they may walk aright.',NULL,32,3),
 (10750,1,'Allah is He Who created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six periods, and He mounted the throne (of authority); you have not besides Him any guardian or any intercessor, will you not then mind?',NULL,32,4),
 (10751,2,'It is Allah Who has created the heavens and the earth, and all between them, in six Days, and is firmly established on the Throne (of Authority): ye have none, besides Him, to protect or intercede (for you): will ye not then receive admonition?',NULL,32,4),
 (10752,3,'Allah it is Who created the heavens and the earth, and that which is between them, in six Days. Then He mounted the Throne. Ye have not, beside Him, a protecting friend or mediator. Will ye not then remember?',NULL,32,4),
 (10753,1,'He regulates the affair from the heaven to the earth; then shall it ascend to Him in a day the measure of which is a thousand years of what you count.',NULL,32,5),
 (10754,2,'He rules (all) affairs from the heavens to the earth: in the end will (all affairs) go up to Him, on a Day, the space whereof will be (as) a thousand years of your reckoning.',NULL,32,5),
 (10755,3,'He directeth the ordinance from the heaven unto the earth; then it ascendeth unto Him in a Day, whereof the measure is a thousand years of that ye reckon.',NULL,32,5),
 (10756,1,'This is the Knower of the unseen and the seen, the Mighty the Merciful,',NULL,32,6),
 (10757,2,'Such is He, the Knower of all things, hidden and open, the Exalted (in power), the Merciful;-',NULL,32,6),
 (10758,3,'Such is the Knower of the Invisible and the Visible, the Mighty, the Merciful,',NULL,32,6),
 (10759,1,'Who made good everything that He has created, and He began the creation of man from dust.',NULL,32,7),
 (10760,2,'He Who has made everything which He has created most good: He began the creation of man with (nothing more than) clay,',NULL,32,7),
 (10761,3,'Who made all things good which He created, and He began the creation of man from clay;',NULL,32,7),
 (10762,1,'Then He made his progeny of an extract, of water held in light estimation.',NULL,32,8),
 (10763,2,'And made his progeny from a quintessence of the nature of a fluid despised:',NULL,32,8),
 (10764,3,'Then He made his seed from a draught of despised fluid;',NULL,32,8),
 (10765,1,'Then He made him complete and breathed into him of His spirit, and made for you the ears and the eyes and the hearts; little is it that you give thanks.',NULL,32,9),
 (10766,2,'But He fashioned him in due proportion, and breathed into him something of His spirit. And He gave you (the faculties of) hearing and sight and feeling (and understanding): little thanks do ye give!',NULL,32,9),
 (10767,3,'Then He fashioned him and breathed into him of His Spirit; and appointed for you hearing and sight and hearts. Small thanks give ye!',NULL,32,9),
 (10768,1,'And they say: What! when we have become lost in the earth, shall we then certainly be in a new creation? Nay! they are disbelievers in the meeting of their Lord.',NULL,32,10),
 (10769,2,'And they say: "What! when we lie, hidden and lost, in the earth, shall we indeed be in a Creation renewed? Nay, they deny the Meeting with their Lord.',NULL,32,10),
 (10770,3,'And they say: When we are lost in the earth, how can we then be re-created? Nay but they are disbelievers in the meeting with their Lord.',NULL,32,10),
 (10771,1,'Say: The angel of death who is given charge of you shall cause you to die, then to your Lord you shall be brought back.',NULL,32,11),
 (10772,2,'Say: "The Angel of Death, put in charge of you, will (duly) take your souls: then shall ye be brought back to your Lord."',NULL,32,11),
 (10773,3,'Say: The angel of death, who hath charge concerning you, will gather you, and afterward unto your Lord ye will be returned.',NULL,32,11),
 (10774,1,'And could you but see when the guilty shall hang down their heads before their Lord: Our Lord! we have seen and we have heard, therefore send us back, we will do good; surely (now) we are certain.',NULL,32,12),
 (10775,2,'If only thou couldst see when the guilty ones will bend low their heads before their Lord, (saying:) "Our Lord! We have seen and we have heard: Now then send us back (to the world): we will work righteousness: for we do indeed (now) believe."',NULL,32,12),
 (10776,3,'Couldst thou but see when the guilty hang their heads before their Lord, (and say): Our Lord! We have now seen and heard, so send us back; we will do right, now we are sure.',NULL,32,12),
 (10777,1,'And if We had pleased We would certainly have given to every soul its guidance, but the word (which had gone forth) from Me was just: I will certainly fill hell with the jinn and men together.',NULL,32,13),
 (10778,2,'If We had so willed, We could certainly have brought every soul its true guidance: but the Word from Me will come true, "I will fill Hell with Jinns and men all together."',NULL,32,13),
 (10779,3,'And if We had so willed, We could have given every soul its guidance, but the word from Me concerning evildoers took effect: that I will fill hell with the jinn and mankind together.',NULL,32,13),
 (10780,1,'So taste, because you neglected the meeting of this day of yours; surely We forsake you; and taste the abiding chastisement for what you did.',NULL,32,14),
 (10781,2,'"Taste ye then - for ye forgot the Meeting of this Day of yours, and We too will forget you - taste ye the Penalty of Eternity for your (evil) deeds!"',NULL,32,14),
 (10782,3,'So taste (the evil of your deeds). Forasmuch as ye forgot the meeting of this your day, lo! We forget you. Taste the doom of immortality because of what ye used to do.',NULL,32,14),
 (10783,1,'Only they believe in Our communications who, when they are reminded of them, fall down in prostration and celebrate the praise of their Lord, and they are not proud.',NULL,32,15),
 (10784,2,'Only those believe in Our Signs, who, when they are recited to them, fall down in prostration, and celebrate the praises of their Lord, nor are they (ever) puffed up with pride.',NULL,32,15),
 (10785,3,'Only those believe in Our revelations who, when they are reminded of them, fall down prostrate and hymn the praise of their Lord, and they are not scornful,',NULL,32,15),
 (10786,1,'Their sides draw away from (their) beds, they call upon their Lord in fear and in hope, and they spend (benevolently) out of what We have given them.',NULL,32,16),
 (10787,2,'Their limbs do forsake their beds of sleep, the while they call on their Lord, in Fear and Hope: and they spend (in charity) out of the sustenance which We have bestowed on them.',NULL,32,16),
 (10788,3,'Who forsake their beds to cry unto their Lord in fear and hope, and spend of that We have bestowed on them.',NULL,32,16),
 (10789,1,'So no soul knows what is hidden for them of that which will refresh the eyes; a reward for what they did.',NULL,32,17),
 (10790,2,'Now no person knows what delights of the eye are kept hidden (in reserve) for them - as a reward for their (good) deeds.',NULL,32,17),
 (10791,3,'No soul knoweth what is kept hid for them of joy, as a reward for what they used to do.',NULL,32,17),
 (10792,1,'Is he then who is a believer like him who is a transgressor? They are not equal.',NULL,32,18),
 (10793,2,'Is then the man who believes no better than the man who is rebellious and wicked? Not equal are they.',NULL,32,18),
 (10794,3,'Is he who is a believer like unto him who is an evil-liver? They are not alike.',NULL,32,18),
 (10795,1,'As for those who believe and do good, the gardens are their abiding-place; an entertainment for what they did.',NULL,32,19),
 (10796,2,'For those who believe and do righteous deeds are Gardens as hospitable homes, for their (good) deeds.',NULL,32,19),
 (10797,3,'But as for those who believe and do good works, for them are the Gardens of Retreat - a welcome (in reward) for what they used to do.',NULL,32,19),
 (10798,1,'And as for those who transgress, their abode is the fire; whenever they desire to go forth from it they shall be brought back into it, and it will be said to them: Taste the chastisement of the fire which you called a lie.',NULL,32,20),
 (10799,2,'As to those who are rebellious and wicked, their abode will be the Fire: every time they wish to get away therefrom, they will be forced thereinto, and it will be said to them: "Taste ye the Penalty of the Fire, the which ye were wont to reject as false."',NULL,32,20),
 (10800,3,'And as for those who do evil, their retreat is the Fire. Whenever they desire to issue forth from thence, they are brought back thither. Unto them it is said: Taste the torment of the Fire which ye used to deny.',NULL,32,20),
 (10801,1,'And most certainly We will make them taste of the nearer chastisement before the greater chastisement that haply they may turn.',NULL,32,21),
 (10802,2,'And indeed We will make them taste of the Penalty of this (life) prior to the supreme Penalty, in order that they may (repent and) return.',NULL,32,21),
 (10803,3,'And verily We make them taste the lower punishment before the greater, that haply they may return.',NULL,32,21),
 (10804,1,'And who is more unjust than he who is reminded of the communications of his Lord, then he turns away from them? Surely We will give punishment to the guilty.',NULL,32,22),
 (10805,2,'And who does more wrong than one to whom are recited the Signs of his Lord, and who then turns away therefrom? Verily from those who transgress We shall exact (due) Retribution.',NULL,32,22),
 (10806,3,'And who doth greater wrong than he who is reminded of the revelations of his Lord, then turneth from them. Lo! We shall requite the guilty.',NULL,32,22),
 (10807,1,'And certainly We gave the Book to Musa, so be not in doubt concerning the receiving of it, and We made it a guide for the children of Israel.',NULL,32,23),
 (10808,2,'We did indeed aforetime give the Book to Moses: be not then in doubt of its reaching (thee): and We made it a guide to the Children of Israel.',NULL,32,23),
 (10809,3,'We verily gave Moses the Scripture; so be not ye in doubt of his receiving it; and We appointed it a guidance for the Children of Israel.',NULL,32,23),
 (10810,1,'And We made of them Imams to guide by Our command when they were patient, and they were certain of Our communications.',NULL,32,24),
 (10811,2,'And We appointed, from among them, leaders, giving guidance under Our command, so long as they persevered with patience and continued to have faith in Our Signs.',NULL,32,24),
 (10812,3,'And when they became steadfast and believed firmly in Our revelations, We appointed from among them leaders who guided by Our command.',NULL,32,24),
 (10813,1,'Surely your Lord will judge between them on the day of resurrection concerning that wherein they differ.',NULL,32,25),
 (10814,2,'Verily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Judgment, in the matters wherein they differ (among themselves)',NULL,32,25),
 (10815,3,'Lo! thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that wherein they used to differ.',NULL,32,25),
 (10816,1,'Does it not point out to them the right way, how many of the generations, in whose abodes they go about, did We destroy before them? Most surely there are signs in this; will they not then hear?',NULL,32,26),
 (10817,2,'Does it not teach them a lesson, how many generations We destroyed before them, in whose dwellings they (now) go to and fro? Verily in that are Signs: Do they not then listen?',NULL,32,26),
 (10818,3,'Is it not a guidance for them (to observe) how many generations We destroyed before them, amid whose dwelling places they do walk? Lo! therein verily are portents! Will they not then heed?',NULL,32,26),
 (10819,1,'Do they not see that We drive the water to a land having no herbage, then We bring forth thereby seed-produce of which their cattle and they themselves eat; will they not then see?',NULL,32,27),
 (10820,2,'And do they not see that We do drive rain to parched soil (bare of herbage), and produce therewith crops, providing food for their cattle and themselves? Have they not the vision?',NULL,32,27),
 (10821,3,'Have they not seen how We lead the water to the barren land and therewith bring forth crops whereof their cattle eat, and they themselves? Will they not then see?',NULL,32,27),
 (10822,1,'And they say: When will this judgment take place, If you are truthful?',NULL,32,28),
 (10823,2,'They say: "When will this decision be, if ye are telling the truth?"',NULL,32,28),
 (10824,3,'And they say: When cometh this victory (of yours) if ye are truthful?',NULL,32,28),
 (10825,1,'Say: On the day of judgment the faith of those who (now) disbelieve will not profit them, nor will they be respited.',NULL,32,29),
 (10826,2,'Say: "On the Day of Decision, no profit will it be to Unbelievers if they (then) believe! nor will they be granted a respite."',NULL,32,29),
 (10827,3,'Say (unto them): On the day of the victory the faith of those who disbelieve (and who then will believe) will not avail them, neither will they be reprieved.',NULL,32,29),
 (10828,1,'Therefore turn away from them and wait, surely they too are waiting.',NULL,32,30),
 (10829,2,'So turn away from them, and wait: they too are waiting.',NULL,32,30),
 (10830,3,'So withdraw from them (O Muhammad), and await (the event). Lo! they (also) are awaiting (it).',NULL,32,30),
 (10831,1,'(All) praise is due to Allah, Whose is what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and to Him is due (all) praise in the hereafter; and He is the Wise, the Aware.',NULL,34,1),
 (10832,2,'Praise be to Allah, to Whom belong all things in the heavens and on earth: to Him be Praise in the Hereafter: and He is Full of Wisdom, acquainted with all things.',NULL,34,1),
 (10833,3,'Praise be to Allah, unto Whom belongeth whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth. His is the praise in the Hereafter, and He is the Wise, the Aware.',NULL,34,1),
 (10834,1,'He knows that which goes down into the earth and that which comes out of it, and that which comes down from the heaven and that which goes up to it; and He is the Merciful, the Forgiving.',NULL,34,2),
 (10835,2,'He knows all that goes into the earth, and all that comes out thereof; all that comes down from the sky and all that ascends thereto and He is the Most Merciful, the Oft-Forgiving.',NULL,34,2),
 (10836,3,'He knoweth that which goeth into the earth and that which cometh forth from it, and that descendeth from the heaven and that which ascendeth into it. He is the Merciful, the Forgiving.',NULL,34,2),
 (10837,1,'And those who disbelieve say: The hour shall not come upon us. Say: Yea! by my Lord, the Knower of the unseen, it shall certainly come upon you; not the weight of an atom becomes absent from Him, in the heavens or in the earth, and neither less than that nor greater, but (all) is in a clear book',NULL,34,3),
 (10838,2,'The Unbelievers say, "Never to us will come the Hour": Say, "Nay! but most surely, by my Lord, it will come upon you;- by Him Who knows the unseen,- from Whom is not hidden the least little atom in the heavens or on earth: Nor is there anything less than that, or greater, but is in the Record Perspicuous:',NULL,34,3),
 (10839,3,'Those who disbelieve say: The Hour will never come unto us. Say: Nay, by my Lord, but it is coming unto you surely. (He is) the Knower of the Unseen. Not an atom''s weight, or less than that or greater, escapeth Him in the heavens or in the earth, but it is in a clear Record,',NULL,34,3),
 (10840,1,'That He may reward those who believe and do good; these it is for whom is forgiveness and an honorable sustenance.',NULL,34,4),
 (10841,2,'That He may reward those who believe and work deeds of righteousness: for such is Forgiveness and a Sustenance Most Generous."',NULL,34,4),
 (10842,3,'That He may reward those who believe and do good works. For them is pardon and a rich provision.',NULL,34,4),
 (10843,1,'And (as for) those who strive hard in opposing Our communications, these it is for whom is a painful chastisement of an evil kind.',NULL,34,5),
 (10844,2,'But those who strive against Our Signs, to frustrate them,- for such will be a Penalty,- a Punishment most humiliating.',NULL,34,5),
 (10845,3,'But those who strive against Our revelations, challenging (Us), theirs will be a painful doom of wrath.',NULL,34,5),
 (10846,1,'And those to whom the knowledge has been given see that which has been revealed to you from your Lord, that is the truth, and it guides into the path of the Mighty, the Praised.',NULL,34,6),
 (10847,2,'And those to whom knowledge has come see that the (Revelation) sent down to thee from thy Lord - that is the Truth, and that it guides to the Path of the Exalted (in might), Worthy of all praise.',NULL,34,6),
 (10848,3,'Those who have been given knowledge see that what is revealed unto thee from thy Lord is the truth and leadeth unto the path of the Mighty, the Owner of Praise.',NULL,34,6),
 (10849,1,'And those who disbelieve say: Shall we point out to you a man who informs you that when you are scattered the utmost scattering you shall then be most surely (raised) in (to) a new creation?',NULL,34,7),
 (10850,2,'The Unbelievers say (in ridicule): "Shall we point out to you a man that will tell you, when ye are all scattered to pieces in disintegration, that ye shall (then be raised) in a New Creation?',NULL,34,7),
 (10851,3,'Those who disbelieve say: Shall we show you a man who will tell you (that) when ye have become dispersed in dust with most complete dispersal still, even then, ye will be created anew?',NULL,34,7),
 (10852,1,'He has forged a lie against Allah or there is madness in him. Nay! those who do not believe in the hereafter are in torment and in great error.',NULL,34,8),
 (10853,2,'"Has he invented a falsehood against Allah, or has a spirit (seized) him?"- Nay, it is those who believe not in the Hereafter, that are in (real) Penalty, and in farthest error.',NULL,34,8),
 (10854,3,'Hath he invented a lie concerning Allah, or is there in him a madness? Nay, but those who disbelieve in the Hereafter are in torment and far error.',NULL,34,8),
 (10855,1,'Do they not then consider what is before them and what is behind them of the heaven and the earth? If We please We will make them disappear in the land or bring down upon them a portion from the heaven; most surely there is a sign in this for every servant turning (to Allah).',NULL,34,9),
 (10856,2,'See they not what is before them and behind them, of the sky and the earth? If We wished, We could cause the earth to swallow them up, or cause a piece of the sky to fall upon them. Verily in this is a Sign for every devotee that turns to Allah (in repentance).',NULL,34,9),
 (10857,3,'Have they not observed what is before them and what is behind them of the sky and the earth? If We will, We can make the earth swallow them, or cause obliteration from the sky to fall on them. Lo! herein surely is a portent for every slave who turneth (to Allah) repentant.',NULL,34,9),
 (10858,1,'And certainly We gave to Dawood excellence from Us: O mountains! sing praises with him, and the birds; and We made the iron pliant to him,',NULL,34,10),
 (10859,2,'We bestowed Grace aforetime on David from ourselves: "O ye Mountains! Sing ye back the Praises of Allah with him! and ye birds (also)! And We made the iron soft for him;-',NULL,34,10),
 (10860,3,'And assuredly We gave David grace from Us, (saying): O ye hills and birds, echo his psalms of praise! And We made the iron supple unto him,',NULL,34,10),
 (10861,1,'Saying: Make ample (coats of mail), and assign a time to the making of coats of mail and do good; surely I am Seeing what you do.',NULL,34,11),
 (10862,2,'(Commanding), "Make thou coast of mail, balancing well the rings of chain armour, and work ye righteousness; for be sure I see (clearly) all that ye do."',NULL,34,11),
 (10863,3,'Saying: Make thou long coats of mail and measure the links (thereof). And do ye right. Lo! I am Seer of what ye do.',NULL,34,11),
 (10864,1,'And (We made) the wind (subservient) to Sulaiman, which made a month''s journey in the morning and a month''s journey m the evening, and We made a fountain of molten copper to flow out for him, and of the jinn there were those who worked before him by the command of his Lord; and whoever turned aside from Our command from among them, We made him taste of the punishment of burning.',NULL,34,12),
 (10865,2,'And to Solomon (We made) the Wind (obedient): Its early morning (stride) was a month''s (journey), and its evening (stride) was a month''s (journey); and We made a Font of molten brass to flow for him; and there were Jinns that worked in front of him, by the leave of his Lord, and if any of them turned aside from our command, We made him taste of the Penalty of the Blazing Fire.',NULL,34,12),
 (10866,3,'And unto Solomon (We gave) the wind, whereof the morning course was a month''s journey and the evening course a month''s journey, and We caused the fount of copper to gush forth for him, and (We gave him) certain of the jinn who worked before him by permission of his Lord. And such of them as deviated from Our command, them We caused to taste the punishment of flaming Fire.',NULL,34,12),
 (10867,1,'They made for him what he pleased of fortresses and images, and bowls (large) as watering-troughs and cooking-pots that will not move from their place; give thanks, O family of Dawood! and very few of My servants are grateful.',NULL,34,13),
 (10868,2,'They worked for him as he desired, (making) arches, images, basons as large as reservoirs, and (cooking) cauldrons fixed (in their places): "Work ye, sons of David, with thanks! but few of My servants are grateful!"',NULL,34,13),
 (10869,3,'They made for him what he willed: synagogues and statues, basins like wells and boilers built into the ground. Give thanks, O House of David! Few of My bondmen are thankful.',NULL,34,13),
 (10870,1,'But when We decreed death for him, naught showed them his death but a creature of the earth that ate away his staff; and when it fell down, the jinn came to know plainly that if they had known the unseen, they would not have tarried in abasing torment.',NULL,34,14),
 (10871,2,'Then, when We decreed (Solomon''s) death, nothing showed them his death except a little worm of the earth, which kept (slowly) gnawing away at his staff: so when he fell down, the Jinns saw plainly that if they had known the unseen, they would not have tarried in the humiliating Penalty (of their Task).',NULL,34,14),
 (10872,3,'And when We decreed death for him, nothing showed his death to them save a creeping creature of the earth which gnawed away his staff. And when he fell the jinn saw clearly how, if they had known the Unseen, they would not have continued in despised toil.',NULL,34,14),
 (10873,1,'Certainly there was a sign for Saba in their abode; two gardens on the right and the left; eat of the sustenance of your Lord and give thanks to Him: a good land and a Forgiving Lord!',NULL,34,15),
 (10874,2,'There was, for Saba, aforetime, a Sign in their home-land - two Gardens to the right and to the left. "Eat of the Sustenance (provided) by your Lord, and be grateful to Him: a territory fair and happy, and a Lord Oft-Forgiving!',NULL,34,15),
 (10875,3,'There was indeed a sign for Sheba in their dwelling-place: Two gardens on the right hand and the left (as who should say): Eat of the provision of your Lord and render thanks to Him. A fair land and an indulgent Lord!',NULL,34,15),
 (10876,1,'But they turned aside, so We sent upon them a torrent of which the rush could not be withstood, and in place of their two gardens We gave to them two gardens yielding bitter fruit and (growing) tamarisk and a few lote-trees.',NULL,34,16),
 (10877,2,'But they turned away (from Allah), and We sent against them the Flood (released) from the dams, and We converted their two garden (rows) into "gardens" producing bitter fruit, and tamarisks, and some few (stunted) Lote-trees.',NULL,34,16),
 (10878,3,'But they were froward, so We sent on them the flood of ''Iram, and in exchange for their two gardens gave them two gardens bearing bitter fruit, the tamarisk and here and there a lote-tree.',NULL,34,16),
 (10879,1,'This We requited them with because they disbelieved; and We do not punish any but the ungrateful.',NULL,34,17),
 (10880,2,'That was the Requital We gave them because they ungratefully rejected Faith: and never do We give (such) requital except to such as are ungrateful rejecters.',NULL,34,17),
 (10881,3,'This We awarded them because of their ingratitude. Punish We ever any save the ingrates?',NULL,34,17),
 (10882,1,'And We made between them and the towns which We had blessed (other) towns to be easily seen, and We apportioned the journey therein: Travel through them nights and days, secure.',NULL,34,18),
 (10883,2,'Between them and the Cities on which We had poured our blessings, We had placed Cities in prominent positions, and between them We had appointed stages of journey in due proportion: "Travel therein, secure, by night and by day."',NULL,34,18),
 (10884,3,'And We set, between them and the towns which We had blessed, towns easy to be seen, and We made the stage between them easy, (saying): Travel in them safely both by night and day.',NULL,34,18),
 (10885,1,'And they said: O our Lord! make spaces to be longer between our journeys; and they were unjust to themselves so We made them stories and scattered them with an utter scattering; most surely there are signs in this for every patient, grateful one',NULL,34,19),
 (10886,2,'But they said: "Our Lord! Place longer distances between our journey-stages": but they wronged themselves (therein). At length We made them as a tale (that is told), and We dispersed them all in scattered fragments. Verily in this are Signs for every (soul that is) patiently constant and grateful.',NULL,34,19),
 (10887,3,'But they said: Our Lord! Make the stage between our journeys longer. And they wronged themselves, therefore We made them bywords (in the land) and scattered them abroad, a total scattering. Lo! herein verily are portents for each steadfast, grateful (heart).',NULL,34,19),
 (10888,1,'And certainly the Shaitan found true his conjecture concerning them, so they follow him, except a party of the believers.',NULL,34,20),
 (10889,2,'And on them did Satan prove true his idea, and they followed him, all but a party that believed.',NULL,34,20),
 (10890,3,'And Satan indeed found his calculation true concerning them, for they follow him, all save a group of true believers.',NULL,34,20),
 (10891,1,'And he has no authority over them, but that We may distinguish him who believes in the hereafter from him who is in doubt concerning it; and your Lord is the Preserver of all things',NULL,34,21),
 (10892,2,'But he had no authority over them,- except that We might test the man who believes in the Hereafter from him who is in doubt concerning it: and thy Lord doth watch over all things.',NULL,34,21),
 (10893,3,'And he had no warrant whatsoever against them, save that We would know him who believeth in the Hereafter from him who is in doubt thereof; and thy Lord (O Muhammad) taketh note of all things.',NULL,34,21),
 (10894,1,'Say: Call upon those whom you assert besides Allah; they do not control the weight of an atom in the heavens or in the earth nor have they any partnership in either, nor has He among them any one to back (Him) up.',NULL,34,22),
 (10895,2,'Say: "Call upon other (gods) whom ye fancy, besides Allah: They have no power,- not the weight of an atom,- in the heavens or on earth: No (sort of) share have they therein, nor is any of them a helper to Allah.',NULL,34,22),
 (10896,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Call upon those whom ye set up beside Allah! They possess not an atom''s weight either in the heavens or in the earth, nor have they any share in either, nor hath He an auxiliary among them.',NULL,34,22),
 (10897,1,'And intercession will not avail aught with Him save of him whom He permits. Until when fear shall be removed from their hearts, They shall say: What is it that your Lord said? They shall say: The truth. And He is the Most High, the Great.',NULL,34,23),
 (10898,2,'"No intercession can avail in His Presence, except for those for whom He has granted permission. So far (is this the case) that, when terror is removed from their hearts (at the Day of Judgment, then) will they say, ''what is it that your Lord commanded?'' they will say, ''That which is true and just; and He is the Most High Most Great''."',NULL,34,23),
 (10899,3,'No intercession availeth with Him save for him whom He permitteth. Yet, when fear is banished from their hearts, they say: What was it that your Lord said? They say: The Truth. And He is the Sublime, the Great.',NULL,34,23),
 (10900,1,'Say: Who gives you the sustenance from the heavens and the earth? Say: Allah. And most surely we or you are on a right way or in manifest error',NULL,34,24),
 (10901,2,'Say: "Who gives you sustenance, from the heavens and the earth?" Say: "It is Allah; and certain it is that either we or ye are on right guidance or in manifest error!"',NULL,34,24),
 (10902,3,'Say: Who giveth you provision from the sky and the earth? Say: Allah, Lo! we or you assuredly are rightly guided or in error manifest.',NULL,34,24),
 (10903,1,'Say: You will not be questioned as to what we are guilty of, nor shall we be questioned as to what you do.',NULL,34,25),
 (10904,2,'Say: "Ye shall not be questioned as to our sins, nor shall we be questioned as to what ye do."',NULL,34,25),
 (10905,3,'Say: Ye will not be asked of what we committed, nor shall we be asked of what ye do.',NULL,34,25),
 (10906,1,'Say: Our Lord will gather us together, then will He judge between us with the truth; and He is the greatest Judge, the All-knowing.',NULL,34,26),
 (10907,2,'Say: "Our Lord will gather us together and will in the end decide the matter between us (and you) in truth and justice: and He is the one to decide, the One Who knows all."',NULL,34,26),
 (10908,3,'Say: Our Lord will bring us all together, then He will judge between us with truth. He is the All-knowing Judge.',NULL,34,26),
 (10909,1,'Say: Show me those whom you have joined with Him as associates; by no means (can you do it). Nay! He is Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,34,27),
 (10910,2,'Say: "Show me those whom ye have joined with Him as partners: by no means (can ye). Nay, He is Allah, the Exalted in Power, the Wise."',NULL,34,27),
 (10911,3,'Say: Show me those whom ye have joined unto Him as partners. Nay (ye dare not)! For He is Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,34,27),
 (10912,1,'And We have not sent you but to all the men as a bearer of good news and as a warner, but most men do not know.',NULL,34,28),
 (10913,2,'We have not sent thee but as a universal (Messenger) to men, giving them glad tidings, and warning them (against sin), but most men understand not.',NULL,34,28),
 (10914,3,'And We have not sent thee (O Muhammad) save as a bringer of good tidings and a warner unto all mankind; but most of mankind know not.',NULL,34,28),
 (10915,1,'And they say: When will this promise be (fulfilled) if you are truthful?',NULL,34,29),
 (10916,2,'They say: "When will this promise (come to pass) if ye are telling the truth?"',NULL,34,29),
 (10917,3,'And they say: When is this promise (to be fulfilled) if ye are truthful?',NULL,34,29),
 (10918,1,'Say: You have the appointment of a day from which you cannot hold back any while, nor can you bring it on.',NULL,34,30),
 (10919,2,'Say: "The appointment to you is for a Day, which ye cannot put back for an hour nor put forward."',NULL,34,30),
 (10920,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Yours is the promise of a Day which ye cannot postpone nor hasten by an hour.',NULL,34,30),
 (10921,1,'And those who disbelieve say: By no means will we believe in this Quran, nor in that which is before it; and could you see when the unjust shall be made to stand before their Lord, bandying words one with another! Those who were reckoned weak shall say to those who were proud: Had it not been for you we would certainly have been believers.',NULL,34,31),
 (10922,2,'The Unbelievers say: "We shall neither believe in this scripture nor in (any) that (came) before it." Couldst thou but see when the wrong-doers will be made to stand before their Lord, throwing back the word (of blame) on one another! Those who had been despised will say to the arrogant ones: "Had it not been for you, we should certainly have been believers!"',NULL,34,31),
 (10923,3,'And those who disbelieve say: We believe not in this Qur''an nor in that which was before it; but oh, if thou couldst see, when the wrong-doers are brought up before their Lord, how they cast the blame one to another; how those who were despised (in the earth) say unto those who were proud: But for you, we should have been believers.',NULL,34,31),
 (10924,1,'Those who were proud shall say to those who were deemed weak: Did we turn you away from the guidance after it had come to you? Nay, you (yourselves) were guilty',NULL,34,32),
 (10925,2,'The arrogant ones will say to those who had been despised: "Was it we who kept you back from Guidance after it reached you? Nay, rather, it was ye who transgressed.',NULL,34,32),
 (10926,3,'Those who were proud say unto those who were despised: Did we drive you away from the guidance after it had come unto you? Nay, but ye were guilty.',NULL,34,32),
 (10927,1,'And those who were deemed weak shall say to those who were proud. Nay, (it was) planning by night and day when you told us to disbelieve in Allah and to set up likes with Him. And they shall conceal regret when they shall see the punishment; and We will put shackles on the necks of those who disbelieved; they shall not be requited but what they did.',NULL,34,33),
 (10928,2,'Those who had been despised will say to the arrogant ones: "Nay! it was a plot (of yours) by day and by night: Behold! Ye (constantly) ordered us to be ungrateful to Allah and to attribute equals to Him!" They will declare (their) repentance when they see the Penalty: We shall put yokes on the necks of the Unbelievers: It would only be a requital for their (ill) Deeds.',NULL,34,33),
 (10929,3,'Those who were despised say unto those who were proud: Nay but (it was your) scheming night and day, when ye commanded us to disbelieve in Allah and set up rivals unto Him. And they are filled with remorse when they behold the doom; and We place carcans on the necks of those who disbelieved. Are they requited aught save what they used to do?',NULL,34,33),
 (10930,1,'And We never sent a warner to a town but those who led lives in ease in it said: We are surely disbelievers in what you are sent with.',NULL,34,34),
 (10931,2,'Never did We send a warner to a population, but the wealthy ones among them said: "We believe not in the (Message) with which ye have been sent."',NULL,34,34),
 (10932,3,'And We sent not unto any township a warner, but its pampered ones declared: Lo! we are disbelievers in that wherewith ye have been sent.',NULL,34,34),
 (10933,1,'And they say: We have more wealth and children, and we shall not be punished.',NULL,34,35),
 (10934,2,'They said: "We have more in wealth and in sons, and we cannot be punished."',NULL,34,35),
 (10935,3,'And they say: We are more (than you) in wealth and children. We are not the punished!',NULL,34,35),
 (10936,1,'Say: Surely my Lord amplifies the means of subsistence for whom He pleases and straitens (for whom He pleases), but most men do not know.',NULL,34,36),
 (10937,2,'Say: "Verily my Lord enlarges and restricts the Provision to whom He pleases, but most men understand not."',NULL,34,36),
 (10938,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Lo! my Lord enlargeth the provision for whom He will and narroweth it (for whom He will). But most of mankind know not.',NULL,34,36),
 (10939,1,'And not your wealth nor your children, are the things which bring you near Us in station, but whoever believes and does good, these it is for whom is a double reward for what they do, and they shall be secure in the highest places.',NULL,34,37),
 (10940,2,'It is not your wealth nor your sons, that will bring you nearer to Us in degree: but only those who believe and work righteousness - these are the ones for whom there is a multiplied Reward for their deeds, while secure they (reside) in the dwellings on high!',NULL,34,37),
 (10941,3,'And it is not your wealth nor your children that will bring you near unto Us, but he who believeth and doeth good (he draweth near). As for such, theirs will be twofold reward for what they did and they will dwell secure in lofty halls.',NULL,34,37),
 (10942,1,'And (as for) those who strive in opposing Our communications, they shall be caused to be brought to the chastisement.',NULL,34,38),
 (10943,2,'Those who strive against Our Signs, to frustrate them, will be given over into Punishment.',NULL,34,38),
 (10944,3,'And as for those who strive against Our revelations, challenging, they will be brought to the doom.',NULL,34,38),
 (10945,1,'Say: Surely my Lord amplifies the means of subsistence for whom He pleases of His servants and straitens (them) for whom (He pleases), and whatever thing you spend, He exceeds it in reward, and He is the best of Sustainers.',NULL,34,39),
 (10946,2,'Say: "Verily my Lord enlarges and restricts the Sustenance to such of his servants as He pleases: and nothing do ye spend in the least (in His cause) but He replaces it: for He is the Best of those who grant Sustenance.',NULL,34,39),
 (10947,3,'Say: Lo! my Lord enlargeth the provision for whom He will of His bondmen, and narroweth (it) for him. And whatsoever ye spend (for good) He replaceth it. And He is the Best of Providers.',NULL,34,39),
 (10948,1,'And on the day when He will gather them all together, then will He say to the angels: Did these worship you?',NULL,34,40),
 (10949,2,'One Day He will gather them all together, and say to the angels, "Was it you that these men used to worship?"',NULL,34,40),
 (10950,3,'And on the day when He will gather them all together, He will say unto the angels: Did these worship you?',NULL,34,40),
 (10951,1,'They shall say: Glory be to Thee! Thou art our Guardian, not they; nay! they worshipped the jinn; most of them were believers in them.',NULL,34,41),
 (10952,2,'They will say, "Glory to Thee! our (tie) is with Thee - as Protector - not with them. Nay, but they worshipped the Jinns: most of them believed in them."',NULL,34,41),
 (10953,3,'They will say: Be Thou Glorified. Thou (alone) art our Guardian, not them! Nay, but they worshipped the jinn; most of them were believers in them.',NULL,34,41),
 (10954,1,'So on that day one of you shall not control profit or harm for another, and We will say to those who were unjust: Taste the chastisement of the fire which you called a lie.',NULL,34,42),
 (10955,2,'So on that Day no power shall they have over each other, for profit or harm: and We shall say to the wrong-doers, "Taste ye the Penalty of the Fire,- the which ye were wont to deny!"',NULL,34,42),
 (10956,3,'That day ye will possess no use nor hurt one for another. And We shall say unto those who did wrong: Taste the doom of the Fire which ye used to deny.',NULL,34,42),
 (10957,1,'And when Our clear communications are recited to them, they say: This is naught but a man who desires to turn you away from that which your fathers worshipped. And they say: This is naught but a lie that is forged. And those who disbelieve say of the truth when it comes to them: This is only clear enchantment.',NULL,34,43),
 (10958,2,'When Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them, they say, "This is only a man who wishes to hinder you from the (worship) which your fathers practised." And they say, "This is only a falsehood invented!" and the Unbelievers say of the Truth when it comes to them, "This is nothing but evident magic!"',NULL,34,43),
 (10959,3,'And if Our revelations are recited unto them in plain terms, they say: This is naught else than a man who would turn you away from what your fathers used to worship; and they say: This is naught else than an invented lie. Those who disbelieve say of the truth when it reacheth them: This is naught else than mere magic.',NULL,34,43),
 (10960,1,'And We have not given them any books which they read, nor did We send to them before you a warner.',NULL,34,44),
 (10961,2,'But We had not given them Books which they could study, nor sent messengers to them before thee as Warners.',NULL,34,44),
 (10962,3,'And We have given them no scriptures which they study, nor sent We unto them, before thee, any warner.',NULL,34,44),
 (10963,1,'And those before them rejected (the truth), and these have not yet attained a tenth of what We gave them, but they gave the lie to My messengers, then how was the manifestation of My disapproval?',NULL,34,45),
 (10964,2,'And their predecessors rejected (the Truth); these have not received a tenth of what We had granted to those: yet when they rejected My messengers, how (terrible) was My rejection (of them)!',NULL,34,45),
 (10965,3,'Those before them denied, and these have not attained a tithe of that which We bestowed on them (of old); yet they denied My messengers. How intense then was My abhorrence (of them)!',NULL,34,45),
 (10966,1,'Say: I exhort you only to one thing, that rise up for Allah''s sake in twos and singly, then ponder: there is no madness in your fellow-citizen; he is only a warner to you before a severe chastisement.',NULL,34,46),
 (10967,2,'Say: "I do admonish you on one point: that ye do stand up before Allah,- (It may be) in pairs, or (it may be) singly,- and reflect (within yourselves): your Companion is not possessed: he is no less than a warner to you, in face of a terrible Penalty."',NULL,34,46),
 (10968,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): I exhort you unto one thing only: that ye awake, for Allah''s sake, by twos and singly, and then reflect: There is no madness in your comrade. He is naught else than a warner unto you in face of a terrific doom.',NULL,34,46),
 (10969,1,'Say: Whatever reward I have asked of you, that is only for yourselves; my reward is only with Allah, and He is a witness of all things.',NULL,34,47),
 (10970,2,'Say: "No reward do I ask of you: it is (all) in your interest: my reward is only due from Allah: And He is witness to all things."',NULL,34,47),
 (10971,3,'Say: Whatever reward I might have asked of you is yours. My reward is the affair of Allah only. He is Witness over all things.',NULL,34,47),
 (10972,1,'Say: Surely my Lord utters the truth, the great Knower of the unseen.',NULL,34,48),
 (10973,2,'Say: "Verily my Lord doth cast the (mantle of) Truth (over His servants),- He that has full knowledge of (all) that is hidden."',NULL,34,48),
 (10974,3,'Say: Lo! my Lord hurleth the truth. (He is) the Knower of Things Hidden.',NULL,34,48),
 (10975,1,'Say: The truth has come, and the falsehood shall vanish and shall not come back.',NULL,34,49),
 (10976,2,'Say: "The Truth has arrived, and Falsehood neither creates anything new, nor restores anything."',NULL,34,49),
 (10977,3,'Say: The Truth hath come, and falsehood showeth not its face and will not return.',NULL,34,49),
 (10978,1,'Say: If I err, I err only against my own soul, and if I follow a right direction, it ?s because of what my Lord reveals to me; surely He is Hearing, Nigh.',NULL,34,50),
 (10979,2,'Say: "If I am astray, I only stray to the loss of my own soul: but if I receive guidance, it is because of the inspiration of my Lord to me: it is He Who hears all things, and is (ever) near."',NULL,34,50),
 (10980,3,'Say: If I err, I err only to my own loss, and if I am rightly guided it is because of that which my Lord hath revealed unto me. Lo! He is Hearer, Nigh.',NULL,34,50),
 (10981,1,'And could you see when they shall become terrified, but (then) there shall be no escape and they shall be seized upon from a near place',NULL,34,51),
 (10982,2,'If thou couldst but see when they will quake with terror; but then there will be no escape (for them), and they will be seized from a position (quite) near.',NULL,34,51),
 (10983,3,'Couldst thou but see when they are terrified with no escape, and are seized from near at hand,',NULL,34,51),
 (10984,1,'And they shall say: We believe in it. And how shall the attaining (of faith) be possible to them from a distant place?',NULL,34,52),
 (10985,2,'And they will say, "We do believe (now) in the (Truth)"; but how could they receive (Faith) from a position (so far off,-',NULL,34,52),
 (10986,3,'And say: We (now) believe therein. But how can they reach (faith) from afar off,',NULL,34,52),
 (10987,1,'And they disbelieved in it before, and they utter conjectures with regard to the unseen from a distant place.',NULL,34,53),
 (10988,2,'Seeing that they did reject Faith (entirely) before, and that they (continually) cast (slanders) on the unseen from a position far off?',NULL,34,53),
 (10989,3,'When they disbelieved in it of yore. They aim at the unseen from afar off.',NULL,34,53),
 (10990,1,'And a barrier shall be placed between them and that which they desire, as was done with the likes of them before: surely they are in a disquieting doubt.',NULL,34,54),
 (10991,2,'And between them and their desires, is placed a barrier, as was done in the past with their partisans: for they were indeed in suspicious (disquieting) doubt.',NULL,34,54),
 (10992,3,'And a gulf is set between them and that which they desire, as was done for people of their kind of old. Lo! they were in hopeless doubt.',NULL,34,54),
 (10993,1,'All praise is due to Allah, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, the Maker of the angels, messengers flying on wings, two, and three, and four; He increases in creation what He pleases; surely Allah has power over all things.',NULL,35,1),
 (10994,2,'Praise be to Allah, Who created (out of nothing) the heavens and the earth, Who made the angels, messengers with wings,- two, or three, or four (pairs): He adds to Creation as He pleases: for Allah has power over all things.',NULL,35,1),
 (10995,3,'Praise be to Allah, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, Who appointeth the angels messengers having wings two, three and four. He multiplieth in creation what He will. Lo! Allah is Able to do all things.',NULL,35,1),
 (10996,1,'Whatever Allah grants to men of (His) mercy, there is none to withhold it, and what He withholds there is none to send it forth after that, and He is the Mighty, the Wise',NULL,35,2),
 (10997,2,'What Allah out of his Mercy doth bestow on mankind there is none can withhold: what He doth withhold, there is none can grant, apart from Him: and He is the Exalted in Power, full of Wisdom.',NULL,35,2),
 (10998,3,'That which Allah openeth unto mankind of mercy none can withhold it; and that which He withholdeth none can release thereafter. He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,35,2),
 (10999,1,'O men! call to mind the favor of Allah on you; is there any creator besides Allah who gives you sustenance from the heaven and the earth? There is no god but He; whence are you then turned away?',NULL,35,3),
 (11000,2,'O men! Call to mind the grace of Allah unto you! is there a creator, other than Allah, to give you sustenance from heaven or earth? There is no god but He: how then are ye deluded away from the Truth?',NULL,35,3),
 (11001,3,'O mankind! Remember Allah''s grace toward you! Is there any creator other than Allah who provideth for you from the sky and the earth? There is no Allah save Him. Whither then are ye turned?',NULL,35,3),
 (11002,1,'And if they call you a liar, truly messengers before you were called liars, and to Allah are all affairs returned.',NULL,35,4),
 (11003,2,'And if they reject thee, so were messengers rejected before thee: to Allah back for decision all affairs.',NULL,35,4),
 (11004,3,'And if they deny thee, (O Muhammad), messengers (of Allah) were denied before thee. Unto Allah all things are brought back.',NULL,35,4),
 (11005,1,'O men! surely the promise of Allah is true, therefore let not the life of this world deceive you, and let not the archdeceiver deceive you respecting Allah.',NULL,35,5),
 (11006,2,'O men! Certainly the promise of Allah is true. Let not then this present life deceive you, nor let the Chief Deceiver deceive you about Allah.',NULL,35,5),
 (11007,3,'O mankind! Lo! the promise of Allah is true. So let not the life of the world beguile you, and let not the (avowed) beguiler beguile you with regard to Allah.',NULL,35,5),
 (11008,1,'Surely the Shaitan is your enemy, so take him for an enemy; he only invites his party that they may be inmates of the burning fire.',NULL,35,6),
 (11009,2,'Verily Satan is an enemy to you: so treat him as an enemy. He only invites his adherents, that they may become Companions of the Blazing Fire.',NULL,35,6),
 (11010,3,'Lo! the devil is an enemy for you, so treat him as an enemy. He only summoneth his faction to be owners of the flaming Fire.',NULL,35,6),
 (11011,1,'(As for) those who disbelieve, they shall have a severe punishment, and (as for) those who believe and do good, they shall have forgiveness and a great reward.',NULL,35,7),
 (11012,2,'For those who reject Allah, is a terrible Penalty: but for those who believe and work righteous deeds, is Forgiveness, and a magnificent Reward.',NULL,35,7),
 (11013,3,'Those who disbelieve, theirs will be an awful doom; and those who believe and do good works, theirs will be forgiveness and a great reward.',NULL,35,7),
 (11014,1,'What! is he whose evil deed is made fairseeming to him so much so that he considers it good? Now surely Allah makes err whom He pleases and guides aright whom He pleases, so let not your soul waste away in grief for them; surely Allah is Cognizant of what they do',NULL,35,8),
 (11015,2,'Is he, then, to whom the evil of his conduct is made alluring, so that he looks upon it as good, (equal to one who is rightly guided)? For Allah leaves to stray whom He wills, and guides whom He wills. So let not thy soul go out in (vainly) sighing after them: for Allah knows well all that they do!',NULL,35,8),
 (11016,3,'Is he, the evil of whose deeds is made fairseeming unto him so that he deemeth it good, (other than Satan''s dupe)? Allah verily sendeth whom He will astray, and guideth whom He will; so let not thy soul expire in sighings for them. Lo! Allah is Aware of what they do!',NULL,35,8),
 (11017,1,'And Allah is He Who sends the winds so they raise a cloud, then We drive it on to a dead country, and therewith We give life to the earth after its death; even so is the quickening.',NULL,35,9),
 (11018,2,'It is Allah Who sends forth the Winds, so that they raise up the Clouds, and We drive them to a land that is dead, and revive the earth therewith after its death: even so (will be) the Resurrection!',NULL,35,9),
 (11019,3,'And Allah it is Who sendeth the winds and they raise a cloud; then We lead it unto a dead land and revive therewith the earth after its death. Such is the Resurrection.',NULL,35,9),
 (11020,1,'Whoever desires honor, then to Allah belongs the honor wholly. To Him do ascend the good words; and the good deeds, lift them up, and (as for) those who plan evil deeds, they shall have a severe chastisement; and (as for) their plan, it shall perish.',NULL,35,10),
 (11021,2,'If any do seek for glory and power,- to Allah belong all glory and power. To Him mount up (all) Words of Purity: It is He Who exalts each Deed of Righteousness. Those that lay Plots of Evil,- for them is a Penalty terrible; and the plotting of such will be void (of result).',NULL,35,10),
 (11022,3,'Whoso desireth power (should know that) all power belongeth to Allah. Unto Him good words ascend, and the pious deed doth He exalt; but those who plot iniquities, theirs will be an awful doom; and the plotting of such (folk) will come to naught.',NULL,35,10),
 (11023,1,'And Allah created you of dust, then of the life-germ, then He made you pairs; and no female bears, nor does she bring forth, except with His knowledge; and no one whose life is lengthened has his life lengthened, nor is aught diminished of one''s life, but it is all in a book; surely this is easy to Allah.',NULL,35,11),
 (11024,2,'And Allah did create you from dust; then from a sperm-drop; then He made you in pairs. And no female conceives, or lays down (her load), but with His knowledge. Nor is a man long-lived granted length of days, nor is a part cut off from his life, but is in a Decree (ordained). All this is easy to Allah.',NULL,35,11),
 (11025,3,'Allah created you from dust, then from a little fluid, then He made you pairs (the male and female). No female beareth or bringeth forth save with His knowledge. And no-one groweth old who groweth old, nor is aught lessened of his life, but it is recorded in a Book, Lo! that is easy for Allah.',NULL,35,11),
 (11026,1,'And the two seas are not alike: the one sweet, that subdues thirst by its excessive sweetness, pleasant to drink; and the other salt, that burns by its saltness; yet from each of them you eat fresh flesh and bring forth ornaments which you wear; and you see the ships cleave through it that you may seek of His bounty and that you may be grateful.',NULL,35,12),
 (11027,2,'Nor are the two bodies of flowing water alike,- the one palatable, sweet, and pleasant to drink, and the other, salt and bitter. Yet from each (kind of water) do ye eat flesh fresh and tender, and ye extract ornaments to wear; and thou seest the ships therein that plough the waves, that ye may seek (thus) of the Bounty of Allah that ye may be grateful.',NULL,35,12),
 (11028,3,'And the two seas are not alike: this, fresh, sweet, good to drink, this (other) bitter, salt. And from them both ye eat fresh meat and derive the ornament that ye wear. And thou seest the ship cleaving them with its prow that ye may seek of His bounty, and that haply ye may give thanks.',NULL,35,12),
 (11029,1,'He causes the night to enter in upon the day, and He causes the day to enter in upon the night, and He has made subservient (to you) the sun and the moon; each one follows its course to an appointed time; this is Allah, your Lord, His is the kingdom; and those whom you call upon besides Him do not control a straw.',NULL,35,13),
 (11030,2,'He merges Night into Day, and he merges Day into Night, and he has subjected the sun and the moon (to his Law): each one runs its course for a term appointed. Such is Allah your Lord: to Him belongs all Dominion. And those whom ye invoke besides Him have not the least power.',NULL,35,13),
 (11031,3,'He maketh the night to pass into the day and He maketh the day to pass into the night. He hath subdued the sun and moon to service. Each runneth unto an appointed term. Such is Allah, your Lord; His is the Sovereignty; and those unto whom ye pray instead of Him own not so much as the white spot on a date-stone.',NULL,35,13),
 (11032,1,'If you call on them they shall not hear your call, and even if they could hear they shall not answer you; and on the resurrection day they will deny your associating them (with Allah); and none can inform you like the One Who is Aware.',NULL,35,14),
 (11033,2,'If ye invoke them, they will not listen to your call, and if they were to listen, they cannot answer your (prayer). On the Day of Judgment they will reject your "Partnership". and none, (O man!) can tell thee (the Truth) like the One Who is acquainted with all things.',NULL,35,14),
 (11034,3,'If ye pray unto them they hear not your prayer, and if they heard they could not grant it you. On the Day of Resurrection they will disown association with you. None can inform you like Him Who is Aware.',NULL,35,14),
 (11035,1,'O men! you are they who stand in need of Allah, and Allah is He Who is the Self-sufficient, the Praised One.',NULL,35,15),
 (11036,2,'O ye men! It is ye that have need of Allah: but Allah is the One Free of all wants, worthy of all praise.',NULL,35,15),
 (11037,3,'O mankind! Ye are the poor in your relation to Allah. And Allah! He is the Absolute, the Owner of Praise.',NULL,35,15),
 (11038,1,'If He please, He will take you off and bring a new generation.',NULL,35,16),
 (11039,2,'If He so pleased, He could blot you out and bring in a New Creation.',NULL,35,16),
 (11040,3,'If He will, He can be rid of you and bring (instead of you) some new creation.',NULL,35,16),
 (11041,1,'And this is not hard to Allah.',NULL,35,17),
 (11042,2,'Nor is that (at all) difficult for Allah.',NULL,35,17),
 (11043,3,'That is not a hard thing for Allah.',NULL,35,17),
 (11044,1,'And a burdened soul cannot bear the burden of another and if one weighed down by burden should cry for (another to carry) its burden, not aught of it shall be carried, even though he be near of kin. You warn only those who fear their Lord in secret and keep up prayer; and whoever purifies himself, he purifies himself only for (the good of) his own soul; and to Allah is the eventual coming.',NULL,35,18),
 (11045,2,'Nor can a bearer of burdens bear another''s burdens if one heavily laden should call another to (bear) his load. Not the least portion of it can be carried (by the other). Even though he be nearly related. Thou canst but admonish such as fear their Lord unseen and establish regular Prayer. And whoever purifies himself does so for the benefit of his own soul; and the destination (of all) is to Allah.',NULL,35,18),
 (11046,3,'And no burdened soul can bear another''s burden, and if one heavy laden crieth for (help with) his load, naught of it will be lifted even though he (unto whom he crieth) be of kin. Thou warnest only those who fear their Lord in secret, and have established worship. He who groweth (in goodness), groweth only for himself, (he cannot by his merit redeem others). Unto Allah is the journeying.',NULL,35,18),
 (11047,1,'And the blind and the seeing are not alike',NULL,35,19),
 (11048,2,'The blind and the seeing are not alike;',NULL,35,19),
 (11049,3,'The blind man is not equal with the seer;',NULL,35,19),
 (11050,1,'Nor the darkness and the light,',NULL,35,20),
 (11051,2,'Nor are the depths of Darkness and the Light;',NULL,35,20),
 (11052,3,'Nor is darkness (tantamount to) light;',NULL,35,20),
 (11053,1,'Nor the shade and the heat,',NULL,35,21),
 (11054,2,'Nor are the (chilly) shade and the (genial) heat of the sun:',NULL,35,21),
 (11055,3,'Nor is the shadow equal with the sun''s full heat;',NULL,35,21),
 (11056,1,'Neither are the living and the dead alike. Surely Allah makes whom He pleases hear, and you cannot make those hear who are m the graves.',NULL,35,22),
 (11057,2,'Nor are alike those that are living and those that are dead. Allah can make any that He wills to hear; but thou canst not make those to hear who are (buried) in graves.',NULL,35,22),
 (11058,3,'Nor are the living equal with the dead. Lo! Allah maketh whom He will to hear. Thou canst not reach those who are in the graves.',NULL,35,22),
 (11059,1,'You are naught but a warner.',NULL,35,23),
 (11060,2,'Thou art no other than a warner.',NULL,35,23),
 (11061,3,'Thou art but a warner.',NULL,35,23),
 (11062,1,'Surely We have sent you with the truth as a bearer of good news and a warner; and there is not a people but a warner has gone among them.',NULL,35,24),
 (11063,2,'Verily We have sent thee in truth, as a bearer of glad tidings, and as a warner: and there never was a people, without a warner having lived among them (in the past).',NULL,35,24),
 (11064,3,'Lo! We have sent thee with the Truth, a bearer of glad tidings and a warner; and there is not a nation but a warner hath passed among them.',NULL,35,24),
 (11065,1,'And if they call you a liar, so did those before them indeed call (their messengers) liars; their messengers had come to them with clear arguments, and with scriptures, and with the illuminating book.',NULL,35,25),
 (11066,2,'And if they reject thee, so did their predecessors, to whom came their messengers with Clear Signs, Books of dark prophecies, and the Book of Enlightenment.',NULL,35,25),
 (11067,3,'And if they deny thee, those before them also denied. Their messengers came unto them with clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty), and with the Psalms and the Scripture giving light.',NULL,35,25),
 (11068,1,'Then did I punish those who disbelieved, so how was the manifestation of My disapproval?',NULL,35,26),
 (11069,2,'In the end did I punish those who rejected Faith: and how (terrible) was My rejection (of them)!',NULL,35,26),
 (11070,3,'Then seized I those who disbelieved, and how intense was My abhorrence!',NULL,35,26),
 (11071,1,'Do you not see that Allah sends down water from the cloud, then We bring forth therewith fruits of various colors; and in the mountains are streaks, white and red, of various hues and (others) intensely black?',NULL,35,27),
 (11072,2,'Seest thou not that Allah sends down rain from the sky? With it We then bring out produce of various colours. And in the mountains are tracts white and red, of various shades of colour, and black intense in hue.',NULL,35,27),
 (11073,3,'Hast thou not seen that Allah causeth water to fall from the sky, and We produce therewith fruit of divers hues; and among the hills are streaks white and red, of divers hues, and (others) raven-black;',NULL,35,27),
 (11074,1,'And of men and beasts and cattle are various species of it likewise; those of His servants only who are possessed of knowledge fear Allah; surely Allah is Mighty, Forgiving.',NULL,35,28),
 (11075,2,'And so amongst men and crawling creatures and cattle, are they of various colours. Those truly fear Allah, among His Servants, who have knowledge: for Allah is Exalted in Might, Oft-Forgiving.',NULL,35,28),
 (11076,3,'And of men and beasts and cattle, in like manner, divers hues? The erudite among His bondmen fear Allah alone. Lo! Allah is Mighty, Forgiving.',NULL,35,28),
 (11077,1,'Surely they who recite the Book of Allah and keep up prayer and spend out of what We have given them secretly and openly, hope for a gain which will not perish.',NULL,35,29),
 (11078,2,'Those who rehearse the Book of Allah, establish regular Prayer, and spend (in Charity) out of what We have provided for them, secretly and openly, hope for a commerce that will never fail:',NULL,35,29),
 (11079,3,'Lo! those who read the Scripture of Allah, and establish worship, and spend of that which We have bestowed on them secretly and openly, they look forward to imperishable gain,',NULL,35,29),
 (11080,1,'That He may pay them back fully their rewards and give them more out of His grace: surely He is Forgiving, Multiplier of rewards.',NULL,35,30),
 (11081,2,'For He will pay them their meed, nay, He will give them (even) more out of His Bounty: for He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (service).',NULL,35,30),
 (11082,3,'That He will pay them their wages and increase them of His grace. Lo! He is Forgiving, Responsive.',NULL,35,30),
 (11083,1,'And that which We have revealed to you of the Book, that is the truth verifying that which is before it; most surely with respect to His servants Allah is Aware, Seeing.',NULL,35,31),
 (11084,2,'That which We have revealed to thee of the Book is the Truth,- confirming what was (revealed) before it: for Allah is assuredly- with respect to His Servants - well acquainted and Fully Observant.',NULL,35,31),
 (11085,3,'As for that which We inspire in thee of the Scripture, it is the Truth confirming that which was (revealed) before it. Lo! Allah is indeed Observer, Seer of His slaves.',NULL,35,31),
 (11086,1,'Then We gave the Book for an inheritance to those whom We chose from among Our servants; but of them is he who makes his soul to suffer a loss, and of them is he who takes a middle course, and of them is he who is foremost in deeds of goodness by Allah''s permission; this is the great excellence.',NULL,35,32),
 (11087,2,'Then We have given the Book for inheritance to such of Our Servants as We have chosen: but there are among them some who wrong their own souls; some who follow a middle course; and some who are, by Allah''s leave, foremost in good deeds; that is the highest Grace.',NULL,35,32),
 (11088,3,'Then We gave the Scripture as inheritance unto those whom We elected of Our bondmen. But of them are some who wrong themselves and of them are some who are lukewarm, and of them are some who outstrip (others) through good deeds, by Allah''s leave. That is the great favour!',NULL,35,32),
 (11089,1,'Gardens of perpetuity, they shall enter therein; they shad be made to wear therein bracelets of gold and pearls, and their dress therein shall be silk.',NULL,35,33),
 (11090,2,'Gardens of Eternity will they enter: therein will they be adorned with bracelets of gold and pearls; and their garments there will be of silk.',NULL,35,33),
 (11091,3,'Gardens of Eden! They enter them wearing armlets of gold and pearl and their raiment therein is silk.',NULL,35,33),
 (11092,1,'And they shall say: (All) praise is due to Allah, Who has made grief to depart from us; most surely our Lord is Forgiving, Multiplier of rewards,',NULL,35,34),
 (11093,2,'And they will say: "Praise be to Allah, Who has removed from us (all) sorrow: for our Lord is indeed Oft-Forgiving Ready to appreciate (service):',NULL,35,34),
 (11094,3,'And they say: Praise be to Allah Who hath put grief away from us. Lo! Our Lord is Forgiving, Bountiful,',NULL,35,34),
 (11095,1,'Who has made us alight in a house abiding for ever out of . His grace; toil shall not touch us therein, nor shall fatigue therein afflict us.',NULL,35,35),
 (11096,2,'"Who has, out of His Bounty, settled us in a Home that will last: no toil nor sense of weariness shall touch us therein."',NULL,35,35),
 (11097,3,'Who, of His grace, hath installed us in the mansion of eternity, where toil toucheth us not nor can weariness affect us.',NULL,35,35),
 (11098,1,'And (as for) those who disbelieve, for them is the fire of hell; it shall not be finished with them entirely so that they should die, nor shall the chastisement thereof be lightened to them: even thus do We retribute every ungrateful one.',NULL,35,36),
 (11099,2,'But those who reject (Allah) - for them will be the Fire of Hell: No term shall be determined for them, so they should die, nor shall its Penalty be lightened for them. Thus do We reward every ungrateful one!',NULL,35,36),
 (11100,3,'But as for those who disbelieve, for them is fire of hell; it taketh not complete effect upon them so that they can die, nor is its torment lightened for them. Thus We punish every ingrate.',NULL,35,36),
 (11101,1,'And they shall cry therein for succour: O our Lord ! take us out, we will do good deeds other than those which we used to do. Did We not preserve you alive long enough, so that he who would be mindful in it should mind? And there came to you the warner; therefore taste; because for the unjust, there is no helper.',NULL,35,37),
 (11102,2,'Therein will they cry aloud (for assistance): "Our Lord! Bring us out: we shall work righteousness, not the (deeds) we used to do!" - "Did We not give you long enough life so that he that would should receive admonition? and (moreover) the warner came to you. So taste ye (the fruits of your deeds): for the wrong-doers there is no helper."',NULL,35,37),
 (11103,3,'And they cry for help there, (saying): Our Lord! Release us; we will do right, not (the wrong) that we used to do. Did not We grant you a life long enough for him who reflected to reflect therein? And the warner came unto you. Now taste (the flavour of your deeds), for evil-doers have no helper.',NULL,35,37),
 (11104,1,'Surely Allah is the Knower of what is unseen m the heavens and the earth; surely He is Cognizant of what IS m the hearts.',NULL,35,38),
 (11105,2,'Verily Allah knows (all) the hidden things of the heavens and the earth: verily He has full knowledge of all that is in (men''s) hearts.',NULL,35,38),
 (11106,3,'Lo! Allah is the Knower of the Unseen of the heavens and the earth. Lo! He is Aware of the secret of (men''s) breasts.',NULL,35,38),
 (11107,1,'He it is Who made you rulers in the land; therefore whoever disbelieves, his unbelief is against himself; and their unbelief does not increase the disbelievers with their Lord in anything except hatred; and their unbelief does not increase the disbelievers m anything except loss.',NULL,35,39),
 (11108,2,'He it is That has made you inheritors in the earth: if, then, any do reject (Allah), their rejection (works) against themselves: their rejection but adds to the odium for the Unbelievers in the sight of their Lord: their rejection but adds to (their own) undoing.',NULL,35,39),
 (11109,3,'He it is Who hath made you regents in the earth; so he who disbelieveth, his disbelief be on his own head. Their disbelief increaseth for the disbelievers, in their Lord''s sight, naught save abhorrence. Their disbelief increaseth for the disbelievers naught save loss.',NULL,35,39),
 (11110,1,'Say: Have you considered your associates which you call upon besides Allah? Show me what part of the earth they have created, or have they any share in the heavens; or, have We given them a book so that they follow a clear argument thereof? Nay, the unjust do not hold out promises one to another but only to deceive.',NULL,35,40),
 (11111,2,'Say: "Have ye seen (these) ''Partners'' of yours whom ye call upon besides Allah? Show Me what it is they have created in the (wide) earth. Or have they a share in the heavens? Or have We given them a Book from which they (can derive) clear (evidence)?- Nay, the wrong-doers promise each other nothing but delusions.',NULL,35,40),
 (11112,3,'Say: Have ye seen your partner-gods to whom ye pray beside Allah? Show me what they created of the earth! Or have they any portion in the heavens? Or have We given them a scripture so they act on clear proof therefrom? Nay, the evil-doers promise one another only to deceive.',NULL,35,40),
 (11113,1,'Surely Allah upholds the heavens and the earth lest they come to naught; and if they should come to naught, there Is none who can uphold them after Him; surely He is the Forbearing, the Forgiving.',NULL,35,41),
 (11114,2,'It is Allah Who sustains the heavens and the earth, lest they cease (to function): and if they should fail, there is none - not one - can sustain them thereafter: Verily He is Most Forbearing, Oft-Forgiving.',NULL,35,41),
 (11115,3,'Lo! Allah graspeth the heavens and the earth that they deviate not, and if they were to deviate there is not one that could grasp them after Him. Lo! He is ever Clement, Forgiving.',NULL,35,41),
 (11116,1,'And they swore by Allah with the strongest of their oaths that if there came to them a warner they would be better guided than any of the nations; but when there came to them a warner it increased them in naught but aversion.',NULL,35,42),
 (11117,2,'They swore their strongest oaths by Allah that if a warner came to them, they would follow his guidance better than any (other) of the Peoples: But when a warner came to them, it has only increased their flight (from righteousness),-',NULL,35,42),
 (11118,3,'And they swore by Allah, their most binding oath, that if a warner came unto them they would be more tractable than any of the nations; yet, when a warner came unto them it aroused in them naught save repugnance,',NULL,35,42),
 (11119,1,'(In) behaving proudly in the land and in planning evil; and the evil plans shall not beset any save the authors of it. Then should they wait for aught except the way of the former people? For you shall not find any alteration in the course of Allah; and you shall not find any change in the course of Allah.',NULL,35,43),
 (11120,2,'On account of their arrogance in the land and their plotting of Evil, but the plotting of Evil will hem in only the authors thereof. Now are they but looking for the way the ancients were dealt with? But no change wilt thou find in Allah''s way (of dealing): no turning off wilt thou find in Allah''s way (of dealing).',NULL,35,43),
 (11121,3,'(Shown in their) behaving arrogantly in the land and plotting evil; and the evil plot encloseth but the men who make it. Then, can they expect aught save the treatment of the folk of old? Thou wilt not find for Allah''s way of treatment any substitute, nor wilt thou find for Allah''s way of treatment aught of power to change.',NULL,35,43),
 (11122,1,'Have they not travelled in the land and seen how was the end of those before them while they were stronger than these in power? And Allah is not such that any thing in the heavens or in the earth should escape Him; surely He is Knowing, Powerful.',NULL,35,44),
 (11123,2,'Do they not travel through the earth, and see what was the End of those before them,- though they were superior to them in strength? Nor is Allah to be frustrated by anything whatever in the heavens or on earth: for He is All-Knowing. All-Powerful.',NULL,35,44),
 (11124,3,'Have they not travelled in the land and seen the nature of the consequence for those who were before them, and they were mightier than these in power? Allah is not such that aught in the heavens or in the earth escapeth Him. Lo! He is the Wise, the Mighty.',NULL,35,44),
 (11125,1,'And were Allah to punish men for what they earn, He would not leave on the back of it any creature, but He respites them till an appointed term; so when their doom shall come, then surely Allah is Seeing with respect to His servants.',NULL,35,45),
 (11126,2,'If Allah were to punish men according to what they deserve. He would not leave on the back of the (earth) a single living creature: but He gives them respite for a stated Term: when their Term expires, verily Allah has in His sight all His Servants.',NULL,35,45),
 (11127,3,'If Allah took mankind to task by that which they deserve, He would not leave a living creature on the surface of the earth; but He reprieveth them unto an appointed term, and when their term cometh - then verily (they will know that) Allah is ever Seer of His slaves.',NULL,35,45),
 (11128,1,'Ya Seen.',NULL,36,1),
 (11129,2,'Ya Sin.',NULL,36,1),
 (11130,3,'Ya Sin.',NULL,36,1),
 (11131,1,'I swear by the Quran full of wisdom',NULL,36,2),
 (11132,2,'By the Qur''an, full of Wisdom,-',NULL,36,2),
 (11133,3,'By the wise Qur''an,',NULL,36,2),
 (11134,1,'Most surely you are one of the messengers',NULL,36,3),
 (11135,2,'Thou art indeed one of the messengers,',NULL,36,3),
 (11136,3,'Lo! thou art of those sent',NULL,36,3),
 (11137,1,'On a right way.',NULL,36,4),
 (11138,2,'On a Straight Way.',NULL,36,4),
 (11139,3,'On a straight path,',NULL,36,4),
 (11140,1,'A revelation of the Mighty, the Merciful.',NULL,36,5),
 (11141,2,'It is a Revelation sent down by (Him), the Exalted in Might, Most Merciful.',NULL,36,5),
 (11142,3,'A revelation of the Mighty, the Merciful,',NULL,36,5),
 (11143,1,'That you may warn a people whose fathers were not warned, so they are heedless.',NULL,36,6),
 (11144,2,'In order that thou mayest admonish a people, whose fathers had received no admonition, and who therefore remain heedless (of the Signs of Allah).',NULL,36,6),
 (11145,3,'That thou mayst warn a folk whose fathers were not warned, so they are heedless.',NULL,36,6),
 (11146,1,'Certainly the word has proved true of most of them, so they do not believe.',NULL,36,7),
 (11147,2,'The Word is proved true against the greater part of them: for they do not believe.',NULL,36,7),
 (11148,3,'Already hath the judgment, (for their infidelity) proved true of most of them, for they believe not.',NULL,36,7),
 (11149,1,'Surely We have placed chains on their necks, and these reach up to their chins, so they have their heads raised aloft.',NULL,36,8),
 (11150,2,'We have put yokes round their necks right up to their chins, so that their heads are forced up (and they cannot see).',NULL,36,8),
 (11151,3,'Lo! We have put on their necks carcans reaching unto the chins, so that they are made stiff-necked.',NULL,36,8),
 (11152,1,'And We have made before them a barrier and a barrier behind them, then We have covered them over so that they do not see.',NULL,36,9),
 (11153,2,'And We have put a bar in front of them and a bar behind them, and further, We have covered them up; so that they cannot see.',NULL,36,9),
 (11154,3,'And We have set a bar before them and a bar behind them, and (thus) have covered them so that they see not.',NULL,36,9),
 (11155,1,'And it is alike to them whether you warn them or warn them not: they do not believe.',NULL,36,10),
 (11156,2,'The same is it to them whether thou admonish them or thou do not admonish them: they will not believe.',NULL,36,10),
 (11157,3,'Whether thou warn them or thou warn them not, it is alike for them, for they believe not.',NULL,36,10),
 (11158,1,'You can only warn him who follows the reminder and fears the Beneficent Allah in secret; so announce to him forgiveness and an honorable reward.',NULL,36,11),
 (11159,2,'Thou canst but admonish such a one as follows the Message and fears the (Lord) Most Gracious, unseen: give such a one, therefore, good tidings, of Forgiveness and a Reward most generous.',NULL,36,11),
 (11160,3,'Thou warnest only him who followeth the Reminder and feareth the Beneficent in secret. To him bear tidings of forgiveness and a rich reward.',NULL,36,11),
 (11161,1,'Surely We give life to the dead, and We write down what they have sent before and their footprints, and We have recorded everything in a clear writing.',NULL,36,12),
 (11162,2,'Verily We shall give life to the dead, and We record that which they send before and that which they leave behind, and of all things have We taken account in a clear Book (of evidence).',NULL,36,12),
 (11163,3,'Lo! We it is Who bring the dead to life. We record that which they send before (them, and their footprints. And all things We have kept in a clear Register.',NULL,36,12),
 (11164,1,'And set out to them an example of the people of the town, when the messengers came to it.',NULL,36,13),
 (11165,2,'Set forth to them, by way of a parable, the (story of) the Companions of the City. Behold!, there came messengers to it.',NULL,36,13),
 (11166,3,'Coin for them a similitude: The people of the city when those sent (from Allah) came unto them;',NULL,36,13),
 (11167,1,'When We sent to them two, they rejected both of them, then We strengthened (them) with a third, so they said: Surely we are messengers to you.',NULL,36,14),
 (11168,2,'When We (first) sent to them two messengers, they rejected them: But We strengthened them with a third: they said, "Truly, we have been sent on a mission to you."',NULL,36,14),
 (11169,3,'When We sent unto them twain, and they denied them both, so We reinforced them with a third, and they said: Lo! we have been sent unto you.',NULL,36,14),
 (11170,1,'They said: You are naught but mortals like ourselves, nor has the Beneficent Allah revealed anything; you only lie.',NULL,36,15),
 (11171,2,'The (people) said: "Ye are only men like ourselves; and (Allah) Most Gracious sends no sort of revelation: ye do nothing but lie."',NULL,36,15),
 (11172,3,'They said: Ye are but mortals like unto us. The Beneficent hath naught revealed. Ye do but lie!',NULL,36,15),
 (11173,1,'They said: Our Lord knows that we are most surely messengers to you.',NULL,36,16),
 (11174,2,'They said: "Our Lord doth know that we have been sent on a mission to you:',NULL,36,16),
 (11175,3,'They answered: Our Lord knoweth that we are indeed sent unto you,',NULL,36,16),
 (11176,1,'And nothing devolves on us but a clear deliverance (of the message).',NULL,36,17),
 (11177,2,'"And our duty is only to proclaim the clear Message."',NULL,36,17),
 (11178,3,'And our duty is but plain conveyance (of the message).',NULL,36,17),
 (11179,1,'They said: Surely we augur evil from you; if you do not desist, we will certainly stone you, and there shall certainly afflict vou a painful chastisement from us.',NULL,36,18),
 (11180,2,'The (people) said: "for us, we augur an evil omen from you: if ye desist not, we will certainly stone you. And a grievous punishment indeed will be inflicted on you by us."',NULL,36,18),
 (11181,3,'(The people of the city) said: We augur ill of you. If ye desist not, we shall surely stone you, and grievous torture will befall you at our hands.',NULL,36,18),
 (11182,1,'They said: Your evil fortune is with you; what! if you are reminded! Nay, you are an extravagant people.',NULL,36,19),
 (11183,2,'They said: "Your evil omens are with yourselves: (deem ye this an evil omen). If ye are admonished? Nay, but ye are a people transgressing all bounds!"',NULL,36,19),
 (11184,3,'They said: Your evil augury be with you! Is it because ye are reminded (of the truth)? Nay, but ye are froward folk!',NULL,36,19),
 (11185,1,'And from the remote part of the city there came a man running, he said: O my people! follow the messengers;',NULL,36,20),
 (11186,2,'Then there came running, from the farthest part of the City, a man, saying, "O my people! Obey the messengers:',NULL,36,20),
 (11187,3,'And there came from the uttermost part of the city a man running. He cried: O my people! Follow those who have been sent!',NULL,36,20),
 (11188,1,'Follow him who does not ask you for reward, and they are the followers of the right course;',NULL,36,21),
 (11189,2,'"Obey those who ask no reward of you (for themselves), and who have themselves received Guidance.',NULL,36,21),
 (11190,3,'Follow those who ask of you no fee, and who are rightly guided.',NULL,36,21),
 (11191,1,'And what reason have I that I should not serve Him Who brought me into existence? And to Him you shall be brought back;',NULL,36,22),
 (11192,2,'"It would not be reasonable in me if I did not serve Him Who created me, and to Whom ye shall (all) be brought back.',NULL,36,22),
 (11193,3,'For what cause should I not serve Him Who hath created me, and unto Whom ye will be brought back?',NULL,36,22),
 (11194,1,'What! shall I take besides Him gods whose intercession, If the Beneficent Allah should desire to afflict me with a harm, shall not avail me aught, nor shall they be able to deliver me?',NULL,36,23),
 (11195,2,'"Shall I take (other) gods besides Him? If (Allah) Most Gracious should intend some adversity for me, of no use whatever will be their intercession for me, nor can they deliver me.',NULL,36,23),
 (11196,3,'Shall I take (other) gods in place of Him when, if the Beneficent should wish me any harm, their intercession will avail me naught, nor can they save?',NULL,36,23),
 (11197,1,'In that case I shall most surely be in clear error:',NULL,36,24),
 (11198,2,'"I would indeed, if I were to do so, be in manifest Error.',NULL,36,24),
 (11199,3,'Then truly I should be in error manifest.',NULL,36,24),
 (11200,1,'Surely I believe in your Lord, therefore hear me.',NULL,36,25),
 (11201,2,'"For me, I have faith in the Lord of you (all): listen, then, to me!"',NULL,36,25),
 (11202,3,'Lo! I have believed in your Lord, so hear me!',NULL,36,25),
 (11203,1,'It was said: Enter the garden. He said: O would that my people had known',NULL,36,26),
 (11204,2,'It was said: "Enter thou the Garden." He said: "Ah me! Would that my People knew (what I know)!-',NULL,36,26),
 (11205,3,'It was said (unto him): Enter paradise. He said: Would that my people knew',NULL,36,26),
 (11206,1,'Of that on account of which my Lord has forgiven me and made me of the honored ones!',NULL,36,27),
 (11207,2,'"For that my Lord has granted me Forgiveness and has enrolled me among those held in honour!"',NULL,36,27),
 (11208,3,'With what (munificence) my Lord hath pardoned me and made me of the honoured ones!',NULL,36,27),
 (11209,1,'And We did not send down upon his people after him any hosts from heaven, nor do We ever send down.',NULL,36,28),
 (11210,2,'And We sent not down against his People, after him, any hosts from heaven, nor was it needful for Us so to do.',NULL,36,28),
 (11211,3,'We sent not down against his people after him a host from heaven, nor do We ever send.',NULL,36,28),
 (11212,1,'It was naught but a single cry, and lo! they were still.',NULL,36,29),
 (11213,2,'It was no more than a single mighty Blast, and behold! they were (like ashes) quenched and silent.',NULL,36,29),
 (11214,3,'It was but one Shout, and lo! they were extinct.',NULL,36,29),
 (11215,1,'Alas for the servants! there comes not to them an messenger but they mock at him.',NULL,36,30),
 (11216,2,'Ah! Alas for (My) Servants! There comes not a messenger to them but they mock him!',NULL,36,30),
 (11217,3,'Ah, the anguish for the bondmen! Never came there unto them a messenger but they did mock him!',NULL,36,30),
 (11218,1,'Do they not consider how many of the generations have We destroyed before them, because they do not turn to them?',NULL,36,31),
 (11219,2,'See they not how many generations before them we destroyed? Not to them will they return:',NULL,36,31),
 (11220,3,'Have they not seen how many generations We destroyed before them, which indeed returned not unto them;',NULL,36,31),
 (11221,1,'And all of them shall surely be brought before Us.',NULL,36,32),
 (11222,2,'But each one of them all - will be brought before Us (for judgment).',NULL,36,32),
 (11223,3,'But all, without exception, will be brought before Us.',NULL,36,32),
 (11224,1,'And a sign to them is the dead earth: We give life to it and bring forth from it grain SQ they eat of it.',NULL,36,33),
 (11225,2,'A Sign for them is the earth that is dead: We do give it life, and produce grain therefrom, of which ye do eat.',NULL,36,33),
 (11226,3,'A token unto them is the dead earth. We revive it, and We bring forth from it grain so that they eat thereof;',NULL,36,33),
 (11227,1,'And We make therein gardens of palms and grapevines and We make springs to flow forth in it,',NULL,36,34),
 (11228,2,'And We produce therein orchard with date-palms and vines, and We cause springs to gush forth therein:',NULL,36,34),
 (11229,3,'And We have placed therein gardens of the date-palm and grapes, and We have caused springs of water to gush forth therein,',NULL,36,34),
 (11230,1,'That they may eat of the fruit thereof, and their hands did not make it; will they not then be grateful?',NULL,36,35),
 (11231,2,'That they may enjoy the fruits of this (artistry): It was not their hands that made this: will they not then give thanks?',NULL,36,35),
 (11232,3,'That they may eat of the fruit thereof, and their hands made it not. Will they not, then, give thanks?',NULL,36,35),
 (11233,1,'Glory be to Him Who created pairs of all things, of what the earth grows, and of their kind and of what they do not know.',NULL,36,36),
 (11234,2,'Glory to Allah, Who created in pairs all things that the earth produces, as well as their own (human) kind and (other) things of which they have no knowledge.',NULL,36,36),
 (11235,3,'Glory be to Him Who created all the sexual pairs, of that which the earth groweth, and of themselves, and of that which they know not!',NULL,36,36),
 (11236,1,'And a sign to them is the night: We draw forth from it the day, then lo! they are in the dark;',NULL,36,37),
 (11237,2,'And a Sign for them is the Night: We withdraw therefrom the Day, and behold they are plunged in darkness;',NULL,36,37),
 (11238,3,'A token unto them is night. We strip it of the day, and lo! they are in darkness.',NULL,36,37),
 (11239,1,'And the sun runs on to a term appointed for it; that is the ordinance of the Mighty, the Knowing.',NULL,36,38),
 (11240,2,'And the sun runs his course for a period determined for him: that is the decree of (Him), the Exalted in Might, the All-Knowing.',NULL,36,38),
 (11241,3,'And the sun runneth on unto a resting-place for him. That is the measuring of the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,36,38),
 (11242,1,'And (as for) the moon, We have ordained for it stages till it becomes again as an old dry palm branch.',NULL,36,39),
 (11243,2,'And the Moon,- We have measured for her mansions (to traverse) till she returns like the old (and withered) lower part of a date-stalk.',NULL,36,39),
 (11244,3,'And for the moon We have appointed mansions till she return like an old shrivelled palm-leaf.',NULL,36,39),
 (11245,1,'Neither is it allowable to the sun that it should overtake the moon, nor can the night outstrip the day; and all float on in a sphere.',NULL,36,40),
 (11246,2,'It is not permitted to the Sun to catch up the Moon, nor can the Night outstrip the Day: Each (just) swims along in (its own) orbit (according to Law).',NULL,36,40),
 (11247,3,'It is not for the sun to overtake the moon, nor doth the night outstrip the day. They float each in an orbit.',NULL,36,40),
 (11248,1,'And a sign to them is that We bear their offspring in the laden ship.',NULL,36,41),
 (11249,2,'And a Sign for them is that We bore their race (through the Flood) in the loaded Ark;',NULL,36,41),
 (11250,3,'And a token unto them is that We bear their offspring in the laden ship,',NULL,36,41),
 (11251,1,'And We have created for them the like of it, what they will ride on.',NULL,36,42),
 (11252,2,'And We have created for them similar (vessels) on which they ride.',NULL,36,42),
 (11253,3,'And have created for them of the like thereof whereon they ride.',NULL,36,42),
 (11254,1,'And if We please, We can drown them, then there shall be no succorer for them, nor shall they be rescued',NULL,36,43),
 (11255,2,'If it were Our Will, We could drown them: then would there be no helper (to hear their cry), nor could they be delivered,',NULL,36,43),
 (11256,3,'And if We will, We drown them, and there is no help for them, neither can they be saved;',NULL,36,43),
 (11257,1,'But (by) mercy from Us and for enjoyment till a time.',NULL,36,44),
 (11258,2,'Except by way of Mercy from Us, and by way of (world) convenience (to serve them) for a time.',NULL,36,44),
 (11259,3,'Unless by mercy from Us and as comfort for a while.',NULL,36,44),
 (11260,1,'And when it is said to them: Guard against what is before you and what is behind you, that mercy may be had on you.',NULL,36,45),
 (11261,2,'When they are told, "Fear ye that which is before you and that which will be after you, in order that ye may receive Mercy," (they turn back).',NULL,36,45),
 (11262,3,'When it is said unto them: Beware of that which is before you and that which is behind you, that haply ye may find mercy (they are heedless).',NULL,36,45),
 (11263,1,'And there comes not to them a communication of the communications of their Lord but they turn aside from it.',NULL,36,46),
 (11264,2,'Not a Sign comes to them from among the Signs of their Lord, but they turn away therefrom.',NULL,36,46),
 (11265,3,'Never came a token of the tokens of their Lord to them, but they did turn away from it!',NULL,36,46),
 (11266,1,'And when it is said to them: Spend out of what Allah has given you, those who disbelieve say to those who believe: Shall we feed him whom, if Allah please, He could feed? You are in naught but clear error.',NULL,36,47),
 (11267,2,'And when they are told, "Spend ye of (the bounties) with which Allah has provided you," the Unbelievers say to those who believe: "Shall we then feed those whom, if Allah had so willed, He would have fed, (Himself)?- Ye are in nothing but manifest error."',NULL,36,47),
 (11268,3,'And when it is said unto them: Spend of that wherewith Allah hath provided you, those who disbelieve say unto those who believe: Shall we feed those whom Allah, if He willed, would feed? Ye are in naught else than error manifest.',NULL,36,47),
 (11269,1,'And they say: When will this threat come to pass, if you are truthful?',NULL,36,48),
 (11270,2,'Further, they say, "When will this promise (come to pass), if what ye say is true?"',NULL,36,48),
 (11271,3,'And they say: When will this promise be fulfilled, if ye are truthful?',NULL,36,48),
 (11272,1,'They wait not for aught but a single cry which will overtake them while they yet contend with one another.',NULL,36,49),
 (11273,2,'They will not (have to) wait for aught but a single Blast: it will seize them while they are yet disputing among themselves!',NULL,36,49),
 (11274,3,'They await but one Shout, which will surprise them while they are disputing.',NULL,36,49),
 (11275,1,'So they shall not be able to make a bequest, nor shall they return to their families.',NULL,36,50),
 (11276,2,'No (chance) will they then have, by will, to dispose (of their affairs), nor to return to their own people!',NULL,36,50),
 (11277,3,'Then they cannot make bequest, nor can they return to their own folk.',NULL,36,50),
 (11278,1,'And the trumpet shall be blown, when lo ! from their graves they shall hasten on to their Lord.',NULL,36,51),
 (11279,2,'The trumpet shall be sounded, when behold! from the sepulchres (men) will rush forth to their Lord!',NULL,36,51),
 (11280,3,'And the trumpet is blown and lo! from the graves they hie unto their Lord,',NULL,36,51),
 (11281,1,'They shall say: O woe to us! who has raised us up from our sleeping-place? This is what the Beneficent Allah promised and the messengers told the truth.',NULL,36,52),
 (11282,2,'They will say: "Ah! Woe unto us! Who hath raised us up from our beds of repose?"... (A voice will say:) "This is what (Allah) Most Gracious had promised. And true was the word of the messengers!"',NULL,36,52),
 (11283,3,'Crying: Woe upon us! Who hath raised us from our place of sleep? This is that which the Beneficent did promise, and the messengers spoke truth.',NULL,36,52),
 (11284,1,'There would be naught but a single cry, when lo ! they shall all be brought before Us;',NULL,36,53),
 (11285,2,'It will be no more than a single Blast, when lo! they will all be brought up before Us!',NULL,36,53),
 (11286,3,'It is but one Shout, and behold them brought together before Us!',NULL,36,53),
 (11287,1,'So this day no soul shall be dealt with unjustly in the least; and you shall not be rewarded aught but that which you did.',NULL,36,54),
 (11288,2,'Then, on that Day, not a soul will be wronged in the least, and ye shall but be repaid the meeds of your past Deeds.',NULL,36,54),
 (11289,3,'This day no soul is wronged in aught; nor are ye requited aught save what ye used to do.',NULL,36,54),
 (11290,1,'Surely the dwellers of the garden shall on that day be in an occupation quite happy.',NULL,36,55),
 (11291,2,'Verily the Companions of the Garden shall that Day have joy in all that they do;',NULL,36,55),
 (11292,3,'Lo! those who merit paradise this day are happily employed,',NULL,36,55),
 (11293,1,'They and their wives shall be in shades, reclining on raised couches.',NULL,36,56),
 (11294,2,'They and their associates will be in groves of (cool) shade, reclining on Thrones (of dignity);',NULL,36,56),
 (11295,3,'They and their wives, in pleasant shade, on thrones reclining;',NULL,36,56),
 (11296,1,'They shall have fruits therein, and they shall have whatever they desire.',NULL,36,57),
 (11297,2,'(Every) fruit (enjoyment) will be there for them; they shall have whatever they call for;',NULL,36,57),
 (11298,3,'Theirs the fruit (of their good deeds) and theirs (all) that they ask;',NULL,36,57),
 (11299,1,'Peace: a word from a Merciful Lord.',NULL,36,58),
 (11300,2,'"Peace!" - a word (of salutation) from a Lord Most Merciful!',NULL,36,58),
 (11301,3,'The word from a Merciful Lord (for them) is: Peace!',NULL,36,58),
 (11302,1,'And get aside today, O guilty ones!',NULL,36,59),
 (11303,2,'"And O ye in sin! Get ye apart this Day!',NULL,36,59),
 (11304,3,'But avaunt ye, O ye guilty, this day!',NULL,36,59),
 (11305,1,'Did I not charge you, O children of Adam ! that you should not serve the Shaitan? Surely he is your open enemy,',NULL,36,60),
 (11306,2,'"Did I not enjoin on you, O ye Children of Adam, that ye should not worship Satan; for that he was to you an enemy avowed?-',NULL,36,60),
 (11307,3,'Did I not charge you, O ye sons of Adam, that ye worship not the devil - Lo! he is your open foe! -',NULL,36,60),
 (11308,1,'And that you should serve Me; this is the right way.',NULL,36,61),
 (11309,2,'"And that ye should worship Me, (for that) this was the Straight Way?',NULL,36,61),
 (11310,3,'But that ye worship Me? That was the right path.',NULL,36,61),
 (11311,1,'And certainly he led astray numerous people from among you. What! could you not then understand?',NULL,36,62),
 (11312,2,'"But he did lead astray a great multitude of you. Did ye not, then, understand?',NULL,36,62),
 (11313,3,'Yet he hath led astray of you a great multitude. Had ye then no sense?',NULL,36,62),
 (11314,1,'This is the hell with which you were threatened.',NULL,36,63),
 (11315,2,'"This is the Hell of which ye were (repeatedly) warned!',NULL,36,63),
 (11316,3,'This is hell which ye were promised (if ye followed him).',NULL,36,63),
 (11317,1,'Enter into it this day because you disbelieved.',NULL,36,64),
 (11318,2,'"Embrace ye the (fire) this Day, for that ye (persistently) rejected (Truth)."',NULL,36,64),
 (11319,3,'Burn therein this day for that ye disbelieved.',NULL,36,64),
 (11320,1,'On that day We will set a seal upon their mouths, and their hands shall speak to Us, and their feet shall bear witness of what they earned.',NULL,36,65),
 (11321,2,'That Day shall We set a seal on their mouths. But their hands will speak to us, and their feet bear witness, to all that they did.',NULL,36,65),
 (11322,3,'This day We seal up their mouths, and their hands speak out to Us and their feet bear witness as to what they used to earn.',NULL,36,65),
 (11323,1,'And if We please We would certainly put out their eyes, then they would run about groping for the way, but how should they see?',NULL,36,66),
 (11324,2,'If it had been our Will, We could surely have blotted out their eyes; then should they have run about groping for the Path, but how could they have seen?',NULL,36,66),
 (11325,3,'And had We willed, We verily could have quenched their eyesight so that they should struggle for the way. Then how could they have seen?',NULL,36,66),
 (11326,1,'And if We please We would surely transform them in their place, then they would not be able to go on, nor will they return.',NULL,36,67),
 (11327,2,'And if it had been Our Will, We could have transformed them (to remain) in their places; then should they have been unable to move about, nor could they have returned (after error).',NULL,36,67),
 (11328,3,'And had We willed, We verily could have fixed them in their place, making them powerless to go forward or turn back.',NULL,36,67),
 (11329,1,'And whomsoever We cause to live long, We reduce (him) to an abject state in constitution; do they not then understand?',NULL,36,68),
 (11330,2,'If We grant long life to any, We cause him to be reversed in nature: Will they not then understand?',NULL,36,68),
 (11331,3,'He whom we bring unto old age, We reverse him in creation (making him go back to weakness after strength). Have ye then no sense?',NULL,36,68),
 (11332,1,'And We have not taught him poetry, nor is it meet for him; it is nothing but a reminder and a plain Quran,',NULL,36,69),
 (11333,2,'We have not instructed the (Prophet) in Poetry, nor is it meet for him: this is no less than a Message and a Qur''an making things clear:',NULL,36,69),
 (11334,3,'And We have not taught him (Muhammad) poetry, nor is it meet for him. This is naught else than a Reminder and a Lecture making plain,',NULL,36,69),
 (11335,1,'That it may warn him who would have life, and (that) the word may prove true against the unbelievers.',NULL,36,70),
 (11336,2,'That it may give admonition to any (who are) alive, and that the charge may be proved against those who reject (Truth).',NULL,36,70),
 (11337,3,'To warn whosoever liveth, and that the word may be fulfilled against the disbelievers.',NULL,36,70),
 (11338,1,'Do they not see that We have created cattle for them, out of what Our hands have wrought, so they are their masters?',NULL,36,71),
 (11339,2,'See they not that it is We Who have created for them - among the things which Our hands have fashioned - cattle, which are under their dominion?-',NULL,36,71),
 (11340,3,'Have they not seen how We have created for them of Our handiwork the cattle, so that they are their owners,',NULL,36,71),
 (11341,1,'And We have subjected them to them, so some of them they have to ride upon, and some of them they eat.',NULL,36,72),
 (11342,2,'And that We have subjected them to their (use)? of them some do carry them and some they eat:',NULL,36,72),
 (11343,3,'And have subdued them unto them, so that some of them they have for riding, some for food?',NULL,36,72),
 (11344,1,'And therein they have advantages and drinks; will they not then be grateful?',NULL,36,73),
 (11345,2,'And they have (other) profits from them (besides), and they get (milk) to drink. Will they not then be grateful?',NULL,36,73),
 (11346,3,'Benefits and (divers) drinks have they from them. Will they not then give thanks?',NULL,36,73),
 (11347,1,'And they have taken gods besides Allah that they may be helped.',NULL,36,74),
 (11348,2,'Yet they take (for worship) gods other than Allah, (hoping) that they might be helped!',NULL,36,74),
 (11349,3,'And they have taken (other) gods beside Allah, in order that they may be helped.',NULL,36,74),
 (11350,1,'(But) they shall not be able to assist them, and they shall be a host brought up before them.',NULL,36,75),
 (11351,2,'They have not the power to help them: but they will be brought up (before Our Judgment-seat) as a troop (to be condemned).',NULL,36,75),
 (11352,3,'It is not in their power to help them; but they (the worshippers) are unto them a host in arms.',NULL,36,75),
 (11353,1,'Therefore let not their speech grieve you; surely We know what they do in secret and what they do openly.',NULL,36,76),
 (11354,2,'Let not their speech, then, grieve thee. Verily We know what they hide as well as what they disclose.',NULL,36,76),
 (11355,3,'So let not their speech grieve thee (O Muhammad). Lo! We know what they conceal and what proclaim.',NULL,36,76),
 (11356,1,'Does not man see that We have created him from the small seed? Then lo! he is an open disputant.',NULL,36,77),
 (11357,2,'Doth not man see that it is We Who created him from sperm? yet behold! he (stands forth) as an open adversary!',NULL,36,77),
 (11358,3,'Hath not man seen that We have created him from a drop of seed? Yet lo! he is an open opponent.',NULL,36,77),
 (11359,1,'And he strikes out a likeness for Us and forgets his own creation. Says he: Who will give life to the bones when they are rotten?',NULL,36,78),
 (11360,2,'And he makes comparisons for Us, and forgets his own (origin and) Creation: He says, "Who can give life to (dry) bones and decomposed ones (at that)?"',NULL,36,78),
 (11361,3,'And he hath coined for Us a similitude, and hath forgotten the fact of his creation, saying: Who will revive these bones when they have rotted away?',NULL,36,78),
 (11362,1,'Say: He will give life to them Who brought them into existence at first, and He is cognizant of all creation',NULL,36,79),
 (11363,2,'Say, "He will give them life Who created them for the first time! for He is Well-versed in every kind of creation!-',NULL,36,79),
 (11364,3,'Say: He will revive them Who produced them at the first, for He is Knower of every creation,',NULL,36,79),
 (11365,1,'He Who has made for you the fire (to burn) from the green tree, so that with it you kindle (fire).',NULL,36,80),
 (11366,2,'"The same Who produces for you fire out of the green tree, when behold! ye kindle therewith (your own fires)!',NULL,36,80),
 (11367,3,'Who hath appointed for you fire from the green tree, and behold! ye kindle from it.',NULL,36,80),
 (11368,1,'Is not He Who created the heavens and the earth able to create the like of them? Yea! and He is the Creator (of all), the Knower.',NULL,36,81),
 (11369,2,'"Is not He Who created the heavens and the earth able to create the like thereof?" - Yea, indeed! for He is the Creator Supreme, of skill and knowledge (infinite)!',NULL,36,81),
 (11370,3,'Is not He Who created the heavens and the earth Able to create the like of them? Aye, that He is! for He is the All-Wise Creator,',NULL,36,81),
 (11371,1,'His command, when He intends anything, is only to say to it: Be, so it is.',NULL,36,82),
 (11372,2,'Verily, when He intends a thing, His Command is, "be", and it is!',NULL,36,82),
 (11373,3,'But His command, when He intendeth a thing, is only that He saith unto it: Be! and it is.',NULL,36,82),
 (11374,1,'Therefore glory be to Him in Whose hand is the kingdom of all things, and to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,36,83),
 (11375,2,'So glory to Him in Whose hands is the dominion of all things: and to Him will ye be all brought back.',NULL,36,83),
 (11376,3,'Therefor Glory be to Him in Whose hand is the dominion over all things! Unto Him ye will be brought back.',NULL,36,83),
 (11377,1,'I swear by those who draw themselves out in ranks',NULL,37,1),
 (11378,2,'By those who range themselves in ranks,',NULL,37,1),
 (11379,3,'By those who set the ranks in battle order',NULL,37,1),
 (11380,1,'Then those who drive away with reproof,',NULL,37,2),
 (11381,2,'And so are strong in repelling (evil),',NULL,37,2),
 (11382,3,'And those who drive away (the wicked) with reproof',NULL,37,2),
 (11383,1,'Then those who recite, being mindful,',NULL,37,3),
 (11384,2,'And thus proclaim the Message (of Allah)!',NULL,37,3),
 (11385,3,'And those who read (the Word) for a reminder,',NULL,37,3),
 (11386,1,'Most surely your Allah is One:',NULL,37,4),
 (11387,2,'Verily, verily, your Allah is one!-',NULL,37,4),
 (11388,3,'Lo! thy Lord is surely One;',NULL,37,4),
 (11389,1,'The Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, and Lord of the easts.',NULL,37,5),
 (11390,2,'Lord of the heavens and of the earth and all between them, and Lord of every point at the rising of the sun!',NULL,37,5),
 (11391,3,'Lord of the heavens and of the earth and all that is between them, and Lord of the sun''s risings.',NULL,37,5),
 (11392,1,'Surely We have adorned the nearest heaven with an adornment, the stars,',NULL,37,6),
 (11393,2,'We have indeed decked the lower heaven with beauty (in) the stars,-',NULL,37,6),
 (11394,3,'Lo! We have adorned the lowest heaven with an ornament, the planets;',NULL,37,6),
 (11395,1,'And (there is) a safeguard against every rebellious Shaitan.',NULL,37,7),
 (11396,2,'(For beauty) and for guard against all obstinate rebellious evil spirits,',NULL,37,7),
 (11397,3,'With security from every froward devil.',NULL,37,7),
 (11398,1,'They cannot listen to the exalted assembly and they are thrown at from every side,',NULL,37,8),
 (11399,2,'(So) they should not strain their ears in the direction of the Exalted Assembly but be cast away from every side,',NULL,37,8),
 (11400,3,'They cannot listen to the Highest Chiefs for they are pelted from every side,',NULL,37,8),
 (11401,1,'Being driven off, and for them is a perpetual chastisement,',NULL,37,9),
 (11402,2,'Repulsed, for they are under a perpetual penalty,',NULL,37,9),
 (11403,3,'Outcast, and theirs is a perpetual torment;',NULL,37,9),
 (11404,1,'Except him who snatches off but once, then there follows him a brightly shining flame.',NULL,37,10),
 (11405,2,'Except such as snatch away something by stealth, and they are pursued by a flaming fire, of piercing brightness.',NULL,37,10),
 (11406,3,'Save him who snatcheth a fragment, and there pursueth him a piercing flame.',NULL,37,10),
 (11407,1,'Then ask them whether they are stronger in creation or those (others) whom We have created. Surely We created them of firm clay.',NULL,37,11),
 (11408,2,'Just ask their opinion: are they the more difficult to create, or the (other) beings We have created? Them have We created out of a sticky clay!',NULL,37,11),
 (11409,3,'Then ask them (O Muhammad): Are they stronger as a creation, or those (others) whom we have created? Lo! We created them of plastic clay.',NULL,37,11),
 (11410,1,'Nay! you wonder while they mock,',NULL,37,12),
 (11411,2,'Truly dost thou marvel, while they ridicule,',NULL,37,12),
 (11412,3,'Nay, but thou dost marvel when they mock',NULL,37,12),
 (11413,1,'And when they are reminded, they mind not,',NULL,37,13),
 (11414,2,'And, when they are admonished, pay no heed,-',NULL,37,13),
 (11415,3,'And heed not when they are reminded,',NULL,37,13),
 (11416,1,'And when they see a sign they incite one another to scoff,',NULL,37,14),
 (11417,2,'And, when they see a Sign, turn it to mockery,',NULL,37,14),
 (11418,3,'And seek to scoff when they behold a portent.',NULL,37,14),
 (11419,1,'And they say: This is nothing but clear magic:',NULL,37,15),
 (11420,2,'And say, "This is nothing but evident sorcery!',NULL,37,15),
 (11421,3,'And they say: Lo! this is mere magic;',NULL,37,15),
 (11422,1,'What! when we are dead and have become dust and bones, shall we then certainly be raised,',NULL,37,16),
 (11423,2,'"What! when we die, and become dust and bones, shall we (then) be raised up (again)',NULL,37,16),
 (11424,3,'When we are dead and have become dust and bones, shall we then, forsooth, be raised (again)?',NULL,37,16),
 (11425,1,'Or our fathers of yore?',NULL,37,17),
 (11426,2,'"And also our fathers of old?"',NULL,37,17),
 (11427,3,'And our forefathers?',NULL,37,17),
 (11428,1,'Say: Aye! and you shall be abject.',NULL,37,18),
 (11429,2,'Say thou: "Yea, and ye shall then be humiliated (on account of your evil)."',NULL,37,18),
 (11430,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Ye, in truth; and ye will be brought low.',NULL,37,18),
 (11431,1,'So it shall only be a single cry, when lo! they shall see.',NULL,37,19),
 (11432,2,'Then it will be a single (compelling) cry; and behold, they will begin to see!',NULL,37,19),
 (11433,3,'There is but one Shout, and lo! they behold,',NULL,37,19),
 (11434,1,'And they shall say: O woe to us! this is the day of requital.',NULL,37,20),
 (11435,2,'They will say, "Ah! Woe to us! This is the Day of Judgment!"',NULL,37,20),
 (11436,3,'And say: Ah, woe for us! This is the Day of Judgment.',NULL,37,20),
 (11437,1,'This is the day of the judgment which you called a lie.',NULL,37,21),
 (11438,2,'(A voice will say,) "This is the Day of Sorting Out, whose truth ye (once) denied!"',NULL,37,21),
 (11439,3,'This is the Day of Separation, which ye used to deny.',NULL,37,21),
 (11440,1,'Gather together those who were unjust and their associates, and what they used to worship',NULL,37,22),
 (11441,2,'"Bring ye up", it shall be said, "The wrong-doers and their wives, and the things they worshipped-',NULL,37,22),
 (11442,3,'(And it is said unto the angels): Assemble those who did wrong, together with their wives and what they used to worship',NULL,37,22),
 (11443,1,'Besides Allah, then lead them to the way to hell.',NULL,37,23),
 (11444,2,'"Besides Allah, and lead them to the Way to the (Fierce) Fire!',NULL,37,23),
 (11445,3,'Instead of Allah, and lead them to the path to hell;',NULL,37,23),
 (11446,1,'And stop them, for they shall be questioned:',NULL,37,24),
 (11447,2,'"But stop them, for they must be asked:',NULL,37,24),
 (11448,3,'And stop them, for they must be questioned.',NULL,37,24),
 (11449,1,'What is the matter with you that you do not help each other?',NULL,37,25),
 (11450,2,'"''What is the matter with you that ye help not each other?''"',NULL,37,25),
 (11451,3,'What aileth you that ye help not one another?',NULL,37,25),
 (11452,1,'Nay! on that day they shall be submissive.',NULL,37,26),
 (11453,2,'Nay, but that day they shall submit (to Judgment);',NULL,37,26),
 (11454,3,'Nay, but this day they make full submission.',NULL,37,26),
