 (11879,2,'"If only we had had before us a Message from those of old,',NULL,37,168),
 (11880,3,'If we had but a reminder from the men of old',NULL,37,168),
 (11881,1,'We would certainly have been the servants of Allah-- the purified ones.',NULL,37,169),
 (11882,2,'"We should certainly have been Servants of Allah, sincere (and devoted)!"',NULL,37,169),
 (11883,3,'We would be single-minded slaves of Allah.',NULL,37,169),
 (11884,1,'But (now) they disbelieve in it, so they will come to know.',NULL,37,170),
 (11885,2,'But (now that the Qur''an has come), they reject it: But soon will they know!',NULL,37,170),
 (11886,3,'Yet (now that it is come) they disbelieve therein; but they will come to know.',NULL,37,170),
 (11887,1,'And certainly Our word has already gone forth in respect of Our servants, the messengers:',NULL,37,171),
 (11888,2,'Already has Our Word been passed before (this) to our Servants sent (by Us),',NULL,37,171),
 (11889,3,'And verily Our word went forth of old unto Our bondmen sent (to warn)',NULL,37,171),
 (11890,1,'Most surely they shall be the assisted ones',NULL,37,172),
 (11891,2,'That they would certainly be assisted,',NULL,37,172),
 (11892,3,'That they verily would be helped,',NULL,37,172),
 (11893,1,'And most surely Our host alone shall be the victorious ones.',NULL,37,173),
 (11894,2,'And that Our forces,- they surely must conquer.',NULL,37,173),
 (11895,3,'And that Our host, they verily would be the victors.',NULL,37,173),
 (11896,1,'Therefore turn away from them till a time,',NULL,37,174),
 (11897,2,'So turn thou away from them for a little while,',NULL,37,174),
 (11898,3,'So withdraw from them (O Muhammad) awhile,',NULL,37,174),
 (11899,1,'And (then) see them, so they too shall see.',NULL,37,175),
 (11900,2,'And watch them (how they fare), and they soon shall see (how thou farest)!',NULL,37,175),
 (11901,3,'And watch, for they will (soon) see.',NULL,37,175),
 (11902,1,'What! would they then hasten on Our chastisement?',NULL,37,176),
 (11903,2,'Do they wish (indeed) to hurry on our Punishment?',NULL,37,176),
 (11904,3,'Would they hasten on Our doom?',NULL,37,176),
 (11905,1,'But when it shall descend in their court, evil shall then be the morning of the warned ones.',NULL,37,177),
 (11906,2,'But when it descends into the open space before them, evil will be the morning for those who were warned (and heeded not)!',NULL,37,177),
 (11907,3,'But when it cometh home to them, then it will be a hapless morn for those who have been warned.',NULL,37,177),
 (11908,1,'And turn away from them till a time',NULL,37,178),
 (11909,2,'So turn thou away from them for a little while,',NULL,37,178),
 (11910,3,'Withdraw from them awhile',NULL,37,178),
 (11911,1,'And (then) see, for they too shall see.',NULL,37,179),
 (11912,2,'And watch (how they fare) and they soon shall see (how thou farest)!',NULL,37,179),
 (11913,3,'And watch, for they will (soon) see.',NULL,37,179),
 (11914,1,'Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Honor, above what they describe.',NULL,37,180),
 (11915,2,'Glory to thy Lord, the Lord of Honour and Power! (He is free) from what they ascribe (to Him)!',NULL,37,180),
 (11916,3,'Glorified be thy Lord, the Lord of Majesty, from that which they attribute (unto Him)',NULL,37,180),
 (11917,1,'And peace be on the messengers.',NULL,37,181),
 (11918,2,'And Peace on the messengers!',NULL,37,181),
 (11919,3,'And peace be unto those sent (to warn).',NULL,37,181),
 (11920,1,'And all praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,37,182),
 (11921,2,'And Praise to Allah, the Lord and Cherisher of the Worlds.',NULL,37,182),
 (11922,3,'And praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,37,182),
 (11923,1,'Suad, I swear by the Quran, full of admonition.',NULL,38,1),
 (11924,2,'Sad: By the Qur''an, Full of Admonition: (This is the Truth).',NULL,38,1),
 (11925,3,'Sad. By the renowned Qur''an,',NULL,38,1),
 (11926,1,'Nay! those who disbelieve are in self-exaltation and opposition.',NULL,38,2),
 (11927,2,'But the Unbelievers (are steeped) in self-glory and Separatism.',NULL,38,2),
 (11928,3,'Nay, but those who disbelieve are in false pride and schism.',NULL,38,2),
 (11929,1,'How many did We destroy before them of the generations, then they cried while the time of escaping had passed away.',NULL,38,3),
 (11930,2,'How many generations before them did We destroy? In the end they cried (for mercy)- when there was no longer time for being saved!',NULL,38,3),
 (11931,3,'How many a generation We destroyed before them, and they cried out when it was no longer the time for escape!',NULL,38,3),
 (11932,1,'And they wonder that there has come to them a warner from among themselves, and the disbelievers say: This IS an enchanter, a liar.',NULL,38,4),
 (11933,2,'So they wonder that a Warner has come to them from among themselves! and the Unbelievers say, "This is a sorcerer telling lies!',NULL,38,4),
 (11934,3,'And they marvel that a warner from among themselves hath come unto them, and the disbelievers say: This is a wizard, a charlatan.',NULL,38,4),
 (11935,1,'What! makes he the gods a single Allah? A strange thing is this, to be sure!',NULL,38,5),
 (11936,2,'"Has he made the gods (all) into one Allah? Truly this is a wonderful thing!"',NULL,38,5),
 (11937,3,'Maketh he the gods One Allah? Lo! that is an astounding thing.',NULL,38,5),
 (11938,1,'And the chief persons of them break forth, saying: Go and steadily adhere to your gods; this is most surely a thing sought after.',NULL,38,6),
 (11939,2,'And the leader among them go away (impatiently), (saying), "Walk ye away, and remain constant to your gods! For this is truly a thing designed (against you)!',NULL,38,6),
 (11940,3,'The chiefs among them go about, exhorting: Go and be staunch to your gods! Lo! this is a thing designed.',NULL,38,6),
 (11941,1,'We never heard of this in the former faith; this is nothing but a forgery:',NULL,38,7),
 (11942,2,'"We never heard (the like) of this among the people of these latter days: this is nothing but a made-up tale!"',NULL,38,7),
 (11943,3,'We have not heard of this in later religion. This is naught but an invention.',NULL,38,7),
 (11944,1,'Has the reminder been revealed to him from among us? Nay! they are in doubt as to My reminder. Nay! they have not yet tasted My chastisement!',NULL,38,8),
 (11945,2,'"What! has the Message been sent to him - (Of all persons) among us?"...but they are in doubt concerning My (Own) Message! Nay, they have not yet tasted My Punishment!',NULL,38,8),
 (11946,3,'Hath the reminder been unto him (alone) among us? Nay, but they are in doubt concerning My reminder; nay but they have not yet tasted My doom.',NULL,38,8),
 (11947,1,'Or is it that they have the treasures of the mercy of your Lord, the Mighty, the great Giver?',NULL,38,9),
 (11948,2,'Or have they the treasures of the mercy of thy Lord,- the Exalted in Power, the Grantor of Bounties without measure?',NULL,38,9),
 (11949,3,'Or are theirs the treasures of the mercy of thy Lord, the Mighty, the Bestower?',NULL,38,9),
 (11950,1,'Or is it that theirs is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and what is between them? Then let them ascend by any',NULL,38,10),
 (11951,2,'Or have they the dominion of the heavens and the earth and all between? If so, let them mount up with the ropes and means (to reach that end)!',NULL,38,10),
 (11952,3,'Or is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them theirs? Then let them ascend by ropes!',NULL,38,10),
 (11953,1,'A host of deserters of the allies shall be here put to flight.',NULL,38,11),
 (11954,2,'But there - will be put to flight even a host of confederates.',NULL,38,11),
 (11955,3,'A defeated host are (all) the factions that are there.',NULL,38,11),
 (11956,1,'The people of Nuh and Ad, and Firon, the lord of spikes, rejected (messengers) before them.',NULL,38,12),
 (11957,2,'Before them (were many who) rejected messengers,- the people of Noah, and ''Ad, and Pharaoh, the Lord of Stakes,',NULL,38,12),
 (11958,3,'The folk of Noah before them denied (their messenger) and (so did the tribe of) A''ad, and Pharaoh firmly planted,',NULL,38,12),
 (11959,1,'And Samood and the people of Lut and the dwellers of the thicket; these were the parties.',NULL,38,13),
 (11960,2,'And Thamud, and the people of Lut, and the Companions of the Wood; - such were the Confederates.',NULL,38,13),
 (11961,3,'And (the tribe of) Thamud, and the folk of Lot, and the dwellers in the wood: these were the factions.',NULL,38,13),
 (11962,1,'There was none of them but called the messengers liars, so just was My retribution.',NULL,38,14),
 (11963,2,'Not one (of them) but rejected the messengers, but My punishment came justly and inevitably (on them).',NULL,38,14),
 (11964,3,'Not one of them but did deny the messengers, therefor My doom was justified,',NULL,38,14),
 (11965,1,'Nor do these await aught but a single cry, there being no delay in it.',NULL,38,15),
 (11966,2,'These (today) only wait for a single mighty Blast, which (when it comes) will brook no delay.',NULL,38,15),
 (11967,3,'These wait for but one Shout, there will be no second thereto.',NULL,38,15),
 (11968,1,'And they say: O our Lord! hasten on to us our portion before the day of reckoning.',NULL,38,16),
 (11969,2,'They say: "Our Lord! hasten to us our sentence (even) before the Day of Account!"',NULL,38,16),
 (11970,3,'They say: Our Lord! Hasten on for us our fate before the Day of Reckoning.',NULL,38,16),
 (11971,1,'Bear patiently what they say, and remember Our servant Dawood, the possessor of power; surely he was frequent m returning (to Allah).',NULL,38,17),
 (11972,2,'Have patience at what they say, and remember our servant David, the man of strength: for he ever turned (to Allah).',NULL,38,17),
 (11973,3,'Bear with what they say, and remember Our bondman David, lord of might, Lo! he was ever turning in repentance (toward Allah).',NULL,38,17),
 (11974,1,'Surely We made the mountains to sing the glory (of Allah) in unison with him at the evening and the sunrise,',NULL,38,18),
 (11975,2,'It was We that made the hills declare, in unison with him, Our Praises, at eventide and at break of day,',NULL,38,18),
 (11976,3,'Lo! We subdued the hills to hymn the praises (of their Lord) with him at nightfall and sunrise,',NULL,38,18),
 (11977,1,'And the birds gathered together; all joined in singing with him.',NULL,38,19),
 (11978,2,'And the birds gathered (in assemblies): all with him did turn (to Allah).',NULL,38,19),
 (11979,3,'And the birds assembled; all were turning unto Him.',NULL,38,19),
 (11980,1,'And We strengthened his kingdom and We gave him wisdom and a clear judgment.',NULL,38,20),
 (11981,2,'We strengthened his kingdom, and gave him wisdom and sound judgment in speech and decision.',NULL,38,20),
 (11982,3,'We made his kingdom strong and gave him wisdom and decisive speech.',NULL,38,20),
 (11983,1,'And has there come to you the story of the litigants, when they made an entry into the private chamber by ascending over the walls?',NULL,38,21),
 (11984,2,'Has the Story of the Disputants reached thee? Behold, they climbed over the wall of the private chamber;',NULL,38,21),
 (11985,3,'And hath the story of the litigants come unto thee? How they climbed the wall into the royal chamber;',NULL,38,21),
 (11986,1,'When they entered in upon Dawood and he was frightened at them, they said: Fear not; two litigants, of whom one has acted wrongfully towards the other, therefore decide between us with justice, and do not act unjustly, and guide us to the right way.',NULL,38,22),
 (11987,2,'When they entered the presence of David, and he was terrified of them, they said: "Fear not: we are two disputants, one of whom has wronged the other: Decide now between us with truth, and treat us not with injustice, but guide us to the even Path..',NULL,38,22),
 (11988,3,'How they burst in upon David, and he was afraid of them. They said: Be not afraid! (We are) two litigants, one of whom hath wronged the other, therefor judge aright between us; be not unjust; and show us the fair way.',NULL,38,22),
 (11989,1,'Surely this is my brother; he has ninety-nine ewes and I have a single ewe; but he said: Make it over to me, and he has prevailed against me in discourse.',NULL,38,23),
 (11990,2,'"This man is my brother: He has nine and ninety ewes, and I have (but) one: Yet he says, ''commit her to my care,'' and is (moreover) harsh to me in speech."',NULL,38,23),
 (11991,3,'Lo! this my brother hath ninety and nine ewes while I had one ewe; and he said: Entrust it to me, and he conquered me in speech.',NULL,38,23),
 (11992,1,'He said: Surely he has been unjust to you in demanding your ewe (to add) to his own ewes; and most surely most of the partners act wrongfully towards one another, save those who believe and do good, and very few are they; and Dawood was sure that We had tried him, so he sought the protection of his Lord and he fell down bowing and turned time after time (to Him).',NULL,38,24),
 (11993,2,'(David) said: "He has undoubtedly wronged thee in demanding thy (single) ewe to be added to his (flock of) ewes: truly many are the partners (in business) who wrong each other: Not so do those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, and how few are they?"...and David gathered that We had tried him: he asked forgiveness of his Lord, fell down, bowing (in prostration), and turned (to Allah in repentance).',NULL,38,24),
 (11994,3,'(David) said: He hath wronged thee in demanding thine ewe in addition to his ewes, and lo! many partners oppress one another, save such as believe and do good works, and they are few. And David guessed that We had tried him, and he sought forgiveness of his Lord, and he bowed himself and fell down prostrate and repented.',NULL,38,24),
 (11995,1,'Therefore We rectified for him this, and most surely he had a nearness to Us and an excellent resort.',NULL,38,25),
 (11996,2,'So We forgave him this (lapse): he enjoyed, indeed, a Near Approach to Us, and a beautiful place of (Final) Return.',NULL,38,25),
 (11997,3,'So We forgave him that; and lo! he had access to Our presence and a happy journey''s end.',NULL,38,25),
 (11998,1,'o Dawood ! surely We have made you a ruler in the land; so judge between men with justice and do not follow desire, lest it should lead you astray from the path of Allah; (as for) those who go astray from the path of Allah, they shall surely have a severe punishment because they forgot the day of reckoning.',NULL,38,26),
 (11999,2,'O David! We did indeed make thee a vicegerent on earth: so judge thou between men in truth (and justice): Nor follow thou the lusts (of thy heart), for they will mislead thee from the Path of Allah: for those who wander astray from the Path of Allah, is a Penalty Grievous, for that they forget the Day of Account.',NULL,38,26),
 (12000,3,'(And it was said unto him): O David! Lo! We have set thee as a viceroy in the earth; therefor judge aright between mankind, and follow not desire that it beguile thee from the way of Allah. Lo! those who wander from the way of Allah have an awful doom, forasmuch as they forgot the Day of Reckoning.',NULL,38,26),
 (12001,1,'And We did not create the heaven and the earth and what is between them in vain; that is the opinion of those who disbelieve then woe to those who disbelieve on account of the fire.',NULL,38,27),
 (12002,2,'Not without purpose did We create heaven and earth and all between! that were the thought of Unbelievers! but woe to the Unbelievers because of the Fire (of Hell)!',NULL,38,27),
 (12003,3,'And We created not the heaven and the earth and all that is between them in vain. That is the opinion of those who disbelieve. And woe unto those who disbelieve, from the Fire!',NULL,38,27),
 (12004,1,'Shall We treat those who believe and do good like the mischief-makers in the earth? Or shall We make those who guard (against evil) like the wicked?',NULL,38,28),
 (12005,2,'Shall We treat those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, the same as those who do mischief on earth? Shall We treat those who guard against evil, the same as those who turn aside from the right?',NULL,38,28),
 (12006,3,'Shall We treat those who believe and do good works as those who spread corruption in the earth; or shall We treat the pious as the wicked?',NULL,38,28),
 (12007,1,'(It is) a Book We have revealed to you abounding in good that they may ponder over its verses, and that those endowed with understanding may be mindful.',NULL,38,29),
 (12008,2,'(Here is) a Book which We have sent down unto thee, full of blessings, that they may mediate on its Signs, and that men of understanding may receive admonition.',NULL,38,29),
 (12009,3,'(This is) a Scripture that We have revealed unto thee, full of blessing, that they may ponder its revelations, and that men of understanding may reflect.',NULL,38,29),
 (12010,1,'And We gave to Dawood Sulaiman, most excellent the servant! Surely he was frequent in returning (to Allah).',NULL,38,30),
 (12011,2,'To David We gave Solomon (for a son),- How excellent in Our service! Ever did he turn (to Us)!',NULL,38,30),
 (12012,3,'And We bestowed on David, Solomon. How excellent a slave! Lo! he was ever turning in repentance (toward Allah).',NULL,38,30),
 (12013,1,'When there were brought to him in the evening (horses) still when standing, swift when running--',NULL,38,31),
 (12014,2,'Behold, there were brought before him, at eventide coursers of the highest breeding, and swift of foot;',NULL,38,31),
 (12015,3,'When there were shown to him at eventide lightfooted coursers',NULL,38,31),
 (12016,1,'Then he said: Surely I preferred the good things to the remembrance of my Lord-- until the sun set and time for Asr prayer was over, (he said):',NULL,38,32),
 (12017,2,'And he said, "Truly do I love the love of good, with a view to the glory of my Lord,"- until (the sun) was hidden in the veil (of night):',NULL,38,32),
 (12018,3,'And he said: Lo! I have preferred the good things (of the world) to the remembrance of my Lord; till they were taken out of sight behind the curtain.',NULL,38,32),
 (12019,1,'Bring them back to me; so he began to slash (their) legs and necks.',NULL,38,33),
 (12020,2,'"Bring them back to me." then began he to pass his hand over (their) legs and their necks.',NULL,38,33),
 (12021,3,'(Then he said): Bring them back to me, and fell to slashing (with his sword their) legs and necks.',NULL,38,33),
 (12022,1,'And certainly We tried Sulaiman, and We put on his throne a (mere) body, so he turned (to Allah).',NULL,38,34),
 (12023,2,'And We did try Solomon: We placed on his throne a body (without life); but he did turn (to Us in true devotion):',NULL,38,34),
 (12024,3,'And verily We tried Solomon, and set upon his throne a (mere) body. Then did he repent.',NULL,38,34),
 (12025,1,'He said: My Lord! do Thou forgive me and grant me a kingdom which is not fit for (being inherited by) anyone after me;',NULL,38,35),
 (12026,2,'He said, "O my Lord! Forgive me, and grant me a kingdom which, (it may be), suits not another after me: for Thou art the Grantor of Bounties (without measure).',NULL,38,35),
 (12027,3,'He said: My Lord! Forgive me and bestow on me sovereignty such as shall not belong to any after me. Lo! Thou art the Bestower.',NULL,38,35),
 (12028,1,'Then We made the wind subservient to him; it made his command to run gently wherever he desired,',NULL,38,36),
 (12029,2,'Then We subjected the wind to his power, to flow gently to his order, Whithersoever he willed,-',NULL,38,36),
 (12030,3,'So We made the wind subservient unto him, setting fair by his command whithersoever he intended.',NULL,38,36),
 (12031,1,'And the shaitans, every builder and diver,',NULL,38,37),
 (12032,2,'As also the evil ones, (including) every kind of builder and diver,-',NULL,38,37),
 (12033,3,'And the unruly, every builder and diver (made We subservient),',NULL,38,37),
 (12034,1,'And others fettered in chains.',NULL,38,38),
 (12035,2,'As also others bound together in fetters.',NULL,38,38),
 (12036,3,'And others linked together in chains,',NULL,38,38),
 (12037,1,'This is Our free gift, therefore give freely or withhold, without reckoning.',NULL,38,39),
 (12038,2,'"Such are Our Bounties: whether thou bestow them (on others) or withhold them, no account will be asked."',NULL,38,39),
 (12039,3,'(Saying): This is Our gift, so bestow thou, or withhold, without reckoning.',NULL,38,39),
 (12040,1,'And most surely he had a nearness to Us and an excellent resort.',NULL,38,40),
 (12041,2,'And he enjoyed, indeed, a Near Approach to Us, and a beautiful Place of (Final) Return.',NULL,38,40),
 (12042,3,'And lo! he hath favour with Us, and a happy journey''s end.',NULL,38,40),
 (12043,1,'And remember Our servant Ayyub, when he called upon his Lord: The Shaitan has afflicted me with toil and torment.',NULL,38,41),
 (12044,2,'Commemorate Our Servant Job. Behold he cried to his Lord: "The Evil One has afflicted me with distress and suffering!"',NULL,38,41),
 (12045,3,'And make mention (O Muhammad) of Our bondman Job, when he cried unto his Lord (saying): Lo! the devil doth afflict me with distress and torment.',NULL,38,41),
 (12046,1,'Urge with your foot; here is a cool washing-place and a drink.',NULL,38,42),
 (12047,2,'(The command was given:) "Strike with thy foot: here is (water) wherein to wash, cool and refreshing, and (water) to drink."',NULL,38,42),
 (12048,3,'(And it was said unto him): Strike the ground with thy foot. This (spring) is a cool bath and a refreshing drink.',NULL,38,42),
 (12049,1,'And We gave him his family and the like of them with them, as a mercy from Us, and as a reminder to those possessed of understanding.',NULL,38,43),
 (12050,2,'And We gave him (back) his people, and doubled their number,- as a Grace from Ourselves, and a thing for commemoration, for all who have Understanding.',NULL,38,43),
 (12051,3,'And We bestowed on him (again) his household and therewith the like thereof, a mercy from Us, and a memorial for men of understanding.',NULL,38,43),
 (12052,1,'And take in your hand a green branch and beat her with It and do not break your oath; surely We found him patient; most excellent the servant! Surely he was frequent m returning (to Allah).',NULL,38,44),
 (12053,2,'"And take in thy hand a little grass, and strike therewith: and break not (thy oath)." Truly We found him full of patience and constancy. How excellent in Our service! ever did he turn (to Us)!',NULL,38,44),
 (12054,3,'And (it was said unto him): Take in thine hand a branch and smite therewith, and break not thine oath. Lo! We found him steadfast, how excellent a slave! Lo! he was ever turning in repentance (to his Lord).',NULL,38,44),
 (12055,1,'And remember Our servants Ibrahim and Ishaq and Yaqoub, men of power and insight.',NULL,38,45),
 (12056,2,'And commemorate Our Servants Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, possessors of Power and Vision.',NULL,38,45),
 (12057,3,'And make mention of Our bondmen, Abraham, Isaac and Jacob, men of parts and vision.',NULL,38,45),
 (12058,1,'Surely We purified them by a pure quality, the keeping m mind of the (final) abode.',NULL,38,46),
 (12059,2,'Verily We did choose them for a special (purpose)- proclaiming the Message of the Hereafter.',NULL,38,46),
 (12060,3,'Lo! We purified them with a pure thought, remembrance of the Home (of the Hereafter).',NULL,38,46),
 (12061,1,'And most surely they were with Us, of the elect, the best.',NULL,38,47),
 (12062,2,'They were, in Our sight, truly, of the company of the Elect and the Good.',NULL,38,47),
 (12063,3,'Lo! in Our sight they are verily of the elect, the excellent.',NULL,38,47),
 (12064,1,'And remember Ismail and Al-Yasha and Zulkifl; and they were all of the best.',NULL,38,48),
 (12065,2,'And commemorate Isma''il, Elisha, and Zul-Kifl: Each of them was of the Company of the Good.',NULL,38,48),
 (12066,3,'And make mention of Ishmael and Elisha and Dhu''l-Kifl. All are of the chosen.',NULL,38,48),
 (12067,1,'This is a reminder; and most surely there is an excellent resort for those who guard (against evil),',NULL,38,49),
 (12068,2,'This is a Message (of admonition): and verily, for the righteous, is a beautiful Place of (Final) Return,-',NULL,38,49),
 (12069,3,'This is a reminder. And lo! for those who ward off (evil) is a happy journey''s end,',NULL,38,49),
 (12070,1,'The gardens of perpetuity, the doors are opened for them.',NULL,38,50),
 (12071,2,'Gardens of Eternity, whose doors will (ever) be open to them;',NULL,38,50),
 (12072,3,'Gardens of Eden, whereof the gates are opened for them,',NULL,38,50),
 (12073,1,'Reclining therein, calling therein for many fruits and drink.',NULL,38,51),
 (12074,2,'Therein will they recline (at ease): Therein can they call (at pleasure) for fruit in abundance, and (delicious) drink;',NULL,38,51),
 (12075,3,'Wherein, reclining, they call for plenteous fruit and cool drink (that is) therein.',NULL,38,51),
 (12076,1,'And with them shall be those restraining their eyes, equals in age.',NULL,38,52),
 (12077,2,'And beside them will be chaste women restraining their glances, (companions) of equal age.',NULL,38,52),
 (12078,3,'And with them are those of modest gaze, companions.',NULL,38,52),
 (12079,1,'This is what you are promised for the day of reckoning.',NULL,38,53),
 (12080,2,'Such is the Promise made, to you for the Day of Account!',NULL,38,53),
 (12081,3,'This it is that ye are promised for the Day of Reckoning.',NULL,38,53),
 (12082,1,'Most surely this is Our sustenance; it shall never come to an end;',NULL,38,54),
 (12083,2,'Truly such will be Our Bounty (to you); it will never fail;-',NULL,38,54),
 (12084,3,'Lo! this in truth is Our provision, which will never waste away.',NULL,38,54),
 (12085,1,'This (shall be so); and most surely there is an evil resort for the inordinate ones;',NULL,38,55),
 (12086,2,'Yea, such! but - for the wrong-doers will be an evil place of (Final) Return!-',NULL,38,55),
 (12087,3,'This (is for the righteous). And lo! for the transgressors there with be an evil journey''s end,',NULL,38,55),
 (12088,1,'Hell; they shall enter it, so evil is the resting-place.',NULL,38,56),
 (12089,2,'Hell!- they will burn therein, - an evil bed (indeed, to lie on)!-',NULL,38,56),
 (12090,3,'Hell, where they will burn, an evil resting-place.',NULL,38,56),
 (12091,1,'This (shall be so); so let them taste it, boiling and intensely cold (drink).',NULL,38,57),
 (12092,2,'Yea, such! - then shall they taste it,- a boiling fluid, and a fluid dark, murky, intensely cold!-',NULL,38,57),
 (12093,3,'Here is a boiling and an ice-cold draught, so let them taste it,',NULL,38,57),
 (12094,1,'And other (punishment) of the same kind-- of various sorts.',NULL,38,58),
 (12095,2,'And other Penalties of a similar kind, to match them!',NULL,38,58),
 (12096,3,'And other (torment) of the kind in pairs (the two extremes)!',NULL,38,58),
 (12097,1,'This is an army plunging in without consideration along with you; no welcome for them, surely they shall enter fire.',NULL,38,59),
 (12098,2,'Here is a troop rushing headlong with you! No welcome for them! truly, they shall burn in the Fire!',NULL,38,59),
 (12099,3,'Here is an army rushing blindly with you. (Those who are already in the Fire say): No word of welcome for them. Lo! they will roast at the Fire.',NULL,38,59),
 (12100,1,'They shall say: Nay! you-- no welcome to you: you did proffer it to us, so evil is the resting-place.',NULL,38,60),
 (12101,2,'(The followers shall cry to the misleaders:) "Nay, ye (too)! No welcome for you! It is ye who have brought this upon us! Now evil is (this) place to stay in!"',NULL,38,60),
 (12102,3,'They say: Nay, but you (misleaders), for you there is no word of welcome. Ye prepared this for us (by your misleading). Now hapless is the plight.',NULL,38,60),
 (12103,1,'They shall say: Our Lord! whoever prepared it first for us, add Thou to him a double chastisement in the fire.',NULL,38,61),
 (12104,2,'They will say: "Our Lord! whoever brought this upon us,- Add to him a double Penalty in the Fire!"',NULL,38,61),
 (12105,3,'They say: Our Lord! Whoever did prepare this for us, oh, give him double portion of the Fire!',NULL,38,61),
 (12106,1,'And they shall say: What is the matter with us that we do not see men whom we used to count among the vicious?',NULL,38,62),
 (12107,2,'And they will say: "What has happened to us that we see not men whom we used to number among the bad ones?',NULL,38,62),
 (12108,3,'And they say: What aileth us that we behold not men whom we were wont to count among the wicked?',NULL,38,62),
 (12109,1,'Was it that we (only) took them in scorn, or have our eyes (now) turned aside from them?',NULL,38,63),
 (12110,2,'"Did we treat them (as such) in ridicule, or have (our) eyes failed to perceive them?"',NULL,38,63),
 (12111,3,'Did we take them (wrongly) for a laughing-stock, or have our eyes missed them?',NULL,38,63),
 (12112,1,'That most surely is the truth: the contending one with another of the inmates of the fire.',NULL,38,64),
 (12113,2,'Truly that is just and fitting,- the mutual recriminations of the People of the Fire!',NULL,38,64),
 (12114,3,'Lo! that is very truth: the wrangling of the dwellers in the Fire.',NULL,38,64),
 (12115,1,'Say: I am only a warner, and there is no god but Allah, the One, the Subduer (of all):',NULL,38,65),
 (12116,2,'Say: "Truly am I a Warner: no god is there but the one Allah, Supreme and Irresistible,-',NULL,38,65),
 (12117,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): I am only a warner, and there is no Allah save Allah, the One, the Absolute,',NULL,38,65),
 (12118,1,'The Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, the Mighty, the most Forgiving.',NULL,38,66),
 (12119,2,'"The Lord of the heavens and the earth, and all between,- Exalted in Might, able to enforce His Will, forgiving again and again."',NULL,38,66),
 (12120,3,'Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, the Mighty, the Pardoning.',NULL,38,66),
 (12121,1,'Say: It is a message of importance,',NULL,38,67),
 (12122,2,'Say: "That is a Message Supreme (above all),-',NULL,38,67),
 (12123,3,'Say: It is tremendous tidings',NULL,38,67),
 (12124,1,'(And) you are turning aside from it:',NULL,38,68),
 (12125,2,'"From which ye do turn away!',NULL,38,68),
 (12126,3,'Whence ye turn away!',NULL,38,68),
 (12127,1,'I had no knowledge of the exalted chiefs when they contended:',NULL,38,69),
 (12128,2,'"No knowledge have I of the Chiefs on high, when they discuss (matters) among themselves.',NULL,38,69),
 (12129,3,'I had no knowledge of the Highest Chiefs when they disputed;',NULL,38,69),
 (12130,1,'Naught is revealed to me save that I am a plain warner.',NULL,38,70),
 (12131,2,'''Only this has been revealed to me: that I am to give warning plainly and publicly."',NULL,38,70),
 (12132,3,'It is revealed unto me only that I may be a plain warner.',NULL,38,70),
 (12133,1,'When your Lord said to the angels; Surely I am going to create a mortal from dust:',NULL,38,71),
 (12134,2,'Behold, thy Lord said to the angels: "I am about to create man from clay:',NULL,38,71),
 (12135,3,'When thy Lord said unto the angels: Lo! I am about to create a mortal out of mire,',NULL,38,71),
 (12136,1,'So when I have made him complete and breathed into him of My spirit, then fall down making obeisance to him.',NULL,38,72),
 (12137,2,'"When I have fashioned him (in due proportion) and breathed into him of My spirit, fall ye down in obeisance unto him."',NULL,38,72),
 (12138,3,'And when I have fashioned him and breathed into him of My Spirit, then fall down before him prostrate,',NULL,38,72),
 (12139,1,'And the angels did obeisance, all of them,',NULL,38,73),
 (12140,2,'So the angels prostrated themselves, all of them together:',NULL,38,73),
 (12141,3,'The angels fell down prostrate, every one,',NULL,38,73),
 (12142,1,'But not Iblis: he was proud and he was one of the unbelievers.',NULL,38,74),
 (12143,2,'Not so Iblis: he was haughty, and became one of those who reject Faith.',NULL,38,74),
 (12144,3,'Saving Iblis; he was scornful and became one of the disbelievers.',NULL,38,74),
 (12145,1,'He said: O Iblis! what prevented you that you should do obeisance to him whom I created with My two hands? Are you proud or are you of the exalted ones?',NULL,38,75),
 (12146,2,'(Allah) said: "O Iblis! What prevents thee from prostrating thyself to one whom I have created with my hands? Art thou haughty? Or art thou one of the high (and mighty) ones?"',NULL,38,75),
 (12147,3,'He said: O Iblis! What hindereth thee from falling prostrate before that which I have created with both My hands? Art thou too proud or art thou of the high exalted?',NULL,38,75),
 (12148,1,'He said: I am better than he; Thou hast created me of fire, and him Thou didst create of dust.',NULL,38,76),
 (12149,2,'(Iblis) said: "I am better than he: thou createdst me from fire, and him thou createdst from clay."',NULL,38,76),
 (12150,3,'He said: I am better than him. Thou createdst me of fire, whilst him Thou didst create of clay.',NULL,38,76),
 (12151,1,'He said: Then get out of it, for surely you are driven away:',NULL,38,77),
 (12152,2,'(Allah) said: "Then get thee out from here: for thou art rejected, accursed.',NULL,38,77),
 (12153,3,'He said: Go forth from hence, for lo! thou art outcast,',NULL,38,77),
 (12154,1,'And surely My curse is on you to the day of judgment.',NULL,38,78),
 (12155,2,'"And My curse shall be on thee till the Day of Judgment."',NULL,38,78),
 (12156,3,'And lo! My curse is on thee till the Day of Judgment.',NULL,38,78),
 (12157,1,'He said: My Lord! then respite me to the day that they are raised.',NULL,38,79),
 (12158,2,'(Iblis) said: "O my Lord! Give me then respite till the Day the (dead) are raised."',NULL,38,79),
 (12159,3,'He said: My Lord! Reprieve me till the day when they are raised.',NULL,38,79),
 (12160,1,'He said: Surely you are of the respited ones,',NULL,38,80),
 (12161,2,'(Allah) said: "Respite then is granted thee-',NULL,38,80),
 (12162,3,'He said: Lo! thou art of those reprieved',NULL,38,80),
 (12163,1,'Till the period of the time made known.',NULL,38,81),
 (12164,2,'"Till the Day of the Time Appointed."',NULL,38,81),
 (12165,3,'Until the day of the time appointed.',NULL,38,81),
 (12166,1,'He said: Then by Thy Might I will surely make them live an evil life, all,',NULL,38,82),
 (12167,2,'(Iblis) said: "Then, by Thy power, I will put them all in the wrong,-',NULL,38,82),
 (12168,3,'He said: Then, by Thy might, I surely will beguile them every one,',NULL,38,82),
 (12169,1,'Except Thy servants from among them, the purified ones.',NULL,38,83),
 (12170,2,'"Except Thy Servants amongst them, sincere and purified (by Thy Grace)."',NULL,38,83),
 (12171,3,'Save Thy single-minded slaves among them.',NULL,38,83),
 (12172,1,'He said: The truth then is and the truth do I speak:',NULL,38,84),
 (12173,2,'(Allah) said: "Then it is just and fitting- and I say what is just and fitting-',NULL,38,84),
 (12174,3,'He said: The Truth is, and the Truth I speak,',NULL,38,84),
 (12175,1,'That I will most certainly fill hell with you and with those among them who follow you, all.',NULL,38,85),
 (12176,2,'"That I will certainly fill Hell with thee and those that follow thee,- every one."',NULL,38,85),
 (12177,3,'That I shall fill hell with thee and with such of them as follow thee, together.',NULL,38,85),
 (12178,1,'Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it; nor am I of those who affect:',NULL,38,86),
 (12179,2,'Say: "No reward do I ask of you for this (Qur''an), nor am I a pretender.',NULL,38,86),
 (12180,3,'Say (O Muhammad, unto mankind): I ask of you no fee for this, and I am no simulating.',NULL,38,86),
 (12181,1,'It is nothing but a reminder to the nations;',NULL,38,87),
 (12182,2,'"This is no less than a Message to (all) the Worlds.',NULL,38,87),
 (12183,3,'Lo! it is naught else than a reminder for all peoples',NULL,38,87),
 (12184,1,'And most certainly you will come to know about it after a time.',NULL,38,88),
 (12185,2,'"And ye shall certainly know the truth of it (all) after a while."',NULL,38,88),
 (12186,3,'And ye will come in time to know the truth thereof.',NULL,38,88),
 (12187,1,'The revelation of the Book is from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,39,1),
 (12188,2,'The revelation of this Book is from Allah, the Exalted in Power, full of Wisdom.',NULL,39,1),
 (12189,3,'The revelation of the Scripture is from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,39,1),
 (12190,1,'Surely We have revealed to you the Book with the truth, therefore serve Allah, being sincere to Him in obedience.',NULL,39,2),
 (12191,2,'Verily it is We Who have revealed the Book to thee in Truth: so serve Allah, offering Him sincere devotion.',NULL,39,2),
 (12192,3,'Lo! We have revealed the Scripture unto thee (Muhammad) with truth; so worship Allah, making religion pure for Him (only).',NULL,39,2),
 (12193,1,'Now, surely, sincere obedience is due to Allah (alone) and (as for) those who take guardians besides Him, (saying), We do not serve them save that they may make us nearer to Allah, surely Allah will judge between them in that in which they differ; surely Allah does not guide him aright who is a liar, ungrateful.',NULL,39,3),
 (12194,2,'Is it not to Allah that sincere devotion is due? But those who take for protectors other than Allah (say): "We only serve them in order that they may bring us nearer to Allah." Truly Allah will judge between them in that wherein they differ. But Allah guides not such as are false and ungrateful.',NULL,39,3),
 (12195,3,'Surely pure religion is for Allah only. And those who choose protecting friends beside Him (say): We worship them only that they may bring us near unto Allah. Lo! Allah will judge between them concerning that wherein they differ. Lo! Allah guideth not him who is a liar, an ingrate.',NULL,39,3),
 (12196,1,'If Allah desire to take a son to Himself, He will surely choose those He pleases from what He has created. Glory be to Him: He is Allah, the One, the Subduer (of all).',NULL,39,4),
 (12197,2,'Had Allah wished to take to Himself a son, He could have chosen whom He pleased out of those whom He doth create: but Glory be to Him! (He is above such things.) He is Allah, the One, the Irresistible.',NULL,39,4),
 (12198,3,'If Allah had willed to choose a son, He could have chosen what He would of that which He hath created. Be He Glorified! He is Allah, the One, the Absolute.',NULL,39,4),
 (12199,1,'He has created the heavens and the earth with the truth; He makes the night cover the day and makes the day overtake the night, and He has made the sun and the moon subservient; each one runs on to an assigned term; now surely He is the Mighty, the great Forgiver.',NULL,39,5),
 (12200,2,'He created the heavens and the earth in true (proportions): He makes the Night overlap the Day, and the Day overlap the Night: He has subjected the sun and the moon (to His law): Each one follows a course for a time appointed. Is not He the Exalted in Power - He Who forgives again and again?',NULL,39,5),
 (12201,3,'He hath created the heavens and the earth with truth. He maketh night to succeed day, and He maketh day to succeed night, and He constraineth the sun and the moon to give service, each running on for an appointed term. Is not He the Mighty, the Forgiver?',NULL,39,5),
 (12202,1,'He has created you from a single being, then made its mate of the same (kind), and He has made for you eight of the cattle in pairs. He creates you in the wombs of your mothers-- a creation after a creation-- in triple darkness; that is Allah your Lord, His is the kingdom; there is no god but He; whence are you then turned away?',NULL,39,6),
 (12203,2,'He created you (all) from a single person: then created, of like nature, his mate; and he sent down for you eight head of cattle in pairs: He makes you, in the wombs of your mothers, in stages, one after another, in three veils of darkness. such is Allah, your Lord and Cherisher: to Him belongs (all) dominion. There is no god but He: then how are ye turned away (from your true Centre)?',NULL,39,6),
 (12204,3,'He created you from one being, then from that (being) He made its mate; and He hath provided for you of cattle eight kinds. He created you in the wombs of your mothers, creation after creation, in a threefold gloom. Such is Allah, your Lord. His is the Sovereignty. There is no Allah save Him. How then are ye turned away?',NULL,39,6),
 (12205,1,'If you are ungrateful, then surely Allah is Self-sufficient above all need of you; and He does not like ungratefulness in His servants; and if you are grateful, He likes it in you; and no bearer of burden shall bear the burden of another; then to your Lord is your return, then will He inform you of what you did; surely He is Cognizant of what is in the breasts.',NULL,39,7),
 (12206,2,'If ye reject (Allah), Truly Allah hath no need of you; but He liketh not ingratitude from His servants: if ye are grateful, He is pleased with you. No bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another. In the end, to your Lord is your Return, when He will tell you the truth of all that ye did (in this life). for He knoweth well all that is in (men''s) hearts.',NULL,39,7),
 (12207,3,'If ye are thankless, yet Allah is Independent of you, though He is not pleased with thanklessness for His bondmen; and if ye are thankful He is pleased therewith for you. No laden soul will bear another''s load. Then unto your Lord is your return; and He will tell you what ye used to do. Lo! He knoweth what is in the breasts (of men).',NULL,39,7),
 (12208,1,'And when distress afflicts a man he calls upon his Lord turning to Him frequently; then when He makes him possess a favor from Him, he forgets that for which he called upon Him before, and sets up rivals to Allah that he may cause (men) to stray off from His path. Say: Enjoy yourself in your ungratefulness a little, surely you are of the inmates of the fire.',NULL,39,8),
 (12209,2,'When some trouble toucheth man, he crieth unto his Lord, turning to Him in repentance: but when He bestoweth a favour upon him as from Himself, (man) doth forget what he cried and prayed for before, and he doth set up rivals unto Allah, thus misleading others from Allah''s Path. Say, "Enjoy thy blasphemy for a little while: verily thou art (one) of the Companions of the Fire!"',NULL,39,8),
 (12210,3,'And when some hurt toucheth man, he crieth unto his Lord, turning unto Him (repentant). Then, when He granteth him a boon from Him he forgetteth that for which he cried unto Him before, and setteth up rivals to Allah that he may beguile (men) from his way. Say (O Muhammad, unto such an one): Take pleasure in thy disbelief a while. Lo! thou art of the owners of the Fire.',NULL,39,8),
 (12211,1,'What! he who is obedient during hours of the night, prostrating himself and standing, takes care of the hereafter and hopes for the mercy of his Lord! Say: Are those who know and those who do not know alike? Only the men of understanding are mindful.',NULL,39,9),
 (12212,2,'Is one who worships devoutly during the hour of the night prostrating himself or standing (in adoration), who takes heed of the Hereafter, and who places his hope in the Mercy of his Lord - (like one who does not)? Say: "Are those equal, those who know and those who do not know? It is those who are endued with understanding that receive admonition.',NULL,39,9),
 (12213,3,'Is he who payeth adoration in the watches of the night, prostrate and standing, bewaring of the Hereafter and hoping for the mercy of his Lord, (to be accounted equal with a disbeliever)? Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Are those who know equal with those who know not? But only men of understanding will pay heed.',NULL,39,9),
 (12214,1,'Say: O my servants who believe! be careful of (your duty to) your Lord; for those who do good in this world is good, and Allah''s earth is spacious; only the patient will be paid back their reward in full without measure.',NULL,39,10),
 (12215,2,'Say: "O ye my servants who believe! Fear your Lord, good is (the reward) for those who do good in this world. Spacious is Allah''s earth! those who patiently persevere will truly receive a reward without measure!"',NULL,39,10),
 (12216,3,'Say: O My bondmen who believe! Observe your duty to your Lord. For those who do good in this world there is good, and Allah''s earth is spacious. Verily the steadfast will be paid their wages without stint.',NULL,39,10),
 (12217,1,'Say: I am commanded that I should serve Allah, being sincere to Him in obedience.',NULL,39,11),
 (12218,2,'Say: "Verily, I am commanded to serve Allah with sincere devotion;',NULL,39,11),
 (12219,3,'Say (O Muhammad): Lo! I am commanded to worship Allah, making religion pure for Him (only).',NULL,39,11),
 (12220,1,'And I am commanded that I shall be the first of those who submit.',NULL,39,12),
 (12221,2,'"And I am commanded to be the first of those who bow to Allah in Islam."',NULL,39,12),
 (12222,3,'And I am commanded to be the first of those who are muslims (surrender unto Him).',NULL,39,12),
 (12223,1,'Say: I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the chastisement of a grievous day.',NULL,39,13),
 (12224,2,'Say: "I would, if I disobeyed my Lord, indeed have fear of the Penalty of a Mighty Day."',NULL,39,13),
 (12225,3,'Say: Lo! if I should disobey my Lord, I fear the doom of a tremendous Day.',NULL,39,13),
 (12226,1,'Say: Allah (it is Whom) I serve, being sincere to Him in my obedience:',NULL,39,14),
 (12227,2,'Say: "It is Allah I serve, with my sincere (and exclusive) devotion:',NULL,39,14),
 (12228,3,'Say: Allah I worship, making my religion pure for Him (only).',NULL,39,14),
 (12229,1,'Serve then what you like besides Him. Say: The losers surely are those who shall have lost themselves and their families on the day of resurrection; now surely that is the clear loss.',NULL,39,15),
 (12230,2,'"Serve ye what ye will besides him." Say: "Truly, those in loss are those who lose their own souls and their People on the Day of Judgment: Ah! that is indeed the (real and) evident Loss!',NULL,39,15),
 (12231,3,'Then worship what ye will beside Him. Say: The losers will be those who lose themselves and their housefolk on the Day of Resurrection. Ah, that will be the manifest loss!',NULL,39,15),
 (12232,1,'They shall have coverings of fire above them and coverings beneath them; with that Allah makes His servants to fear, so be careful of (your duty to) Me, O My servants!',NULL,39,16),
 (12233,2,'They shall have Layers of Fire above them, and Layers (of Fire) below them: with this doth Allah warn off his servants: "O My Servants! then fear ye Me!"',NULL,39,16),
 (12234,3,'They have an awning of fire above them and beneath them a dais (of fire). With this doth Allah appal His bondmen. O My bondmen, therefor fear Me!',NULL,39,16),
 (12235,1,'And (as for) those who keep off from the worship of the idols and turn to Allah, they shall have good news, therefore give good news to My servants,',NULL,39,17),
 (12236,2,'Those who eschew Evil,- and fall not into its worship,- and turn to Allah (in repentance),- for them is Good News: so announce the Good News to My Servants,-',NULL,39,17),
 (12237,3,'And those who put away false gods lest they should worship them and turn to Allah in repentance, for them there are glad tidings. Therefor give good tidings (O Muhammad) to My bondmen',NULL,39,17),
 (12238,1,'Those who listen to the word, then follow the best of it; those are they whom Allah has guided, and those it is who are the men of understanding.',NULL,39,18),
 (12239,2,'Those who listen to the Word, and follow the best (meaning) in it: those are the ones whom Allah has guided, and those are the ones endued with understanding.',NULL,39,18),
 (12240,3,'Who hear advice and follow the best thereof. Such are those whom Allah guideth, and such are men of understanding.',NULL,39,18),
 (12241,1,'What! as for him then against whom the sentence of chastisement is due: What! can you save him who is in the fire?',NULL,39,19),
 (12242,2,'Is, then, one against whom the decree of Punishment is justly due (equal to one who eschews Evil)? Wouldst thou, then, deliver one (who is) in the Fire?',NULL,39,19),
 (12243,3,'Is he on whom the word of doom is fulfilled (to be helped), and canst thou (O Muhammad) rescue him who is in the Fire?',NULL,39,19),
 (12244,1,'But (as for) those who are careful of (their duty to) their Lord, they shall have high places, above them higher places, built (for them), beneath which flow rivers; (this is) the promise of Allah: Allah will not fail in (His) promise.',NULL,39,20),
 (12245,2,'But it is for those who fear their Lord. That lofty mansions, one above another, have been built: beneath them flow rivers (of delight): (such is) the Promise of Allah: never doth Allah fail in (His) promise.',NULL,39,20),
 (12246,3,'But those who keep their duty to their Lord, for them are lofty halls with lofty halls above them, built (for them), beneath which rivers flow. (It is) a promise of Allah. Allah faileth not His promise.',NULL,39,20),
 (12247,1,'Do you not see that Allah sends down water from the cloud, then makes it go along in the earth in springs, then brings forth therewith herbage of various colors, then it withers so that you see it becoming yellow, then He makes it a thing crushed and broken into pieces? Most surely there is a reminder in this for the men of understanding.',NULL,39,21),
 (12248,2,'Seest thou not that Allah sends down rain from the sky, and leads it through springs in the earth? Then He causes to grow, therewith, produce of various colours: then it withers; thou wilt see it grow yellow; then He makes it dry up and crumble away. Truly, in this, is a Message of remembrance to men of understanding.',NULL,39,21),
 (12249,3,'Hast thou not seen how Allah hath sent down water from the sky and hath caused it to penetrate the earth as watersprings, and afterward thereby produceth crops of divers hues; and afterward they wither and thou seest them turn yellow; then He maketh them chaff. Lo! herein verily is a reminder for men of understanding.',NULL,39,21),
 (12250,1,'What! is he whose heart Allah has opened for Islam so that he is in a light from his Lord (like the hard-hearted)? Nay, woe to those whose hearts are hard against the remembrance of Allah; those are in clear error.',NULL,39,22),
 (12251,2,'Is one whose heart Allah has opened to Islam, so that he has received Enlightenment from Allah, (no better than one hard-hearted)? Woe to those whose hearts are hardened against celebrating the praises of Allah! they are manifestly wandering (in error)!',NULL,39,22),
 (12252,3,'Is he whose bosom Allah hath expanded for Al-Islam, so that he followeth a light from his Lord, (as he who disbelieveth)? Then woe unto those whose hearts are hardened against remembrance of Allah. Such are in plain error.',NULL,39,22),
 (12253,1,'Allah has revealed the best announcement, a book conformable in its various parts, repeating, whereat do shudder the skins of those who fear their Lord, then their skins and their hearts become pliant to the remembrance of Allah; this is Allah''s guidance, He guides with it whom He pleases; and (as for) him whom Allah makes err, there is no guide for him.',NULL,39,23),
 (12254,2,'Allah has revealed (from time to time) the most beautiful Message in the form of a Book, consistent with itself, (yet) repeating (its teaching in various aspects): the skins of those who fear their Lord tremble thereat; then their skins and their hearts do soften to the celebration of Allah''s praises. Such is the guidance of Allah: He guides therewith whom He pleases, but such as Allah leaves to stray, can have none to guide.',NULL,39,23),
 (12255,3,'Allah hath (now) revealed the fairest of statements, a Scripture consistent, (wherein promises of reward are) paired (with threats of punishment), whereat doth creep the flesh of those who fear their Lord, so that their flesh and their hearts soften to Allah''s reminder. Such is Allah''s guidance, wherewith He guideth whom He will. And him whom Allah sendeth astray, for him there is no guide.',NULL,39,23),
 (12256,1,'Is he then who has to guard himself with his own person against the evil chastisement on the resurrection day? And it will be said to the unjust: Taste what you earned.',NULL,39,24),
 (12257,2,'Is, then, one who has to fear the brunt of the Penalty on the Day of Judgment (and receive it) on his face, (like one guarded therefrom)? It will be said to the wrong-doers: "Taste ye (the fruits of) what ye earned!"',NULL,39,24),
 (12258,3,'Is he then, who will strike his face against the awful doom upon the Day of Resurrection (as he who doeth right)? And it will be said unto the wrong-doers: Taste what ye used to earn.',NULL,39,24),
 (12259,1,'Those before them rejected (prophets), therefore there came to them the chastisement from whence they perceived not.',NULL,39,25),
 (12260,2,'Those before them (also) rejected (revelation), and so the Punishment came to them from directions they did not perceive.',NULL,39,25),
 (12261,3,'Those before them denied, and so the doom came on them whence they knew not.',NULL,39,25),
 (12262,1,'So Allah made them taste the disgrace in this world''s life, and certainly the punishment of the hereafter is greater; did they but know!',NULL,39,26),
 (12263,2,'So Allah gave them a taste of humiliation in the present life, but greater is the punishment of the Hereafter, if they only knew!',NULL,39,26),
 (12264,3,'Thus Allah made them taste humiliation in the life of the world, and verily the doom of the Hereafter will be greater if they did but know.',NULL,39,26),
 (12265,1,'And certainly We have set forth to men in this Quran similitudes of every sort that they may mind.',NULL,39,27),
 (12266,2,'We have put forth for men, in this Qur''an every kind of Parable, in order that they may receive admonition.',NULL,39,27),
 (12267,3,'And verily We have coined for mankind in this Qur''an all kinds of similitudes, that haply they may reflect;',NULL,39,27),
 (12268,1,'An Arabic Quran without any crookedness, that they may guard (against evil).',NULL,39,28),
 (12269,2,'(It is) a Qur''an in Arabic, without any crookedness (therein): in order that they may guard against Evil.',NULL,39,28),
 (12270,3,'A Lecture in Arabic, containing no crookedness, that haply they may ward off (evil).',NULL,39,28),
 (12271,1,'Allah sets forth an example: There is a slave in whom are (several) partners differing with one another, and there is another slave wholly owned by one man. Are the two alike in condition? (All) praise is due to Allah. Nay! most of them do not know.',NULL,39,29),
 (12272,2,'Allah puts forth a Parable a man belonging to many partners at variance with each other, and a man belonging entirely to one master: are those two equal in comparison? Praise be to Allah! but most of them have no knowledge.',NULL,39,29),
 (12273,3,'Allah coineth a similitude: A man in relation to whom are several part-owners, quarrelling, and a man belonging wholly to one man. Are the two equal in similitude? Praise be to Allah! But most of them know not.',NULL,39,29),
 (12274,1,'Surely you shall die and they (too) shall surely die.',NULL,39,30),
 (12275,2,'Truly thou wilt die (one day), and truly they (too) will die (one day).',NULL,39,30),
 (12276,3,'Lo! thou wilt die, and lo! they will die;',NULL,39,30),
 (12277,1,'Then surely on the day of resurrection you will contend one with another before. your Lord.',NULL,39,31),
 (12278,2,'In the end will ye (all), on the Day of Judgment, settle your disputes in the presence of your Lord.',NULL,39,31),
 (12279,3,'Then lo! on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord ye will dispute.',NULL,39,31),
 (12280,1,'Who is then more unjust than he who utters a lie against Allah and (he who) gives the lie to the truth when it comes to him; is there not in hell an abode for the unbelievers?',NULL,39,32),
 (12281,2,'Who, then, doth more wrong than one who utters a lie concerning Allah, and rejects the Truth when it comes to him; is there not in Hell an abode for blasphemers?',NULL,39,32),
 (12282,3,'And who doth greater wrong than he who telleth a lie against Allah, and denieth the truth when it reacheth him? Will not the home of disbelievers be in hell?',NULL,39,32),
 (12283,1,'And he who brings the truth and (he who) accepts it as the truth-- these are they that guard (against evil).',NULL,39,33),
 (12284,2,'And he who brings the Truth and he who confirms (and supports) it - such are the men who do right.',NULL,39,33),
 (12285,3,'And whoso bringeth the truth and believeth therein - Such are the dutiful.',NULL,39,33),
 (12286,1,'They shall have with their Lord what they please; that is the reward of the doers of good;',NULL,39,34),
 (12287,2,'They shall have all that they wish for, in the presence of their Lord: such is the reward of those who do good:',NULL,39,34),
 (12288,3,'They shall have what they will of their Lord''s bounty. That is the reward of the good:',NULL,39,34),
 (12289,1,'So that Allah will do away with the worst of what they did and give them their reward for the best of what they do.',NULL,39,35),
 (12290,2,'So that Allah will turn off from them (even) the worst in their deeds and give them their reward according to the best of what they have done.',NULL,39,35),
 (12291,3,'That Allah will remit from them the worst of what they did, and will pay them for reward the best they used to do.',NULL,39,35),
 (12292,1,'Is not Allah sufficient for His servant? And they seek to frighten you with those besides Him; and whomsoever Allah makes err, there is no guide for him.',NULL,39,36),
 (12293,2,'Is not Allah enough for his Servant? But they try to frighten thee with other (gods) besides Him! for such as Allah leaves to stray, there can be no guide.',NULL,39,36),
 (12294,3,'Will not Allah defend His slave? Yet they would frighten thee with those beside Him. He whom Allah sendeth astray, for him there is no guide.',NULL,39,36),
 (12295,1,'And whom Allah guides, there is none that can lead him astray; is not Allah Mighty, the Lord of retribution?',NULL,39,37),
 (12296,2,'And such as Allah doth guide there can be none to lead astray. Is not Allah Exalted in Power, (Able to enforce His Will), Lord of Retribution?',NULL,39,37),
 (12297,3,'And he whom Allah guideth, for him there can be no misleader. Is not Allah Mighty, Able to Requite (the wrong)?',NULL,39,37),
 (12298,1,'And should you ask them, Who created the heavens and the earth? They would most certainly say: Allah. Say: Have you then considered that what you call upon besides Allah, would they, if Allah desire to afflict me with harm, be the removers of His harm, or (would they), if Allah desire to show me mercy, be the withholders of His mercy? Say: Allah is sufficient for me; on Him do the reliant rely.',NULL,39,38),
 (12299,2,'If indeed thou ask them who it is that created the heavens and the earth, they would be sure to say, "Allah". Say: "See ye then? the things that ye invoke besides Allah,- can they, if Allah wills some Penalty for me, remove His Penalty?- Or if He wills some Grace for me, can they keep back his Grace?" Say: "Sufficient is Allah for me! In Him trust those who put their trust."',NULL,39,38),
 (12300,3,'And verily, if thou shouldst ask them: Who created the heavens and the earth? they will say: Allah. Say: Bethink you then of those ye worship beside Allah, if Allah willed some hurt for me, could they remove from me His hurt; or if He willed some mercy for me, could they restrain His mercy? Say: Allah is my all. In Him do (all) the trusting put their trust.',NULL,39,38),
 (12301,1,'Say: O my people! work in your place, surely I am a worker, so you will come to know.',NULL,39,39),
 (12302,2,'Say: "O my People! Do whatever ye can: I will do (my part): but soon will ye know-',NULL,39,39),
 (12303,3,'Say: O my people! Act in your manner. Lo! I (too) am acting. Thus ye will come to know',NULL,39,39),
 (12304,1,'Who it is to whom there shall come a punishment which will disgrace him and to whom will be due a lasting punishment.',NULL,39,40),
 (12305,2,'"Who it is to whom comes a Penalty of ignominy, and on whom descends a Penalty that abides."',NULL,39,40),
 (12306,3,'Who it is unto whom cometh a doom that will abase him, and on whom there falleth everlasting doom.',NULL,39,40),
 (12307,1,'Surely We have revealed to you the Book with the truth for the sake of men; so whoever follows the right way, it is for his own soul and whoever errs, he errs only to its detriment; and you are not a custodian over them.',NULL,39,41),
 (12308,2,'Verily We have revealed the Book to thee in Truth, for (instructing) mankind. He, then, that receives guidance benefits his own soul: but he that strays injures his own soul. Nor art thou set over them to dispose of their affairs.',NULL,39,41),
 (12309,3,'Lo! We have revealed unto thee (Muhammad) the Scripture for mankind with truth. Then whosoever goeth right it is for his soul, and whosoever strayeth, strayeth only to its hurt. And thou art not a warder over them.',NULL,39,41),
 (12310,1,'Allah takes the souls at the time of their death, and those that die not during their sleep; then He withholds those on whom He has passed the decree of death and sends the others back till an appointed term; most surely there are signs in this for a people who reflect.',NULL,39,42),
 (12311,2,'It is Allah that takes the souls (of men) at death; and those that die not (He takes) during their sleep: those on whom He has passed the decree of death, He keeps back (from returning to life), but the rest He sends (to their bodies) for a term appointed verily in this are Signs for those who reflect.',NULL,39,42),
 (12312,3,'Allah receiveth (men''s) souls at the time of their death, and that (soul) which dieth not (yet) in its sleep. He keepeth that (soul) for which He hath ordained death and dismisseth the rest till an appointed term. Lo! herein verily are portents for people who take thought.',NULL,39,42),
 (12313,1,'Or have they taken intercessors besides Allah? Say: what! even though they did not ever have control over anything, nor do they understand.',NULL,39,43),
 (12314,2,'What! Do they take for intercessors others besides Allah? Say: "Even if they have no power whatever and no intelligence?"',NULL,39,43),
 (12315,3,'Or choose they intercessors other than Allah? Say: What! Even though they have power over nothing and have no intelligence?',NULL,39,43),
 (12316,1,'Say: Allah''s is the intercession altogether; His is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, then to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,39,44),
 (12317,2,'Say: "To Allah belongs exclusively (the right to grant) intercession: to Him belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth: In the End, it is to Him that ye shall be brought back."',NULL,39,44),
 (12318,3,'Say: Unto Allah belongeth all intercession. His is the Sovereignty of the heavens and the earth. And afterward unto Him ye will be brought back.',NULL,39,44),
 (12319,1,'And when Allah alone is mentioned, the hearts of those who do not believe in the hereafter shrink, and when those besides Him are mentioned, lo! they are joyful.',NULL,39,45),
 (12320,2,'When Allah, the One and Only, is mentioned, the hearts of those who believe not in the Hereafter are filled with disgust and horror; but when (gods) other than He are mentioned, behold, they are filled with joy!',NULL,39,45),
 (12321,3,'And when Allah alone is mentioned, the hearts of those who believe not in the Hereafter are repelled, and when those (whom they worship) beside Him are mentioned, behold! they are glad.',NULL,39,45),
 (12322,1,'Say: O Allah! Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen! Thou (only) judgest between Thy servants as to that wherein they differ.',NULL,39,46),
 (12323,2,'Say: "O Allah! Creator of the heavens and the earth! Knower of all that is hidden and open! it is Thou that wilt judge between Thy Servants in those matters about which they have differed."',NULL,39,46),
 (12324,3,'Say: O Allah! Creator of the heavens and the earth! Knower of the Invisible and the Visible! Thou wilt judge between Thy slaves concerning that wherein they used to differ.',NULL,39,46),
 (12325,1,'And had those who are unjust all that is in the earth and the like of it with it, they would certainly offer it as ransom (to be saved) from the evil of the punishment on the day of resurrection; and what they never thought of shall become plain to them from Allah.',NULL,39,47),
 (12326,2,'Even if the wrong-doers had all that there is on earth, and as much more, (in vain) would they offer it for ransom from the pain of the Penalty on the Day of Judgment: but something will confront them from Allah, which they could never have counted upon!',NULL,39,47),
 (12327,3,'And though those who do wrong possess all that is in the earth, and therewith as much again, they verily will seek to ransom themselves therewith on the Day of Resurrection from the awful doom; and there will appear unto them, from their Lord, that wherewith they never reckoned.',NULL,39,47),
 (12328,1,'And the evil (consequences) of what they wrought shall become plain to them, and the very thing they mocked at shall beset them.',NULL,39,48),
 (12329,2,'For the evils of their Deeds will confront them, and they will be (completely) encircled by that which they used to mock at!',NULL,39,48),
 (12330,3,'And the evils that they earned will appear unto them, and that whereat they used to scoff will surround them.',NULL,39,48),
 (12331,1,'So when harm afflicts a man he calls upon Us; then, when We give him a favor from Us, he says: I have been given it only by means of knowledge. Nay, it is a trial, but most of them do not know.',NULL,39,49),
 (12332,2,'Now, when trouble touches man, he cries to Us: But when We bestow a favour upon him as from Ourselves, he says, "This has been given to me because of a certain knowledge (I have)!" Nay, but this is but a trial, but most of them understand not!',NULL,39,49),
 (12333,3,'Now when hurt toucheth a man he crieth unto Us, and afterward when We have granted him a boon from Us, he saith: Only by force of knowledge I obtained it. Nay, but it is a test. But most of them know not.',NULL,39,49),
 (12334,1,'Those before them did say it indeed, but what they earned availed them not.',NULL,39,50),
 (12335,2,'Thus did the (generations) before them say! But all that they did was of no profit to them.',NULL,39,50),
 (12336,3,'Those before them said it, yet (all) that they had earned availed them not;',NULL,39,50),
 (12337,1,'So there befell them the evil (consequences) of what they earned; and (as for) those who are unjust from among these, there shall befall them the evil (consequences) of what they earn, and they shall not escape.',NULL,39,51),
 (12338,2,'Nay, the evil results of their Deeds overtook them. And the wrong-doers of this (generation)- the evil results of their Deeds will soon overtake them (too), and they will never be able to frustrate (Our Plan)!',NULL,39,51),
 (12339,3,'But the evils that they earned smote them; and such of these as do wrong, the evils that they earn will smite them; they cannot escape.',NULL,39,51),
 (12340,1,'Do they not know that Allah makes ample the means of subsistence to whom He pleases, and He straitens; most surely there are signs in this for a people who believe.',NULL,39,52),
 (12341,2,'Know they not that Allah enlarges the provision or restricts it, for any He pleases? Verily, in this are Signs for those who believe!',NULL,39,52),
 (12342,3,'Know they not that Allah enlargeth providence for whom He will, and straiteneth it (for whom He will). Lo! herein verily are portents for people who believe.',NULL,39,52),
 (12343,1,'Say: O my servants! who have acted extravagantly against their own souls, do not despair of the mercy of Allah; surely Allah forgives the faults altogether; surely He is the Forgiving the Merciful.',NULL,39,53),
 (12344,2,'Say: "O my Servants who have transgressed against their souls! Despair not of the Mercy of Allah: for Allah forgives all sins: for He is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,39,53),
 (12345,3,'Say: O My slaves who have been prodigal to their own hurt! Despair not of the mercy of Allah, Who forgiveth all sins. Lo! He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,39,53),
 (12346,1,'And return to your Lord time after time and submit to Him before there comes to you the punishment, then you shall not be helped.',NULL,39,54),
 (12347,2,'"Turn ye to our Lord (in repentance) and bow to His (Will), before the Penalty comes on you: after that ye shall not be helped.',NULL,39,54),
 (12348,3,'Turn unto your Lord repentant, and surrender unto Him, before there come unto you the doom, when ye cannot be helped.',NULL,39,54),
 (12349,1,'And follow the best that has been revealed to you from your Lord before there comes to you the punishment all of a sudden while you do not even perceive;',NULL,39,55),
 (12350,2,'"And follow the best of (the courses) revealed to you from your Lord, before the Penalty comes on you - of a sudden while ye perceive not!-',NULL,39,55),
 (12351,3,'And follow the better (guidance) of that which is revealed unto you from your Lord, before the doom cometh on you suddenly when ye know not,',NULL,39,55),
 (12352,1,'Lest a soul should say: O woe to me! for what I fell short of my duty to Allah, and most surely I was of those who laughed to scorn;',NULL,39,56),
 (12353,2,'"Lest the soul should (then) say: ''Ah! Woe is me!- In that I neglected (my duty) towards Allah, and was but among those who mocked!''-',NULL,39,56),
 (12354,3,'Lest any soul should say: Alas, my grief that I was unmindful of Allah, and I was indeed among the scoffers!',NULL,39,56),
 (12355,1,'Or it should say: Had Allah guided me, I would certainly have been of those who guard (against evil);',NULL,39,57),
 (12356,2,'"Or (lest) it should say: ''If only Allah had guided me, I should certainly have been among the righteous!''-',NULL,39,57),
 (12357,3,'Or should say: If Allah had but guided me I should have been among the dutiful!',NULL,39,57),
 (12358,1,'Or it should say when it sees the punishment: Were there only a returning for me, I should be of the doers of good.',NULL,39,58),
 (12359,2,'"Or (lest) it should say when it (actually) sees the penalty: ''If only I had another chance, I should certainly be among those who do good!''',NULL,39,58),
 (12360,3,'Or should say, when it seeth the doom: Oh, that I had but a second chance that I might be among the righteous!',NULL,39,58),
 (12361,1,'Aye! My communications came to you, but you rejected them, and you were proud and you were one of the unbelievers.',NULL,39,59),
 (12362,2,'"(The reply will be:) ''Nay, but there came to thee my Signs, and thou didst reject them: thou wast Haughty, and became one of those who reject faith!''"',NULL,39,59),
 (12363,3,'(But now the answer will be): Nay, for My revelations came unto thee, but thou didst deny them and wast scornful and wast among the disbelievers.',NULL,39,59),
 (12364,1,'And on the day of resurrection you shall see those who lied against Allah; their faces shall be blackened. Is there not in hell an abode for the proud?',NULL,39,60),
 (12365,2,'On the Day of Judgment wilt thou see those who told lies against Allah;- their faces will be turned black; Is there not in Hell an abode for the Haughty?',NULL,39,60),
 (12366,3,'And on the Day of Resurrection thou (Muhammad) seest those who lied concerning Allah with their faces blackened. Is not the home of the scorners in hell?',NULL,39,60),
 (12367,1,'And Allah shall deliver those who guard (against evil) with their achievement; evil shall not touch them, nor shall they grieve.',NULL,39,61),
 (12368,2,'But Allah will deliver the righteous to their place of salvation: no evil shall touch them, nor shall they grieve.',NULL,39,61),
 (12369,3,'And Allah delivereth those who ward off (evil) because of their deserts. Evil toucheth them not, nor do they grieve.',NULL,39,61),
 (12370,1,'Allah is the Creator of every thing and He has charge over every thing.',NULL,39,62),
 (12371,2,'Allah is the Creator of all things, and He is the Guardian and Disposer of all affairs.',NULL,39,62),
 (12372,3,'Allah is Creator of all things, and He is Guardian over all things.',NULL,39,62),
 (12373,1,'His are the treasures of the heavens and the earth; and (as for) those who disbelieve in the communications of Allah, these it is that are the losers.',NULL,39,63),
 (12374,2,'To Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth: and those who reject the Signs of Allah,- it is they who will be in loss.',NULL,39,63),
 (12375,3,'His are the keys of the heavens and the earth, and they who disbelieve the revelations of Allah - such are they who are the losers.',NULL,39,63),
 (12376,1,'Say: What! Do you then bid me serve others than Allah, O ignorant men?',NULL,39,64),
 (12377,2,'Say: "Is it some one other than Allah that ye order me to worship, O ye ignorant ones?"',NULL,39,64),
 (12378,3,'Say (O Muhammad, to the disbelievers): Do ye bid me serve other than Allah? O ye fools!',NULL,39,64),
 (12379,1,'And certainly, it has been revealed to you and to those before you: Surely if you associate (with Allah), your work would certainly come to naught and you would certainly be of the losers.',NULL,39,65),
 (12380,2,'But it has already been revealed to thee,- as it was to those before thee,- "If thou wert to join (gods with Allah), truly fruitless will be thy work (in life), and thou wilt surely be in the ranks of those who lose (all spiritual good)".',NULL,39,65),
 (12381,3,'And verily it hath been revealed unto thee as unto those before thee (saying): If thou ascribe a partner to Allah thy work will fail and thou indeed wilt be among the losers.',NULL,39,65),
 (12382,1,'Nay! but serve Allah alone and be of the thankful.',NULL,39,66),
 (12383,2,'Nay, but worship Allah, and be of those who give thanks.',NULL,39,66),
 (12384,3,'Nay, but Allah must thou serve, and be among the thankful!',NULL,39,66),
 (12385,1,'And they have not honored Allah with the honor that is due to Him; and the whole earth shall be in His grip on the day of resurrection and the heavens rolled up in His right hand; glory be to Him, and may He be exalted above what they associate (with Him).',NULL,39,67),
 (12386,2,'No just estimate have they made of Allah, such as is due to Him: On the Day of Judgment the whole of the earth will be but His handful, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right hand: Glory to Him! High is He above the Partners they attribute to Him!',NULL,39,67),
 (12387,3,'And they esteem not Allah as He hath the right to be esteemed, when the whole earth is His handful on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens are rolled in His right hand. Glorified is He and High Exalted from all that they ascribe as partner (unto Him).',NULL,39,67),
 (12388,1,'And the trumpet shall be blown, so all those that are in the heavens and all those that are in the earth shall swoon, except such as Allah please; then it shall be blown again, then lo! they shall stand up awaiting.',NULL,39,68),
 (12389,2,'The Trumpet will (just) be sounded, when all that are in the heavens and on earth will swoon, except such as it will please Allah (to exempt). Then will a second one be sounded, when, behold, they will be standing and looking on!',NULL,39,68),
 (12390,3,'And the trumpet is blown, and all who are in the heavens and all who are in the earth swoon away, save him whom Allah willeth. Then it is blown a second time, and behold them standing waiting!',NULL,39,68),
 (12391,1,'And the earth shall beam with the light of its Lord, and the Book shall be laid down, and the prophets and the witnesses shall be brought up, and judgment shall be given between them with justice, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.',NULL,39,69),
 (12392,2,'And the Earth will shine with the Glory of its Lord: the Record (of Deeds) will be placed (open); the prophets and the witnesses will be brought forward and a just decision pronounced between them; and they will not be wronged (in the least).',NULL,39,69),
 (12393,3,'And the earth shineth with the light of her Lord, and the Book is set up, and the prophets and the witnesses are brought, and it is judged between them with truth, and they are not wronged.',NULL,39,69),
 (12394,1,'And every soul shall be paid back fully what it has done, and He knows best what they do.',NULL,39,70),
 (12395,2,'And to every soul will be paid in full (the fruit) of its Deeds; and (Allah) knoweth best all that they do.',NULL,39,70),
 (12396,3,'And each soul is paid in full for what it did. And He is Best Aware of what they do.',NULL,39,70),
 (12397,1,'And those who disbelieve shall be driven to hell in companies; until, when they come to it, its doors shall be opened, and the keepers of it shall say to them: Did not there come to you messengers from among you reciting to you the communications of your Lord and warning you of the meeting of this day of yours? They shall say: Yea! But the sentence of punishment was due against the unbelievers.',NULL,39,71),
 (12398,2,'The Unbelievers will be led to Hell in crowd: until, when they arrive, there, its gates will be opened. And its keepers will say, "Did not messengers come to you from among yourselves, rehearsing to you the Signs of your Lord, and warning you of the Meeting of This Day of yours?" The answer will be: "True: but the Decree of Punishment has been proved true against the Unbelievers!"',NULL,39,71),
 (12399,3,'And those who disbelieve are driven unto hell in troops till, when they reach it and the gates thereof are opened, and the warders thereof say unto them: Came there not unto you messengers of your own, reciting unto you the revelations of your Lord and warning you of the meeting of this your Day? they say: Yea, verily. But the word of doom of disbelievers is fulfilled.',NULL,39,71),
 (12400,1,'It shall be said: Enter the gates of hell to abide therein; so evil is the abode of the proud.',NULL,39,72),
 (12401,2,'(To them) will be said: "Enter ye the gates of Hell, to dwell therein: and evil is (this) Abode of the Arrogant!"',NULL,39,72),
 (12402,3,'It is said (unto them): Enter ye the gates of hell to dwell therein. Thus hapless is the journey''s end of the scorners.',NULL,39,72),
 (12403,1,'And those who are careful of (their duty to) their Lord shall be conveyed to the garden in companies; until when they come to it, and its doors shall be opened, and the keepers of it shall say to them: Peace be on you, you shall be happy; therefore enter it to abide.',NULL,39,73),
 (12404,2,'And those who feared their Lord will be led to the Garden in crowds: until behold, they arrive there; its gates will be opened; and its keepers will say: "Peace be upon you! well have ye done! enter ye here, to dwell therein."',NULL,39,73),
 (12405,3,'And those who keep their duty to their Lord are driven unto the Garden in troops till, when they reach it, and the gates thereof are opened, and the warders thereof say unto them: Peace be unto you! Ye are good, so enter ye (the Garden of delight), to dwell therein;',NULL,39,73),
 (12406,1,'And they shall say: (All) praise is due to Allah, Who has made good to us His promise, and He has made us inherit the land; we may abide in the garden where we please; so goodly is the reward of the workers.',NULL,39,74),
 (12407,2,'They will say: "Praise be to Allah, Who has truly fulfilled His Promise to us, and has given us (this) land in heritage: We can dwell in the Garden as we will: how excellent a reward for those who work (righteousness)!"',NULL,39,74),
 (12408,3,'They say: Praise be to Allah, Who hath fulfilled His promise unto us and hath made us inherit the land, sojourning in the Garden where we will! So bounteous is the wage of workers.',NULL,39,74),
 (12409,1,'And you shall see the angels going round about the throne glorifying the praise of their Lord; and judgment shall be given between them with justice, and it shall be said: All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,39,75),
 (12410,2,'And thou wilt see the angels surrounding the Throne (Divine) on all sides, singing Glory and Praise to their Lord. The Decision between them (at Judgment) will be in (perfect) justice, and the cry (on all sides) will be, "Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!"',NULL,39,75),
 (12411,3,'And thou (O Muhammad) seest the angels thronging round the Throne, hymning the praises of their Lord. And they are judged aright. And it is said: Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,39,75),
 (12412,1,'Ha Mim.',NULL,40,1),
 (12413,2,'Ha Mim',NULL,40,1),
 (12414,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,40,1),
 (12415,1,'The revelation of the Book is from Allah, the Mighty, the Knowing,',NULL,40,2),
 (12416,2,'The revelation of this Book is from Allah, Exalted in Power, Full of Knowledge,-',NULL,40,2),
 (12417,3,'The revelation of the Scripture is from Allah, the Mighty, the Knower,',NULL,40,2),
 (12418,1,'The Forgiver of the faults and the Acceptor of repentance, Severe to punish, Lord of bounty; there is no god but He; to Him is the eventual coming.',NULL,40,3),
 (12419,2,'Who forgiveth sin, accepteth repentance, is strict in punishment, and hath a long reach (in all things). there is no god but He: to Him is the final goal.',NULL,40,3),
 (12420,3,'The Forgiver of sin, the Accepter of repentance, the Stern in punishment, the Bountiful. There is no Allah save Him. Unto Him is the journeying.',NULL,40,3),
 (12421,1,'None dispute concerning the communications of Allah but those who disbelieve, therefore let not their going to and fro in the cities deceive you.',NULL,40,4),
 (12422,2,'None can dispute about the Signs of Allah but the Unbelievers. Let not, then, their strutting about through the land deceive thee!',NULL,40,4),
 (12423,3,'None argue concerning the revelations of Allah save those who disbelieve, so let not their turn of fortune in the land deceive thee (O Muhammad).',NULL,40,4),
 (12424,1,'The people of Nuh and the parties after them rejected (prophets) before them, and every nation purposed against their messenger to destroy him, and they disputed by means of the falsehood that they might thereby render null the truth, therefore I destroyed them; how was then My retribution!',NULL,40,5),
 (12425,2,'But (there were people) before them, who denied (the Signs),- the People of Noah, and the Confederates (of Evil) after them; and every People plotted against their prophet, to seize him, and disputed by means of vanities, therewith to condemn the Truth; but it was I that seized them! and how (terrible) was My Requital!',NULL,40,5),
 (12426,3,'The folk of Noah and the factions after them denied (their messengers) before these, and every nation purposed to seize their messenger and argued falsely, (thinking) thereby to refute the Truth. Then I seized them, and how (awful) was My punishment.',NULL,40,5),
 (12427,1,'And thus did the word of your Lord prove true against those who disbelieved that they are the inmates of the fire.',NULL,40,6),
 (12428,2,'Thus was the Decree of thy Lord proved true against the Unbelievers; that truly they are Companions of the Fire!',NULL,40,6),
 (12429,3,'Thus was the word of thy Lord concerning those who disbelieve fulfilled: That they are owners of the Fire.',NULL,40,6),
 (12430,1,'Those who bear the power and those around Him celebrate the praise of their Lord and believe in Him and ask protection for those who believe: Our Lord! Thou embracest all things in mercy and knowledge, therefore grant protection to those who turn (to Thee) and follow Thy way, and save them from the punishment of the hell:',NULL,40,7),
 (12431,2,'Those who sustain the Throne (of Allah) and those around it Sing Glory and Praise to their Lord; believe in Him; and implore Forgiveness for those who believe: "Our Lord! Thy Reach is over all things, in Mercy and Knowledge. Forgive, then, those who turn in Repentance, and follow Thy Path; and preserve them from the Penalty of the Blazing Fire!',NULL,40,7),
 (12432,3,'Those who bear the Throne, and all who are round about it, hymn the praises of their Lord and believe in Him and ask forgiveness for those who believe (saying): Our Lord! Thou comprehendest all things in mercy and knowledge, therefor forgive those who repent and follow Thy way. Ward off from them the punishment of hell.',NULL,40,7),
 (12433,1,'Our Lord! and make them enter the gardens of perpetuity which Thou hast promised to them and those who do good of their fathers and their wives and their offspring, surely Thou are the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,40,8),
 (12434,2,'"And grant, our Lord! that they enter the Gardens of Eternity, which Thou hast promised to them, and to the righteous among their fathers, their wives, and their posterity! For Thou art (He), the Exalted in Might, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,40,8),
 (12435,3,'Our Lord! And make them enter the Gardens of Eden which thou hast promised them, with such of their fathers and their wives and their descendants as do right. Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,40,8),
 (12436,1,'And keep them from evil deeds, and whom Thou keepest from evil deeds this day, indeed Thou hast mercy on him, and that is the mighty achievement.',NULL,40,9),
 (12437,2,'"And preserve them from (all) ills; and any whom Thou dost preserve from ills that Day,- on them wilt Thou have bestowed Mercy indeed: and that will be truly (for them) the highest Achievement".',NULL,40,9),
 (12438,3,'And ward off from them ill-deeds; and he from whom Thou wardest off ill-deeds that day, him verily hast Thou taken into mercy. That is the supreme triumph.',NULL,40,9),
 (12439,1,'Surely those who disbelieve shall be cried out to: Certainly Allah''s hatred (of you) when you were called upon to the faith and you rejected, is much greater than your hatred of yourselves.',NULL,40,10),
 (12440,2,'The Unbelievers will be addressed: "Greater was the aversion of Allah to you than (is) your aversion to yourselves, seeing that ye were called to the Faith and ye used to refuse."',NULL,40,10),
 (12441,3,'Lo! (on that day) those who disbelieve are informed by proclamation: Verily Allah''s abhorrence is more terrible than your abhorrence one of another, when ye were called unto the faith but did refuse.',NULL,40,10),
 (12442,1,'They shall say: Our Lord! twice didst Thou make us subject to death, and twice hast Thou given us life, so we do confess our faults; is there then a way to get out?',NULL,40,11),
 (12443,2,'They will say: "Our Lord! twice hast Thou made us without life, and twice hast Thou given us Life! Now have we recognised our sins: Is there any way out (of this)?"',NULL,40,11),
 (12444,3,'They say: Our Lord! Twice hast Thou made us die, and twice hast Thou made us live. Now we confess our sins. Is there any way to go out?',NULL,40,11),
 (12445,1,'That is because when Allah alone was called upon, you disbelieved, and when associates were given to Him, you believed; so judgment belongs to Allah, the High, the Great.',NULL,40,12),
 (12446,2,'(The answer will be:) "This is because, when Allah was invoked as the Only (object of worship), ye did reject Faith, but when partners were joined to Him, ye believed! the Command is with Allah, Most High, Most Great!"',NULL,40,12),
 (12447,3,'(It is said unto them): This is (your plight) because, when Allah only was invoked, ye disbelieved, but when some partner was ascribed to Him ye were believing. But the command belongeth only to Allah, the Sublime, the Majestic.',NULL,40,12),
 (12448,1,'He it is Who shows you His signs and sends down for you sustenance from heaven, and none minds but he who turns (to Him) again and again.',NULL,40,13),
 (12449,2,'He it is Who showeth you his Signs, and sendeth down sustenance for you from the sky: but only those receive admonition who turn (to Allah).',NULL,40,13),
 (12450,3,'He it is Who showeth you His portents, and sendeth down for you provision from the sky. None payeth heed save him who turneth (unto Him) repentant.',NULL,40,13),
 (12451,1,'Therefore call upon Allah, being sincere to Him in obedience, though the unbelievers are averse:',NULL,40,14),
 (12452,2,'Call ye, then, upon Allah with sincere devotion to Him, even though the Unbelievers may detest it.',NULL,40,14),
 (12453,3,'Therefor (O believers) pray unto Allah, making religion pure for Him (only), however much the disbelievers be averse -',NULL,40,14),
 (12454,1,'Possessor of the highest rank, Lord of power: He makes the inspiration to light by His command upon whom He pleases of His servants, that he may warn (men) of the day of meeting.',NULL,40,15),
 (12455,2,'Raised high above ranks (or degrees), (He is) the Lord of the Throne (of Authority): by His Command doth He send the Spirit (of inspiration) to any of His servants he pleases, that it may warn (men) of the Day of Mutual Meeting,-',NULL,40,15),
 (12456,3,'The Exalter of Ranks, the Lord of the Throne. He causeth the Spirit of His command upon whom He will of His slaves, that He may warn of the Day of Meeting,',NULL,40,15),
 (12457,1,'(Of) the day when they shall come forth, nothing concerning them remains hidden to Allah. To whom belongs the kingdom this day? To Allah, the One, the Subduer (of all).',NULL,40,16),
 (12458,2,'The Day whereon they will (all) come forth: not a single thing concerning them is hidden from Allah. Whose will be the dominion that Day?" That of Allah, the One the Irresistible!',NULL,40,16),
 (12459,3,'The day when they come forth, nothing of them being hidden from Allah. Whose is the Sovereignty this day? It is Allah''s, the One, the Almighty.',NULL,40,16),
 (12460,1,'This day every soul shall be rewarded for what it has earned; no injustice (shall be done) this day; surely Allah is quick in reckoning.',NULL,40,17),
 (12461,2,'That Day will every soul be requited for what it earned; no injustice will there be that Day, for Allah is Swift in taking account.',NULL,40,17),
 (12462,3,'This day is each soul requited that which it hath earned; no wrong (is done) this day. Lo! Allah is swift at reckoning.',NULL,40,17),
 (12463,1,'And warn them of the day that draws near, when hearts shall rise up to the throats, grieving inwardly; the unjust shall not have any compassionate friend nor any intercessor who should be obeyed.',NULL,40,18),
 (12464,2,'Warn them of the Day that is (ever) drawing near, when the hearts will (come) right up to the throats to choke (them); No intimate friend nor intercessor will the wrong-doers have, who could be listened to.',NULL,40,18),
 (12465,3,'Warn them (O Muhammad) of the Day of the approaching (doom), when the hearts will be choking the throats, (when) there will be no friend for the wrong-doers, nor any intercessor who will be heard.',NULL,40,18),
 (12466,1,'He knows the stealthy looks and that which the breasts conceal.',NULL,40,19),
 (12467,2,'(Allah) knows of (the tricks) that deceive with the eyes, and all that the hearts (of men) conceal.',NULL,40,19),
 (12468,3,'He knoweth the traitor of the eyes, and that which the bosoms hide.',NULL,40,19),
 (12469,1,'And Allah judges with the truth; and those whom they call upon besides Him cannot judge aught; surely Allah is the Hearing, the Seeing.',NULL,40,20),
 (12470,2,'And Allah will judge with (justice and) Truth: but those whom (men) invoke besides Him, will not (be in a position) to judge at all. Verily it is Allah (alone) Who hears and sees (all things).',NULL,40,20),
 (12471,3,'Allah judgeth with truth, while those to whom they cry instead of Him judge not at all. Lo! Allah, He is the Hearer, the Seer.',NULL,40,20),
 (12472,1,'Have they not travelled in the earth and seen how was the end of those who were before them? Mightier than these were they in strength-- and in fortifications in the land, but Allah destroyed them for their sins; and there was not for them any defender against Allah.',NULL,40,21),
 (12473,2,'Do they not travel through the earth and see what was the End of those before them? They were even superior to them in strength, and in the traces (they have left) in the land: but Allah did call them to account for their sins, and none had they to defend them against Allah.',NULL,40,21),
 (12474,3,'Have they not travelled in the land to see the nature of the consequence for those who disbelieved before them? They were mightier than these in power and (in the) traces (which they left behind them) in the earth. Yet Allah seized them for their sins, and they had no protector from Allah.',NULL,40,21),
 (12475,1,'That was because there came to them their messengers with clear arguments, but they rejected (them), therefore Allah destroyed them; surely He is Strong, Severe in retribution.',NULL,40,22),
 (12476,2,'That was because there came to them their messengers with Clear (Signs), but they rejected them: So Allah called them to account: for He is Full of Strength, Strict in Punishment.',NULL,40,22),
 (12477,3,'That was because their messengers kept bringing them clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty) but they disbelieved; so Allah seized them. Lo! He is Strong, severe in punishment.',NULL,40,22),
 (12478,1,'And certainly We sent Musa with Our communications and clear authority,',NULL,40,23),
 (12479,2,'Of old We sent Moses, with Our Signs and an authority manifest,',NULL,40,23),
 (12480,3,'And verily We sent Moses with Our revelations and a clear warrant',NULL,40,23),
 (12481,1,'To Firon and Haman and Qaroun, but they said: A lying magician.',NULL,40,24),
 (12482,2,'To Pharaoh, Haman, and Qarun; but they called (him)" a sorcerer telling lies!"...',NULL,40,24),
 (12483,3,'Unto Pharaoh and Haman and Korah, but they said: A lying sorcerer!',NULL,40,24),
 (12484,1,'So when he brought to them the truth from Us, they said: Slay the sons of those who believe with him and keep their women alive; and the struggle of the unbelievers will only come to a state of perdition.',NULL,40,25),
 (12485,2,'Now, when he came to them in Truth, from Us, they said, "Slay the sons of those who believe with him, and keep alive their females," but the plots of Unbelievers (end) in nothing but errors (and delusions)!...',NULL,40,25),
 (12486,3,'And when he brought them the Truth from Our presence, they said: Slay the sons of those who believe with him, and spare their women. But the plot of disbelievers is in naught but error.',NULL,40,25),
 (12487,1,'And Firon said: Let me alone that I may slay Musa and let him call upon his Lord; surely I fear that he will change your religion or that he will make mischief to appear in the land.',NULL,40,26),
 (12488,2,'Said Pharaoh: "Leave me to slay Moses; and let him call on his Lord! What I fear is lest he should change your religion, or lest he should cause mischief to appear in the land!"',NULL,40,26),
 (12489,3,'And Pharaoh said: Suffer me to kill Moses, and let him cry unto his Lord. Lo! I fear that he will alter your religion or that he will cause confusion in the land.',NULL,40,26),
 (12490,1,'And Musa said: Surely I take refuge with my Lord and-- your Lord from every proud one who does not believe in the day of reckoning.',NULL,40,27),
 (12491,2,'Moses said: "I have indeed called upon my Lord and your Lord (for protection) from every arrogant one who believes not in the Day of Account!"',NULL,40,27),
 (12492,3,'Moses said: Lo! I seek refuge in my Lord and your Lord from every scorner who believeth not in a Day of Reckoning.',NULL,40,27),
 (12493,1,'And a believing man of Firon''s people who hid his faith said: What! will you slay a man because he says: My Lord is Allah, and indeed he has brought to you clear arguments from your Lord? And if he be a liar, on him will be his lie, and if he be truthful, there will befall you some of that which he threatens you (with); surely Allah does not guide him who is extravagant, a liar:',NULL,40,28),
 (12494,2,'A believer, a man from among the people of Pharaoh, who had concealed his faith, said: "Will ye slay a man because he says, ''My Lord is Allah''?- when he has indeed come to you with Clear (Signs) from your Lord? and if he be a liar, on him is (the sin of) his lie: but, if he is telling the Truth, then will fall on you something of the (calamity) of which he warns you: Truly Allah guides not one who transgresses and lies!',NULL,40,28),
 (12495,3,'And a believing man of Pharaoh''s family, who hid his faith, said: Would ye kill a man because he saith: My Lord is Allah, and hath brought you clear proofs from your Lord? If he is lying, then his lie is upon him; and if he is truthful, then some of that wherewith he threateneth you will strike you. Lo! Allah guideth not one who is a prodigal, a liar.',NULL,40,28),
 (12496,1,'O my people! yours is the kingdom this day, being masters in the land, but who will help us against the punishment of Allah if it come to us? Firon said: I do not show you aught but that which I see (myself), and I do not make you follow any but the right way.',NULL,40,29),
 (12497,2,'"O my People! Yours is the dominion this day: Ye have the upper hand in the land: but who will help us from the Punishment of Allah, should it befall us?" Pharaoh said: "I but point out to you that which I see (myself); Nor do I guide you but to the Path of Right!"',NULL,40,29),
 (12498,3,'O my people! Yours is the kingdom to-day, ye being uppermost in the land. But who would save us from the wrath of Allah should it reach us? Pharaoh said: I do but show you what I think, and I do but guide you to wise policy.',NULL,40,29),
 (12499,1,'And he who believed said: O my people! surely I fear for you the like of what befell the parties:',NULL,40,30),
 (12500,2,'Then said the man who believed: "O my people! Truly I do fear for you something like the Day (of disaster) of the Confederates (in sin)!-',NULL,40,30),
 (12501,3,'And he who believed said: O my people! Lo! I fear for you a fate like that of the factions (of old);',NULL,40,30),
 (12502,1,'The like of what befell the people of Nuh and Ad and Samood and those after them, and Allah does not desire injustice for (His) servants;',NULL,40,31),
 (12503,2,'"Something like the fate of the People of Noah, the ''Ad, and the Thamud, and those who came after them: but Allah never wishes injustice to his Servants.',NULL,40,31),
 (12504,3,'A plight like that of Noah''s folk, and A''ad and Thamud, and those after them, and Allah willeth no injustice for (His) slaves.',NULL,40,31),
 (12505,1,'And, O my people! I fear for you the day of calling out,',NULL,40,32),
 (12506,2,'"And O my people! I fear for you a Day when there will be Mutual calling (and wailing),-',NULL,40,32),
 (12507,3,'And, O my people! Lo! I fear for you a Day of Summoning,',NULL,40,32),
 (12508,1,'The day on which you will turn back retreating; there shall be no savior for you from Allah, and whomsoever Allah causes to err, there is no guide for him:',NULL,40,33),
 (12509,2,'"A Day when ye shall turn your backs and flee: No defender shall ye have from Allah: Any whom Allah leaves to stray, there is none to guide...',NULL,40,33),
 (12510,3,'A day when ye will turn to flee, having no preserver from Allah: and he whom Allah sendeth astray, for him there is no guide.',NULL,40,33),
 (12511,1,'And certainly Yusuf came to you before with clear arguments, but you ever remained in doubt as to what he brought; until when he died, you said: Allah will never raise a messenger after him. Thus does Allah cause him to err who is extravagant, a doubter',NULL,40,34),
 (12512,2,'"And to you there came Joseph in times gone by, with Clear Signs, but ye ceased not to doubt of the (Mission) for which he had come: At length, when he died, ye said: ''No messenger will Allah send after him.'' thus doth Allah leave to stray such as transgress and live in doubt,-',NULL,40,34),
 (12513,3,'And verily Joseph brought you of old clear proofs, yet ye ceased not to be in doubt concerning what he brought you till, when he died, ye said: Allah will not send any messenger after him. Thus Allah deceiveth him who is a prodigal, a doubter.',NULL,40,34),
 (12514,1,'Those who dispute concerning the communications of Allah without any authority that He has given them; greatly hated is it by Allah and by-those who believe. Thus does Allah set a seal over the heart of every proud, haughty one.',NULL,40,35),
 (12515,2,'"(Such) as dispute about the Signs of Allah, without any authority that hath reached them, grievous and odious (is such conduct) in the sight of Allah and of the Believers. Thus doth Allah, seal up every heart - of arrogant and obstinate Transgressors."',NULL,40,35),
 (12516,3,'Those who wrangle concerning the revelations of Allah without any warrant that hath come unto them, it is greatly hateful in the sight of Allah and in the sight of those who believe. Thus doth Allah print on every arrogant, disdainful heart.',NULL,40,35),
 (12517,1,'And Firon said: O Haman! build for me a tower that I may attain the means of access,',NULL,40,36),
 (12518,2,'Pharaoh said: "O Haman! Build me a lofty palace, that I may attain the ways and means-',NULL,40,36),
 (12519,3,'And Pharaoh said: O Haman! Build for me a tower that haply I may reach the roads,',NULL,40,36),
 (12520,1,'The means of access to the heavens, then reach the god of Musa, and I surely think him to be a liar. And thus the evil of his deed was made fairseeming to Firon, and he was turned away from the way; and the struggle of Firon was not (to end) in aught but destruction.',NULL,40,37),
 (12521,2,'"The ways and means of (reaching) the heavens, and that I may mount up to the god of Moses: But as far as I am concerned, I think (Moses) is a liar!" Thus was made alluring, in Pharaoh''s eyes, the evil of his deeds, and he was hindered from the Path; and the plot of Pharaoh led to nothing but perdition (for him).',NULL,40,37),
 (12522,3,'The roads of the heavens, and may look upon the god of Moses, though verily I think him a liar. Thus was the evil that he did made fairseeming unto Pharaoh, and he was debarred from the (right) way. The plot of Pharaoh ended but in ruin.',NULL,40,37),
 (12523,1,'And he who believed said: O my people! follow me, I will guide you to the right course;',NULL,40,38),
 (12524,2,'The man who believed said further: "O my people! Follow me: I will lead you to the Path of Right.',NULL,40,38),
 (12525,3,'And he who believed said: O my people! Follow me. I will show you the way of right conduct.',NULL,40,38),
 (12526,1,'O my people! this life of the world is only a (passing) enjoyment, and surely the hereafter is the abode to settle;',NULL,40,39),
 (12527,2,'"O my people! This life of the present is nothing but (temporary) convenience: It is the Hereafter that is the Home that will last.',NULL,40,39),
 (12528,3,'O my people! Lo! this life of the world is but a passing comfort, and lo! the Hereafter, that is the enduring home.',NULL,40,39),
 (12529,1,'Whoever does an evil, he shall not be recompensed (with aught) but the like of it, and whoever does good, whether male or female, and he is a believer, these shall enter the garden, in which they shall be given sustenance without measure.',NULL,40,40),
 (12530,2,'"He that works evil will not be requited but by the like thereof: and he that works a righteous deed - whether man or woman - and is a Believer- such will enter the Garden (of Bliss): Therein will they have abundance without measure.',NULL,40,40),
 (12531,3,'Whoso doeth an ill-deed, he will be repaid the like thereof, while whoso doeth right, whether male or female, and is a believer, (all) such will enter the Garden, where they will be nourished without stint.',NULL,40,40),
 (12532,1,'And, O my people! how is it that I call you to salvation and you call me to the fire?',NULL,40,41),
 (12533,2,'"And O my people! How (strange) it is for me to call you to Salvation while ye call me to the Fire!',NULL,40,41),
 (12534,3,'And, O my people! What aileth me that I call you unto deliverance when ye call me unto the Fire?',NULL,40,41),
 (12535,1,'You call on me that I should disbelieve in Allah and associate with Him that of which I have no knowledge, and I call you to the Mighty, the most Forgiving;',NULL,40,42),
 (12536,2,'"Ye do call upon me to blaspheme against Allah, and to join with Him partners of whom I have no knowledge; and I call you to the Exalted in Power, Who forgives again and again!"',NULL,40,42),
 (12537,3,'Ye call me to disbelieve in Allah and ascribe unto Him as partners that whereof I have no knowledge, while I call you unto the Mighty, the Forgiver.',NULL,40,42),
 (12538,1,'No doubt that what you call me to has no title to be called to in this world, nor in the hereafter, and that our turning back is to Allah, and that the extravagant are the inmates of the fire;',NULL,40,43),
 (12539,2,'"Without doubt ye do call me to one who is not fit to be called to, whether in this world, or in the Hereafter; our return will be to Allah; and the Transgressors will be Companions of the Fire!',NULL,40,43),
 (12540,3,'Assuredly that whereunto ye call me hath no claim in the world or in the Hereafter, and our return will be unto Allah, and the prodigals will be owners of the Fire.',NULL,40,43),
 (12541,1,'So you shall remember what I say to you, and I entrust my affair to Allah, Surely Allah sees the servants.',NULL,40,44),
 (12542,2,'"Soon will ye remember what I say to you (now), My (own) affair I commit to Allah: for Allah (ever) watches over His Servants."',NULL,40,44),
 (12543,3,'And ye will remember what I say unto you. I confide my cause unto Allah. Lo! Allah is Seer of (His) slaves.',NULL,40,44),
 (12544,1,'So Allah protected him from the evil (consequences) of what they planned, and the most evil punishment overtook Firon''s people:',NULL,40,45),
 (12545,2,'Then Allah saved him from (every) ill that they plotted (against him), but the burnt of the Penalty encompassed on all sides the People of Pharaoh.',NULL,40,45),
 (12546,3,'So Allah warded off from him the evils which they plotted, while a dreadful doom encompassed Pharaoh''s folk,',NULL,40,45),
 (12547,1,'The fire; they shall be brought before it (every) morning and evening and on the day when the hour shall come to pass: Make Firon''s people enter the severest chastisement.',NULL,40,46),
 (12548,2,'In front of the Fire will they be brought, morning and evening: And (the sentence will be) on the Day that Judgment will be established: "Cast ye the People of Pharaoh into the severest Penalty!"',NULL,40,46),
 (12549,3,'The Fire; they are exposed to it morning and evening; and on the day when the Hour upriseth (it is said): Cause Pharaoh''s folk to enter the most awful doom.',NULL,40,46),
 (12550,1,'And when they shall contend one with another in the fire, then the weak shall say to those who were proud: Surely we were your followers; will you then avert from us a portion of the fire?',NULL,40,47),
 (12551,2,'Behold, they will dispute with each other in the Fire! The weak ones (who followed) will say to those who had been arrogant, "We but followed you: Can ye then take (on yourselves) from us some share of the Fire?',NULL,40,47),
 (12552,3,'And when they wrangle in the Fire, the weak say unto those who were proud: Lo! we were a following unto you; will ye therefor rid us of a portion of the Fire?',NULL,40,47),
 (12553,1,'Those who were proud shall say: Surely we are all in it: surely Allah has judged between the servants.',NULL,40,48),
 (12554,2,'Those who had been arrogant will say: "We are all in this (Fire)! Truly, Allah has judged between (his) Servants!"',NULL,40,48),
 (12555,3,'Those who were proud say: Lo! we are all (together) herein. Lo! Allah hath judged between (His) slaves.',NULL,40,48),
 (12556,1,'And those who are in the fire shall say to the keepers of hell: Call upon your Lord that He may lighten to us one day of the punishment.',NULL,40,49),
 (12557,2,'Those in the Fire will say to the Keepers of Hell: "Pray to your Lord to lighten us the Penalty for a day (at least)!"',NULL,40,49),
 (12558,3,'And those in the Fire say unto the guards of hell: Entreat your Lord that He relieve us of a day of the torment.',NULL,40,49),
 (12559,1,'They shall say: Did not your messengers come to you with clear arguments? They shall say: Yea. They shall say: Then call. And the call of the unbelievers is only in error.',NULL,40,50),
 (12560,2,'They will say: "Did there not come to you your messengers with Clear Signs?" They will say, "Yes". They will reply, "Then pray (as ye like)! But the prayer of those without Faith is nothing but (futile wandering) in (mazes of) error!"',NULL,40,50),
 (12561,3,'They say: Came not your messengers unto you with clear proofs? They say: Yea, verily. They say: Then do ye pray, although the prayer of disbelievers is in vain.',NULL,40,50),
 (12562,1,'Most surely We help Our messengers, and those who believe, in this world''s life and on the day when the witnesses shall stand',NULL,40,51),
 (12563,2,'We will, without doubt, help our messengers and those who believe, (both) in this world''s life and on the Day when the Witnesses will stand forth,-',NULL,40,51),
 (12564,3,'Lo! We verily do help Our messengers, and those who believe, in the life of the world and on the day when the witnesses arise,',NULL,40,51),
 (12565,1,'The day on which their excuse shall not benefit the unjust, and for them is curse and for them is the evil abode.',NULL,40,52),
 (12566,2,'The Day when no profit will it be to Wrong-doers to present their excuses, but they will (only) have the Curse and the Home of Misery.',NULL,40,52),
 (12567,3,'The day when their excuse availeth not the evil-doers, and theirs is the curse, and theirs the ill abode.',NULL,40,52),
 (12568,1,'And certainly We gave Musa the guidance, and We made the children of Israel inherit the Book,',NULL,40,53),
 (12569,2,'We did aforetime give Moses the (Book of) Guidance, and We gave the book in inheritance to the Children of Israel,-',NULL,40,53),
 (12570,3,'And We verily gave Moses the guidance, and We caused the Children of Israel to inherit the Scripture,',NULL,40,53),
 (12571,1,'A guidance and a reminder to the men of understanding.',NULL,40,54),
 (12572,2,'A Guide and a Message to men of Understanding.',NULL,40,54),
 (12573,3,'A guide and a reminder for men of understanding.',NULL,40,54),
 (12574,1,'Therefore be patient; surely the promise of Allah is true; and ask protection for your fault and sing the praise of your Lord in the evening and the morning.',NULL,40,55),
 (12575,2,'Patiently, then, persevere: for the Promise of Allah is true: and ask forgiveness for thy fault, and celebrate the Praises of thy Lord in the evening and in the morning.',NULL,40,55),
 (12576,3,'Then have patience (O Muhammad). Lo! the promise of Allah is true. And ask forgiveness of thy sin, and hymn the praise of thy Lord at fall of night and in the early hours.',NULL,40,55),
 (12577,1,'Surely (as for) those who dispute about the communications of Allah without any authority that has come to them, there is naught in their breasts but (a desire) to become great which they shall never attain to; Therefore seek refuge in Allah, surely He is the Hearing, the Seeing.',NULL,40,56),
 (12578,2,'Those who dispute about the signs of Allah without any authority bestowed on them,- there is nothing in their breasts but (the quest of) greatness, which they shall never attain to: seek refuge, then, in Allah: It is He Who hears and sees (all things).',NULL,40,56),
 (12579,3,'Lo! those who wrangle concerning the revelations of Allah without a warrant having come unto them, there is naught else in their breasts save pride which they will never attain. So take thou refuge in Allah. Lo! He, only He, is the Hearer, the Seer.',NULL,40,56),
 (12580,1,'Certainly the creation of the heavens and the earth is greater than the creation of the men, but most people do not know',NULL,40,57),
 (12581,2,'Assuredly the creation of the heavens and the earth is a greater (matter) than the creation of men: Yet most men understand not.',NULL,40,57),
 (12582,3,'Assuredly the creation of the heavens and the earth is greater than the creation of mankind; but most of mankind know not.',NULL,40,57),
 (12583,1,'And the blind and the seeing are not alike, nor those who believe and do good and the evil-doer; little is it that you are mindful.',NULL,40,58),
 (12584,2,'Not equal are the blind and those who (clearly) see: Nor are (equal) those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, and those who do evil. Little do ye learn by admonition!',NULL,40,58),
 (12585,3,'And the blind man and the seer are not equal, neither are those who believe and do good works (equal with) the evil-doer. Little do ye reflect!',NULL,40,58),
 (12586,1,'Most surely the hour is coming, there is no doubt therein, but most people do not believe.',NULL,40,59),
 (12587,2,'The Hour will certainly come: Therein is no doubt: Yet most men believe not.',NULL,40,59),
 (12588,3,'Lo! the Hour is surely coming, there is no doubt thereof; yet most of mankind believe not.',NULL,40,59),
 (12589,1,'And your Lord says: Call upon Me, I will answer you; surely those who are too proud for My service shall soon enter hell abased.',NULL,40,60),
 (12590,2,'And your Lord says: "Call on Me; I will answer your (Prayer): but those who are too arrogant to serve Me will surely find themselves in Hell - in humiliation!"',NULL,40,60),
 (12591,3,'And your Lord hath said: Pray unto Me and I will hear your prayer. Lo! those who scorn My service, they will enter hell, disgraced.',NULL,40,60),
 (12592,1,'Allah is He Who made for you the night that you may rest therein and the day to see; most surely Allah is Gracious to men, but most men do not give thanks.',NULL,40,61),
 (12593,2,'It is Allah Who has made the Night for you, that ye may rest therein, and the days as that which helps (you) to see. Verily Allah is full of Grace and Bounty to men: yet most men give no thanks.',NULL,40,61),
 (12594,3,'Allah it is Who hath appointed for you night that ye may rest therein, and day for seeing. Lo! Allah is a Lord of bounty for mankind, yet most of mankind give not thanks.',NULL,40,61),
 (12595,1,'That is Allah, your Lord, the Creator of everything; there is no Allah but He; whence are you then turned away?',NULL,40,62),
 (12596,2,'Such is Allah, your Lord, the Creator of all things, there is no god but He: Then how ye are deluded away from the Truth!',NULL,40,62),
 (12597,3,'Such is Allah, your Lord, the Creator of all things, There is no Allah save Him. How then are ye perverted?',NULL,40,62),
 (12598,1,'Thus were turned away those who denied the communications of Allah.',NULL,40,63),
 (12599,2,'Thus are deluded those who are wont to reject the Signs of Allah.',NULL,40,63),
 (12600,3,'Thus are they perverted who deny the revelations of Allah.',NULL,40,63),
 (12601,1,'Allah is He Who made the earth a resting-place for you and the heaven a canopy, and He formed you, then made goodly your forms, and He provided you with goodly things; that is Allah, your Lord; blessed then is Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,40,64),
 (12602,2,'It is Allah Who has made for you the earth as a resting place, and the sky as a canopy, and has given you shape- and made your shapes beautiful,- and has provided for you Sustenance, of things pure and good;- such is Allah your Lord. So Glory to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,40,64),
 (12603,3,'Allah it is Who appointed for you the earth for a dwelling-place and the sky for a canopy, and fashioned you and perfected your shapes, and hath provided you with good things. Such is Allah, your Lord. Then blessed be Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,40,64),
 (12604,1,'He is the Living, there is no god but He, therefore call on Him, being sincere to Him in obedience; (all) praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,40,65),
 (12605,2,'He is the Living (One): There is no god but He: Call upon Him, giving Him sincere devotion. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,40,65),
 (12606,3,'He is the Living One. There is no Allah save Him. So pray unto Him, making religion pure for Him (only). Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds!',NULL,40,65),
 (12607,1,'Say: I am forbidden to serve those whom you call upon besides Allah when clear arguments have come to me from my Lord, and I am commanded that I should submit to the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,40,66),
 (12608,2,'Say: "I have been forbidden to invoke those whom ye invoke besides Allah,- seeing that the Clear Signs have come to me from my Lord; and I have been commanded to bow (in Islam) to the Lord of the Worlds."',NULL,40,66),
 (12609,3,'Say (O Muhammad): I am forbidden to worship those unto whom ye cry beside Allah since there have come unto me clear proofs from my Lord, and I am commanded to surrender to the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,40,66),
 (12610,1,'He it is Who created you from dust, then from a small lifegerm, then from a clot, then He brings you forth as a child, then that you may attain your maturity, then that you may be old-- and of you there are some who are caused to die before-- and that you may reach an appointed term, and that you may understand.',NULL,40,67),
 (12611,2,'It is He Who has created you from dust then from a sperm-drop, then from a leech-like clot; then does he get you out (into the light) as a child: then lets you (grow and) reach your age of full strength; then lets you become old,- though of you there are some who die before;- and lets you reach a Term appointed; in order that ye may learn wisdom.',NULL,40,67),
 (12612,3,'He it is Who created you from dust, then from a drop (of seed) then from a clot, then bringeth you forth as a child, then (ordaineth) that ye attain full strength and afterward that ye become old men - though some among you die before - and that ye reach an appointed term, that haply ye may understand.',NULL,40,67),
 (12613,1,'He it is Who gives life and brings death, so when He decrees an affair, He only says to it: Be, and it is.',NULL,40,68),
 (12614,2,'It is He Who gives Life and Death; and when He decides upon an affair, He says to it, "Be", and it is.',NULL,40,68),
 (12615,3,'He it is Who quickeneth and giveth death. When He ordaineth a thing, He saith unto it only: Be! and it is.',NULL,40,68),
 (12616,1,'Have you not seen those who dispute with respect to the communications of Allah: how are they turned away?',NULL,40,69),
 (12617,2,'Seest thou not those that dispute concerning the Signs of Allah? How are they turned away (from Reality)?-',NULL,40,69),
 (12618,3,'Hast thou not seen those who wrangle concerning the revelations of Allah, how they are turned away? -',NULL,40,69),
 (12619,1,'Those who reject the Book and that with which We have sent Our Messenger; but they shall soon come to know,',NULL,40,70),
 (12620,2,'Those who reject the Book and the (revelations) with which We sent our messengers: but soon shall they know,-',NULL,40,70),
 (12621,3,'Those who deny the Scripture and that wherewith We send Our messengers. But they will come to know,',NULL,40,70),
 (12622,1,'When the fetters and the chains shall be on their necks; they shall be dragged',NULL,40,71),
 (12623,2,'When the yokes (shall be) round their necks, and the chains; they shall be dragged along-',NULL,40,71),
 (12624,3,'When carcans are about their necks and chains. They are dragged',NULL,40,71),
 (12625,1,'Into boiling water, then in the fire shall they be burned;',NULL,40,72),
 (12626,2,'In the boiling fetid fluid: then in the Fire shall they be burned;',NULL,40,72),
 (12627,3,'Through boiling waters; then they are thrust into the Fire.',NULL,40,72),
 (12628,1,'Then shall it be said to them: Where is that which you used to set up',NULL,40,73),
 (12629,2,'Then shall it be said to them: "Where are the (deities) to which ye gave part-worship-',NULL,40,73),
 (12630,3,'Then it is said unto them: Where are (all) that ye used to make partners (in the Sovereignty)',NULL,40,73),
 (12631,1,'Besides Allah? They shall say: They are gone away from us, nay, we used not to call upon anything before. Thus does Allah confound the unbelievers.',NULL,40,74),
 (12632,2,'"In derogation of Allah?" They will reply: "They have left us in the lurch: Nay, we invoked not, of old, anything (that had real existence)." Thus does Allah leave the Unbelievers to stray.',NULL,40,74),
 (12633,3,'Beside Allah? They say: They have failed us; but we used not to pray to anything before. Thus doth Allah send astray the disbelievers (in His guidance).',NULL,40,74),
 (12634,1,'That is because you exulted in the land unjustly and because you behaved insolently.',NULL,40,75),
 (12635,2,'"That was because ye were wont to rejoice on the earth in things other than the Truth, and that ye were wont to be insolent.',NULL,40,75),
 (12636,3,'(And it is said unto them): This is because ye exulted in the earth without right, and because ye were petulant.',NULL,40,75),
 (12637,1,'Enter the gates of hell to abide therein, evil then is the abode of the proud.',NULL,40,76),
 (12638,2,'"Enter ye the gates of Hell, to dwell therein: and evil is (this) abode of the arrogant!"',NULL,40,76),
 (12639,3,'Enter ye the gates of hell, to dwell therein. Evil is the habitation of the scornful.',NULL,40,76),
 (12640,1,'So be patient, surely the promise of Allah is true. So should We make you see part of what We threaten them with, or should We cause you to die, to Us shall they be returned.',NULL,40,77),
 (12641,2,'So persevere in patience; for the Promise of Allah is true: and whether We show thee (in this life) some part of what We promise them,- or We take thy soul (to Our Mercy) (before that),-(in any case) it is to Us that they shall (all) return.',NULL,40,77),
 (12642,3,'Then have patience (O Muhammad). Lo! the promise of Allah is true. And whether we let thee see a part of that which We promise them, or (whether) We cause thee to die, still unto Us they will be brought back.',NULL,40,77),
 (12643,1,'And certainly We sent messengers before you: there are some of them that We have mentioned to you and there are others whom We have not mentioned to you, and it was not meet for a messenger that he should bring a sign except with Allah''s permission, but when the command of Allah came, judgment was given with truth, and those who treated (it) as a lie were lost.',NULL,40,78),
 (12644,2,'We did aforetime send messengers before thee: of them there are some whose story We have related to thee, and some whose story We have not related to thee. It was not (possible) for any messenger to bring a sign except by the leave of Allah: but when the Command of Allah issued, the matter was decided in truth and justice, and there perished, there and then those who stood on Falsehoods.',NULL,40,78),
 (12645,3,'Verily We sent messengers before thee, among them those of whom We have told thee, and some of whom We have not told thee; and it was not given to any messenger that he should bring a portent save by Allah''s leave, but when Allah''s commandment cometh (the cause) is judged aright, and the followers of vanity will then be lost.',NULL,40,78),
 (12646,1,'Allah is He Who made the cattle for you that you may ride on some of them, and some of them you eat.',NULL,40,79),
 (12647,2,'It is Allah Who made cattle for you, that ye may use some for riding and some for food;',NULL,40,79),
 (12648,3,'Allah it is Who hath appointed for you cattle, that ye may ride on some of them, and eat of some -',NULL,40,79),
 (12649,1,'And there are advantages for you in them, and that you may attain thereon a want which is in your breasts, and upon them and upon the ships you are borne.',NULL,40,80),
 (12650,2,'And there are (other) advantages in them for you (besides); that ye may through them attain to any need (there may be) in your hearts; and on them and on ships ye are carried.',NULL,40,80),
 (12651,3,'(Many) benefits ye have from them - and that ye may satisfy by their means a need that is in your breasts, and may be borne upon them as upon the ship.',NULL,40,80),
 (12652,1,'And He shows you His signs: which then of Allah''s signs will you deny?',NULL,40,81),
 (12653,2,'And He shows you (always) His Signs: then which of the Signs of Allah will ye deny?',NULL,40,81),
 (12654,3,'And He showeth you His tokens. Which, then, of the tokens of Allah do ye deny?',NULL,40,81),
 (12655,1,'Have they not then journeyed in the land and seen how was the end of those before them? They were more (in numbers) than these and greater in strength and in fortifications in the land, but what they earned did not avail them.',NULL,40,82),
 (12656,2,'Do they not travel through the earth and see what was the End of those before them? They were more numerous than these and superior in strength and in the traces (they have left) in the land: Yet all that they accomplished was of no profit to them.',NULL,40,82),
 (12657,3,'Have they not travelled in the land to see the nature of the consequence for those before them? They were more numerous than these, and mightier in power and (in the) traces (which they left behind them) in the earth. But all that they used to earn availed them not.',NULL,40,82),
 (12658,1,'Then when their messengers came to them with clear arguments, they exulted in what they had with them of knowledge, and there beset them that which they used to mock.',NULL,40,83),
 (12659,2,'For when their messengers came to them with Clear Signs, they exulted in such knowledge (and skill) as they had; but that very (Wrath) at which they were wont to scoff hemmed them in.',NULL,40,83),
 (12660,3,'And when their messengers brought them clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty) they exulted in the knowledge they (themselves) possessed. And that which they were wont to mock befell them.',NULL,40,83),
 (12661,1,'But when they saw Our punishment, they said: We believe in Allah alone and we deny what we used to associate with Him.',NULL,40,84),
 (12662,2,'But when they saw Our Punishment, they said: "We believe in Allah,- the one Allah - and we reject the partners we used to join with Him."',NULL,40,84),
 (12663,3,'Then, when they saw Our doom, they said: We believe in Allah only and reject (all) that we used to associate (with Him).',NULL,40,84),
 (12664,1,'But their belief was not going to profit them when they had seen Our punishment; (this is) Allah''s law, which has indeed obtained in the matter of His servants, and there the unbelievers are lost.',NULL,40,85),
 (12665,2,'But their professing the Faith when they (actually) saw Our Punishment was not going to profit them. (Such has been) Allah''s Way of dealing with His Servants (from the most ancient times). And even thus did the Rejecters of Allah perish (utterly)!',NULL,40,85),
 (12666,3,'But their faith could not avail them when they saw Our doom. This is Allah''s law which hath ever taken course for His bondmen. And then the disbelievers will be ruined.',NULL,40,85),
 (12667,1,'Ha Mim!',NULL,41,1),
 (12668,2,'Ha Mim:',NULL,41,1),
 (12669,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,41,1),
 (12670,1,'A revelation from the Beneficent, the Merciful Allah:',NULL,41,2),
 (12671,2,'A Revelation from (Allah), Most Gracious, Most Merciful;-',NULL,41,2),
 (12672,3,'A revelation from the Beneficent, the Merciful,',NULL,41,2),
 (12673,1,'A Book of which the verses are made plain, an Arabic Quran for a people who know:',NULL,41,3),
 (12674,2,'A Book, whereof the verses are explained in detail;- a Qur''an in Arabic, for people who understand;-',NULL,41,3),
 (12675,3,'A Scripture whereof the verses are expounded, a Lecture in Arabic for people who have knowledge,',NULL,41,3),
 (12676,1,'A herald of good news and a warner, but most of them turn aside so they hear not.',NULL,41,4),
 (12677,2,'Giving good news and admonition: yet most of them turn away, and so they hear not.',NULL,41,4),
 (12678,3,'Good tidings and a warning. But most of them turn away so that they hear not.',NULL,41,4),
 (12679,1,'And they say: Our hearts are under coverings from that to which you call us, and there is a heaviness in our ears, and a veil hangs between us and you, so work, we too are working.',NULL,41,5),
 (12680,2,'They say: "Our hearts are under veils, (concealed) from that to which thou dost invite us, and in our ears in a deafness, and between us and thee is a screen: so do thou (what thou wilt); for us, we shall do (what we will!)"',NULL,41,5),
 (12681,3,'And they say: Our hearts are protected from that unto which thou (O Muhammad) callest us, and in our ears there is a deafness, and between us and thee there is a veil. Act, then. Lo! we also shall be acting.',NULL,41,5),
 (12682,1,'Say: I am only a mortal like you; it is revealed to me that your Allah is one Allah, therefore follow the right way to Him and ask His forgiveness; and woe to the polytheists;',NULL,41,6),
 (12683,2,'Say thou: "I am but a man like you: It is revealed to me by Inspiration, that your Allah is one Allah: so stand true to Him, and ask for His Forgiveness." And woe to those who join gods with Allah,-',NULL,41,6),
 (12684,3,'Say (unto them O Muhammad): I am only a mortal like you. It is inspired in me that your Allah is One Allah, therefor take the straight path unto Him and seek forgiveness of Him. And woe unto the idolaters,',NULL,41,6),
 (12685,1,'(To) those who do not give poor-rate and they are unbelievers in the hereafter.',NULL,41,7),
 (12686,2,'Those who practise not regular Charity, and who even deny the Hereafter.',NULL,41,7),
 (12687,3,'Who give not the poor-due, and who are disbelievers in the Hereafter.',NULL,41,7),
 (12688,1,'(As for) those who believe and do good, they shall surely have a reward never to be cut off.',NULL,41,8),
 (12689,2,'For those who believe and work deeds of righteousness is a reward that will never fail.',NULL,41,8),
 (12690,3,'Lo! as for those who believe and do good works, for them is a reward enduring.',NULL,41,8),
 (12691,1,'Say: What! do you indeed disbelieve in Him Who created the earth in two periods, and do you set up equals with Him? That is the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,41,9),
 (12692,2,'Say: Is it that ye deny Him Who created the earth in two Days? And do ye join equals with Him? He is the Lord of (all) the Worlds.',NULL,41,9),
 (12693,3,'Say (O Muhammad, unto the idolaters): Disbelieve ye verily in Him Who created the earth in two Days, and ascribe ye unto Him rivals? He (and none else) is the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,41,9),
 (12694,1,'And He made in it mountains above its surface, and He blessed therein and made therein its foods, in four periods: alike for the seekers.',NULL,41,10),
 (12695,2,'He set on the (earth), mountains standing firm, high above it, and bestowed blessings on the earth, and measure therein all things to give them nourishment in due proportion, in four Days, in accordance with (the needs of) those who seek (Sustenance).',NULL,41,10),
 (12696,3,'He placed therein firm hills rising above it, and blessed it and measured therein its sustenance in four Days, alike for (all) who ask;',NULL,41,10),
 (12697,1,'Then He directed Himself to the heaven and it is a vapor, so He said to it and to the earth: Come both, willingly or unwillingly. They both said: We come willingly.',NULL,41,11),
 (12698,2,'Moreover He comprehended in His design the sky, and it had been (as) smoke: He said to it and to the earth: "Come ye together, willingly or unwillingly." They said: "We do come (together), in willing obedience."',NULL,41,11),
 (12699,3,'Then turned He to the heaven when it was smoke, and said unto it and unto the earth: Come both of you, willingly or loth. They said: We come, obedient.',NULL,41,11),
 (12700,1,'So He ordained them seven heavens in two periods, and revealed in every heaven its affair; and We adorned the lower heaven with brilliant stars and (made it) to guard; that is the decree of the Mighty, the Knowing.',NULL,41,12),
 (12701,2,'So He completed them as seven firmaments in two Days, and He assigned to each heaven its duty and command. And We adorned the lower heaven with lights, and (provided it) with guard. Such is the Decree of (Him) the Exalted in Might, Full of Knowledge.',NULL,41,12),
 (12702,3,'Then He ordained them seven heavens in two Days and inspired in each heaven its mandate; and We decked the nether heaven with lamps, and rendered it inviolable. That is the measuring of the Mighty, the Knower.',NULL,41,12),
 (12703,1,'But if they turn aside, then say: I have warned you of a scourge like the scourge of Ad and Samood.',NULL,41,13),
 (12704,2,'But if they turn away, say thou: "I have warned you of a stunning Punishment (as of thunder and lightning) like that which (overtook) the ''Ad and the Thamud!"',NULL,41,13),
 (12705,3,'But if they turn away, then say: I warn you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt (which fell of old upon the tribes) of A''ad and Thamud;',NULL,41,13),
 (12706,1,'When their messengers came to them from before them and from behind them, saying, Serve nothing but Allah, they said: If our Lord had pleased He would certainly have sent down angels, so we are surely unbelievers in that with which you are sent.',NULL,41,14),
 (12707,2,'Behold, the messengers came to them, from before them and behind them, (preaching): "Serve none but Allah." They said, "If our Lord had so pleased, He would certainly have sent down angels (to preach). Now we reject your mission (altogether)."',NULL,41,14),
 (12708,3,'When their messengers came unto them from before them and behind them, saying: Worship none but Allah! they said: If our Lord had willed, He surely would have sent down angels (unto us), so lo! we are disbelievers in that wherewith ye have been sent.',NULL,41,14),
 (12709,1,'Then as to Ad, they were unjustly proud in the land, and they said: Who is mightier in strength than we? Did they not see that Allah Who created them was mightier than they in strength, and they denied Our communications?',NULL,41,15),
 (12710,2,'Now the ''Ad behaved arrogantly through the land, against (all) truth and reason, and said: "Who is superior to us in strength?" What! did they not see that Allah, Who created them, was superior to them in strength? But they continued to reject Our Signs!',NULL,41,15),
 (12711,3,'As for A''ad, they were arrogant in the land without right, and they said: Who is mightier than us in power? Could they not see that Allah Who created them, He was mightier than them in power? And they denied Our revelations.',NULL,41,15),
 (12712,1,'So We sent on them a furious wind in unlucky days, that We may make them taste the chastisement of abasement in this world''s life; and certainly the chastisement of the hereafter is much more abasing, and they shall not be helped.',NULL,41,16),
 (12713,2,'So We sent against them a furious Wind through days of disaster, that We might give them a taste of a Penalty of humiliation in this life; but the Penalty of a Hereafter will be more humiliating still: and they will find no help.',NULL,41,16),
 (12714,3,'Therefor We let loose on them a raging wind in evil days, that We might make them taste the torment of disgrace in the life of the world. And verily the doom of the Hereafter will be more shameful, and they will not be helped.',NULL,41,16),
 (12715,1,'And as to Samood, We showed them the right way, but they chose error above guidance, so there overtook them the scourge of an abasing chastisement for what they earned.',NULL,41,17),
 (12716,2,'As to the Thamud, We gave them Guidance, but they preferred blindness (of heart) to Guidance: so the stunning Punishment of humiliation seized them, because of what they had earned.',NULL,41,17),
 (12717,3,'And as for Thamud, We gave them guidance, but they preferred blindness to the guidance, so the bolt of the doom of humiliation overtook them because of what they used to earn.',NULL,41,17),
 (12718,1,'And We delivered those who believed and guarded (against evil).',NULL,41,18),
 (12719,2,'But We delivered those who believed and practised righteousness.',NULL,41,18),
 (12720,3,'And We delivered those who believed and used to keep their duty to Allah.',NULL,41,18),
 (12721,1,'And on the day that the enemies of Allah shall be brought together to the fire, then they shall be formed into groups.',NULL,41,19),
 (12722,2,'On the Day that the enemies of Allah will be gathered together to the Fire, they will be marched in ranks.',NULL,41,19),
 (12723,3,'And (make mention of) the day when the enemies of Allah are gathered unto the Fire, they are driven on',NULL,41,19),
 (12724,1,'Until when they come to it, their ears and their eyes and their skins shall bear witness against them as to what they did.',NULL,41,20),
 (12725,2,'At length, when they reach the (Fire), their hearing, their sight, and their skins will bear witness against them, as to (all) their deeds.',NULL,41,20),
 (12726,3,'Till, when they reach it, their ears and their eyes and their skins testify against them as to what they used to do.',NULL,41,20),
 (12727,1,'And they shall say to their skins: Why have you borne witness against us? They shall say: Allah Who makes everything speak has made us speak, and He created you at first, and to Him you shall be brought back.',NULL,41,21),
 (12728,2,'They will say to their skins: "Why bear ye witness against us?" They will say: "Allah hath given us speech,- (He) Who giveth speech to everything: He created you for the first time, and unto Him were ye to return.',NULL,41,21),
 (12729,3,'And they say unto their skins: Why testify ye against us? They say: Allah hath given us speech Who giveth speech to all things, and Who created you at the first, and unto Whom ye are returned.',NULL,41,21),
 (12730,1,'And you did not veil yourselves lest your ears and your eyes and your skins should bear witness against you, but you thought that Allah did not know most of what you did.',NULL,41,22),
 (12731,2,'"Ye did not seek to hide yourselves, lest your hearing, your sight, and your skins should bear witness against you! But ye did think that Allah knew not many of the things that ye used to do!',NULL,41,22),
 (12732,3,'Ye did not hide yourselves lest your ears and your eyes and your skins should testify against you, but ye deemed that Allah knew not much of what ye did.',NULL,41,22),
 (12733,1,'And that was your (evil) thought which you entertained about your Lord that has tumbled you down into perdition, so are you become of the lost ones.',NULL,41,23),
 (12734,2,'"But this thought of yours which ye did entertain concerning your Lord, hath brought you to destruction, and (now) have ye become of those utterly lost!"',NULL,41,23),
 (12735,3,'That, your thought which ye did think about your Lord, hath ruined you; and ye find yourselves (this day) among the lost.',NULL,41,23),
 (12736,1,'Then if they will endure, still the fire is their abode, and if they ask for goodwill, then are they not of those who shall be granted goodwill.',NULL,41,24),
 (12737,2,'If, then, they have patience, the Fire will be a home for them! and if they beg to be received into favour, into favour will they not (then) be received.',NULL,41,24),
 (12738,3,'And though they are resigned, yet the Fire is still their home; and if they ask for favour, yet they are not of those unto whom favour can be shown.',NULL,41,24),
 (12739,1,'And We have appointed for them comrades so they have made fair-seeming to them what is before them and what is behind them, and the word proved true against them-- among the nations of the jinn and the men that have passed away before them-- that they shall surely be losers.',NULL,41,25),
 (12740,2,'And We have destined for them intimate companions (of like nature), who made alluring to them what was before them and behind them; and the sentence among the previous generations of Jinns and men, who have passed away, is proved against them; for they are utterly lost.',NULL,41,25),
 (12741,3,'And We assigned them comrades (in the world), who made their present and their past fairseeming unto them. And the Word concerning nations of the jinn and humankind who passed away before them hath effect for them. Lo! they were ever losers.',NULL,41,25),
 (12742,1,'And those who disbelieve say: Do not listen to this Quran and make noise therein, perhaps you may overcome.',NULL,41,26),
 (12743,2,'The Unbelievers say: "Listen not to this Qur''an, but talk at random in the midst of its (reading), that ye may gain the upper hand!"',NULL,41,26),
 (12744,3,'Those who disbelieve say: Heed not this Qur''an, and drown the hearing of it; haply ye may conquer.',NULL,41,26),
 (12745,1,'Therefore We will most certainly make those who disbelieve taste a severe punishment, and We will most certainly reward them for the evil deeds they used to do.',NULL,41,27),
 (12746,2,'But We will certainly give the Unbelievers a taste of a severe Penalty, and We will requite them for the worst of their deeds.',NULL,41,27),
 (12747,3,'But verily We shall cause those who disbelieve to taste an awful doom, and verily We shall requite them the worst of what they used to do.',NULL,41,27),
 (12748,1,'That is the reward of the enemies of Allah-- the fire; for them therein shall be the house of long abiding; a reward for their denying Our communications.',NULL,41,28),
 (12749,2,'Such is the requital of the enemies of Allah,- the Fire: therein will be for them the Eternal Home: a (fit) requital, for that they were wont to reject Our Signs.',NULL,41,28),
 (12750,3,'That is the reward of Allah''s enemies: the Fire. Therein is their immortal home, payment forasmuch as they denied Our revelations.',NULL,41,28),
 (12751,1,'And those who disbelieve will say: Our Lord! show us those who led us astray from among the jinn and the men that we may trample them under our feet so that they may be of the lowest.',NULL,41,29),
 (12752,2,'And the Unbelievers will say: "Our Lord! Show us those, among Jinns and men, who misled us: We shall crush them beneath our feet, so that they become the vilest (before all)."',NULL,41,29),
 (12753,3,'And those who disbelieve will say: Our Lord! Show us those who beguiled us of the jinn and humankind. We will place them underneath our feet that they may be among the nethermost.',NULL,41,29),
 (12754,1,'(As for) those who say: Our Lord is Allah, then continue in the right way, the angels descend upon them, saying: Fear not, nor be grieved, and receive good news of the garden which you were promised.',NULL,41,30),
 (12755,2,'In the case of those who say, "Our Lord is Allah", and, further, stand straight and steadfast, the angels descend on them (from time to time): "Fear ye not!" (they suggest), "Nor grieve! but receive the Glad Tidings of the Garden (of Bliss), the which ye were promised!',NULL,41,30),
 (12756,3,'Lo! those who say: Our Lord is Allah, and afterward are upright, the angels descend upon them, saying: Fear not nor grieve, but hear good tidings of the paradise which ye are promised.',NULL,41,30),
 (12757,1,'We are your guardians in this world''s life and in the hereafter, and you shall have therein what your souls desire and you shall have therein what you ask for:',NULL,41,31),
 (12758,2,'"We are your protectors in this life and in the Hereafter: therein shall ye have all that your souls shall desire; therein shall ye have all that ye ask for!-',NULL,41,31),
 (12759,3,'We are your protecting friends in the life of the world and in the Hereafter. There ye will have (all) that your souls desire, and there ye will have (all) for which ye pray.',NULL,41,31),
 (12760,1,'A provision from the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,41,32),
 (12761,2,'"A hospitable gift from one Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful!"',NULL,41,32),
 (12762,3,'A gift of welcome from One Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,41,32),
 (12763,1,'And who speaks better than he who calls to Allah while he himself does good, and says: I am surely of those who submit?',NULL,41,33),
 (12764,2,'Who is better in speech than one who calls (men) to Allah, works righteousness, and says, "I am of those who bow in Islam"?',NULL,41,33),
 (12765,3,'And who is better in speech than him who prayeth unto his Lord and doeth right, and saith: Lo! I am of those who are muslims (surrender unto Him).',NULL,41,33),
 (12766,1,'And not alike are the good and the evil. Repel (evil) with what is best, when lo! he between whom and you was enmity would be as if he were a warm friend.',NULL,41,34),
 (12767,2,'Nor can goodness and Evil be equal. Repel (Evil) with what is better: Then will he between whom and thee was hatred become as it were thy friend and intimate!',NULL,41,34),
 (12768,3,'The good deed and the evil deed are not alike. Repel the evil deed with one which is better, then lo! he, between whom and thee there was enmity (will become) as though he was a bosom friend.',NULL,41,34),
 (12769,1,'And none are made to receive it but those who are patient, and none are made to receive it but those who have a mighty good fortune.',NULL,41,35),
 (12770,2,'And no one will be granted such goodness except those who exercise patience and self-restraint,- none but persons of the greatest good fortune.',NULL,41,35),
 (12771,3,'But none is granted it save those who are steadfast, and none is granted it save the owner of great happiness.',NULL,41,35),
 (12772,1,'And if an interference of the Shaitan should cause you mischief, seek refuge in Allah; surely He is the Hearing, the Knowing.',NULL,41,36),
 (12773,2,'And if (at any time) an incitement to discord is made to thee by the Evil One, seek refuge in Allah. He is the One Who hears and knows all things.',NULL,41,36),
 (12774,3,'And if a whisper from the devil reach thee (O Muhammad) then seek refuge in Allah. Lo! He is the Hearer, the Knower.',NULL,41,36),
 (12775,1,'And among His signs are the night and the day and the sun and the moon; do not prostrate to the sun nor to the moon; and prostrate to Allah Who created them, if Him it is that you serve.',NULL,41,37),
 (12776,2,'Among His Signs are the Night and the Day, and the Sun and the Moon. Do not prostrate to the sun and the moon, but prostrate to Allah, Who created them, if it is Him ye wish to serve.',NULL,41,37),
 (12777,3,'And of His portents are the night and the day and the sun and the moon. Do not prostrate to the sun or the moon; but prostrate to Allah Who created them, if it is in truth Him Whom ye worship.',NULL,41,37),
 (12778,1,'But if they are proud, yet those with your Lord glorify Him during the night and the day, and they are not tired.',NULL,41,38),
 (12779,2,'But is the (Unbelievers) are arrogant, (no matter): for in the presence of thy Lord are those who celebrate His praises by night and by day. And they never flag (nor feel themselves above it).',NULL,41,38),
 (12780,3,'But if they are too proud - still those who are with thy Lord glorify Him night and day, and tire not.',NULL,41,38),
 (12781,1,'And among His signs is this, that you see the earth still, but when We send down on it the water, it stirs and swells: most surely He Who gives it life is the Giver of life to the dead; surely He has power over all things.',NULL,41,39),
 (12782,2,'And among His Signs in this: thou seest the earth barren and desolate; but when We send down rain to it, it is stirred to life and yields increase. Truly, He Who gives life to the (dead) earth can surely give life to (men) who are dead. For He has power over all things.',NULL,41,39),
 (12783,3,'And of His portents (is this): that thou seest the earth lowly, but when We send down water thereon it thrilleth and groweth. Lo! He Who quickeneth it is verily the Quickener of the Dead. Lo! He is Able to do all things.',NULL,41,39),
 (12784,1,'Surely they who deviate from the right way concerning Our communications are not hidden from Us. What! is he then who is cast into the fire better, or he who comes safe on the day of resurrection? Do what you like, surely He sees what you do.',NULL,41,40),
 (12785,2,'Those who pervert the Truth in Our Signs are not hidden from Us. Which is better?- he that is cast into the Fire, or he that comes safe through, on the Day of Judgment? Do what ye will: verily He seeth (clearly) all that ye do.',NULL,41,40),
 (12786,3,'Lo! those who distort Our revelations are not hid from Us. Is he who is hurled into the Fire better, or he who cometh secure on the Day of Resurrection? Do what ye will. Lo! He is Seer of what ye do.',NULL,41,40),
 (12787,1,'Surely those who disbelieve in the reminder when it comes to them, and most surely it is a Mighty Book:',NULL,41,41),
 (12788,2,'Those who reject the Message when it comes to them (are not hidden from Us). And indeed it is a Book of exalted power.',NULL,41,41),
 (12789,3,'Lo! those who disbelieve in the Reminder when it cometh unto them (are guilty), for lo! it is an unassailable Scripture.',NULL,41,41),
 (12790,1,'Falsehood shall not come to it from before it nor from behind it; a revelation from the Wise, the Praised One.',NULL,41,42),
 (12791,2,'No falsehood can approach it from before or behind it: It is sent down by One Full of Wisdom, Worthy of all Praise.',NULL,41,42),
 (12792,3,'Falsehood cannot come at it from before it or from behind it. (It is) a revelation from the Wise, the Owner of Praise.',NULL,41,42),
 (12793,1,'Naught is said to you but what was said indeed to the messengers before you; surely your Lord is the Lord of forgiveness and the Lord of painful retribution.',NULL,41,43),
 (12794,2,'Nothing is said to thee that was not said to the messengers before thee: that thy lord has at his Command (all) forgiveness as well as a most Grievous Penalty.',NULL,41,43),
 (12795,3,'Naught is said unto thee (Muhammad) save what was said unto the messengers before thee. Lo! thy Lord is owner of forgiveness, and owner (also) of dire punishment.',NULL,41,43),
 (12796,1,'And if We had made it a Quran in a foreign tongue, they would certainly have said: Why have not its communications been made clear? What! a foreign (tongue) and an Arabian! Say: It is to those who believe a guidance and a healing; and (as for) those who do not believe, there is a heaviness in their ears and it is obscure to them; these shall be called to from a far-off place.',NULL,41,44),
 (12797,2,'Had We sent this as a Qur''an (in the language) other than Arabic, they would have said: "Why are not its verses explained in detail? What! (a Book) not in Arabic and (a Messenger an Arab?" Say: "It is a Guide and a Healing to those who believe; and for those who believe not, there is a deafness in their ears, and it is blindness in their (eyes): They are (as it were) being called from a place far distant!"',NULL,41,44),
 (12798,3,'And if We had appointed it a Lecture in a foreign tongue they would assuredly have said: If only its verses were expounded (so that we might understand)? What! A foreign tongue and an Arab? - Say unto them (O Muhammad): For those who believe it is a guidance and a healing; and as for those who disbelieve, there is a deafness in their ears, and it is blindness for them. Such are called to from afar.',NULL,41,44),
 (12799,1,'And certainly We gave the Book to Musa, but it has been differed about, and had not a word already gone forth from your Lord, judgment would certainly have been given between them; and most surely they are in a disquieting doubt about it.',NULL,41,45),
 (12800,2,'We certainly gave Moses the Book aforetime: but disputes arose therein. Had it not been for a Word that went forth before from thy Lord, (their differences) would have been settled between them: but they remained in suspicious disquieting doubt thereon.',NULL,41,45),
 (12801,3,'And We verily gave Moses the Scripture, but there hath been dispute concerning it; and but for a Word that had already gone forth from thy Lord, it would ere now have been judged between them; but lo! they are in hopeless doubt concerning it.',NULL,41,45),
 (12802,1,'Whoever does good, it is for his own soul, and whoever does evil, it is against it; and your Lord is not in the least unjust to the servants.',NULL,41,46),
 (12803,2,'Whoever works righteousness benefits his own soul; whoever works evil, it is against his own soul: nor is thy Lord ever unjust (in the least) to His Servants.',NULL,41,46),
 (12804,3,'Whoso doeth right it is for his soul, and whoso doeth wrong it is against it. And thy Lord is not at all a tyrant to His slaves.',NULL,41,46),
 (12805,1,'To Him is referred the knowledge of the hour, and there come not forth any of the fruits from their coverings, nor does a female bear, nor does she give birth, but with His knowledge; and on the day when He shall call out to them, Where are (those whom you called) My associates? They shall say: We declare to Thee, none of us is a witness.',NULL,41,47),
 (12806,2,'To Him is referred the Knowledge of the Hour (of Judgment: He knows all): No date-fruit comes out of its sheath, nor does a female conceive (within her womb) nor bring forth the Day that (Allah) will propound to them the (question), "Where are the partners (ye attributed to Me?" They will say, "We do assure thee not one of us can bear witness!"',NULL,41,47),
 (12807,3,'Unto Him is referred (all) knowledge of the Hour. And no fruits burst forth from their sheaths, and no female carrieth or bringeth forth but with His knowledge. And on the day when He calleth unto them: Where are now My partners? they will say: We confess unto Thee, not one of us is a witness (for them).',NULL,41,47),
 (12808,1,'And away from them shall go what they called upon before, and they shall know for certain that there is no escape for them.',NULL,41,48),
 (12809,2,'The (deities) they used to invoke aforetime will leave them in the lurch, and they will perceive that they have no way of escape.',NULL,41,48),
 (12810,3,'And those to whom they used to cry of old have failed them, and they perceive they have no place of refuge.',NULL,41,48),
 (12811,1,'Man is never tired of praying for good, and if evil touch him, then he is despairing, hopeless.',NULL,41,49),
 (12812,2,'Man does not weary of asking for good (things), but if ill touches him, he gives up all hope (and) is lost in despair.',NULL,41,49),
 (12813,3,'Man tireth not of praying for good, and if ill toucheth him, then he is disheartened, desperate.',NULL,41,49),
 (12814,1,'And if We make him taste mercy from Us after distress that has touched him, he would most certainly say: This is of me, and I do not think the hour will come to pass, and if I am sent back to my Lord, I shall have with Him sure good; but We will most certainly inform those who disbelieved of what they did, and We will most certainly make them taste of hard chastisement.',NULL,41,50),
 (12815,2,'When we give him a taste of some Mercy from Ourselves, after some adversity has touched him, he is sure to say, "This is due to my (merit): I think not that the Hour (of Judgment) will (ever) be established; but if I am brought back to my Lord, I have (much) good (stored) in His sight!" But We will show the Unbelievers the truth of all that they did, and We shall give them the taste of a severe Penalty.',NULL,41,50),
 (12816,3,'And verily, if We cause him to taste mercy after some hurt that hath touched him, he will say: This is my own; and I deem not that the Hour will ever rise, and if I am brought back to my Lord, I surely shall be better off with Him - But We verily shall tell those who disbelieve (all) that they did, and We verily shall make them taste hard punishment.',NULL,41,50),
 (12817,1,'And when We show favor to man, he turns aside and withdraws himself; and when evil touches him, he makes lengthy supplications.',NULL,41,51),
 (12818,2,'When We bestow favours on man, he turns away, and gets himself remote on his side (instead of coming to Us); and when evil seizes him, (he comes) full of prolonged prayer!',NULL,41,51),
 (12819,3,'When We show favour unto man, he withdraweth and turneth aside, but when ill toucheth him then he aboundeth in prayer.',NULL,41,51),
 (12820,1,'Say: Tell me if it is from Allah; then you disbelieve in it, who is in greater error than he who is in a prolonged opposition?',NULL,41,52),
 (12821,2,'Say: "See ye if the (Revelation) is (really) from Allah, and yet do ye reject it? Who is more astray than one who is in a schism far (from any purpose)?"',NULL,41,52),
 (12822,3,'Bethink you: If it is from Allah and ye reject it - Who is further astray than one who is at open feud (with Allah)?',NULL,41,52),
 (12823,1,'We will soon show them Our signs in the Universe and in their own souls, until it will become quite clear to them that it is the truth. Is it not sufficient as regards your Lord that He is a witness over all things?',NULL,41,53),
 (12824,2,'Soon will We show them our Signs in the (furthest) regions (of the earth), and in their own souls, until it becomes manifest to them that this is the Truth. Is it not enough that thy Lord doth witness all things?',NULL,41,53),
 (12825,3,'We shall show them Our portents on the horizons and within themselves until it will be manifest unto them that it is the Truth. Doth not thy Lord suffice, since He is Witness over all things?',NULL,41,53),
 (12826,1,'Now surely they are in doubt as to the meeting of their Lord; now surely He encompasses all things.',NULL,41,54),
 (12827,2,'Ah indeed! Are they in doubt concerning the Meeting with their Lord? Ah indeed! It is He that doth encompass all things!',NULL,41,54),
 (12828,3,'How! Are they still in doubt about the meeting with their Lord? Lo! Is not He surrounding all things?',NULL,41,54),
 (12829,1,'Ha Mim.',NULL,42,1),
 (12830,2,'Ha-Mim',NULL,42,1),
 (12831,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,42,1),
 (12832,1,'Ain Sin Qaf.',NULL,42,2),
 (12833,2,'''Ain. Sin. Qaf.',NULL,42,2),
 (12834,3,'A''in. Sin. Qaf.',NULL,42,2),
 (12835,1,'Thus does Allah, the Mighty, the Wise, reveal to you, and (thus He revealed) to those before you.',NULL,42,3),
 (12836,2,'Thus doth (He) send inspiration to thee as (He did) to those before thee,- Allah, Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,42,3),
 (12837,3,'Thus Allah the Mighty, the Knower inspireth thee (Muhammad) as (He inspired) those before thee.',NULL,42,3),
 (12838,1,'His is what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, and He is the High, the Great.',NULL,42,4),
 (12839,2,'To Him belongs all that is in the heavens and on earth: and He is Most High, Most Great.',NULL,42,4),
 (12840,3,'Unto Him belongeth all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth, and He is the Sublime, the Tremendous.',NULL,42,4),
 (12841,1,'The heavens may almost rend asunder from above them and the angels sing the praise of their Lord and ask forgiveness for those on earth; now surely Allah is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,42,5),
 (12842,2,'The heavens are almost rent asunder from above them (by Him Glory): and the angels celebrate the Praises of their Lord, and pray for forgiveness for (all) beings on earth: Behold! Verily Allah is He, the Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,42,5),
 (12843,3,'Almost might the heavens above be rent asunder while the angels hymn the praise of their Lord and ask forgiveness for those on the earth. Lo! Allah, He is the Forgiver, the Merciful.',NULL,42,5),
 (12844,1,'And (as for) those who take guardians besides Him, Allah watches over them, and you have not charge over them.',NULL,42,6),
 (12845,2,'And those who take as protectors others besides Him,- Allah doth watch over them; and thou art not the disposer of their affairs.',NULL,42,6),
 (12846,3,'And as for those who choose protecting friends beside Him, Allah is Warden over them, and thou art in no wise a guardian over them.',NULL,42,6),
 (12847,1,'And thus have We revealed to you an Arabic Quran, that you may warn the mother city and those around it, and that you may give warning of the day of gathering together wherein is no doubt; a party shall be in the garden and (another) party in the burning fire.',NULL,42,7),
 (12848,2,'Thus have We sent by inspiration to thee an Arabic Qur''an: that thou mayest warn the Mother of Cities and all around her,- and warn (them) of the Day of Assembly, of which there is no doubt: (when) some will be in the Garden, and some in the Blazing Fire.',NULL,42,7),
 (12849,3,'And thus We have inspired in thee a Lecture in Arabic, that thou mayst warn the mother-town and those around it, and mayst warn of a day of assembling whereof there is no doubt. A host will be in the Garden, and a host of them in the Flame.',NULL,42,7),
 (12850,1,'And if Allah had pleased He would surely have made them a single community, but He makes whom He pleases enter into His mercy, and the unjust it is that shall have no guardian or helper.',NULL,42,8),
 (12851,2,'If Allah had so willed, He could have made them a single people; but He admits whom He will to His Mercy; and the Wrong-doers will have no protector nor helper.',NULL,42,8),
 (12852,3,'Had Allah willed, He could have made them one community, but Allah bringeth whom He will into His mercy. And the wrong-doers have no friend nor helper.',NULL,42,8),
 (12853,1,'Or have they taken guardians besides Him? But Allah is the Guardian, and He gives life to the dead, and He has power over all things.',NULL,42,9),
 (12854,2,'What! Have they taken (for worship) protectors besides Him? But it is Allah,- He is the Protector, and it is He Who gives life to the dead: It is He Who has power over all things,',NULL,42,9),
 (12855,3,'Or have they chosen protecting friends besides Him? But Allah, He (alone) is the Protecting Friend. He quickeneth the dead, and He is Able to do all things.',NULL,42,9),
 (12856,1,'And in whatever thing you disagree, the judgment thereof is (in) Allah''s (hand); that is Allah, my Lord, on Him do I rely and to Him do I turn time after time.',NULL,42,10),
 (12857,2,'Whatever it be wherein ye differ, the decision thereof is with Allah: such is Allah my Lord: In Him I trust, and to Him I turn.',NULL,42,10),
 (12858,3,'And in whatsoever ye differ, the verdict therein belongeth to Allah. Such is my Lord, in Whom I put my trust, and unto Whom I turn.',NULL,42,10),
 (12859,1,'The Originator of the heavens and the earth; He made mates for you from among yourselves, and mates of the cattle too, multiplying you thereby; nothing like a likeness of Him; and He is the Hearing, the Seeing.',NULL,42,11),
 (12860,2,'(He is) the Creator of the heavens and the earth: He has made for you pairs from among yourselves, and pairs among cattle: by this means does He multiply you: there is nothing whatever like unto Him, and He is the One that hears and sees (all things).',NULL,42,11),
 (12861,3,'The Creator of the heavens and the earth. He hath made for you pairs of yourselves, and of the cattle also pairs, whereby He multiplieth you. Naught is as His likeness; and He is the Hearer, the Seer.',NULL,42,11),
 (12862,1,'His are the treasures of the heavens and the earth; He makes ample and straitens the means of subsistence for whom He pleases; surely He is Cognizant of all things.',NULL,42,12),
 (12863,2,'To Him belong the keys of the heavens and the earth: He enlarges and restricts. The Sustenance to whom He will: for He knows full well all things.',NULL,42,12),
 (12864,3,'His are the keys of the heavens and the earth. He enlargeth providence for whom He will and straiteneth (it for whom He will). Lo! He is Knower of all things.',NULL,42,12),
 (12865,1,'He has made plain to you of the religion what He enjoined upon Nuh and that which We have revealed to you and that which We enjoined upon Ibrahim and Musa and Isa that keep to obedience and be not divided therein; hard to the unbelievers is that which you call them to; Allah chooses for Himself whom He pleases, and guides to Himself him who turns (to Him), frequently.',NULL,42,13),
 (12866,2,'The same religion has He established for you as that which He enjoined on Noah - the which We have sent by inspiration to thee - and that which We enjoined on Abraham, Moses, and Jesus: Namely, that ye should remain steadfast in religion, and make no divisions therein: to those who worship other things than Allah, hard is the (way) to which thou callest them. Allah chooses to Himself those whom He pleases, and guides to Himself those who turn (to Him).',NULL,42,13),
 (12867,3,'He hath ordained for you that religion which He commended unto Noah, and that which We inspire in thee (Muhammad), and that which We commended unto Abraham and Moses and Jesus, saying: Establish the religion, and be not divided therein. Dreadful for the idolaters is that unto which thou callest them. Allah chooseth for Himself whom He will, and guideth unto Himself him who turneth (toward Him).',NULL,42,13),
 (12868,1,'And they did not become divided until after knowledge had come to them out of envy among themselves; and had not a word gone forth from your Lord till an appointed term, certainly judgment would have been given between them; and those who were made to inherit the Book after them are most surely in disquieting doubt concerning it.',NULL,42,14),
 (12869,2,'And they became divided only after Knowledge reached them,- through selfish envy as between themselves. Had it not been for a Word that went forth before from thy Lord, (tending) to a Term appointed, the matter would have been settled between them: But truly those who have inherited the Book after them are in suspicious (disquieting) doubt concerning it.',NULL,42,14),
 (12870,3,'And they were not divided until after the knowledge came unto them, through rivalry among themselves; and had it not been for a Word that had already gone forth from thy Lord for an appointed term, it surely had been judged between them. And those who were made to inherit the Scripture after them are verily in hopeless doubt concerning it.',NULL,42,14),
 (12871,1,'To this then go on inviting, and go on steadfastly on the right way as you are commanded, and do not follow their low desires, and say: I believe in what Allah has revealed of the Book, and I am commanded to do justice between you: Allah is our Lord and your Lord; we shall have our deeds and you shall have your deeds; no plea need there be (now) between us and you: Allah will gather us together, and to Him is the return.',NULL,42,15),
 (12872,2,'Now then, for that (reason), call (them to the Faith), and stand steadfast as thou art commanded, nor follow thou their vain desires; but say: "I believe in the Book which Allah has sent down; and I am commanded to judge justly between you. Allah is our Lord and your Lord: for us (is the responsibility for) our deeds, and for you for your deeds. There is no contention between us and you. Allah will bring us together, and to Him is (our) Final Goal.',NULL,42,15),
 (12873,3,'Unto this, then, summon (O Muhammad). And be thou upright as thou art commanded, and follow not their lusts, but say: I believe in whatever scripture Allah hath sent down, and I am commanded to be just among you. Allah is our Lord and your Lord. Unto us our works and unto you your works; no argument between us and you. Allah will bring us together, and unto Him is the journeying.',NULL,42,15),
 (12874,1,'And (as for) those who dispute about Allah after that obedience has been rendered to Him, their plea is null with their Lord, and upon them is wrath, and for them is severe punishment.',NULL,42,16),
 (12875,2,'But those who dispute concerning Allah after He has been accepted,- futile is their dispute in the Sight of their Lord: on them will be a Penalty terrible.',NULL,42,16),
 (12876,3,'And those who argue concerning Allah after He hath been acknowledged, their argument hath no weight with their Lord, and wrath is upon them and theirs will be an awful doom.',NULL,42,16),
 (12877,1,'Allah it is Who revealed the Book with truth, and the balance, and what shall make you know that haply the hour be nigh?',NULL,42,17),
 (12878,2,'It is Allah Who has sent down the Book in Truth, and the Balance (by which to weigh conduct). And what will make thee realise that perhaps the Hour is close at hand?',NULL,42,17),
 (12879,3,'Allah it is Who hath revealed the Scripture with truth, and the Balance. How canst thou know? It may be that the Hour is nigh.',NULL,42,17),
 (12880,1,'Those who do not believe in it would hasten it on, and those who believe are in fear from it, and they know that it is the truth. Now most surely those who dispute obstinately concerning the hour are in a great error.',NULL,42,18),
 (12881,2,'Only those wish to hasten it who believe not in it: those who believe hold it in awe, and know that it is the Truth. Behold, verily those that dispute concerning the Hour are far astray.',NULL,42,18),
 (12882,3,'Those who believe not therein seek to hasten it, while those who believe are fearful of it and know that it is the Truth. Are not they who dispute, in doubt concerning the Hour, far astray?',NULL,42,18),
 (12883,1,'Allah is Benignant to His servants; He gives sustenance to whom He pleases, and He is the Strong, the Mighty.',NULL,42,19),
 (12884,2,'Gracious is Allah to His servants: He gives Sustenance to whom He pleases: and He has power and can carry out His Will.',NULL,42,19),
 (12885,3,'Allah is gracious unto His slaves. He provideth for whom He will. And He is the Strong, the Mighty.',NULL,42,19),
 (12886,1,'Whoever desires the gain of the hereafter, We will give him more of that gain; and whoever desires the gain of this world, We give him of it, and in the hereafter he has no portion.',NULL,42,20),
 (12887,2,'To any that desires the tilth of the Hereafter, We give increase in his tilth, and to any that desires the tilth of this world, We grant somewhat thereof, but he has no share or lot in the Hereafter.',NULL,42,20),
 (12888,3,'Whoso desireth the harvest of the Hereafter, We give him increase in its harvest. And whoso desireth the harvest of the world, We give him thereof, and he hath no portion in the Hereafter.',NULL,42,20),
 (12889,1,'Or have they associates who have prescribed for them any religion that Allah does not sanction? And were it not for the word of judgment, decision would have certainly been given between them; and surely the unjust shall have a painful punishment.',NULL,42,21),
 (12890,2,'What! have they partners (in godhead), who have established for them some religion without the permission of Allah? Had it not been for the Decree of Judgment, the matter would have been decided between them (at once). But verily the Wrong-doers will have a grievous Penalty.',NULL,42,21),
 (12891,3,'Or have they partners (of Allah) who have made lawful for them in religion that which Allah allowed not? And but for a decisive word (gone forth already), it would have been judged between them. Lo! for wrong-doers is a painful doom.',NULL,42,21),
 (12892,1,'You will see the unjust fearing on account of what they have earned, and it must befall them; and those who believe and do good shall be in the meadows of the gardens; they shall have what they please with their Lord: that is the great grace.',NULL,42,22),
 (12893,2,'Thou wilt see the Wrong-doers in fear on account of what they have earned, and (the burden of) that must (necessarily) fall on them. But those who believe and work righteous deeds will be in the luxuriant meads of the Gardens: they shall have, before their Lord, all that they wish for. That will indeed be the magnificent Bounty (of Allah).',NULL,42,22),
 (12894,3,'Thou seest the wrong-doers fearful of that which they have earned, and it will surely befall them, while those who believe and do good works (will be) in flowering meadows of the Gardens, having what they wish from their Lord. This is the great preferment.',NULL,42,22),
 (12895,1,'That is of which Allah gives the good news to His servants, (to) those who believe and do good deeds. Say: I do not ask of you any reward for it but love for my near relatives; and whoever earns good, We give him more of good therein; surely Allah is Forgiving, Grateful.',NULL,42,23),
 (12896,2,'That is (the Bounty) whereof Allah gives Glad Tidings to His Servants who believe and do righteous deeds. Say: "No reward do I ask of you for this except the love of those near of kin." And if any one earns any good, We shall give him an increase of good in respect thereof: for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Ready to appreciate (service).',NULL,42,23),
 (12897,3,'This it is which Allah announceth unto His bondmen who believe and do good works. Say (O Muhammad, unto mankind): I ask of you no fee therefor, save lovingkindness among kinsfolk. And whoso scoreth a good deed We add unto its good for him. Lo! Allah is Forgiving, Responsive.',NULL,42,23),
 (12898,1,'Or do they say: He has forged a lie against Allah? But if Allah pleased, He would seal your heart; and Allah will blot out the falsehood and confirm the truth with His words; surely He is Cognizant of what is in the breasts.',NULL,42,24),
 (12899,2,'What! Do they say, "He has forged a falsehood against Allah"? But if Allah willed, He could seal up thy heart. And Allah blots out Vanity, and proves the Truth by His Words. For He knows well the secrets of all hearts.',NULL,42,24),
 (12900,3,'Or say they: He hath invented a lie concerning Allah? If Allah willed, He could have sealed thy heart (against them). And Allah will wipe out the lie and will vindicate the truth by His words. Lo! He is Aware of what is hidden in the breasts (of men).',NULL,42,24),
 (12901,1,'And He it is Who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons the evil deeds and He knows what you do;',NULL,42,25),
 (12902,2,'He is the One that accepts repentance from His Servants and forgives sins: and He knows all that ye do.',NULL,42,25),
 (12903,3,'And He it is Who accepteth repentance from His bondmen, and pardoneth the evil deeds, and knoweth what ye do,',NULL,42,25),
 (12904,1,'And He answers those who believe and do good deeds, and gives them more out of His grace; and (as for) the unbelievers, they shall have a severe punishment.',NULL,42,26),
 (12905,2,'And He listens to those who believe and do deeds of righteousness, and gives them increase of His Bounty: but for the Unbelievers their is a terrible Penalty.',NULL,42,26),
 (12906,3,'And accepteth those who do good works, and giveth increase unto them of His bounty. And as for disbelievers, theirs will be an awful doom.',NULL,42,26),
 (12907,1,'And if Allah should amplify the provision for His servants they would certainly revolt in the earth; but He sends it down according to a measure as He pleases; surely He is Aware of, Seeing, His servants.',NULL,42,27),
 (12908,2,'If Allah were to enlarge the provision for His Servants, they would indeed transgress beyond all bounds through the earth; but he sends (it) down in due measure as He pleases. For He is with His Servants Well-acquainted, Watchful.',NULL,42,27),
 (12909,3,'And if Allah were to enlarge the provision for His slaves they would surely rebel in the earth, but He sendeth down by measure as He willeth. Lo! He is Informed, a Seer of His bondmen.',NULL,42,27),
 (12910,1,'And He it is Who sends down the rain after they have despaired, and He unfolds His mercy; and He is the Guardian, the Praised One.',NULL,42,28),
 (12911,2,'He is the One that sends down rain (even) after (men) have given up all hope, and scatters His Mercy (far and wide). And He is the Protector, Worthy of all Praise.',NULL,42,28),
 (12912,3,'And He it is Who sendeth down the saving rain after they have despaired, and spreadeth out His mercy. He is the Protecting Friend, the Praiseworthy.',NULL,42,28),
 (12913,1,'And one of His signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth and what He has spread forth in both of them of living beings; and when He pleases He is all-powerful to gather them together.',NULL,42,29),
 (12914,2,'And among His Signs is the creation of the heavens and the earth, and the living creatures that He has scattered through them: and He has power to gather them together when He wills.',NULL,42,29),
 (12915,3,'And of His portents is the creation of the heaven and the earth, and of whatever beasts He hath dispersed therein. And He is Able to gather them when He will.',NULL,42,29),
 (12916,1,'And whatever affliction befalls you, it is on account of what your hands have wrought, and (yet) He pardons most (of your faults).',NULL,42,30),
 (12917,2,'Whatever misfortune happens to you, is because on the things your hands have wrought, and for many (of them) He grants forgiveness.',NULL,42,30),
 (12918,3,'Whatever of misfortune striketh you, it is what your right hands have earned. And He forgiveth much.',NULL,42,30),
 (12919,1,'And you cannot escape in the earth, and you shall not have a guardian or a helper besides Allah.',NULL,42,31),
 (12920,2,'Nor can ye frustrate (aught), (fleeing) through the earth; nor have ye, besides Allah, any one to protect or to help.',NULL,42,31),
 (12921,3,'Ye cannot escape in the earth, for beside Allah ye have no protecting friend nor any helper.',NULL,42,31),
 (12922,1,'And among His signs are the ships in the sea like mountains.',NULL,42,32),
 (12923,2,'And among His Signs are the ships, smooth-running through the ocean, (tall) as mountains.',NULL,42,32),
 (12924,3,'And of His portents are the ships, like banners on the sea;',NULL,42,32),
 (12925,1,'If He pleases, He causes the wind to become still so that they lie motionless on its back; most surely there are signs in this for every patient, grateful one,',NULL,42,33),
 (12926,2,'If it be His Will He can still the Wind: then would they become motionless on the back of the (ocean). Verily in this are Signs for everyone who patiently perseveres and is grateful.',NULL,42,33),
 (12927,3,'If He will He calmeth the wind so that they keep still upon its surface - Lo! herein verily are signs for every steadfast grateful (heart). -',NULL,42,33),
 (12928,1,'Or He may make them founder for what they have earned, and (even then) pardon most;',NULL,42,34),
 (12929,2,'Or He can cause them to perish because of the (evil) which (the men) have earned; but much doth He forgive.',NULL,42,34),
 (12930,3,'Or He causeth them to perish on account of that which they have earned - And He forgiveth much -',NULL,42,34),
 (12931,1,'And (that) those who dispute about Our communications may know; there is no place of refuge for them.',NULL,42,35),
 (12932,2,'But let those know, who dispute about Our Signs, that there is for them no way of escape.',NULL,42,35),
 (12933,3,'And that those who argue concerning Our revelations may know they have no refuge.',NULL,42,35),
 (12934,1,'So whatever thing you are given, that is only a provision of this world''s life, and what is with Allah is better and more lasting for those who believe and rely on their Lord.',NULL,42,36),
 (12935,2,'Whatever ye are given (here) is (but) a convenience of this life: but that which is with Allah is better and more lasting: (it is) for those who believe and put their trust in their Lord:',NULL,42,36),
 (12936,3,'Now whatever ye have been given is but a passing comfort for the life of the world, and that which Allah hath is better and more lasting for those who believe and put their trust in their Lord,',NULL,42,36),
 (12937,1,'And those who. shun the great sins and indecencies, and whenever they are angry they forgive.',NULL,42,37),
 (12938,2,'Those who avoid the greater crimes and shameful deeds, and, when they are angry even then forgive;',NULL,42,37),
 (12939,3,'And those who shun the worst of sins and indecencies and, when they are wroth, forgive,',NULL,42,37),
 (12940,1,'And those who respond to their Lord and keep up prayer, and their rule is to take counsel among themselves, and who spend out of what We have given them.',NULL,42,38),
 (12941,2,'Those who hearken to their Lord, and establish regular Prayer; who (conduct) their affairs by mutual Consultation; who spend out of what We bestow on them for Sustenance;',NULL,42,38),
 (12942,3,'And those who answer the call of their Lord and establish worship, and whose affairs are a matter of counsel, and who spend of what We have bestowed on them,',NULL,42,38),
 (12943,1,'And those who, when great wrong afflicts them, defend themselves.',NULL,42,39),
 (12944,2,'And those who, when an oppressive wrong is inflicted on them, (are not cowed but) help and defend themselves.',NULL,42,39),
 (12945,3,'And those who, when great wrong is done to them, defend themselves,',NULL,42,39),
 (12946,1,'And the recompense of evil is punishment like it, but whoever forgives and amends, he shall have his reward from Allah; surely He does not love the unjust.',NULL,42,40),
 (12947,2,'The recompense for an injury is an injury equal thereto (in degree): but if a person forgives and makes reconciliation, his reward is due from Allah: for (Allah) loveth not those who do wrong.',NULL,42,40),
 (12948,3,'The guerdon of an ill-deed is an ill the like thereof. But whosoever pardoneth and amendeth, his wage is the affair of Allah. Lo! He loveth not wrong-doers.',NULL,42,40),
 (12949,1,'And whoever defends himself after his being oppressed, these it is against whom there is no way (to blame).',NULL,42,41),
 (12950,2,'But indeed if any do help and defend themselves after a wrong (done) to them, against such there is no cause of blame.',NULL,42,41),
 (12951,3,'And whoso defendeth himself after he hath suffered wrong - for such, there is no way (of blame) against them.',NULL,42,41),
 (12952,1,'The way (to blame) is only against those who oppress men and revolt in the earth unjustly; these shall have a painful punishment.',NULL,42,42),
 (12953,2,'The blame is only against those who oppress men and wrong-doing and insolently transgress beyond bounds through the land, defying right and justice: for such there will be a penalty grievous.',NULL,42,42),
 (12954,3,'The way (of blame) is only against those who oppress mankind, and wrongfully rebel in the earth. For such there is a painful doom.',NULL,42,42),
 (12955,1,'And whoever is patient and forgiving, these most surely are actions due to courage.',NULL,42,43),
 (12956,2,'But indeed if any show patience and forgive, that would truly be an exercise of courageous will and resolution in the conduct of affairs.',NULL,42,43),
 (12957,3,'And verily whoso is patient and forgiveth - lo! that, verily, is (of) the steadfast heart of things.',NULL,42,43),
 (12958,1,'And whomsoever Allah makes err, he has no guardian after Him; and you shall see the unjust, when they see the punishment, saying: Is there any way to return?',NULL,42,44),
 (12959,2,'For any whom Allah leaves astray, there is no protector thereafter. And thou wilt see the Wrong-doers, when in sight of the Penalty, Say: "Is there any way (to effect) a return?"',NULL,42,44),
 (12960,3,'He whom Allah sendeth astray, for him there is no protecting friend after Him. And thou (Muhammad) wilt see the evil-doers when they see the doom, (how) they say: Is there any way of return?',NULL,42,44),
 (12961,1,'And you shall see them brought before it humbling themselves because of the abasements, looking with a faint glance. And those who believe shall say: Surely the losers are they who have lost themselves and their followers on the resurrection day. Now surely the iniquitous shall remain in lasting chastisement.',NULL,42,45),
 (12962,2,'And thou wilt see them brought forward to the (Penalty), in a humble frame of mind because of (their) disgrace, (and) looking with a stealthy glance. And the Believers will say: "Those are indeed in loss, who have given to perdition their own selves and those belonging to them on the Day of Judgment. Behold! Truly the Wrong-doers are in a lasting Penalty!"',NULL,42,45),
 (12963,3,'And thou wilt see them exposed to (the Fire), made humble by disgrace, and looking with veiled eyes. And those who believe will say: Lo! the (eternal) losers are they who lose themselves and their housefolk on the Day of Resurrection. Lo! are not the wrong-doers in perpetual torment?',NULL,42,45),
 (12964,1,'And they shall have no friends to help them besides Allah; and-- whomsoever Allah makes err, he shall have no way.',NULL,42,46),
 (12965,2,'And no protectors have they to help them, other than Allah. And for any whom Allah leaves to stray, there is no way (to the Goal).',NULL,42,46),
 (12966,3,'And they will have no protecting friends to help them instead of Allah. He whom Allah sendeth astray, for him there is no road.',NULL,42,46),
 (12967,1,'Hearken to your Lord before there comes the day from Allah for which there shall be no averting; you shall have no refuge on that day, nor shall it be yours to make a denial.',NULL,42,47),
 (12968,2,'Hearken ye to your Lord, before there come a Day which there will be no putting back, because of (the Ordainment of) Allah! that Day there will be for you no place of refuge nor will there be for you any room for denial (of your sins)!',NULL,42,47),
 (12969,3,'Answer the call of your Lord before there cometh unto you from Allah a Day which there is no averting. Ye have no refuge on that Day, nor have a ye any (power of) refusal.',NULL,42,47),
 (12970,1,'But if they turn aside, We have not sent you as a watcher over them; on you is only to deliver (the message); and surely when We make man taste mercy from Us, he rejoices thereat; and if an evil afflicts them on account of what their hands have already done, then-surely man is ungrateful.',NULL,42,48),
 (12971,2,'If then they run away, We have not sent thee as a guard over them. Thy duty is but to convey (the Message). And truly, when We give man a taste of a Mercy from Ourselves, he doth exult thereat, but when some ill happens to him, on account of the deeds which his hands have sent forth, truly then is man ungrateful!',NULL,42,48),
 (12972,3,'But if they are averse, We have not sent thee as a warder over them. Thine is only to convey (the message). And lo! when We cause man to taste of mercy from Us he exulteth therefor. And if some evil striketh them because of that which their own hands have sent before, then lo! man is an ingrate.',NULL,42,48),
 (12973,1,'Allah''s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; He creates what He pleases; He grants to whom He pleases daughters and grants to whom He pleases sons.',NULL,42,49),
 (12974,2,'To Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. He creates what He wills (and plans). He bestows (children) male or female according to His Will (and Plan),',NULL,42,49),
 (12975,3,'Unto Allah belongeth the Sovereignty of the heavens and the earth. He createth what He will. He bestoweth female (offspring) upon whom He will, and bestoweth male (offspring) upon whom He will;',NULL,42,49),
 (12976,1,'Or He makes them of both sorts, male and female; and He makes whom He pleases barren; surely He is the Knowing, the Powerful.',NULL,42,50),
 (12977,2,'Or He bestows both males and females, and He leaves barren whom He will: for He is full of Knowledge and Power.',NULL,42,50),
 (12978,3,'Or He mingleth them, males and females, and He maketh barren whom He will. Lo! He is Knower, Powerful.',NULL,42,50),
 (12979,1,'And it is not for any mortal that Allah should speak to them, they could not bear to hear and they did not see.',NULL,42,51),
 (12980,2,'It is not fitting for a man that Allah should speak to him except by inspiration, or from behind a veil, or by the sending of a messenger to reveal, with Allah''s permission, what Allah wills: for He is Most High, Most Wise.',NULL,42,51),
 (12981,3,'And it was not (vouchsafed) to any mortal that Allah should speak to him unless (it be) by revelation or from behind a veil, or (that) He sendeth a messenger to reveal what He will by His leave. Lo! He is Exalted, Wise.',NULL,42,51),
 (12982,1,'And thus did We reveal to you an inspired book by Our command. You did not know what the Book was, nor (what) the faith (was), but We made it a light, guiding thereby whom We please of Our servants; and most surely you show the way to the right path:',NULL,42,52),
 (12983,2,'And thus have We, by Our Command, sent inspiration to thee: thou knewest not (before) what was Revelation, and what was Faith; but We have made the (Qur''an) a Light, wherewith We guide such of Our servants as We will; and verily thou dost guide (men) to the Straight Way,-',NULL,42,52),
 (12984,3,'And thus have We inspired in thee (Muhammad) a Spirit of Our command. Thou knewest not what the Scripture was, nor what the Faith. But We have made it a light whereby We guide whom We will of Our bondmen. And lo! thou verily dost guide unto a right path,',NULL,42,52),
 (12985,1,'The path of Allah, Whose is whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; now surely to Allah do all affairs eventually come.',NULL,42,53),
 (12986,2,'The Way of Allah, to Whom belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on earth. Behold (how) all affairs tend towards Allah!',NULL,42,53),
 (12987,3,'The path of Allah, unto Whom belongeth whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth. Do not all things reach Allah at last?',NULL,42,53),
 (12988,1,'Ha Mim.',NULL,43,1),
 (12989,2,'Ha-Mim',NULL,43,1),
 (12990,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,43,1),
 (12991,1,'I swear by the Book that makes things clear:',NULL,43,2),
 (12992,2,'By the Book that makes things clear,-',NULL,43,2),
 (12993,3,'By the Scripture which maketh plain,',NULL,43,2),
 (12994,1,'Surely We have made it an Arabic Quran that you may understand.',NULL,43,3),
 (12995,2,'We have made it a Qur''an in Arabic, that ye may be able to understand (and learn wisdom).',NULL,43,3),
 (12996,3,'Lo! We have appointed it a Lecture, in Arabic that haply ye may understand.',NULL,43,3),
 (12997,1,'And surely it is in the original of the Book with Us, truly elevated, full of wisdom.',NULL,43,4),
 (12998,2,'And verily, it is in the Mother of the Book, in Our Presence, high (in dignity), full of wisdom.',NULL,43,4),
 (12999,3,'And Lo! in the Source of Decrees, which We possess, it is indeed sublime, decisive.',NULL,43,4),
 (13000,1,'What! shall We then turn away the reminder from you altogether because you are an extravagant people?',NULL,43,5),
 (13001,2,'Shall We then take away the Message from you and repel (you), for that ye are a people transgressing beyond bounds?',NULL,43,5),
 (13002,3,'Shall We utterly ignore you because ye are a wanton folk?',NULL,43,5),
 (13003,1,'And how many a prophet have We sent among the ancients.',NULL,43,6),
 (13004,2,'But how many were the prophets We sent amongst the peoples of old?',NULL,43,6),
 (13005,3,'How many a prophet did We send among the men of old!',NULL,43,6),
 (13006,1,'And there came not to them a prophet but they mocked at him.',NULL,43,7),
 (13007,2,'And never came there a prophet to them but they mocked him.',NULL,43,7),
 (13008,3,'And never came there unto them a prophet but they used to mock him.',NULL,43,7),
 (13009,1,'Then We destroyed those who were stronger than these in prowess, and the case of the ancients has gone before,',NULL,43,8),
 (13010,2,'So We destroyed (them)- stronger in power than these;- and (thus) has passed on the Parable of the peoples of old.',NULL,43,8),
 (13011,3,'Then We destroyed men mightier than these in prowess; and the example of the men of old hath gone (before them).',NULL,43,8),
 (13012,1,'And if you should ask them, Who created the heavens and the earth? they would most certainly say: The Mighty, the Knowing One, has created them;',NULL,43,9),
 (13013,2,'If thou wert to question them, ''Who created the heavens and the earth?'' They would be sure to reply, ''they were created by (Him), the Exalted in Power, Full of Knowledge'';-',NULL,43,9),
 (13014,3,'And if thou (Muhammad) ask them: Who created the heavens and the earth, they will surely answer: The Mighty, the Knower created them;',NULL,43,9),
 (13015,1,'He Who made the earth a resting-place for you, and made in it ways for you that you may go aright;',NULL,43,10),
 (13016,2,'(Yea, the same that) has made for you the earth (like a carpet) spread out, and has made for you roads (and channels) therein, in order that ye may find guidance (on the way);',NULL,43,10),
 (13017,3,'Who made the earth a resting-place for you, and placed roads for you therein, that haply ye may find your way;',NULL,43,10),
 (13018,1,'And He Who sends down water from the cloud according to a measure, then We raise to life thereby a dead country, even thus shall you be brought forth;',NULL,43,11),
 (13019,2,'That sends down (from time to time) rain from the sky in due measure;- and We raise to life therewith a land that is dead; even so will ye be raised (from the dead);-',NULL,43,11),
 (13020,3,'And Who sendeth down water from the sky in (due) measure, and We revive a dead land therewith. Even so will ye be brought forth;',NULL,43,11),
 (13021,1,'And He Who created pairs of all things, and made for you of the ships and the cattle what you ride on,',NULL,43,12),
 (13022,2,'That has created pairs in all things, and has made for you ships and cattle on which ye ride,',NULL,43,12),
 (13023,3,'He Who created all the pairs, and appointed for you ships and cattle whereupon ye ride.',NULL,43,12),
 (13024,1,'That you may firmly sit on their backs, then remember the favor of your Lord when you are firmly seated thereon, and say: Glory be to Him Who made this subservient to us and we were not able to do it',NULL,43,13),
 (13025,2,'In order that ye may sit firm and square on their backs, and when so seated, ye may celebrate the (kind) favour of your Lord, and say, "Glory to Him Who has subjected these to our (use), for we could never have accomplished this (by ourselves),',NULL,43,13),
 (13026,3,'That ye may mount upon their backs, and may remember your Lord''s favour when ye mount thereon, and may say: Glorified be He Who hath subdued these unto us, and we were not capable (of subduing them);',NULL,43,13),
 (13027,1,'And surely to our Lord we must return.',NULL,43,14),
 (13028,2,'"And to our Lord, surely, must we turn back!"',NULL,43,14),
 (13029,3,'And lo! unto our Lord we surely are returning.',NULL,43,14),
 (13030,1,'And they assign to Him a part of His servants; man, to be sure, is clearly ungrateful.',NULL,43,15),
 (13031,2,'Yet they attribute to some of His servants a share with Him (in his godhead)! truly is man a blasphemous ingrate avowed!',NULL,43,15),
 (13032,3,'And they allot to Him a portion of His bondmen! Lo! man is verily a mere ingrate.',NULL,43,15),
 (13033,1,'What! has He taken daughters to Himself of what He Himself creates and chosen you to have sons?',NULL,43,16),
 (13034,2,'What! has He taken daughters out of what He himself creates, and granted to you sons for choice?',NULL,43,16),
 (13035,3,'Or chooseth He daughters of all that He hath created, and honoureth He you with sons?',NULL,43,16),
 (13036,1,'And when one of them is given news of that of which he sets up as a likeness for the Beneficent Allah, his face becomes black and he is full of rage.',NULL,43,17),
 (13037,2,'When news is brought to one of them of (the birth of) what he sets up as a likeness to (Allah) Most Gracious, his face darkens, and he is filled with inward grief!',NULL,43,17),
 (13038,3,'And if one of them hath tidings of that which he likeneth to the Beneficent One, his countenance becometh black and he is full of inward rage.',NULL,43,17),
 (13039,1,'What! that which is made in ornaments and which in contention is unable to make plain speech!',NULL,43,18),
 (13040,2,'Is then one brought up among trinkets, and unable to give a clear account in a dispute (to be associated with Allah)?',NULL,43,18),
 (13041,3,'(Liken they then to Allah) that which is bred up in outward show, and in dispute cannot make itself plain?',NULL,43,18),
 (13042,1,'And they make the angels-- them who are the servants of the Beneficent Allah-- female (divinities). What! did they witness their creation? Their evidence shall be written down and they shall be questioned.',NULL,43,19),
 (13043,2,'And they make into females angels who themselves serve Allah. Did they witness their creation? Their evidence will be recorded, and they will be called to account!',NULL,43,19),
 (13044,3,'And they make the angels, who are the slaves of the Beneficent, females. Did they witness their creation? Their testimony will be recorded and they will be questioned.',NULL,43,19),
 (13045,1,'And they say: If the Beneficent Allah had pleased, we should never have worshipped them. They have no knowledge of this; they only lie.',NULL,43,20),
 (13046,2,'("Ah!") they say, "If it had been the will of (Allah) Most Gracious, we should not have worshipped such (deities)!" Of that they have no knowledge! they do nothing but lie!',NULL,43,20),
 (13047,3,'And they say: If the Beneficent One had (so) willed, we should not have worshipped them. They have no knowledge whatsoever of that. They do but guess.',NULL,43,20),
 (13048,1,'Or have We given them a book before it so that they hold fast to it?',NULL,43,21),
 (13049,2,'What! have We given them a Book before this, to which they are holding fast?',NULL,43,21),
 (13050,3,'Or have We given them any scripture before (this Qur''an) so that they are holding fast thereto?',NULL,43,21),
 (13051,1,'Nay! they say: We found our fathers on a course, and surely we are guided by their footsteps.',NULL,43,22),
 (13052,2,'Nay! they say: "We found our fathers following a certain religion, and we do guide ourselves by their footsteps."',NULL,43,22),
 (13053,3,'Nay, for they say only: Lo! we found our fathers following a religion, and we are guided by their footprints.',NULL,43,22),
 (13054,1,'And thus, We did not send before you any warner in a town, but those who led easy lives in it said: Surely we found our fathers on a course, and surely we are followers of their footsteps.',NULL,43,23),
 (13055,2,'Just in the same way, whenever We sent a Warner before thee to any people, the wealthy ones among them said: "We found our fathers following a certain religion, and we will certainly follow in their footsteps."',NULL,43,23),
 (13056,3,'And even so We sent not a warner before thee (Muhammad) into any township but its luxurious ones said: Lo! we found our fathers following a religion, and we are following their footprints.',NULL,43,23),
 (13057,1,'(The warner) said: What! even if I bring to you a better guide than that on which you found your fathers? They said: Surely we are unbelievers in that with which you are sent.',NULL,43,24),
 (13058,2,'He said: "What! Even if I brought you better guidance than that which ye found your fathers following?" They said: "For us, we deny that ye (prophets) are sent (on a mission at all)."',NULL,43,24),
 (13059,3,'(And the warner) said: What! Even though I bring you better guidance than that ye found your fathers following? They answered: Lo! in what ye bring we are disbelievers.',NULL,43,24),
 (13060,1,'So We inflicted retribution on them, then see how was the end of the rejecters.',NULL,43,25),
 (13061,2,'So We exacted retribution from them: now see what was the end of those who rejected (Truth)!',NULL,43,25),
 (13062,3,'So We requited them. Then see the nature of the consequence for the rejecters!',NULL,43,25),
 (13063,1,'And when Ibrahim said to his father and his people: Surely I am clear of what you worship,',NULL,43,26),
 (13064,2,'Behold! Abraham said to his father and his people: "I do indeed clear myself of what ye worship:',NULL,43,26),
 (13065,3,'And when Abraham said unto his father and his folk: Lo! I am innocent of what ye worship',NULL,43,26),
 (13066,1,'Save Him Who created me, for surely He will guide me.',NULL,43,27),
 (13067,2,'"(I worship) only Him Who made me, and He will certainly guide me."',NULL,43,27),
 (13068,3,'Save Him Who did create me, for He will surely guide me.',NULL,43,27),
 (13069,1,'And he made it a word to continue in his posterity that they may return.',NULL,43,28),
 (13070,2,'And he left it as a Word to endure among those who came after him, that they may turn back (to Allah).',NULL,43,28),
 (13071,3,'And he made it a word enduring among his seed, that haply they might return.',NULL,43,28),
 (13072,1,'Nay! I gave them and their fathers to enjoy until there came to them the truth and a Messenger making manifest (the truth).',NULL,43,29),
 (13073,2,'Yea, I have given the good things of this life to these (men) and their fathers, until the Truth has come to them, and a messenger making things clear.',NULL,43,29),
 (13074,3,'Nay, but I let these and their fathers enjoy life (only) till there should come unto them the Truth and a messenger making plain.',NULL,43,29),
 (13075,1,'And when there came to them the truth they said: This is magic, and surely we are disbelievers in it.',NULL,43,30),
 (13076,2,'But when the Truth came to them, they said: "This is sorcery, and we do reject it."',NULL,43,30),
 (13077,3,'And now that the Truth hath come unto them they say: This is mere magic, and lo! we are disbelievers therein.',NULL,43,30),
 (13078,1,'And they say: Why was not this Quran revealed to a man of importance in the two towns?',NULL,43,31),
 (13079,2,'Also, they say: "Why is not this Qur''an sent down to some leading man in either of the two (chief) cities?"',NULL,43,31),
 (13080,3,'And they say: If only this Qur''an had been revealed to some great man of the two towns?',NULL,43,31),
 (13081,1,'Will they distribute the mercy of your Lord? We distribute among them their livelihood in the life of this world, and We j have exalted some of them above others in degrees, that some of them may take others in subjection; and the mercy of your Lord is better than what they amass.',NULL,43,32),
 (13082,2,'Is it they who would portion out the Mercy of thy Lord? It is We Who portion out between them their livelihood in the life of this world: and We raise some of them above others in ranks, so that some may command work from others. But the Mercy of thy Lord is better than the (wealth) which they amass.',NULL,43,32),
 (13083,3,'Is it they who apportion thy Lord''s mercy? We have apportioned among them their livelihood in the life of the world, and raised some of them above others in rank that some of them may take labour from others; and the mercy of thy Lord is better than (the wealth) that they amass.',NULL,43,32),
 (13084,1,'And were it not that all people had been a single nation, We would certainly have assigned to those who disbelieve in the Beneficent Allah (to make) of silver the roofs of their houses and the stairs by which they ascend.',NULL,43,33),
 (13085,2,'And were it not that (all) men might become of one (evil) way of life, We would provide, for everyone that blasphemes against (Allah) Most Gracious, silver roofs for their houses and (silver) stair-ways on which to go up,',NULL,43,33),
 (13086,3,'And were it not that mankind would have become one community, We might well have appointed, for those who disbelieve in the Beneficent, roofs of silver for their houses and stairs (of silver) whereby to mount,',NULL,43,33),
 (13087,1,'And the doors of their houses and the couches on which they recline,',NULL,43,34),
 (13088,2,'And (silver) doors to their houses, and thrones (of silver) on which they could recline,',NULL,43,34),
 (13089,3,'And for their houses doors (of silver) and couches of silver whereon to recline,',NULL,43,34),
 (13090,1,'And (other) embellishments of gold; and all this is naught but provision of this world''s life, and the hereafter is with your Lord only for those who guard (against evil).',NULL,43,35),
 (13091,2,'And also adornments of gold. But all this were nothing but conveniences of the present life: The Hereafter, in the sight of thy Lord is for the Righteous.',NULL,43,35),
 (13092,3,'And ornaments of gold. Yet all that would have been but a provision of the life of the world. And the Hereafter with your Lord would have been for those who keep from evil.',NULL,43,35),
 (13093,1,'And whoever turns himself away from the remembrance of the Beneficent Allah, We appoint for him a Shaitan, so he becomes his associate.',NULL,43,36),
 (13094,2,'If anyone withdraws himself from remembrance of (Allah) Most Gracious, We appoint for him an evil one, to be an intimate companion to him.',NULL,43,36),
 (13095,3,'And he whose sight is dim to the remembrance of the Beneficent, We assign unto him a devil who becometh his comrade;',NULL,43,36),
 (13096,1,'And most surely they turn them away from the path, and they think that they are guided aright:',NULL,43,37),
 (13097,2,'Such (evil ones) really hinder them from the Path, but they think that they are being guided aright!',NULL,43,37),
 (13098,3,'And lo! they surely turn them from the way of Allah, and yet they deem that they are rightly guided;',NULL,43,37),
 (13099,1,'Until when he comes to Us, he says: O would that between me and you there were the distance of the East and the West; so evil is the associate!',NULL,43,38),
 (13100,2,'At length, when (such a one) comes to Us, he says (to his evil companion): "Would that between me and thee were the distance of East and West!" Ah! evil is the companion (indeed)!',NULL,43,38),
 (13101,3,'Till, when he cometh unto Us, he saith (unto his comrade): Ah, would that between me and thee there were the distance of the two horizons - an evil comrade!',NULL,43,38),
 (13102,1,'And since you were unjust, it will not profit you this day that you are sharers in the chastisement.',NULL,43,39),
 (13103,2,'When ye have done wrong, it will avail you nothing, that Day, that ye shall be partners in Punishment!',NULL,43,39),
 (13104,3,'And it profiteth you not this day, because ye did wrong, that ye will be sharers in the doom.',NULL,43,39),
 (13105,1,'What! can you then make the deaf to hear or guide the blind and him who is in clear error?',NULL,43,40),
 (13106,2,'Canst thou then make the deaf to hear, or give direction to the blind or to such as (wander) in manifest error?',NULL,43,40),
 (13107,3,'Canst thou (Muhammad) make the deaf to hear, or canst thou guide the blind or him who is in error manifest?',NULL,43,40),
 (13108,1,'But if We should take you away, still We shall inflict retribution on them;',NULL,43,41),
 (13109,2,'Even if We take thee away, We shall be sure to exact retribution from them,',NULL,43,41),
 (13110,3,'And if We take thee away, We surely shall take vengeance on them,',NULL,43,41),
 (13111,1,'Rather We will certainly show you that which We have promised them; for surely We are the possessors of full power over them.',NULL,43,42),
 (13112,2,'Or We shall show thee that (accomplished) which We have promised them: for verily We shall prevail over them.',NULL,43,42),
 (13113,3,'Or (if) We show thee that wherewith We threaten them; for lo! We have complete command of them.',NULL,43,42),
 (13114,1,'Therefore hold fast to that which has been revealed to you; surely you are on the right path.',NULL,43,43),
 (13115,2,'So hold thou fast to the Revelation sent down to thee; verily thou art on a Straight Way.',NULL,43,43),
 (13116,3,'So hold thou fast to that which is inspired in thee. Lo! thou art on a right path.',NULL,43,43),
 (13117,1,'And most surely it is a reminder for you and your people, and you shall soon be questioned.',NULL,43,44),
 (13118,2,'The (Qur''an) is indeed the message, for thee and for thy people; and soon shall ye (all) be brought to account.',NULL,43,44),
 (13119,3,'And lo! it is in truth a Reminder for thee and for thy folk; and ye will be questioned.',NULL,43,44),
 (13120,1,'And ask those of Our messengers whom We sent before you: Did We ever appoint gods to be worshipped besides the Beneficent Allah?',NULL,43,45),
 (13121,2,'And question thou our messengers whom We sent before thee; did We appoint any deities other than (Allah) Most Gracious, to be worshipped?',NULL,43,45),
 (13122,3,'And ask those of Our messengers whom We sent before thee: Did We ever appoint gods to be worshipped beside the Beneficent?',NULL,43,45),
 (13123,1,'And certainly We sent Musa with Our communications to Firon and his chiefs, so he said: Surely I am the messenger of the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,43,46),
 (13124,2,'We did send Moses aforetime, with Our Signs, to Pharaoh and his Chiefs: He said, "I am a messenger of the Lord of the Worlds."',NULL,43,46),
 (13125,3,'And verily We sent Moses with Our revelations unto Pharaoh and his chiefs, and he said: I am a messenger of the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,43,46),
 (13126,1,'But when he came to them with Our signs, lo! they laughed at them.',NULL,43,47),
 (13127,2,'But when he came to them with Our Signs, behold they ridiculed them.',NULL,43,47),
 (13128,3,'But when he brought them Our tokens, behold! they laughed at them.',NULL,43,47),
 (13129,1,'And We did not show them a sign but it was greater than its like, and We overtook them with chastisement that they may turn.',NULL,43,48),
 (13130,2,'We showed them Sign after Sign, each greater than its fellow, and We seized them with Punishment, in order that they might turn (to Us).',NULL,43,48),
 (13131,3,'And every token that We showed them was greater than its sister (token), and We grasped them with the torment, that haply they might turn again.',NULL,43,48),
 (13132,1,'And they said: O magician! call on your Lord for our sake, as He has made the covenant with you; we shall surely be the followers of the right way.',NULL,43,49),
 (13133,2,'And they said, "O thou sorcerer! Invoke thy Lord for us according to His covenant with thee; for we shall truly accept guidance."',NULL,43,49),
 (13134,3,'And they said: O wizard! Entreat thy Lord for us by the pact that He hath made with thee. Lo! we verily will walk aright.',NULL,43,49),
 (13135,1,'But when We removed from them the chastisement, lo! they broke the pledge.',NULL,43,50),
 (13136,2,'But when We removed the Penalty from them, behold, they broke their word.',NULL,43,50),
 (13137,3,'But when We eased them of the torment, behold! they broke their word.',NULL,43,50),
 (13138,1,'And Firon proclaimed amongst his people: O my people! is not the kingdom of Egypt mine? And these rivers flow beneath me; do you not then see?',NULL,43,51),
 (13139,2,'And Pharaoh proclaimed among his people, saying: "O my people! Does not the dominion of Egypt belong to me, (witness) these streams flowing underneath my (palace)? What! see ye not then?',NULL,43,51),
 (13140,3,'And Pharaoh caused a proclamation to be made among his people saying: O my people! Is not mine the sovereignty of Egypt and these rivers flowing under me? Can ye not then discern?',NULL,43,51),
 (13141,1,'Nay! I am better than this fellow, who is contemptible, and who can hardly speak distinctly:',NULL,43,52),
 (13142,2,'"Am I not better than this (Moses), who is a contemptible wretch and can scarcely express himself clearly?',NULL,43,52),
 (13143,3,'I am surely better than this fellow, who is despicable and can hardly make (his meaning) plain!',NULL,43,52),
 (13144,1,'But why have not bracelets of gold been put upon him, or why have there not come with him angels as companions?',NULL,43,53),
 (13145,2,'"Then why are not gold bracelets bestowed on him, or (why) come (not) with him angels accompanying him in procession?"',NULL,43,53),
 (13146,3,'Why, then, have armlets of gold not been set upon him, or angels sent along with him?',NULL,43,53),
 (13147,1,'So he incited his people to levity and they obeyed him: surely they were a transgressing people.',NULL,43,54),
 (13148,2,'Thus did he make fools of his people, and they obeyed him: truly were they a people rebellious (against Allah).',NULL,43,54),
 (13149,3,'Thus he persuaded his people to make light (of Moses), and they obeyed him. Lo! they were a wanton folk.',NULL,43,54),
 (13150,1,'Then when they displeased Us, We inflicted a retribution on them, so We drowned them all together,',NULL,43,55),
 (13151,2,'When at length they provoked Us, We exacted retribution from them, and We drowned them all.',NULL,43,55),
 (13152,3,'So, when they angered Us, We punished them and drowned them every one.',NULL,43,55),
 (13153,1,'And We made them a precedent and example to the later generations.',NULL,43,56),
 (13154,2,'And We made them (a people) of the Past and an Example to later ages.',NULL,43,56),
 (13155,3,'And We made them a thing past, and an example for those after (them).',NULL,43,56),
 (13156,1,'And when a description of the son of Marium is given, lo! your people raise a clamor thereat.',NULL,43,57),
 (13157,2,'When (Jesus) the son of Mary is held up as an example, behold, thy people raise a clamour thereat (in ridicule)!',NULL,43,57),
 (13158,3,'And when the son of Mary is quoted as an example, behold! the folk laugh out,',NULL,43,57),
 (13159,1,'And they say: Are our gods better, or is he? They do not set it forth to you save by way of disputation; nay, they are a contentious people.',NULL,43,58),
 (13160,2,'And they say, "Are our gods best, or he?" This they set forth to thee, only by way of disputation: yea, they are a contentious people.',NULL,43,58),
 (13161,3,'And say: Are our gods better, or is he? They raise not the objection save for argument. Nay! but they are a contentious folk.',NULL,43,58),
 (13162,1,'He was naught but a servant on whom We bestowed favor, and We made him an example for the children of Israel.',NULL,43,59),
 (13163,2,'He was no more than a servant: We granted Our favour to him, and We made him an example to the Children of Israel.',NULL,43,59),
 (13164,3,'He is nothing but a slave on whom We bestowed favour, and We made him a pattern for the Children of Israel.',NULL,43,59),
 (13165,1,'And if We please, We could make among you angels to be successors in the land.',NULL,43,60),
 (13166,2,'And if it were Our Will, We could make angels from amongst you, succeeding each other on the earth.',NULL,43,60),
 (13167,3,'And had We willed We could have set among you angels to be viceroys in the earth.',NULL,43,60),
 (13168,1,'And most surely it is a knowledge of the hour, therefore have no doubt about it and follow me: this is the right path.',NULL,43,61),
 (13169,2,'And (Jesus) shall be a Sign (for the coming of) the Hour (of Judgment): therefore have no doubt about the (Hour), but follow ye Me: this is a Straight Way.',NULL,43,61),
 (13170,3,'And lo! verily there is knowledge of the Hour. So doubt ye not concerning it, but follow Me. This is the right path.',NULL,43,61),
 (13171,1,'And let not the Shaitan prevent you; surely he is your j open enemy.',NULL,43,62),
 (13172,2,'Let not the Evil One hinder you: for he is to you an enemy avowed.',NULL,43,62),
 (13173,3,'And let not Satan turn you aside. Lo! he is an open enemy for you.',NULL,43,62),
 (13174,1,'And when Isa came with clear arguments he said: I have come to you indeed with wisdom, and that I may make clear to you part of what you differ in; so be careful of (your duty to) Allah and obey me:',NULL,43,63),
 (13175,2,'When Jesus came with Clear Signs, he said: "Now have I come to you with Wisdom, and in order to make clear to you some of the (points) on which ye dispute: therefore fear Allah and obey me.',NULL,43,63),
 (13176,3,'When Jesus came with clear proofs (of Allah''s Sovereignty), he said: I have come unto you with wisdom, and to make plain some of that concerning which ye differ. So keep your duty to Allah, and obey me.',NULL,43,63),
 (13177,1,'Surely Allah is my Lord and your Lord, therefore serve Him; this is the right path:',NULL,43,64),
 (13178,2,'"For Allah, He is my Lord and your Lord: so worship ye Him: this is a Straight Way."',NULL,43,64),
 (13179,3,'Lo! Allah, He is my Lord and your Lord. So worship Him. This is a right path.',NULL,43,64),
 (13180,1,'But parties from among them differed, so woe to those who were unjust because of the chastisement of a painful day.',NULL,43,65),
 (13181,2,'But sects from among themselves fell into disagreement: then woe to the wrong-doers, from the Penalty of a Grievous Day!',NULL,43,65),
 (13182,3,'But the factions among them differed. Then woe unto those who do wrong from the doom of a painful day.',NULL,43,65),
 (13183,1,'Do they wait for aught but the hour, that it should come ! upon them all of a sudden while they do not perceive?',NULL,43,66),
 (13184,2,'Do they only wait for the Hour - that it should come on them all of a sudden, while they perceive not?',NULL,43,66),
 (13185,3,'Await they aught save the Hour, that it shall come upon them suddenly, when they know not?',NULL,43,66),
 (13186,1,'The friends shall on that day be enemies one to another, except those who guard (against evil).',NULL,43,67),
 (13187,2,'Friends on that day will be foes, one to another,- except the Righteous.',NULL,43,67),
 (13188,3,'Friends on that day will be foes one to another, save those who kept their duty (to Allah).',NULL,43,67),
 (13189,1,'O My servants! there is no fear for you this day, nor shall you grieve.',NULL,43,68),
 (13190,2,'My devotees! no fear shall be on you that Day, nor shall ye grieve,-',NULL,43,68),
 (13191,3,'O My slaves! For you there is no fear this day, nor is it ye who grieve;',NULL,43,68),
 (13192,1,'Those who believed in Our communications and were submissive:',NULL,43,69),
 (13193,2,'(Being) those who have believed in Our Signs and bowed (their wills to Ours) in Islam.',NULL,43,69),
 (13194,3,'(Ye) who believed Our revelations and were self-surrendered,',NULL,43,69),
 (13195,1,'Enter the garden, you and your wives; you shall be made happy.',NULL,43,70),
 (13196,2,'Enter ye the Garden, ye and your wives, in (beauty and) rejoicing.',NULL,43,70),
 (13197,3,'Enter the Garden, ye and your wives, to be made glad.',NULL,43,70),
 (13198,1,'There shall be sent round to them golden bowls and drinking-cups and therein shall be what their souls yearn after and (wherein) the eyes shall delight, and you shall abide therein.',NULL,43,71),
 (13199,2,'To them will be passed round, dishes and goblets of gold: there will be there all that the souls could desire, all that their ayes could delight in: and ye shall abide therein (for eye).',NULL,43,71),
 (13200,3,'Therein are brought round for them trays of gold and goblets, and therein is all that souls desire and eyes find sweet. And ye are immortal therein.',NULL,43,71),
 (13201,1,'And this is the garden which you are given as an inheritance on account of what you did.',NULL,43,72),
 (13202,2,'Such will be the Garden of which ye are made heirs for your (good) deeds (in life).',NULL,43,72),
 (13203,3,'This is the Garden which ye are made to inherit because of what ye used to do.',NULL,43,72),
 (13204,1,'For you therein are many fruits of which you shall eat.',NULL,43,73),
 (13205,2,'Ye shall have therein abundance of fruit, from which ye shall have satisfaction.',NULL,43,73),
 (13206,3,'Therein for you is fruit in plenty whence to eat.',NULL,43,73),
 (13207,1,'Surely the guilty shall abide in the chastisement of hell.',NULL,43,74),
 (13208,2,'The sinners will be in the Punishment of Hell, to dwell therein (for aye):',NULL,43,74),
 (13209,3,'Lo! the guilty are immortal in hell''s torment.',NULL,43,74),
 (13210,1,'It shall not be abated from them and they shall therein be despairing.',NULL,43,75),
 (13211,2,'Nowise will the (Punishment) be lightened for them, and in despair will they be there overwhelmed.',NULL,43,75),
 (13212,3,'It is not relaxed for them, and they despair therein.',NULL,43,75),
 (13213,1,'And We are not unjust to them, but they themselves were unjust.',NULL,43,76),
 (13214,2,'Nowise shall We be unjust to them: but it is they who have been unjust themselves.',NULL,43,76),
 (13215,3,'We wronged them not, but they it was who did the wrong.',NULL,43,76),
 (13216,1,'And they shall call out: O Malik! let your Lord make an end of us. He shall say: Surely you shall tarry.',NULL,43,77),
 (13217,2,'They will cry: "O Malik! would that thy Lord put an end to us!" He will say, "Nay, but ye shall abide!"',NULL,43,77),
 (13218,3,'And they cry: O master! Let thy Lord make an end of us. He saith: Lo! here ye must remain.',NULL,43,77),
 (13219,1,'Certainly We have brought you the truth, but most of you are averse to the truth.',NULL,43,78),
 (13220,2,'Verily We have brought the Truth to you: but most of you have a hatred for Truth.',NULL,43,78),
 (13221,3,'We verily brought the Truth unto you, but ye were, most of you, averse to the Truth.',NULL,43,78),
 (13222,1,'Or have they settled an affair? Then surely We are the settlers.',NULL,43,79),
 (13223,2,'What! have they settled some plan (among themselves)? But it is We Who settle things.',NULL,43,79),
 (13224,3,'Or do they determine any thing (against the Prophet)? Lo! We (also) are determining.',NULL,43,79),
 (13225,1,'Or do they think that We do not hear what they conceal and their secret discourses? Aye! and Our messengers with them write down.',NULL,43,80),
 (13226,2,'Or do they think that We hear not their secrets and their private counsels? Indeed (We do), and Our messengers are by them, to record.',NULL,43,80),
 (13227,3,'Or deem they that We cannot hear their secret thoughts and private confidences? Nay, but Our envoys, present with them, do record.',NULL,43,80),
 (13228,1,'Say: If the Beneficent Allah has a son, I am the foremost of those who serve.',NULL,43,81),
 (13229,2,'Say: "If (Allah) Most Gracious had a son, I would be the first to worship."',NULL,43,81),
 (13230,3,'Say (O Muhammad): If the Beneficent One hath a son, then, I shall be first among the worshippers. (But there is no son).',NULL,43,81),
 (13231,1,'Glory to the Lord of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of power, from what they describe.',NULL,43,82),
 (13232,2,'Glory to the Lord of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of the Throne (of Authority)! (He is free) from the things they attribute (to him)!',NULL,43,82),
 (13233,3,'Glorified be the Lord of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of the Throne, from that which they ascribe (unto Him)!',NULL,43,82),
 (13234,1,'So leave them plunging into false discourses and sporting until they meet their day which they are threatened with.',NULL,43,83),
 (13235,2,'So leave them to babble and play (with vanities) until they meet that Day of theirs, which they have been promised.',NULL,43,83),
 (13236,3,'So let them flounder (in their talk) and play until they meet the Day which they are promised.',NULL,43,83),
 (13237,1,'And He it is Who is Allah in the heavens and Allah in the earth; and He is the Wise, the Knowing.',NULL,43,84),
 (13238,2,'It is He Who is Allah in heaven and Allah on earth; and He is full of Wisdom and Knowledge.',NULL,43,84),
 (13239,3,'And He it is Who in the heaven is Allah, and in the earth Allah. He is the Wise, the Knower.',NULL,43,84),
 (13240,1,'And blessed is He Whose is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, and with Him is the knowledge of the hour, and to Him shall you be brought back.',NULL,43,85),
 (13241,2,'And blessed is He to Whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and all between them: with Him is the Knowledge of the Hour (of Judgment): and to Him shall ye be brought back.',NULL,43,85),
 (13242,3,'And blessed be He unto Whom belongeth the Sovereignty of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, and with Whom is knowledge of the Hour, and unto Whom ye will be returned.',NULL,43,85),
 (13243,1,'And those whom they call upon besides Him have no authority for intercession, but he who bears witness of the truth and they know (him).',NULL,43,86),
 (13244,2,'And those whom they invoke besides Allah have no power of intercession;- only he who bears witness to the Truth, and they know (him).',NULL,43,86),
 (13245,3,'And those unto whom they cry instead of Him possess no power of intercession, saving him who beareth witness unto the Truth knowingly.',NULL,43,86),
 (13246,1,'And if you should ask them who created them, they would certainly say: Allah. Whence are they then turned back?',NULL,43,87),
 (13247,2,'If thou ask them, who created them, they will certainly say, Allah: How then are they deluded away (from the Truth)?',NULL,43,87),
 (13248,3,'And if thou ask them who created them, they will surely say: Allah. How then are they turned away?',NULL,43,87),
 (13249,1,'Consider his cry: O my Lord! surely they are a people who do not believe.',NULL,43,88),
 (13250,2,'(Allah has knowledge) of the (Prophet''s) cry, "O my Lord! Truly these are people who will not believe!"',NULL,43,88),
 (13251,3,'And he saith: O my Lord! Lo! these are a folk who believe not.',NULL,43,88),
 (13252,1,'So turn away from them and say, Peace, for they shall soon come to know.',NULL,43,89),
 (13253,2,'But turn away from them, and say "Peace!" But soon shall they know!',NULL,43,89),
 (13254,3,'Then bear with them (O Muhammad) and say: Peace. But they will come to know.',NULL,43,89),
 (13255,1,'Ha Mim!',NULL,44,1),
 (13256,2,'Ha-Mim.',NULL,44,1),
 (13257,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,44,1),
 (13258,1,'I swear by the Book that makes manifest (the truth).',NULL,44,2),
 (13259,2,'By the Book that makes things clear;-',NULL,44,2),
 (13260,3,'By the Scripture that maketh plain',NULL,44,2),
 (13261,1,'Surely We revealed it on a blessed night surely We are ever warning--',NULL,44,3),
 (13262,2,'We sent it down during a Blessed Night: for We (ever) wish to warn (against Evil).',NULL,44,3),
 (13263,3,'Lo! We revealed it on a blessed night - Lo! We are ever warning -',NULL,44,3),
 (13264,1,'Therein every wise affair is made distinct,',NULL,44,4),
 (13265,2,'In the (Night) is made distinct every affair of wisdom,',NULL,44,4),
 (13266,3,'Whereon every wise command is made clear',NULL,44,4),
 (13267,1,'A command from Us; surely We are the senders (of messengers),',NULL,44,5),
 (13268,2,'By command, from Our Presence. For We (ever) send (revelations),',NULL,44,5),
 (13269,3,'As a command from Our presence - Lo! We are ever sending -',NULL,44,5),
 (13270,1,'A mercy from your Lord, surely He is the Hearing, the Knowing,',NULL,44,6),
 (13271,2,'As Mercy from thy Lord: for He hears and knows (all things);',NULL,44,6),
 (13272,3,'A mercy from thy Lord. Lo! He, even He is the Hearer, the Knower,',NULL,44,6),
 (13273,1,'The Lord of the heavens and the earth and what is between them, if you would be sure.',NULL,44,7),
 (13274,2,'The Lord of the heavens and the earth and all between them, if ye (but) have an assured faith.',NULL,44,7),
 (13275,3,'Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is between them, if ye would be sure.',NULL,44,7),
 (13276,1,'There is no god but He; He gives life and causes death, your Lord and the Lord of your fathers of yore.',NULL,44,8),
 (13277,2,'There is no god but He: It is He Who gives life and gives death,- The Lord and Cherisher to you and your earliest ancestors.',NULL,44,8),
 (13278,3,'There is no Allah save Him. He quickeneth and giveth death; your Lord and Lord of your forefathers.',NULL,44,8),
 (13279,1,'Nay, they are in doubt, they sport.',NULL,44,9),
 (13280,2,'Yet they play about in doubt.',NULL,44,9),
 (13281,3,'Nay, but they play in doubt.',NULL,44,9),
 (13282,1,'Therefore keep waiting for the day when the heaven shall bring an evident smoke,',NULL,44,10),
 (13283,2,'Then watch thou for the Day that the sky will bring forth a kind of smoke (or mist) plainly visible,',NULL,44,10),
 (13284,3,'But watch thou (O Muhammad) for the day when the sky will produce visible smoke',NULL,44,10),
 (13285,1,'That shall overtake men; this is a painful punishment.',NULL,44,11),
 (13286,2,'Enveloping the people: this will be a Penalty Grievous.',NULL,44,11),
 (13287,3,'That will envelop the people. This will be a painful torment.',NULL,44,11),
 (13288,1,'Our Lord! remove from us the punishment; surely we are believers.',NULL,44,12),
 (13289,2,'(They will say:) "Our Lord! remove the Penalty from us, for we do really believe!"',NULL,44,12),
 (13290,3,'(Then they will say): Our Lord relieve us of the torment. Lo! we are believers.',NULL,44,12),
 (13291,1,'How shall they be reminded, and there came to them an Messenger making clear (the truth),',NULL,44,13),
 (13292,2,'How shall the message be (effectual) for them, seeing that an Messenger explaining things clearly has (already) come to them,-',NULL,44,13),
 (13293,3,'How can there be remembrance for them, when a messenger making plain (the Truth) had already come unto them,',NULL,44,13),
 (13294,1,'Yet they turned their backs on him and said: One taught (by others), a madman.',NULL,44,14),
 (13295,2,'Yet they turn away from him and say: "Tutored (by others), a man possessed!"',NULL,44,14),
 (13296,3,'And they had turned away from him and said: One taught (by others), a madman?',NULL,44,14),
 (13297,1,'Surely We will remove the punishment a little, (but) you will surely return (to evil).',NULL,44,15),
 (13298,2,'We shall indeed remove the Penalty for a while, (but) truly ye will revert (to your ways).',NULL,44,15),
 (13299,3,'Lo! We withdraw the torment a little. Lo! ye return (to disbelief).',NULL,44,15),
 (13300,1,'On the day when We will seize (them) with the most violent seizing; surely We will inflict retribution.',NULL,44,16),
 (13301,2,'One day We shall seize you with a mighty onslaught: We will indeed (then) exact Retribution!',NULL,44,16),
 (13302,3,'On the day when We shall seize them with the greater seizure, (then) in truth We shall punish.',NULL,44,16),
 (13303,1,'And certainly We tried before them the people of Firon, and there came to them a noble messenger,',NULL,44,17),
 (13304,2,'We did, before them, try the people of Pharaoh: there came to them a messenger most honourable,',NULL,44,17),
 (13305,3,'And verily We tried before them Pharaoh''s folk, when there came unto them a noble messenger,',NULL,44,17),
 (13306,1,'Saying: Deliver to me the servants of Allah, surely I am a faithful messenger to you,',NULL,44,18),
 (13307,2,'Saying: "Restore to me the Servants of Allah: I am to you an messenger worthy of all trust;',NULL,44,18),
 (13308,3,'Saying: Give up to me the slaves of Allah. Lo! I am a faithful messenger unto you.',NULL,44,18),
 (13309,1,'And that do not exalt yourselves against Allah, surely I will bring to you a clear authority:',NULL,44,19),
 (13310,2,'"And be not arrogant as against Allah: for I come to you with authority manifest.',NULL,44,19),
 (13311,3,'And saying: Be not proud against Allah. Lo! I bring you a clear warrant.',NULL,44,19),
 (13312,1,'And surely I take refuge with my Lord and your Lord that you should stone me to death:',NULL,44,20),
 (13313,2,'"For me, I have sought safety with my Lord and your Lord, against your injuring me.',NULL,44,20),
 (13314,3,'And lo! I have sought refuge in my Lord and your Lord lest ye stone me to death.',NULL,44,20),
 (13315,1,'And if you do not believe in me, then leave me alone.',NULL,44,21),
 (13316,2,'"If ye believe me not, at least keep yourselves away from me."',NULL,44,21),
 (13317,3,'And if ye put no faith in me, then let me go.',NULL,44,21),
 (13318,1,'Then he called upon his Lord: These are a guilty people.',NULL,44,22),
 (13319,2,'(But they were aggressive:) then he cried to his Lord: "These are indeed a people given to sin."',NULL,44,22),
 (13320,3,'And he cried unto his Lord, (saying): These are guilty folk.',NULL,44,22),
 (13321,1,'So go forth with My servants by night; surely you will be pursued:',NULL,44,23),
 (13322,2,'(The reply came:) "March forth with My Servants by night: for ye are sure to be pursued.',NULL,44,23),
 (13323,3,'Then (his Lord commanded): Take away My slaves by night. Lo! ye will be followed,',NULL,44,23),
 (13324,1,'And leave the sea intervening; surely they are a host that shall be drowned.',NULL,44,24),
 (13325,2,'"And leave the sea as a furrow (divided): for they are a host (destined) to be drowned."',NULL,44,24),
 (13326,3,'And leave the sea behind at rest, for lo! they are a drowned host.',NULL,44,24),
 (13327,1,'How many of the gardens and fountains have they left!',NULL,44,25),
 (13328,2,'How many were the gardens and springs they left behind,',NULL,44,25),
 (13329,3,'How many were the gardens and the watersprings that they left behind,',NULL,44,25),
 (13330,1,'And cornfields and noble places!',NULL,44,26),
 (13331,2,'And corn-fields and noble buildings,',NULL,44,26),
 (13332,3,'And the cornlands and the goodly sites',NULL,44,26),
 (13333,1,'And goodly things wherein they rejoiced;',NULL,44,27),
 (13334,2,'And wealth (and conveniences of life), wherein they had taken such delight!',NULL,44,27),
 (13335,3,'And pleasant things wherein they took delight!',NULL,44,27),
 (13336,1,'Thus (it was), and We gave them as a heritage to another people.',NULL,44,28),
 (13337,2,'Thus (was their end)! And We made other people inherit (those things)!',NULL,44,28),
 (13338,3,'Even so (it was), and We made it an inheritance for other folk;',NULL,44,28),
 (13339,1,'So the heaven and the earth did not weep for them, nor were they respited.',NULL,44,29),
 (13340,2,'And neither heaven nor earth shed a tear over them: nor were they given a respite (again).',NULL,44,29),
 (13341,3,'And the heaven and the earth wept not for them, nor were they reprieved.',NULL,44,29),
 (13342,1,'And certainly We delivered the children of Israel from the abasing chastisement,',NULL,44,30),
 (13343,2,'We did deliver aforetime the Children of Israel from humiliating Punishment,',NULL,44,30),
 (13344,3,'And We delivered the Children of Israel from the shameful doom;',NULL,44,30),
 (13345,1,'From Firon; surely he was haughty, (and) one of the extravagant.',NULL,44,31),
 (13346,2,'Inflicted by Pharaoh, for he was arrogant (even) among inordinate transgressors.',NULL,44,31),
 (13347,3,'(We delivered them) from Pharaoh. Lo! he was a tyrant of the wanton ones.',NULL,44,31),
 (13348,1,'And certainly We chose them, having knowledge, above the nations.',NULL,44,32),
 (13349,2,'And We chose them aforetime above the nations, knowingly,',NULL,44,32),
 (13350,3,'And We chose them, purposely, above (all) creatures.',NULL,44,32),
 (13351,1,'And We gave them of the communications wherein was clear blessing.',NULL,44,33),
 (13352,2,'And granted them Signs in which there was a manifest trial',NULL,44,33),
 (13353,3,'And We gave them portents wherein was a clear trial.',NULL,44,33),
 (13354,1,'Most surely these do say:',NULL,44,34),
 (13355,2,'As to these (Quraish), they say forsooth:',NULL,44,34),
 (13356,3,'Lo! these, forsooth, are saying:',NULL,44,34),
 (13357,1,'There is naught but our first death and we shall not be raised again.',NULL,44,35),
 (13358,2,'"There is nothing beyond our first death, and we shall not be raised again.',NULL,44,35),
 (13359,3,'There is naught but our first death, and we shall not be raised again.',NULL,44,35),
 (13360,1,'So bring our fathers (back), if you are truthful.',NULL,44,36),
 (13361,2,'"Then bring (back) our forefathers, if what ye say is true!"',NULL,44,36),
 (13362,3,'Bring back our fathers, if ye speak the truth!',NULL,44,36),
 (13363,1,'Are they better or the people of Tubba and those before them? We destroyed them, for surely they were guilty.',NULL,44,37),
 (13364,2,'What! Are they better than the people of Tubba and those who were before them? We destroyed them because they were guilty of sin.',NULL,44,37),
 (13365,3,'Are they better, or the folk of Tubb''a and those before them? We destroyed them, for surely they were guilty.',NULL,44,37),
 (13366,1,'And We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them in sport.',NULL,44,38),
 (13367,2,'We created not the heavens, the earth, and all between them, merely in (idle) sport:',NULL,44,38),
 (13368,3,'And We created not the heavens and the earth, and all that is between them, in play.',NULL,44,38),
 (13369,1,'We did not create them both but with the truth, but most of them do not know.',NULL,44,39),
 (13370,2,'We created them not except for just ends: but most of them do not understand.',NULL,44,39),
 (13371,3,'We created them not save with truth; but most of them know not.',NULL,44,39),
 (13372,1,'Surely the day of separation is their appointed term, of all of them',NULL,44,40),
 (13373,2,'Verily the Day of sorting out is the time appointed for all of them,-',NULL,44,40),
 (13374,3,'Assuredly the Day of Decision is the term for all of them,',NULL,44,40),
 (13375,1,'The day on which a friend shall not avail (his) friend aught, nor shall they be helped,',NULL,44,41),
 (13376,2,'The Day when no protector can avail his client in aught, and no help can they receive,',NULL,44,41),
 (13377,3,'A day when friend can in naught avail friend, nor can they be helped,',NULL,44,41),
 (13378,1,'Save those on whom Allah shall have mercy; surely He is the Mighty the Merciful.',NULL,44,42),
 (13379,2,'Except such as receive Allah''s Mercy: for He is Exalted in Might, Most Merciful.',NULL,44,42),
 (13380,3,'Save him on whom Allah hath mercy. Lo! He is the Mighty, the Merciful.',NULL,44,42),
 (13381,1,'Surely the tree of the Zaqqum,',NULL,44,43),
 (13382,2,'Verily the tree of Zaqqum',NULL,44,43),
 (13383,3,'Lo! the tree of Zaqqum,',NULL,44,43),
 (13384,1,'Is the food of the sinful',NULL,44,44),
 (13385,2,'Will be the food of the Sinful,-',NULL,44,44),
 (13386,3,'The food of the sinner!',NULL,44,44),
 (13387,1,'Like dregs of oil; it shall boil in (their) bellies,',NULL,44,45),
 (13388,2,'Like molten brass; it will boil in their insides.',NULL,44,45),
 (13389,3,'Like molten brass, it seetheth in their bellies',NULL,44,45),
 (13390,1,'Like the boiling of hot water.',NULL,44,46),
 (13391,2,'Like the boiling of scalding water.',NULL,44,46),
 (13392,3,'As the seething of boiling water.',NULL,44,46),
 (13393,1,'Seize him, then drag him down into the middle of the hell;',NULL,44,47),
 (13394,2,'(A voice will cry: "Seize ye him and drag him into the midst of the Blazing Fire!',NULL,44,47),
 (13395,3,'(And it will be said): Take him and drag him to the midst of hell,',NULL,44,47),
 (13396,1,'Then pour above his head of the torment of the boiling water:',NULL,44,48),
 (13397,2,'"Then pour over his head the Penalty of Boiling Water,',NULL,44,48),
 (13398,3,'Then pour upon his head the torment of boiling water.',NULL,44,48),
 (13399,1,'Taste; you forsooth are the mighty, the honorable:',NULL,44,49),
 (13400,2,'"Taste thou (this)! Truly wast thou mighty, full of honour!',NULL,44,49),
 (13401,3,'(Saying): Taste! Lo! thou wast forsooth the mighty, the noble!',NULL,44,49),
 (13402,1,'Surely this is what you disputed about.',NULL,44,50),
 (13403,2,'"Truly this is what ye used to doubt!"',NULL,44,50),
 (13404,3,'Lo! this is that whereof ye used to doubt.',NULL,44,50),
 (13405,1,'Surely those who guard (against evil) are in a secure place,',NULL,44,51),
 (13406,2,'As to the Righteous (they will be) in a position of Security,',NULL,44,51),
 (13407,3,'Lo! those who kept their duty will be in a place secured.',NULL,44,51),
 (13408,1,'In gardens and springs;',NULL,44,52),
 (13409,2,'Among Gardens and Springs;',NULL,44,52),
 (13410,3,'Amid gardens and watersprings,',NULL,44,52),
 (13411,1,'They shall wear of fine and thick silk, (sitting) face to face;',NULL,44,53),
 (13412,2,'Dressed in fine silk and in rich brocade, they will face each other;',NULL,44,53),
 (13413,3,'Attired in silk and silk embroidery, facing one another.',NULL,44,53),
 (13414,1,'Thus (shall it be), and We will wed them with Houris pure, beautiful ones.',NULL,44,54),
 (13415,2,'So; and We shall join them to fair women with beautiful, big, and lustrous eyes.',NULL,44,54),
 (13416,3,'Even so (it will be). And We shall wed them unto fair ones with wide, lovely eyes.',NULL,44,54),
 (13417,1,'They shall call therein for every fruit in security;',NULL,44,55),
 (13418,2,'There can they call for every kind of fruit in peace and security;',NULL,44,55),
 (13419,3,'They call therein for every fruit in safety.',NULL,44,55),
 (13420,1,'They shall not taste therein death except the first death, and He will save them from the punishment of the hell,',NULL,44,56),
 (13421,2,'Nor will they there taste Death, except the first death; and He will preserve them from the Penalty of the Blazing Fire,-',NULL,44,56),
 (13422,3,'They taste not death therein, save the first death. And He hath saved them from the doom of hell,',NULL,44,56),
 (13423,1,'A grace from your Lord; this is the great achievement.',NULL,44,57),
 (13424,2,'As a Bounty from thy Lord! that will be the supreme achievement!',NULL,44,57),
 (13425,3,'A bounty from thy Lord. That is the supreme triumph.',NULL,44,57),
 (13426,1,'So have We made it easy in your tongue that they may be mindful.',NULL,44,58),
 (13427,2,'Verily, We have made this (Qur''an) easy, in thy tongue, in order that they may give heed.',NULL,44,58),
 (13428,3,'And We have made (this Scripture) easy in thy language only that they may heed.',NULL,44,58),
 (13429,1,'Therefore wait; surely they are waiting.',NULL,44,59),
 (13430,2,'So wait thou and watch; for they (too) are waiting.',NULL,44,59),
 (13431,3,'Wait then (O Muhammad). Lo! they (too) are waiting.',NULL,44,59),
 (13432,1,'Ha Mim.',NULL,45,1),
 (13433,2,'Ha-Mim.',NULL,45,1),
 (13434,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,45,1),
 (13435,1,'The revelation of the Book is from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,45,2),
 (13436,2,'The revelation of the Book is from Allah the Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,45,2),
 (13437,3,'The revelation of the Scripture is from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,45,2),
 (13438,1,'Most surely in the heavens and the earth there are signs for the believers.',NULL,45,3),
 (13439,2,'Verily in the heavens and the earth, are Signs for those who believe.',NULL,45,3),
 (13440,3,'Lo! in the heavens and the earth are portents for believers.',NULL,45,3),
 (13441,1,'And in your (own) creation and in what He spreads abroad of animals there are signs for a people that are sure;',NULL,45,4),
 (13442,2,'And in the creation of yourselves and the fact that animals are scattered (through the earth), are Signs for those of assured Faith.',NULL,45,4),
 (13443,3,'And in your creation, and all the beasts that He scattereth in the earth, are portents for a folk whose faith is sure.',NULL,45,4),
 (13444,1,'And (in) the variation of the night and the day, and (in) what Allah sends down of sustenance from the cloud, then gives life thereby to the earth after its death, and (in) the changing of the winds, there are signs for a people who understand.',NULL,45,5),
 (13445,2,'And in the alternation of Night and Day, and the fact that Allah sends down Sustenance from the sky, and revives therewith the earth after its death, and in the change of the winds,- are Signs for those that are wise.',NULL,45,5),
 (13446,3,'And the difference of night and day and the provision that Allah sendeth down from the sky and thereby quickeneth the earth after her death, and the ordering of the winds, are portents for a people who have sense.',NULL,45,5),
 (13447,1,'These are the communications of Allah which We recite to you with truth; then in what announcement would they believe after Allah and His communications?',NULL,45,6),
 (13448,2,'Such are the Signs of Allah, which We rehearse to thee in Truth; then in what exposition will they believe after (rejecting) Allah and His Signs?',NULL,45,6),
 (13449,3,'These are the portents of Allah which We recite unto thee (Muhammad) with truth. Then in what fact, after Allah and His portents, will they believe?',NULL,45,6),
 (13450,1,'Woe to every sinful liar,',NULL,45,7),
 (13451,2,'Woe to each sinful dealer in Falsehoods:',NULL,45,7),
 (13452,3,'Woe unto each sinful liar,',NULL,45,7),
 (13453,1,'Who hears the communications of Allah recited to him, then persists proudly as though he had not heard them; so announce to him a painful punishment.',NULL,45,8),
 (13454,2,'He hears the Signs of Allah rehearsed to him, yet is obstinate and lofty, as if he had not heard them: then announce to him a Penalty Grievous!',NULL,45,8),
 (13455,3,'Who heareth the revelations of Allah recited unto him, and then continueth in pride as though he heard them not. Give him tidings of a painful doom.',NULL,45,8),
 (13456,1,'And when he comes to know of any of Our communications, he takes it for a jest; these it is that shall have abasing chastisement.',NULL,45,9),
 (13457,2,'And when he learns something of Our Signs, he takes them in jest: for such there will be a humiliating Penalty.',NULL,45,9),
 (13458,3,'And when he knoweth aught of Our revelations he maketh it a jest. For such there is a shameful doom.',NULL,45,9),
 (13459,1,'Before them is hell, and there shall not avail them aught of what they earned, nor those whom they took for guardians besides Allah, and they shall have a grievous punishment.',NULL,45,10),
 (13460,2,'In front of them is Hell: and of no profit to them is anything they may have earned, nor any protectors they may have taken to themselves besides Allah: for them is a tremendous Penalty.',NULL,45,10),
 (13461,3,'Beyond them there is hell, and that which they have earned will naught avail them, nor those whom they have chosen for protecting friends beside Allah. Theirs will be an awful doom.',NULL,45,10),
 (13462,1,'This is guidance; and (as for) those who disbelieve in the communications of their Lord, they shall have a painful punishment on account of uncleanness.',NULL,45,11),
 (13463,2,'This is (true) Guidance and for those who reject the Signs of their Lord, is a grievous Penalty of abomination.',NULL,45,11),
 (13464,3,'This is guidance. And those who disbelieve the revelations of their Lord, for them there is a painful doom of wrath.',NULL,45,11),
 (13465,1,'Allah is He Who made subservient to you the sea that the ships may run therein by His command, and that you may seek of His grace, and that you may give thanks.',NULL,45,12),
 (13466,2,'It is Allah Who has subjected the sea to you, that ships may sail through it by His command, that ye may seek of his Bounty, and that ye may be grateful.',NULL,45,12),
 (13467,3,'Allah it is Who hath made the sea of service unto you that the ships may run thereon by His command, and that ye may seek of His bounty, and that haply ye may be thankful;',NULL,45,12),
 (13468,1,'And He has made subservient to you whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth, all, from Himself; most surely there are signs in this for a people who reflect.',NULL,45,13),
 (13469,2,'And He has subjected to you, as from Him, all that is in the heavens and on earth: Behold, in that are Signs indeed for those who reflect.',NULL,45,13),
 (13470,3,'And hath made of service unto you whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth; it is all from Him. Lo! herein verily are portents for a people who reflect.',NULL,45,13),
 (13471,1,'Say to those who believe (that) they forgive those who do not fear the days of Allah that He may reward a people for what they earn.',NULL,45,14),
 (13472,2,'Tell those who believe, to forgive those who do not look forward to the Days of Allah: It is for Him to recompense (for good or ill) each People according to what they have earned.',NULL,45,14),
 (13473,3,'Tell those who believe to forgive those who hope not for the days of Allah; in order that He may requite folk what they used to earn.',NULL,45,14),
 (13474,1,'Whoever does good, it is for his own soul, and whoever does evil, it is against himself; then you shall be brought back to your-- Lord.',NULL,45,15),
 (13475,2,'If any one does a righteous deed, it ensures to the benefit of his own soul; if he does evil, it works against (his own soul). In the end will ye (all) be brought back to your Lord.',NULL,45,15),
 (13476,3,'Whoso doeth right, it is for his soul, and whoso doeth wrong, it is against it. And afterward unto your Lord ye will be brought back.',NULL,45,15),
 (13477,1,'And certainly We gave the Book and the wisdom and the prophecy to the children of Israel, and We gave them of the goodly things, and We made them excel the nations.',NULL,45,16),
 (13478,2,'We did aforetime grant to the Children of Israel the Book the Power of Command, and Prophethood; We gave them, for Sustenance, things good and pure; and We favoured them above the nations.',NULL,45,16),
 (13479,3,'And verily we gave the Children of Israel the Scripture and the Command and the Prophethood, and provided them with good things and favoured them above (all) peoples;',NULL,45,16),
 (13480,1,'And We gave them clear arguments in the affair, but they did not differ until after knowledge had come to them out of envy among themselves; surely your -Lord will judge between them on the day of resurrection concerning that wherein they differed.',NULL,45,17),
 (13481,2,'And We granted them Clear Signs in affairs (of Religion): it was only after knowledge had been granted to them that they fell into schisms, through insolent envy among themselves. Verily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Judgment as to those matters in which they set up differences.',NULL,45,17),
 (13482,3,'And gave them plain commandments. And they differed not until after the knowledge came unto them, through rivalry among themselves. Lo! thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that wherein they used to differ.',NULL,45,17),
 (13483,1,'Then We have made you follow a course in the affair, therefore follow it, and do not follow the low desires of those who do not know.',NULL,45,18),
 (13484,2,'Then We put thee on the (right) Way of Religion: so follow thou that (Way), and follow not the desires of those who know not.',NULL,45,18),
 (13485,3,'And now have We set thee (O Muhammad) on a clear road of (Our) commandment; so follow it, and follow not the whims of those who know not.',NULL,45,18),
 (13486,1,'Surely they shall not avail you in the least against Allah; and surely the unjust are friends of each other, and Allah is the guardian of those who guard (against evil).',NULL,45,19),
 (13487,2,'They will be of no use to thee in the sight of Allah: it is only Wrong-doers (that stand as) protectors, one to another: but Allah is the Protector of the Righteous.',NULL,45,19),
 (13488,3,'Lo! they can avail thee naught against Allah. And lo! as for the wrong-doers, some of them are friends of others; and Allah is the Friend of those who ward off (evil).',NULL,45,19),
 (13489,1,'These are clear proofs for men, and a guidance and a mercy for a people who are sure.',NULL,45,20),
 (13490,2,'These are clear evidences to men and a Guidance and Mercy to those of assured Faith.',NULL,45,20),
 (13491,3,'This is clear indication for mankind, and a guidance and a mercy for a folk whose faith is sure.',NULL,45,20),
 (13492,1,'Nay! do those who have wrought evil deeds think that We will make them like those who believe and do good-- that their life and their death shall be equal? Evil it is that they judge.',NULL,45,21),
 (13493,2,'What! Do those who seek after evil ways think that We shall hold them equal with those who believe and do righteous deeds,- that equal will be their life and their death? Ill is the judgment that they make.',NULL,45,21),
 (13494,3,'Or do those who commit ill-deeds suppose that We shall make them as those who believe and do good works, the same in life and death? Bad is their judgment!',NULL,45,21),
 (13495,1,'And Allah created the heavens and the earth with truth and that every soul may be rewarded for what it has earned and they shall not be wronged.',NULL,45,22),
 (13496,2,'Allah created the heavens and the earth for just ends, and in order that each soul may find the recompense of what it has earned, and none of them be wronged.',NULL,45,22),
 (13497,3,'And Allah hath created the heavens and the earth with truth, and that every soul may be repaid what it hath earned. And they will not be wronged.',NULL,45,22),
 (13498,1,'Have you then considered him who takes his low desire for his god, and Allah has made him err having knowledge and has set a seal upon his ear and his heart and put a covering upon his eye. Who can then guide him after Allah? Will you not then be mindful?',NULL,45,23),
 (13499,2,'Then seest thou such a one as takes as his god his own vain desire? Allah has, knowing (him as such), left him astray, and sealed his hearing and his heart (and understanding), and put a cover on his sight. Who, then, will guide him after Allah (has withdrawn Guidance)? Will ye not then receive admonition?',NULL,45,23),
 (13500,3,'Hast thou seen him who maketh his desire his god, and Allah sendeth him astray purposely, and sealeth up his hearing and his heart, and setteth on his sight a covering? Then who will lead him after Allah (hath condemned him)? Will ye not then heed?',NULL,45,23),
 (13501,1,'And they say: There is nothing but our life in this world; we live and die and nothing destroys us but time, and they have no knowledge of that; they only conjecture.',NULL,45,24),
 (13502,2,'And they say: "What is there but our life in this world? We shall die and we live, and nothing but time can destroy us." But of that they have no knowledge: they merely conjecture:',NULL,45,24),
 (13503,3,'And they say: There is naught but our life of the world; we die and we live, and naught destroyeth us save time; when they have no knowledge whatsoever of (all) that; they do but guess.',NULL,45,24),
 (13504,1,'And when Our clear communications are recited to them, their argument is no other than that they say: Bring our fathers (back) if you are truthful.',NULL,45,25),
 (13505,2,'And when Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them their argument is nothing but this: They say, "Bring (back) our forefathers, if what ye say is true!"',NULL,45,25),
 (13506,3,'And when Our clear revelations are recited unto them their only argument is that they say: Bring (back) our fathers. then, if ye are truthful.',NULL,45,25),
 (13507,1,'Say: Allah gives you life, then He makes you die, then will He gather you to the day of resurrection wherein is no doubt, but most people do not know.',NULL,45,26),
 (13508,2,'Say: "It is Allah Who gives you life, then gives you death; then He will gather you together for the Day of Judgment about which there is no doubt": But most men do not understand.',NULL,45,26),
 (13509,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Allah giveth life to you, then causeth you to die, then gathereth you unto the Day of Resurrection whereof there is no doubt. But most of mankind know not.',NULL,45,26),
 (13510,1,'And Allah''s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and on the day when the hour shall come to pass, on that day shall they perish who say false things.',NULL,45,27),
 (13511,2,'To Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and the Day that the Hour of Judgment is established,- that Day will the dealers in Falsehood perish!',NULL,45,27),
 (13512,3,'And unto Allah belongeth the Sovereignty of the heavens and the earth; and on the day when the Hour riseth, on that day those who follow falsehood will be lost.',NULL,45,27),
 (13513,1,'And you shall see every nation kneeling down; every nation shall be called to its book: today you shall be rewarded for what you did.',NULL,45,28),
 (13514,2,'And thou wilt see every sect bowing the knee: Every sect will be called to its Record: "This Day shall ye be recompensed for all that ye did!',NULL,45,28),
 (13515,3,'And thou wilt see each nation crouching, each nation summoned to its record. (And it will be said unto them): This day ye are requited what ye used to do.',NULL,45,28),
 (13516,1,'This is Our book that speaks against you with justice; surely We wrote what you did,',NULL,45,29),
 (13517,2,'"This Our Record speaks about you with truth: For We were wont to put on Record all that ye did."',NULL,45,29),
 (13518,3,'This Our Book pronounceth against you with truth. Lo! We have caused (all) that ye did to be recorded.',NULL,45,29),
 (13519,1,'Then as to those who believed and did good, their Lord will make them enter into His mercy; that is the manifest achievement.',NULL,45,30),
 (13520,2,'Then, as to those who believed and did righteous deeds, their Lord will admit them to His Mercy that will be the achievement for all to see.',NULL,45,30),
 (13521,3,'Then, as for those who believed and did good works, their Lord will bring them in unto His mercy. That is the evident triumph.',NULL,45,30),
 (13522,1,'As to those who disbelieved: What! were not My communications recited to you? But you were proud and you were a guilty people.',NULL,45,31),
 (13523,2,'But as to those who rejected Allah, (to them will be said): "Were not Our Signs rehearsed to you? But ye were arrogant, and were a people given to sin!',NULL,45,31),
 (13524,3,'And as for those who disbelieved (it will be said unto them): Were not Our revelations recited unto you? But ye were scornful and became a guilty folk.',NULL,45,31),
 (13525,1,'And when it was said, Surely the promise of Allah is true and as for the hour, there is no doubt about it, you said: We do not know what the hour is; we do not think (that it will come to pass) save a passing thought, and we are not at all sure.',NULL,45,32),
 (13526,2,'"And when it was said that the promise of Allah was true, and that the Hour- there was no doubt about its (coming), ye used to say, ''We know not what is the hour: we only think it is an idea, and we have no firm assurance.''"',NULL,45,32),
 (13527,3,'And when it was said: Lo! Allah''s promise is the truth, and there is no doubt of the Hour''s coming, ye said: We know not what the Hour is. We deem it naught but a conjecture, and we are by no means convinced.',NULL,45,32),
 (13528,1,'And the evil (consequences) of what they did shall become manifest to them and that which they mocked shall encompass them.',NULL,45,33),
 (13529,2,'Then will appear to them the evil (fruits) of what they did, and they will be completely encircled by that which they used to mock at!',NULL,45,33),
 (13530,3,'And the evils of what they did will appear unto them, and that which they used to deride will befall them.',NULL,45,33),
 (13531,1,'And it shall be said: Today We forsake you as you neglected the meeting of this day of yours and your abode is the fire, and there are not for you any helpers:',NULL,45,34),
 (13532,2,'It will also be said: "This Day We will forget you as ye forgot the meeting of this Day of yours! and your abode is the Fire, and no helpers have ye!',NULL,45,34),
 (13533,3,'And it will be said: This day We forget you, even as ye forgot the meeting of this your day; and your habitation is the Fire, and there is none to help you.',NULL,45,34),
 (13534,1,'That is because you took the communications of Allah for a jest and the life of this world deceived you. So on that day they shall not be brought forth from it, nor shall they be granted goodwill.',NULL,45,35),
 (13535,2,'"This, because ye used to take the Signs of Allah in jest, and the life of the world deceived you:" (From) that Day, therefore, they shall not be taken out thence, nor shall they be received into Grace.',NULL,45,35),
 (13536,3,'This, forasmuch as ye made the revelations of Allah a jest, and the life of the world beguiled you. Therefor this day they come not forth from thence, nor can they make amends.',NULL,45,35),
 (13537,1,'Therefore to Allah is due (all) praise, the Lord of the heavens and the Lord of the earth, the Lord of the worlds.',NULL,45,36),
 (13538,2,'Then Praise be to Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth,- Lord and Cherisher of all the Worlds!',NULL,45,36),
 (13539,3,'Then praise be to Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, the Lord of the Worlds.',NULL,45,36),
 (13540,1,'And to Him belongs greatness in the heavens and the earth, and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,45,37),
 (13541,2,'To Him be glory throughout the heavens and the earth: and He is Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom!',NULL,45,37),
 (13542,3,'And unto Him (alone) belongeth Majesty in the heavens and the earth, and He is the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,45,37),
 (13543,1,'Ha Mim.',NULL,46,1),
 (13544,2,'Ha-Mim.',NULL,46,1),
 (13545,3,'Ha. Mim.',NULL,46,1),
 (13546,1,'The revelation of the Book is from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,46,2),
 (13547,2,'The Revelation of the Book is from Allah the Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,46,2),
 (13548,3,'The revelation of the Scripture is from Allah the Mighty, the Wise.',NULL,46,2),
 (13549,1,'We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them two save with truth and (for) an appointed term; and those who disbelieve turn aside from what they are warned of.',NULL,46,3),
 (13550,2,'We created not the heavens and the earth and all between them but for just ends, and for a Term Appointed: But those who reject Faith turn away from that whereof they are warned.',NULL,46,3),
 (13551,3,'We created not the heavens and the earth and all that is between them save with truth, and for a term appointed. But those who disbelieve turn away from that whereof they are warned.',NULL,46,3),
 (13552,1,'Say: Have you considered what you call upon besides Allah? Show me what they have created of the earth, or have they a share in the heavens? Bring me a book before this or traces of knowledge, if you are truthful.',NULL,46,4),
 (13553,2,'Say: "Do ye see what it is ye invoke besides Allah? Show me what it is they have created on earth, or have they a share in the heavens bring me a book (revealed) before this, or any remnant of knowledge (ye may have), if ye are telling the truth!',NULL,46,4),
 (13554,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Have ye thought on all that ye invoke beside Allah? Show me what they have created of the earth. Or have they any portion in the heavens? Bring me a scripture before this (Scripture), or some vestige of knowledge (in support of what ye say), if ye are truthful.',NULL,46,4),
 (13555,1,'And who is in greater error than he who calls besides Allah upon those that will not answer him till the day of resurrection and they are heedless of their call?',NULL,46,5),
 (13556,2,'And who is more astray than one who invokes besides Allah, such as will not answer him to the Day of Judgment, and who (in fact) are unconscious of their call (to them)?',NULL,46,5),
 (13557,3,'And who is further astray than those who, instead of Allah, pray unto such as hear not their prayer until the Day of Resurrection, and are unconscious of their prayer,',NULL,46,5),
 (13558,1,'And when men are gathered together they shall be their enemies, and shall be deniers of their worshipping (them).',NULL,46,6),
 (13559,2,'And when mankind are gathered together (at the Resurrection), they will be hostile to them and reject their worship (altogether)!',NULL,46,6),
 (13560,3,'And when mankind are gathered (to the Judgment) will become enemies for them, and will become deniers of having been worshipped.',NULL,46,6),
 (13561,1,'And when Our clear communications are recited to them, those who disbelieve say with regard to the truth when it comes to them: This is clear magic.',NULL,46,7),
 (13562,2,'When Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them, the Unbelievers say, of the Truth when it comes to them: "This is evident sorcery!"',NULL,46,7),
 (13563,3,'And when Our clear revelations are recited unto them, those who disbelieve say of the Truth when it reacheth them: This is mere magic.',NULL,46,7),
 (13564,1,'Nay! they say: He has forged it. Say: If I have forged it, you do not control anything for me from Allah; He knows best what you utter concerning it; He is enough as a witness between me and you, and He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,46,8),
 (13565,2,'Or do they say, "He has forged it"? Say: "Had I forged it, then can ye obtain no single (blessing) for me from Allah. He knows best of that whereof ye talk (so glibly)! Enough is He for a witness between me and you! And he is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful."',NULL,46,8),
 (13566,3,'Or say they: He hath invented it? Say (O Muhammad): If I have invented it, still ye have no power to support me against Allah. He is Best Aware of what ye say among yourselves concerning it. He sufficeth for a witness between me and you. And He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.',NULL,46,8),
 (13567,1,'Say: I am not the first of the messengers, and I do not know what will be done with me or with you: I do not follow anything but that which is revealed to me, and I am nothing but a plain warner.',NULL,46,9),
 (13568,2,'Say: "I am no bringer of new-fangled doctrine among the messengers, nor do I know what will be done with me or with you. I follow but that which is revealed to me by inspiration; I am but a Warner open and clear."',NULL,46,9),
 (13569,3,'Say: I am no new thing among the messengers (of Allah), nor know I what will be done with me or with you. I do but follow that which is inspired in me, and I am but a plain warner.',NULL,46,9),
 (13570,1,'Say: Have you considered if it is from Allah, and you disbelieve in it, and a witness from among the children of Israel has borne witness of one like it, so he believed, while you are big with pride; surely Allah does not guide the unjust people.',NULL,46,10),
 (13571,2,'Say: "See ye? If (this teaching) be from Allah, and ye reject it, and a witness from among the Children of Israel testifies to its similarity (with earlier scripture), and has believed while ye are arrogant, (how unjust ye are!) truly, Allah guides not a people unjust."',NULL,46,10),
 (13572,3,'Bethink you: If it is from Allah and ye disbelieve therein, and a witness of the Children of Israel hath already testified to the like thereof and hath believed, and ye are too proud (what plight is yours)? Lo! Allah guideth not wrong-doing folk.',NULL,46,10),
 (13573,1,'And those who disbelieve say concerning those who believe: If it had been a good, they would not have gone ahead of us therein. And as they do not seek to be rightly directed thereby, they say: It is an old lie.',NULL,46,11),
 (13574,2,'The Unbelievers say of those who believe: "If (this Message) were a good thing, (such men) would not have gone to it first, before us!" And seeing that they guide not themselves thereby, they will say, "this is an (old,) falsehood!"',NULL,46,11),
 (13575,3,'And those who disbelieve say of those who believe: If it had been (any) good, they would not have been before us in attaining it. And since they will not be guided by it, they say: This is an ancient lie;',NULL,46,11),
 (13576,1,'And before it the Book of Musa was a guide and a mercy: and this is a Book verifying (it) in the Arabic language that it may warn those who are unjust and as good news for the doers of good.',NULL,46,12),
 (13577,2,'And before this, was the Book of Moses as a guide and a mercy: And this Book confirms (it) in the Arabic tongue; to admonish the unjust, and as Glad Tidings to those who do right.',NULL,46,12),
 (13578,3,'When before it there was the Scripture of Moses, an example and a mercy; and this is a confirming Scripture in the Arabic language, that it may warn those who do wrong and bring good tidings for the righteous.',NULL,46,12),
 (13579,1,'Surely those who say, Our Lord is Allah, then they continue on the right way, they shall have no fear nor shall they grieve.',NULL,46,13),
 (13580,2,'Verily those who say, "Our Lord is Allah," and remain firm (on that Path),- on them shall be no fear, nor shall they grieve.',NULL,46,13),
 (13581,3,'Lo! those who say: Our Lord is Allah, and thereafter walk aright, there shall no fear come upon them neither shall they grieve.',NULL,46,13),
 (13582,1,'These are the dwellers of the garden, abiding therein: a reward for what they did.',NULL,46,14),
 (13583,2,'Such shall be Companions of the Gardens, dwelling therein (for aye): a recompense for their (good) deeds.',NULL,46,14),
 (13584,3,'Such are rightful owners of the Garden, immortal therein, as a reward for what they used to do.',NULL,46,14),
 (13585,1,'And We have enjoined on man doing of good to his parents; with trouble did his mother bear him and with trouble did she bring him forth; and the bearing of him and the weaning of him was thirty months; until when he attains his maturity and reaches forty years, he says: My Lord! grant me that I may give thanks for Thy favor which Thou hast bestowed on me and on my parents, and that I may do good which pleases Thee and do good to me in respect of my offspring; surely I turn to Thee, and surely I am of those who submit.',NULL,46,15),
 (13586,2,'We have enjoined on man kindness to his parents: In pain did his mother bear him, and in pain did she give him birth. The carrying of the (child) to his weaning is (a period of) thirty months. At length, when he reaches the age of full strength and attains forty years, he says, "O my Lord! Grant me that I may be grateful for Thy favour which Thou has bestowed upon me, and upon both my parents, and that I may work righteousness such as Thou mayest approve; and be gracious to me in my issue. Truly have I turned to Thee and truly do I bow (to Thee) in Islam."',NULL,46,15),
 (13587,3,'And We have commended unto man kindness toward parents. His mother beareth him with reluctance, and bringeth him forth with reluctance, and the bearing of him and the weaning of him is thirty months, till, when he attaineth full strength and reacheth forty years, he saith: My Lord! Arouse me that I may give thanks for the favour wherewith Thou hast favoured me and my parents, and that I may do right acceptable unto Thee. And be gracious unto me in the matter of my seed. Lo! I have turned unto Thee repentant, and lo! I am of those who surrender (unto Thee).',NULL,46,15),
 (13588,1,'These are they from whom We accept the best of what they have done and pass over their evil deeds, among the dwellers of the garden; the promise of truth which they were promised.',NULL,46,16),
 (13589,2,'Such are they from whom We shall accept the best of their deeds and pass by their ill deeds: (They shall be) among the Companions of the Garden: a promise! of truth, which was made to them (in this life).',NULL,46,16),
 (13590,3,'Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they do, and overlook their evil deeds. (They are) among the owners of the Garden. This is the true promise which they were promised (in the world).',NULL,46,16),
 (13591,1,'And he who says to his parents: Fie on you! do you threaten me that I shall be brought forth when generations have already passed away before me? And they both call for Allah''s aid: Woe to you! believe, surely the promise of Allah is true. But he says: This is nothing but stories of the ancients.',NULL,46,17),
 (13592,2,'But (there is one) who says to his parents, "Fie on you! Do ye hold out the promise to me that I shall be raised up, even though generations have passed before me (without rising again)?" And they two seek Allah''s aid, (and rebuke the son): "Woe to thee! Have faith! for the promise of Allah is true." But he says, "This is nothing but tales of the ancients!"',NULL,46,17),
 (13593,3,'And whoso saith unto his parents: Fie upon you both! Do ye threaten me that I shall be brought forth (again) when generations before me have passed away? And they twain cry unto Allah for help (and say): Woe unto thee! Believe! Lo! the promise of Allah is true. But he saith: This is naught save fables of the men of old:',NULL,46,17),
 (13594,1,'These are they against whom the word has proved true among nations of the jinn and the men that have already passed away before them; surely they are losers.',NULL,46,18),
 (13595,2,'Such are they against whom is proved the sentence among the previous generations of Jinns and men, that have passed away; for they will be (utterly) lost.',NULL,46,18),
 (13596,3,'Such are those on whom the Word concerning nations of the jinn and mankind which have passed away before them hath effect. Lo! they are the losers.',NULL,46,18),
 (13597,1,'And for all are degrees according to what they did, and that He may pay them back fully their deeds and they shall not be wronged.',NULL,46,19),
 (13598,2,'And to all are (assigned) degrees according to the deeds which they (have done), and in order that (Allah) may recompense their deeds, and no injustice be done to them.',NULL,46,19),
 (13599,3,'And for all there will be ranks from what they do, that He may pay them for their deeds; and they will not be wronged.',NULL,46,19),
 (13600,1,'And on the day when those who disbelieve shall be brought before the fire: You did away with your good things in your life of the world and you enjoyed them for a while, so today you shall be rewarded with the punishment of abasement because you were unjustly proud in the land and because you transgressed.',NULL,46,20),
 (13601,2,'And on the Day that the Unbelievers will be placed before the Fire, (It will be said to them): "Ye received your good things in the life of the world, and ye took your pleasure out of them: but today shall ye be recompensed with a Penalty of humiliation: for that ye were arrogant on earth without just cause, and that ye (ever) transgressed."',NULL,46,20),
 (13602,3,'And on the day when those who disbelieve are exposed to the Fire (it will be said): Ye squandered your good things in the life of the world and sought comfort therein. Now this day ye are rewarded with the doom of ignominy because ye were disdainful in the land without a right, and because ye used to transgress.',NULL,46,20),
 (13603,1,'And mention the brother of Ad; when he warned his people in the sandy plains,-- and indeed warners came before him and after him-- saying Serve none but Allah; surely I fear for you the punishment of a grievous day.',NULL,46,21),
 (13604,2,'Mention (Hud) one of ''Ad''s (own) brethren: Behold, he warned his people about the winding Sand-tracts: but there have been warners before him and after him: "Worship ye none other than Allah: Truly I fear for you the Penalty of a Mighty Day."',NULL,46,21),
 (13605,3,'And make mention (O Muhammad) of the brother of A''ad when he warned his folk among the wind-curved sandhills - and verily warners came and went before and after him - saying: Serve none but Allah. Lo! I fear for you the doom of a tremendous Day.',NULL,46,21),
 (13606,1,'They said: Have you come to us to turn us away from our gods; then bring us what you threaten us with, if you are of the truthful ones.',NULL,46,22),
 (13607,2,'They said: "Hast thou come in order to turn us aside from our gods? Then bring upon us the (calamity) with which thou dost threaten us, if thou art telling the truth?"',NULL,46,22),
 (13608,3,'They said: Hast come to turn us away from our gods? Then bring upon us that wherewith thou threatenest us, if thou art of the truthful.',NULL,46,22),
 (13609,1,'He said: The knowledge is only with Allah, and I deliver to you the message with which I am sent, but I see you are a people who are ignorant.',NULL,46,23),
 (13610,2,'He said: "The Knowledge (of when it will come) is only with Allah: I proclaim to you the mission on which I have been sent: But I see that ye are a people in ignorance!"..',NULL,46,23),
 (13611,3,'He said: The knowledge is with Allah only. I convey unto you that wherewith I have been sent, but I see you are a folk that know not.',NULL,46,23),
 (13612,1,'So when they saw it as a cloud appearing in the sky advancing towards their valleys, they said: This is a cloud which will give us rain. Nay! it is what you sought to hasten on, a blast of wind in which is a painful punishment,',NULL,46,24),
 (13613,2,'Then, when they saw the (Penalty in the shape of) a cloud traversing the sky, coming to meet their valleys, they said, "This cloud will give us rain!" "Nay, it is the (Calamity) ye were asking to be hastened!- A wind wherein is a Grievous Penalty!',NULL,46,24),
 (13614,3,'Then, when they beheld it as a dense cloud coming toward their valleys, they said: Here is a cloud bringing us rain. Nay, but it is that which ye did seek to hasten, a wind wherein is painful torment,',NULL,46,24),
 (13615,1,'Destroying everything by the command of its Lord, so they became such that naught could be seen except their dwellings. Thus do We reward the guilty people.',NULL,46,25),
 (13616,2,'"Everything will it destroy by the command of its Lord!" Then by the morning they - nothing was to be seen but (the ruins of) their houses! thus do We recompense those given to sin!',NULL,46,25),
 (13617,3,'Destroying all things by commandment of its Lord. And morning found them so that naught could be seen save their dwellings. Thus do We reward the guilty folk.',NULL,46,25),
 (13618,1,'And certainly We had established them in what We have not established you in, and We had given-- them ears and eyes and hearts, but neither their ears, nor their eyes, nor their hearts availed them aught, since they denied the communications of Allah, and that which they mocked encompassed them.',NULL,46,26),
 (13619,2,'And We had firmly established them in a (prosperity and) power which We have not given to you (ye Quraish!) and We had endowed them with (faculties of) hearing, seeing, heart and intellect: but of no profit to them were their (faculties of) hearing, sight, and heart and intellect, when they went on rejecting the Signs of Allah; and they were (completely) encircled by that which they used to mock at!',NULL,46,26),
 (13620,3,'And verily We had empowered them with that wherewith We have not empowered you, and had assigned them ears and eyes and hearts; but their ears and eyes and hearts availed them naught since they denied the revelations of Allah; and what they used to mock befell them.',NULL,46,26),
 (13621,1,'And certainly We destroyed the towns which are around you, and We repeat the communications that they might turn.',NULL,46,27),
 (13622,2,'We destroyed aforetime populations round about you; and We have shown the Signs in various ways, that they may turn (to Us).',NULL,46,27),
 (13623,3,'And verily We have destroyed townships round about you, and displayed (for them) Our revelation, that haply they might return.',NULL,46,27),
 (13624,1,'Why did not then those help them whom they took for gods besides Allah to draw (them) nigh (to Him)? Nay! they were lost to them; and this was their lie and what they forged.',NULL,46,28),
 (13625,2,'Why then was no help forthcoming to them from those whom they worshipped as gods, besides Allah, as a means of access (to Allah)? Nay, they left them in the lurch: but that was their falsehood and their invention.',NULL,46,28),
 (13626,3,'Then why did those whom they had chosen for gods as a way of approach (unto Allah) not help them? Nay, but they did fail them utterly. And (all) that was their lie, and what they used to invent.',NULL,46,28),
 (13627,1,'And when We turned towards you a party of the jinn who listened to the Quran; so when they came to it, they said: Be silent; then when it was finished, they turned back to their people warning (them).',NULL,46,29),
 (13628,2,'Behold, We turned towards thee a company of Jinns (quietly) listening to the Qur''an: when they stood in the presence thereof, they said, "Listen in silence!" When the (reading) was finished, they returned to their people, to warn (them of their sins).',NULL,46,29),
 (13629,3,'And when We inclined toward thee (Muhammad) certain of the jinn, who wished to hear the Qur''an and, when they were in its presence, said: Give ear! and, when it was finished, turned back to their people, warning.',NULL,46,29),
 (13630,1,'They said: O our people! we have listened to a Book revealed after Musa verifying that which is before it, guiding to the truth and to a right path:',NULL,46,30),
 (13631,2,'They said, "O our people! We have heard a Book revealed after Moses, confirming what came before it: it guides (men) to the Truth and to a Straight Path.',NULL,46,30),
 (13632,3,'They said: O our people! Lo! we have heard a scripture which hath been revealed after Moses, confirming that which was before it, guiding unto the truth and a right road.',NULL,46,30),
 (13633,1,'O our people! accept the Divine caller and believe in Him, He will forgive you of your faults and protect you from a painful punishment.',NULL,46,31),
 (13634,2,'"O our people, hearken to the one who invites (you) to Allah, and believe in him: He will forgive you your faults, and deliver you from a Penalty Grievous.',NULL,46,31),
 (13635,3,'O our people! respond to Allah''s summoner and believe in Him. He will forgive you some of your sins and guard you from a painful doom.',NULL,46,31),
 (13636,1,'And whoever does not accept the-Divine caller, he shall not escape in the earth and he shall not have guardians besides Him, these are in manifest error.',NULL,46,32),
 (13637,2,'"If any does not hearken to the one who invites (us) to Allah, he cannot frustrate (Allah''s Plan) on earth, and no protectors can he have besides Allah: such men (wander) in manifest error."',NULL,46,32),
 (13638,3,'And whoso respondeth not to Allah''s summoner he can nowise escape in the earth, and he hath no protecting friends instead of Him. Such are in error manifest.',NULL,46,32),
 (13639,1,'Have they not considered that Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth and was not tired by their creation, is able to give life to the dead? Aye! He has surely power over all things.',NULL,46,33),
 (13640,2,'See they not that Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth, and never wearied with their creation, is able to give life to the dead? Yea, verily He has power over all things.',NULL,46,33),
 (13641,3,'Have they not seen that Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth and was not wearied by their creation, is Able to give life to the dead? Aye, He verily is Able to do all things.',NULL,46,33),
 (13642,1,'And on the day when those who disbelieve shall be brought before the fire: Is it not true? They shall say: Aye! by our Lord! He will say: Then taste the punishment, because you disbelieved.',NULL,46,34),
 (13643,2,'And on the Day that the Unbelievers will be placed before the Fire, (they will be asked,) "Is this not the Truth?" they will say, "Yea, by our Lord!" (One will say:) "Then taste ye the Penalty, for that ye were wont to deny (Truth)!"',NULL,46,34),
 (13644,3,'And on the day when those who disbelieve are exposed to the Fire (they will be asked): Is not this real? They will say: Yea, by our Lord. He will say: Then taste the doom for that ye disbelieved.',NULL,46,34),
 (13645,1,'Therefore bear up patiently as did the messengers endowed with constancy bear up with patience and do not seek to hasten for them (their doom). On the day that they shall see what they are promised they shall be as if they had not tarried save an hour of the day. A sufficient exposition! Shall then any be destroyed save the transgressing people?',NULL,46,35),
 (13646,2,'Therefore patiently persevere, as did (all) messengers of inflexible purpose; and be in no haste about the (Unbelievers). On the Day that they see the (Punishment) promised them, (it will be) as if they had not tarried more than an hour in a single day. (Thine but) to proclaim the Message: but shall any be destroyed except those who transgress?',NULL,46,35),
 (13647,3,'Then have patience (O Muhammad) even as the stout of heart among the messengers (of old) had patience, and seek not to hasten on (the doom) for them. On the day when they see that which they are promised (it will seem to them) as though they had tarried but an hour of daylight. A clear message. Shall any be destroyed save evil-living folk?',NULL,46,35),
 (13648,1,'(As for) those who disbelieve and turn away from Allah''s way, He shall render their works ineffective.',NULL,47,1),
 (13649,2,'Those who reject Allah and hinder (men) from the Path of Allah,- their deeds will Allah render astray (from their mark).',NULL,47,1),
 (13650,3,'Those who disbelieve and turn (men) from the way of Allah, He rendereth their actions vain.',NULL,47,1),
 (13651,1,'And (as for) those who believe and do good, and believe in what has been revealed to Muhammad, and it is the very truth from their Lord, He will remove their evil from them and improve their condition.',NULL,47,2),
 (13652,2,'But those who believe and work deeds of righteousness, and believe in the (Revelation) sent down to Muhammad - for it is the Truth from their Lord,- He will remove from them their ills and improve their condition.',NULL,47,2),
 (13653,3,'And those who believe and do good works and believe in that which is revealed unto Muhammad - and it is the truth from their Lord - He riddeth them of their ill-deeds and improveth their state.',NULL,47,2),
 (13654,1,'That is because those who disbelieve follow falsehood, and those who believe follow the truth from their Lord; thus does Allah set forth to men their examples.',NULL,47,3),
 (13655,2,'This because those who reject Allah follow vanities, while those who believe follow the Truth from their Lord: Thus does Allah set forth for men their lessons by similitudes.',NULL,47,3),
 (13656,3,'That is because those who disbelieve follow falsehood and because those who believe follow the truth from their Lord. Thus Allah coineth their similitudes for mankind.',NULL,47,3),
 (13657,1,'So when you meet in battle those who disbelieve, then smite the necks until when you have overcome them, then make (them) prisoners, and afterwards either set them free as a favor or let them ransom (themselves) until the war terminates. That (shall be so); and if Allah had pleased He would certainly have exacted what is due from them, but that He may try some of you by means of others; and (as for) those who are slain in the way of Allah, He will by no means allow their deeds to perish.',NULL,47,4),
 (13658,2,'Therefore, when ye meet the Unbelievers (in fight), smite at their necks; At length, when ye have thoroughly subdued them, bind a bond firmly (on them): thereafter (is the time for) either generosity or ransom: Until the war lays down its burdens. Thus (are ye commanded): but if it had been Allah''s Will, He could certainly have exacted retribution from them (Himself); but (He lets you fight) in order to test you, some with others. But those who are slain in the Way of Allah,- He will never let their deeds be lost.',NULL,47,4),
 (13659,3,'Now when ye meet in battle those who disbelieve, then it is smiting of the necks until, when ye have routed them, then making fast of bonds; and afterward either grace or ransom till the war lay down its burdens. That (is the ordinance). And if Allah willed He could have punished them (without you) but (thus it is ordained) that He may try some of you by means of others. And those who are slain in the way of Allah, He rendereth not their actions vain.',NULL,47,4),
 (13660,1,'He will guide them and improve their condition.',NULL,47,5),
 (13661,2,'Soon will He guide them and improve their condition,',NULL,47,5),
 (13662,3,'He will guide them and improve their state,',NULL,47,5),
 (13663,1,'And cause them to enter the garden which He has made known to them.',NULL,47,6),
 (13664,2,'And admit them to the Garden which He has announced for them.',NULL,47,6),
 (13665,3,'And bring them in unto the Garden which He hath made known to them.',NULL,47,6),
 (13666,1,'O you who believe ! if you help (the cause of) Allah, He will help you and make firm your feet.',NULL,47,7),
 (13667,2,'O ye who believe! If ye will aid (the cause of) Allah, He will aid you, and plant your feet firmly.',NULL,47,7),
 (13668,3,'O ye who believe! If ye help Allah, He will help you and will make your foothold firm.',NULL,47,7),
 (13669,1,'And (as for) those who disbelieve, for them is destruction and He has made their deeds ineffective.',NULL,47,8),
 (13670,2,'But those who reject (Allah),- for them is destruction, and (Allah) will render their deeds astray (from their mark).',NULL,47,8),
 (13671,3,'And those who disbelieve, perdition is for them, and He will make their actions vain.',NULL,47,8),
 (13672,1,'That is because they hated what Allah revealed, so He rendered their deeds null.',NULL,47,9),
 (13673,2,'That is because they hate the Revelation of Allah; so He has made their deeds fruitless.',NULL,47,9),
 (13674,3,'That is because they are averse to that which Allah hath revealed, therefor maketh He their actions fruitless.',NULL,47,9),
 (13675,1,'Have they not then journeyed in the land and seen how was the end of those before them: Allah brought down destruction upon them, and the unbelievers shall have the like of it.',NULL,47,10),
 (13676,2,'Do they not travel through the earth, and see what was the End of those before them (who did evil)? Allah brought utter destruction on them, and similar (fates await) those who reject Allah.',NULL,47,10),
 (13677,3,'Have they not travelled in the land to see the nature of the consequence for those who were before them? Allah wiped them out. And for the disbelievers there will be the like thereof.',NULL,47,10),
 (13678,1,'That is because Allah is the Protector of those who believe, and because the unbelievers shall have no protector for them.',NULL,47,11),
 (13679,2,'That is because Allah is the Protector of those who believe, but those who reject Allah have no protector.',NULL,47,11),
 (13680,3,'That is because Allah is patron of those who believe, and because the disbelievers have no patron.',NULL,47,11),
 (13681,1,'Surely Allah will make those who believe and do good enter gardens beneath which rivers flow; and those who disbelieve enjoy themselves and eat as the beasts eat, and the fire is their abode.',NULL,47,12),
 (13682,2,'Verily Allah will admit those who believe and do righteous deeds, to Gardens beneath which rivers flow; while those who reject Allah will enjoy (this world) and eat as cattle eat; and the Fire will be their abode.',NULL,47,12),
 (13683,3,'Lo! Allah will cause those who believe and do good works to enter Gardens underneath which rivers flow; while those who disbelieve take their comfort in this life and eat even as the cattle eat, and the Fire is their habitation.',NULL,47,12),
 (13684,1,'And how many a town which was far more powerful than the town of yours which has driven you out: We destroyed them so there was no helper for them.',NULL,47,13),
 (13685,2,'And how many cities, with more power than thy city which has driven thee out, have We destroyed (for their sins)? and there was none to aid them.',NULL,47,13),
 (13686,3,'And how many a township stronger than thy township (O Muhammad) which hath cast thee out, have We destroyed, and they had no helper!',NULL,47,13),
 (13687,1,'What! is he who has a clear argument from his Lord like him to whom the evil of his work is made fairseeming: and they follow their low desires.',NULL,47,14),
 (13688,2,'Is then one who is on a clear (Path) from his Lord, no better than one to whom the evil of his conduct seems pleasing, and such as follow their own lusts?',NULL,47,14),
 (13689,3,'Is he who relieth on a clear proof from his Lord like those for whom the evil that they do is beautified while they follow their own lusts?',NULL,47,14),
 (13690,1,'A parable of the garden which those guarding (against evil) are promised: Therein are rivers of water that does not alter, and rivers of milk the taste whereof does not change, and rivers of drink delicious to those who drink, and rivers of honey clarified and for them therein are all fruits and protection from their Lord. (Are these) like those who abide in the fire and who are made to drink boiling water so it rends their bowels asunder.',NULL,47,15),
 (13691,2,'(Here is) a Parable of the Garden which the righteous are promised: in it are rivers of water incorruptible; rivers of milk of which the taste never changes; rivers of wine, a joy to those who drink; and rivers of honey pure and clear. In it there are for them all kinds of fruits; and Grace from their Lord. (Can those in such Bliss) be compared to such as shall dwell for ever in the Fire, and be given, to drink, boiling water, so that it cuts up their bowels (to pieces)?',NULL,47,15),
 (13692,3,'A similitude of the Garden which those who keep their duty (to Allah) are promised: Therein are rivers of water unpolluted, and rivers of milk whereof the flavour changeth not, and rivers of wine delicious to the drinkers, and rivers of clear-run honey; therein for them is every kind of fruit, with pardon from their Lord. (Are those who enjoy all this) like those who are immortal in the Fire and are given boiling water to drink so that it teareth their bowels?',NULL,47,15),
 (13693,1,'And there are those of them who seek to listen to you, until when they go forth from you, they say to those who have been given the knowledge: What was it that he said just now? These are they upon whose hearts Allah has set a seal and they follow their low desires.',NULL,47,16),
 (13694,2,'And among them are men who listen to thee, but in the end, when they go out from thee, they say to those who have received Knowledge, "What is it he said just then?" Such are men whose hearts Allah has sealed, and who follow their own lusts.',NULL,47,16),
 (13695,3,'Among them are some who give ear unto thee (Muhammad) till, when they go forth from thy presence they say unto those who have been given knowledge: What was that he said just now? Those are they whose hearts Allah hath sealed, and they follow their own lusts.',NULL,47,16),
 (13696,1,'And (as for) those who follow the right direction, He increases them in guidance and gives them their guarding (against evil).',NULL,47,17),
 (13697,2,'But to those who receive Guidance, He increases the (light of) Guidance, and bestows on them their Piety and Restraint (from evil).',NULL,47,17),
 (13698,3,'While as for those who walk aright, He addeth to their guidance, and giveth them their protection (against evil).',NULL,47,17),
 (13699,1,'Do they then wait for aught but the hour that it should come to them all of a sudden? Now indeed the tokens of it have (already) come, but how shall they have their reminder when it comes on them?',NULL,47,18),
 (13700,2,'Do they then only wait for the Hour,- that it should come on them of a sudden? But already have come some tokens thereof, and when it (actually) is on them, how can they benefit then by their admonition?',NULL,47,18),
 (13701,3,'Await they aught save the Hour, that it should come upon them unawares? And the beginnings thereof have already come. But how, when it hath come upon them, can they take their warning?',NULL,47,18),
 (13702,1,'So know that there is no god but Allah, and, ask protection for your fault and for the believing men and the believing women; and Allah knows the place of your returning and the place of your abiding.',NULL,47,19),
 (13703,2,'Know, therefore, that there is no god but Allah, and ask forgiveness for thy fault, and for the men and women who believe: for Allah knows how ye move about and how ye dwell in your homes.',NULL,47,19),
 (13704,3,'So know (O Muhammad) that there is no Allah save Allah, and ask forgiveness for thy sin and for believing men and believing women. Allah knoweth (both) your place of turmoil and your place of rest.',NULL,47,19),
 (13705,1,'And those who believe say: Why has not a chapter been revealed? But when a decisive chapter is revealed, and fighting is mentioned therein you see those in whose hearts is a disease look to you with the look of one fainting because of death. Woe to them then!',NULL,47,20),
 (13706,2,'Those who believe say, "Why is not a sura sent down (for us)?" But when a sura of basic or categorical meaning is revealed, and fighting is mentioned therein, thou wilt see those in whose hearts is a disease looking at thee with a look of one in swoon at the approach of death. But more fitting for them-',NULL,47,20),
 (13707,3,'And those who believe say: If only a surah were revealed! But when a decisive surah is revealed and war is mentioned therein, thou seest those in whose hearts is a disease looking at thee with the look of men fainting unto death. Therefor woe unto them!',NULL,47,20),
 (13708,1,'Obedience and a gentle word (was proper); but when the affair becomes settled, then if they remain true to Allah it would certainly be better for them.',NULL,47,21),
 (13709,2,'Were it to obey and say what is just, and when a matter is resolved on, it were best for them if they were true to Allah.',NULL,47,21),
 (13710,3,'Obedience and a civil word. Then, when the matter is determined, if they are loyal to Allah it will be well for them.',NULL,47,21),
 (13711,1,'But if you held command, you were sure to make mischief in the land and cut off the ties of kinship!',NULL,47,22),
 (13712,2,'Then, is it to be expected of you, if ye were put in authority, that ye will do mischief in the land, and break your ties of kith and kin?',NULL,47,22),
 (13713,3,'Would ye then, if ye were given the command, work corruption in the land and sever your ties of kinship?',NULL,47,22),
 (13714,1,'Those it is whom Allah has cursed so He has made them deaf and blinded their eyes.',NULL,47,23),
 (13715,2,'Such are the men whom Allah has cursed for He has made them deaf and blinded their sight.',NULL,47,23),
 (13716,3,'Such are they whom Allah curseth so that He deafeneth them and maketh blind their eyes.',NULL,47,23),
 (13717,1,'Do they not then reflect on the Quran? Nay, on the hearts there are locks.',NULL,47,24),
 (13718,2,'Do they not then earnestly seek to understand the Qur''an, or are their hearts locked up by them?',NULL,47,24),
 (13719,3,'Will they then not meditate on the Qur''an, or are there locks on the hearts?',NULL,47,24),
 (13720,1,'Surely (as for) those who return on their backs after that guidance has become manifest to them, the Shaitan has made it a light matter to them; and He gives them respite.',NULL,47,25),
 (13721,2,'Those who turn back as apostates after Guidance was clearly shown to them,- the Evil One has instigated them and busied them up with false hopes.',NULL,47,25),
 (13722,3,'Lo! those who turn back after the guidance hath been manifested unto them, Satan hath seduced them, and He giveth them the rein.',NULL,47,25),
 (13723,1,'That is because they say to those who hate what Allah has revealed: We will obey you in some of the affairs; and Allah knows their secrets.',NULL,47,26),
 (13724,2,'This, because they said to those who hate what Allah has revealed, "We will obey you in part of (this) matter"; but Allah knows their (inner) secrets.',NULL,47,26),
 (13725,3,'That is because they say unto those who hate what Allah hath revealed: We will obey you in some matters; and Allah knoweth their secret talk.',NULL,47,26),
 (13726,1,'But how will it be when the angels cause them to die smiting their backs.',NULL,47,27),
 (13727,2,'But how (will it be) when the angels take their souls at death, and smite their faces and their backs?',NULL,47,27),
 (13728,3,'Then how (will it be with them) when the angels gather them, smiting their faces and their backs!',NULL,47,27),
 (13729,1,'That is because they follow what is displeasing to Allah and are averse to His pleasure, therefore He has made null their deeds.',NULL,47,28),
 (13730,2,'This because they followed that which called forth the Wrath of Allah, and they hated Allah''s good pleasure; so He made their deeds of no effect.',NULL,47,28),
 (13731,3,'That will be because they followed that which angereth Allah, and hated that which pleaseth Him. Therefor He hath made their actions vain.',NULL,47,28),
 (13732,1,'Or do those in whose hearts is a disease think that Allah will not bring forth their spite?',NULL,47,29),
 (13733,2,'Or do those in whose hearts is a disease, think that Allah will not bring to light all their rancour?',NULL,47,29),
 (13734,3,'Or do those in whose hearts is a disease deem that Allah will not bring to light their (secret) hates?',NULL,47,29),
 (13735,1,'And if We please We would have made you know them so that you would certainly have recognized them by their marks and most certainly you can recognize them by the intent of (their) speech; and Allah knows your deeds.',NULL,47,30),
 (13736,2,'Had We so wiled, We could have shown them up to thee, and thou shouldst have known them by their marks: but surely thou wilt know them by the tone of their speech! And Allah knows all that ye do.',NULL,47,30),
 (13737,3,'And if We would, We could show them unto thee (Muhammad) so that thou shouldst know them surely by their marks. And thou shalt know them by the burden of their talk. And Allah knoweth your deeds.',NULL,47,30),
 (13738,1,'And most certainly We will try you until We have known those among you who exert themselves hard, and the patient, and made your case manifest.',NULL,47,31),
 (13739,2,'And We shall try you until We test those among you who strive their utmost and persevere in patience; and We shall try your reported (mettle).',NULL,47,31),
 (13740,3,'And verily We shall try you till We know those of you who strive hard (for the cause of Allah) and the steadfast, and till We test your record.',NULL,47,31),
 (13741,1,'Surely those who disbelieve and turn away from Allah''s way and oppose the Messenger after that guidance has become clear to them cannot harm Allah in any way, and He will make null their deeds.',NULL,47,32),
 (13742,2,'Those who reject Allah, hinder (men) from the Path of Allah, and resist the Messenger, after Guidance has been clearly shown to them, will not injure Allah in the least, but He will make their deeds of no effect.',NULL,47,32),
 (13743,3,'Lo! those who disbelieve and turn from the way of Allah and oppose the messenger after the guidance hath been manifested unto them, they hurt Allah not a jot, and He will make their actions fruitless.',NULL,47,32),
 (13744,1,'O you who believe! obey Allah and obey the Messenger, and do not make your deeds of no effect.',NULL,47,33),
 (13745,2,'O ye who believe! Obey Allah, and obey the messenger, and make not vain your deeds!',NULL,47,33),
 (13746,3,'O ye who believe! Obey Allah and obey the messenger, and render not your actions vain.',NULL,47,33),
 (13747,1,'Surely those who disbelieve and turn away from Allah''s way, then they die while they are unbelievers, Allah will by no means forgive them.',NULL,47,34),
 (13748,2,'Those who reject Allah, and hinder (men) from the Path of Allah, then die rejecting Allah,- Allah will not forgive them.',NULL,47,34),
 (13749,3,'Lo! those who disbelieve and turn from the way of Allah and then die disbelievers, Allah surely will not pardon them.',NULL,47,34),
 (13750,1,'And be not slack so as to cry for peace and you have the upper hand, and Allah is with you, and He will not bring your deeds to naught.',NULL,47,35),
 (13751,2,'Be not weary and faint-hearted, crying for peace, when ye should be uppermost: for Allah is with you, and will never put you in loss for your (good) deeds.',NULL,47,35),
 (13752,3,'So do not falter and cry out for peace when ye (will be) the uppermost, and Allah is with you, and He will not grudge (the reward of) your actions.',NULL,47,35),
 (13753,1,'The life of this world is only idle sport and play, and if you believe and guard (against evil) He will give you your rewards, and will not ask of you your possessions.',NULL,47,36),
 (13754,2,'The life of this world is but play and amusement: and if ye believe and guard against Evil, He will grant you your recompense, and will not ask you (to give up) your possessions.',NULL,47,36),
 (13755,3,'The life of the world is but a sport and a pastime. And if ye believe and ward off (evil). He will give you your wages, and will not ask of you your wordly wealth.',NULL,47,36),
 (13756,1,'If He should ask you for it and urge you, you will be niggardly, and He will bring forth your malice.',NULL,47,37),
 (13757,2,'If He were to ask you for all of them, and press you, ye would covetously withhold, and He would bring out all your ill-feeling.',NULL,47,37),
 (13758,3,'If He should ask it of you and importune you, ye would hoard it, and He would bring to light your (secret) hates.',NULL,47,37),
 (13759,1,'Behold! you are those who are called upon to spend in Allah''s way, but among you are those who are niggardly, and whoever is niggardly is niggardly against his own soul; and Allah is Self-sufficient and you have need (of Him), and if you turn back He will bring in your place another people, then they will not be like you.',NULL,47,38),
 (13760,2,'Behold, ye are those invited to spend (of your substance) in the Way of Allah: But among you are some that are niggardly. But any who are niggardly are so at the expense of their own souls. But Allah is free of all wants, and it is ye that are needy. If ye turn back (from the Path), He will substitute in your stead another people; then they would not be like you!',NULL,47,38),
 (13761,3,'Lo! ye are those who are called to spend in the way of Allah, yet among you there are some who hoard. And as for him who hoardeth, he hoardeth only from his soul. And Allah is the Rich, and ye are the poor. And if ye turn away He will exchange you for some other folk, and they will not be the likes of you.',NULL,47,38),
 (13762,1,'Surely We have given to you a clear victory',NULL,48,1),
 (13763,2,'Verily We have granted thee a manifest Victory:',NULL,48,1),
 (13764,3,'Lo! We have given thee (O Muhammad) a signal victory,',NULL,48,1),
 (13765,1,'That Allah may forgive your community their past faults and those to follow and complete His favor to you and keep you on a right way,',NULL,48,2),
 (13766,2,'That Allah may forgive thee thy faults of the past and those to follow; fulfil His favour to thee; and guide thee on the Straight Way;',NULL,48,2),
 (13767,3,'That Allah may forgive thee of thy sin that which is past and that which is to come, and may perfect His favour unto thee, and may guide thee on a right path,',NULL,48,2),
 (13768,1,'And that Allah might help you with a mighty help.',NULL,48,3),
 (13769,2,'And that Allah may help thee with powerful help.',NULL,48,3),
 (13770,3,'And that Allah may help thee with strong help -',NULL,48,3),
 (13771,1,'He it is Who sent down tranquillity into the hearts of the believers that they might have more of faith added to their faith-- and Allah''s are the hosts of the heavens and the earth, and Allah is Knowing, Wise--',NULL,48,4),
 (13772,2,'It is He Who sent down tranquillity into the hearts of the Believers, that they may add faith to their faith;- for to Allah belong the Forces of the heavens and the earth; and Allah is Full of Knowledge and Wisdom;-',NULL,48,4),
 (13773,3,'He it is Who sent down peace of reassurance into the hearts of the believers that they might add faith unto their faith. Allah''s are the hosts of the heavens and the earth, and Allah is ever Knower, Wise -',NULL,48,4),
 (13774,1,'That He may cause the believing men and the believing women to enter gardens beneath which rivers flow to abide therein and remove from them their evil; and that is a grand achievement with Allah',NULL,48,5),
 (13775,2,'That He may admit the men and women who believe, to Gardens beneath which rivers flow, to dwell therein for aye, and remove their ills from them;- and that is, in the sight of Allah, the highest achievement (for man),-',NULL,48,5),
 (13776,3,'That He may bring the believing men and the believing women into Gardens underneath which rivers flow, wherein they will abide, and may remit from them their evil deeds - That, in the sight of Allah, is the supreme triumph -',NULL,48,5),
 (13777,1,'And (that) He may punish the hypocritical men and the hypocritical women, and the polytheistic men and the polytheistic women, the entertainers of evil thoughts about Allah. On them is the evil turn, and Allah is wroth with them and has cursed them and prepared hell for them, and evil is the resort.',NULL,48,6),
 (13778,2,'And that He may punish the Hypocrites, men and women, and the Polytheists men and women, who imagine an evil opinion of Allah. On them is a round of Evil: the Wrath of Allah is on them: He has cursed them and got Hell ready for them: and evil is it for a destination.',NULL,48,6),
 (13779,3,'And may punish the hypocritical men and the hypocritical women, and the idolatrous men and the idolatrous women, who think an evil thought concerning Allah. For them is the evil turn of fortune, and Allah is wroth against them and hath cursed them, and hath made ready for them hell, a hapless journey''s end.',NULL,48,6),
 (13780,1,'And Allah''s are the hosts of the heavens and the earth; and Allah is Mighty, Wise.',NULL,48,7),
 (13781,2,'For to Allah belong the Forces of the heavens and the earth; and Allah is Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,48,7),
 (13782,3,'Allah''s are the hosts of the heavens and the earth, and Allah is ever Mighty, Wise.',NULL,48,7),
 (13783,1,'Surely We have sent you as a witness and as a bearer of good news and as a warner,',NULL,48,8),
 (13784,2,'We have truly sent thee as a witness, as a bringer of Glad Tidings, and as a Warner:',NULL,48,8),
 (13785,3,'Lo! We have sent thee (O Muhammad) as a witness and a bearer of good tidings and a warner,',NULL,48,8),
 (13786,1,'That you may believe in Allah and His Messenger and may aid him and revere him; and (that) you may declare His glory, morning and evening.',NULL,48,9),
 (13787,2,'In order that ye (O men) may believe in Allah and His Messenger, that ye may assist and honour Him, and celebrate His praise morning and evening.',NULL,48,9),
 (13788,3,'That ye (mankind) may believe in Allah and His messenger, and may honour Him, and may revere Him, and may glorify Him at early dawn and at the close of day.',NULL,48,9),
 (13789,1,'Surely those who swear allegiance to you do but swear allegiance to Allah; the hand of Allah is above their hands. Therefore whoever breaks (his faith), he breaks it only to the injury of his own soul, and whoever fulfills what he has covenanted with Allah, He will grant him a mighty reward.',NULL,48,10),
 (13790,2,'Verily those who plight their fealty to thee do no less than plight their fealty to Allah: the Hand of Allah is over their hands: then any one who violates his oath, does so to the harm of his own soul, and any one who fulfils what he has covenanted with Allah,- Allah will soon grant him a great Reward.',NULL,48,10),
 (13791,3,'Lo! those who swear allegiance unto thee (Muhammad), swear allegiance only unto Allah. The Hand of Allah is above their hands. So whosoever breaketh his oath, breaketh it only to his soul''s hurt; while whosoever keepeth his covenant with Allah, on him will He bestow immense reward.',NULL,48,10),
 (13792,1,'Those of the dwellers of the desert who were left behind will say to you: Our property and our families kept us busy, so ask forgiveness for us. They say with their tongues what is not in their hearts. Say: Then who can control anything for you from Allah if He intends to do you harm or if He intends to do you good; nay, Allah is Aware of what you do:',NULL,48,11),
 (13793,2,'The desert Arabs who lagged behind will say to thee: "We were engaged in (looking after) our flocks and herds, and our families: do thou then ask forgiveness for us." They say with their tongues what is not in their hearts. Say: "Who then has any power at all (to intervene) on your behalf with Allah, if His Will is to give you some loss or to give you some profit? But Allah is well acquainted with all that ye do.',NULL,48,11),
 (13794,3,'Those of the wandering Arabs who were left behind will tell thee: Our possessions and our households occupied us, so ask forgiveness for us! They speak with their tongues that which is not in their hearts. Say: Who can avail you aught against Allah, if He intend you hurt or intend you profit? Nay, but Allah is ever Aware of what ye do.',NULL,48,11),
 (13795,1,'Nay! you rather thought that the Messenger and the believers would not return to their families ever, and that was made fairseeming to your hearts and you thought an evil thought and you were a people doomed to perish.',NULL,48,12),
 (13796,2,'"Nay, ye thought that the Messenger and the Believers would never return to their families; this seemed pleasing in your hearts, and ye conceived an evil thought, for ye are a people lost (in wickedness)."',NULL,48,12),
 (13797,3,'Nay, but ye deemed that the messenger and the believers would never return to their own folk, and that was made fairseeming in your hearts, and ye did think an evil thought, and ye were worthless folk.',NULL,48,12),
 (13798,1,'And whoever does not believe in Allah and His Messenger, then surely We have prepared burning fire for the unbelievers.',NULL,48,13),
 (13799,2,'And if any believe not in Allah and His Messenger, We have prepared, for those who reject Allah, a Blazing Fire!',NULL,48,13),
 (13800,3,'And so for him who believeth not in Allah and His messenger - Lo! We have prepared a flame for disbelievers.',NULL,48,13),
 (13801,1,'And Allah''s is the kingdom. of the heavens and the earth; He forgives whom He pleases and punishes whom He pleases, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,48,14),
 (13802,2,'To Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth: He forgives whom He wills, and He punishes whom He wills: but Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,48,14),
 (13803,3,'And Allah''s is the Sovereignty of the heavens and the earth. He forgiveth whom He will, and punisheth whom He will. And Allah is ever Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,48,14),
 (13804,1,'Those who are left behind will say when you set forth for the gaining of acquisitions: Allow us (that) we may follow you. They desire to change the word of Allah. Say: By no means shall you follow us; thus did Allah say before. But they will say: Nay! you are jealous of us. Nay! they do not understand but a little.',NULL,48,15),
 (13805,2,'Those who lagged behind (will say), when ye (are free to) march and take booty (in war): "Permit us to follow you." They wish to change Allah''s decree: Say: "Not thus will ye follow us: Allah has already declared (this) beforehand": then they will say, "But ye are jealous of us." Nay, but little do they understand (such things).',NULL,48,15),
 (13806,3,'Those who were left behind will say, when ye set forth to capture booty: Let us go with you. They fain would change the verdict of Allah. Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Ye shall not go with us. Thus hath Allah said beforehand. Then they will say: Ye are envious of us. Nay, but they understand not, save a little.',NULL,48,15),
 (13807,1,'Say to those of the dwellers of the desert who were left behind: You shall soon be invited (to fight) against a people possessing mighty prowess; you will fight against them until they submit; then if you obey, Allah will grant you a good reward; and if you turn back as you turned back before, He will punish you with a painful punishment.',NULL,48,16),
 (13808,2,'Say to the desert Arabs who lagged behind: "Ye shall be summoned (to fight) against a people given to vehement war: then shall ye fight, or they shall submit. Then if ye show obedience, Allah will grant you a goodly reward, but if ye turn back as ye did before, He will punish you with a grievous Penalty."',NULL,48,16),
 (13809,3,'Say unto those of the wandering Arabs who were left behind: Ye will be called against a folk of mighty prowess, to fight them until they surrender; and if ye obey, Allah will give you a fair reward; but if ye turn away as ye did turn away before, He will punish you with a painful doom.',NULL,48,16),
 (13810,1,'There is no harm in the blind, nor is there any harm in the lame, nor is there any harm in the sick (if they do not go forth); and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger, He will cause him to enter gardens beneath which rivers flow, and whoever turns back, He will punish him with a painful punishment.',NULL,48,17),
 (13811,2,'No blame is there on the blind, nor is there blame on the lame, nor on one ill (if he joins not the war): But he that obeys Allah and his Messenger,- (Allah) will admit him to Gardens beneath which rivers flow; and he who turns back, (Allah) will punish him with a grievous Penalty.',NULL,48,17),
 (13812,3,'There is no blame for the blind, nor is there blame for the lame, nor is there blame for the sick (that they go not forth to war). And whoso obeyeth Allah and His messenger, He will make him enter Gardens underneath which rivers flow; and whoso turneth back, him will He punish with a painful doom.',NULL,48,17),
 (13813,1,'Certainly Allah was well pleased with the believers when they swore allegiance to you under the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts, so He sent down tranquillity on them and rewarded them with a near victory,',NULL,48,18),
 (13814,2,'Allah''s Good Pleasure was on the Believers when they swore Fealty to thee under the Tree: He knew what was in their hearts, and He sent down Tranquillity to them; and He rewarded them with a speedy Victory;',NULL,48,18),
 (13815,3,'Allah was well pleased with the believers when they swore allegiance unto thee beneath the tree, and He knew what was in their hearts, and He sent down peace of reassurance on them, and hath rewarded them with a near victory;',NULL,48,18),
 (13816,1,'And many acquisitions which they will take; and Allah is Mighty, Wise.',NULL,48,19),
 (13817,2,'And many gains will they acquire (besides): and Allah is Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom.',NULL,48,19),
 (13818,3,'And much booty that they will capture. Allah is ever Mighty, Wise.',NULL,48,19),
 (13819,1,'Allah promised you many acquisitions which you will take, then He hastened on this one for you and held back the hands of men from you, and that it may be a sign for the believers and that He may guide you on a right path.',NULL,48,20),
 (13820,2,'Allah has promised you many gains that ye shall acquire, and He has given you these beforehand; and He has restrained the hands of men from you; that it may be a Sign for the Believers, and that He may guide you to a Straight Path;',NULL,48,20),
 (13821,3,'Allah promiseth you much booty that ye will capture, and hath given you this in advance, and hath withheld men''s hands from you, that it may be a token for the believers, and that He may guide you on a right path.',NULL,48,20),
 (13822,1,'And others which you have not yet been able to achieve Allah has surely encompassed them, and Allah has power over all things.',NULL,48,21),
 (13823,2,'And other gains (there are), which are not within your power, but which Allah has compassed: and Allah has power over all things.',NULL,48,21),
 (13824,3,'And other (gain), which ye have not been able to achieve, Allah will compass it, Allah is Able to do all things.',NULL,48,21),
 (13825,1,'And if those who disbelieve fight with you, they would certainly turn (their) backs, then they would not find any protector or a helper.',NULL,48,22),
 (13826,2,'If the Unbelievers should fight you, they would certainly turn their backs; then would they find neither protector nor helper.',NULL,48,22),
 (13827,3,'And if those who disbelieve join battle with you they will take to flight, and afterward they will find no protecting friend nor helper.',NULL,48,22),
 (13828,1,'Such has been the course of Allah that has indeed run before, and you shall not find a change in Allah''s course.',NULL,48,23),
 (13829,2,'(Such has been) the practice (approved) of Allah already in the past: no change wilt thou find in the practice (approved) of Allah.',NULL,48,23),
 (13830,3,'It is the law of Allah which hath taken course aforetime. Thou wilt not find for the law of Allah aught of power to change.',NULL,48,23),
 (13831,1,'And He it is Who held back their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Mecca after He had given you victory over them; and Allah is Seeing what you do.',NULL,48,24),
 (13832,2,'And it is He Who has restrained their hands from you and your hands from them in the midst of Makka, after that He gave you the victory over them. And Allah sees well all that ye do.',NULL,48,24),
 (13833,3,'And He it is Who hath withheld men''s hands from you, and hath withheld your hands from them, in the valley of Mecca, after He had made you victors over them. Allah is Seer of what ye do.',NULL,48,24),
 (13834,1,'It is they who disbelieved and turned you away from the Sacred Mosque and (turned off) the offering withheld from arriving at its destined place; and were it not for the believing men and the believing women, whom, not having known, you might have trodden down, and thus something hateful might have afflicted you on their account without knowledge-- so that Allah may cause to enter into His mercy whomsoever He pleases; had they been widely separated one from another, We would surely have punished those who disbelieved from among them with a painful punishment.',NULL,48,25),
 (13835,2,'They are the ones who denied Revelation and hindered you from the Sacred Mosque and the sacrificial animals, detained from reaching their place of sacrifice. Had there not been believing men and believing women whom ye did not know that ye were trampling down and on whose account a crime would have accrued to you without (your) knowledge, (Allah would have allowed you to force your way, but He held back your hands) that He may admit to His Mercy whom He will. If they had been apart, We should certainly have punished the Unbelievers among them with a grievous Punishment.',NULL,48,25),
 (13836,3,'These it was who disbelieved and debarred you from the Inviolable Place of Worship, and debarred the offering from reaching its goal. And if it had not been for believing men and believing women, whom ye know not - lest ye should tread them under foot and thus incur guilt for them unknowingly; that Allah might bring into His mercy whom He will - If (the believers and the disbelievers) had been clearly separated We verily had punished those of them who disbelieved with painful punishment.',NULL,48,25),
 (13837,1,'When those who disbelieved harbored in their hearts (feelings of) disdain, the disdain of (the days of) ignorance, but Allah sent down His tranquillity on His Messenger and on the believers, and made them keep the word of guarding (against evil), and they were entitled to it and worthy of it; and Allah is Cognizant of all things.',NULL,48,26),
 (13838,2,'While the Unbelievers got up in their hearts heat and cant - the heat and cant of ignorance,- Allah sent down His Tranquillity to his Messenger and to the Believers, and made them stick close to the command of self-restraint; and well were they entitled to it and worthy of it. And Allah has full knowledge of all things.',NULL,48,26),
 (13839,3,'When those who disbelieve had set up in their hearts zealotry, the zealotry of the Age of Ignorance, then Allah sent down His peace of reassurance upon His messenger and upon the believers and imposed on them the word of self-restraint, for they were worthy of it and meet for it. And Allah is Aware of all things.',NULL,48,26),
 (13840,1,'Certainly Allah had shown to His Messenger the vision with truth: you shall most certainly enter the Sacred Mosque, if Allah pleases, in security, (some) having their heads shaved and (others) having their hair cut, you shall not fear, but He knows what you do not know, so He brought about a near victory before that.',NULL,48,27),
 (13841,2,'Truly did Allah fulfil the vision for His Messenger: ye shall enter the Sacred Mosque, if Allah wills, with minds secure, heads shaved, hair cut short, and without fear. For He knew what ye knew not, and He granted, besides this, a speedy victory.',NULL,48,27),
 (13842,3,'Allah hath fulfilled the vision for His messenger in very truth. Ye shall indeed enter the Inviolable Place of Worship, if Allah will, secure, (having your hair) shaven and cut, not fearing. But He knoweth that which ye know not, and hath given you a near victory beforehand.',NULL,48,27),
 (13843,1,'He it is Who sent His Messenger with the guidance and the true religion that He may make it prevail over all the religions; and Allah is enough for a witness.',NULL,48,28),
 (13844,2,'It is He Who has sent His Messenger with Guidance and the Religion of Truth, to proclaim it over all religion: and enough is Allah for a Witness.',NULL,48,28),
 (13845,3,'He it is Who hath sent His messenger with the guidance and the religion of truth, that He may cause it to prevail over all religion. And Allah sufficeth as a Witness.',NULL,48,28),
 (13846,1,'Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and those with him are firm of heart against the unbelievers, compassionate among themselves; you will see them bowing down, prostrating themselves, seeking grace from Allah and pleasure; their marks are in their faces because of the effect of prostration; that is their description in the Taurat and their description in the Injeel; like as seed-produce that puts forth its sprout, then strengthens it, so it becomes stout and stands firmly on its stem, delighting the sowers that He may enrage the unbelievers on account of them; Allah has promised those among them who believe and do good, forgiveness and a great reward.',NULL,48,29),
 (13847,2,'Muhammad is the messenger of Allah; and those who are with him are strong against Unbelievers, (but) compassionate amongst each other. Thou wilt see them bow and prostrate themselves (in prayer), seeking Grace from Allah and (His) Good Pleasure. On their faces are their marks, (being) the traces of their prostration. This is their similitude in the Taurat; and their similitude in the Gospel is: like a seed which sends forth its blade, then makes it strong; it then becomes thick, and it stands on its own stem, (filling) the sowers with wonder and delight. As a result, it fills the Unbelievers with rage at them. Allah has promised those among them who believe and do righteous deeds forgiveness, and a great Reward.',NULL,48,29),
 (13848,3,'Muhammad is the messenger of Allah. And those with him are hard against the disbelievers and merciful among themselves. Thou (O Muhammad) seest them bowing and falling prostrate (in worship), seeking bounty from Allah and (His) acceptance. The mark of them is on their foreheads from the traces of prostration. Such is their likeness in the Torah and their likeness in the Gospel - like as sown corn that sendeth forth its shoot and strengtheneth it and riseth firm upon its stalk, delighting the sowers - that He may enrage the disbelievers with (the sight of) them. Allah hath promised, unto such of them as believe and do good works, forgiveness and immense reward.',NULL,48,29),
 (13849,1,'O you who believe! be not forward in the presence of Allah and His Messenger, and be careful of (your duty to) Allah; surely Allah is Hearing, Knowing.',NULL,49,1),
 (13850,2,'O Ye who believe! Put not yourselves forward before Allah and His Messenger; but fear Allah: for Allah is He Who hears and knows all things.',NULL,49,1),
 (13851,3,'O ye who believe! Be not forward in the presence of Allah and His messenger, and keep your duty to Allah. Lo! Allah is Hearer, Knower.',NULL,49,1),
 (13852,1,'O you who believe! do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, and do not speak loud to him as you speak loud to one another, lest your deeds became null while you do not perceive.',NULL,49,2),
 (13853,2,'O ye who believe! Raise not your voices above the voice of the Prophet, nor speak aloud to him in talk, as ye may speak aloud to one another, lest your deeds become vain and ye perceive not.',NULL,49,2),
 (13854,3,'O ye who believe! Lift not up your voices above the voice of the Prophet, nor shout when speaking to him as ye shout one to another, lest your works be rendered vain while ye perceive not.',NULL,49,2),
 (13855,1,'Surely those who lower their voices before Allah''s Messenger are they whose hearts Allah has proved for guarding (against evil); they shall have forgiveness and a great reward.',NULL,49,3),
 (13856,2,'Those that lower their voices in the presence of Allah''s Messenger,- their hearts has Allah tested for piety: for them is Forgiveness and a great Reward.',NULL,49,3),
 (13857,3,'Lo! they who subdue their voices in the presence of the messenger of Allah, those are they whose hearts Allah hath proven unto righteousness. Theirs will be forgiveness and immense reward.',NULL,49,3),
 (13858,1,'(As for) those who call out to you from behind the private chambers, surely most of them do not understand.',NULL,49,4),
 (13859,2,'Those who shout out to thee from without the inner apartments - most of them lack understanding.',NULL,49,4),
 (13860,3,'Lo! those who call thee from behind the private apartments, most of them have no sense.',NULL,49,4),
 (13861,1,'And if they wait patiently until you come out to them, it would certainly be better for them, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,49,5),
 (13862,2,'If only they had patience until thou couldst come out to them, it would be best for them: but Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,49,5),
 (13863,3,'And if they had had patience till thou camest forth unto them, it had been better for them. And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,49,5),
 (13864,1,'O you who believe! if an evil-doer comes to you with a report, look carefully into it, lest you harm a people in ignorance, then be sorry for what you have done.',NULL,49,6),
 (13865,2,'O ye who believe! If a wicked person comes to you with any news, ascertain the truth, lest ye harm people unwittingly, and afterwards become full of repentance for what ye have done.',NULL,49,6),
 (13866,3,'O ye who believe! If an evil-liver bring you tidings, verify it, lest ye smite some folk in ignorance and afterward repent of what ye did.',NULL,49,6),
 (13867,1,'And know that among you is Allah''s Messenger; should he obey you in many a matter, you would surely fall into distress, but Allah has endeared the faith to you and has made it seemly in your hearts, and He has made hateful to you unbelief and transgression and disobedience; these it is that are the followers of a right way.',NULL,49,7),
 (13868,2,'And know that among you is Allah''s Messenger: were he, in many matters, to follow your (wishes), ye would certainly fall into misfortune: But Allah has endeared the Faith to you, and has made it beautiful in your hearts, and He has made hateful to you Unbelief, wickedness, and rebellion: such indeed are those who walk in righteousness;-',NULL,49,7),
 (13869,3,'And know that the messenger of Allah is among you. If he were to obey you in much of the government, ye would surely be in trouble; but Allah hath endeared the faith to you and hath beautified it in your hearts, and hath made disbelief and lewdness and rebellion hateful unto you. Such are they who are the rightly guided.',NULL,49,7),
 (13870,1,'By grace from Allah and as a favor; and Allah is Knowing, Wise.',NULL,49,8),
 (13871,2,'A Grace and Favour from Allah; and Allah is full of Knowledge and Wisdom.',NULL,49,8),
 (13872,3,'(It is) a bounty and a grace from Allah; and Allah is Knower, Wise.',NULL,49,8),
 (13873,1,'And if two parties of the believers quarrel, make peace between them; but if one of them acts wrongfully towards the other, fight that which acts wrongfully until it returns to Allah''s command; then if it returns, make peace between them with justice and act equitably; surely Allah loves those who act equitably.',NULL,49,9),
 (13874,2,'If two parties among the Believers fall into a quarrel, make ye peace between them: but if one of them transgresses beyond bounds against the other, then fight ye (all) against the one that transgresses until it complies with the command of Allah; but if it complies, then make peace between them with justice, and be fair: for Allah loves those who are fair (and just).',NULL,49,9),
 (13875,3,'And if two parties of believers fall to fighting, then make peace between them. And if one party of them doeth wrong to the other, fight ye that which doeth wrong till it return unto the ordinance of Allah; then, if it return, make peace between them justly, and act equitably. Lo! Allah loveth the equitable.',NULL,49,9),
 (13876,1,'The believers are but brethren, therefore make peace between your brethren and be careful of (your duty to) Allah that mercy may be had on you.',NULL,49,10),
 (13877,2,'The Believers are but a single Brotherhood: So make peace and reconciliation between your two (contending) brothers; and fear Allah, that ye may receive Mercy.',NULL,49,10),
 (13878,3,'The believers are naught else than brothers. Therefore make peace between your brethren and observe your duty to Allah that haply ye may obtain mercy.',NULL,49,10),
 (13879,1,'O you who believe! let not (one) people laugh at (another) people perchance they may be better than they, nor let women (laugh) at (other) women, perchance they may be better than they; and do not find fault with your own people nor call one another by nicknames; evil is a bad name after faith, and whoever does not turn, these it is that are the unjust.',NULL,49,11),
 (13880,2,'O ye who believe! Let not some men among you laugh at others: It may be that the (latter) are better than the (former): Nor let some women laugh at others: It may be that the (latter are better than the (former): Nor defame nor be sarcastic to each other, nor call each other by (offensive) nicknames: Ill-seeming is a name connoting wickedness, (to be used of one) after he has believed: And those who do not desist are (indeed) doing wrong.',NULL,49,11),
 (13881,3,'O ye who believe! Let not a folk deride a folk who may be better than they (are), not let women (deride) women who may be better than they are; neither defame one another, nor insult one another by nicknames. Bad is the name of lewdness after faith. And whoso turneth not in repentance, such are evil-doers.',NULL,49,11),
 (13882,1,'O you who believe! avoid most of suspicion, for surely suspicion in some cases is a sin, and do not spy nor let some of you backbite others. Does one of you like to eat the flesh of his dead brother? But you abhor it; and be careful of (your duty to) Allah, surely Allah is Oft-returning (to mercy), Merciful.',NULL,49,12),
 (13883,2,'O ye who believe! Avoid suspicion as much (as possible): for suspicion in some cases is a sin: And spy not on each other behind their backs. Would any of you like to eat the flesh of his dead brother? Nay, ye would abhor it...But fear Allah: For Allah is Oft-Returning, Most Merciful.',NULL,49,12),
 (13884,3,'O ye who believe! Shun much suspicion; for lo! some suspicion is a crime. And spy not, neither backbite one another. Would one of you love to eat the flesh of his dead brother? Ye abhor that (so abhor the other)! And keep your duty (to Allah). Lo! Allah is Relenting, Merciful.',NULL,49,12),
 (13885,1,'O you men! surely We have created you of a male and a female, and made you tribes and families that you may know each other; surely the most honorable of you with Allah is the one among you most careful (of his duty); surely Allah is Knowing, Aware.',NULL,49,13),
 (13886,2,'O mankind! We created you from a single (pair) of a male and a female, and made you into nations and tribes, that ye may know each other (not that ye may despise (each other). Verily the most honoured of you in the sight of Allah is (he who is) the most righteous of you. And Allah has full knowledge and is well acquainted (with all things).',NULL,49,13),
 (13887,3,'O mankind! Lo! We have created you male and female, and have made you nations and tribes that ye may know one another. Lo! the noblest of you, in the sight of Allah, is the best in conduct. Lo! Allah is Knower, Aware.',NULL,49,13),
 (13888,1,'The dwellers of the desert say: We believe. Say: You do not believe but say, We submit; and faith has not yet entered into your hearts; and if you obey Allah and His Messenger, He will not diminish aught of your deeds; surely Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,49,14),
 (13889,2,'The desert Arabs say, "We believe." Say, "Ye have no faith; but ye (only)say, ''We have submitted our wills to Allah,'' For not yet has Faith entered your hearts. But if ye obey Allah and His Messenger, He will not belittle aught of your deeds: for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful."',NULL,49,14),
 (13890,3,'The wandering Arabs say: We believe. Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Ye believe not, but rather say "We submit," for the faith hath not yet entered into your hearts. Yet, if ye obey Allah and His messenger, He will not withhold from you aught of (the reward of) your deeds. Lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,49,14),
 (13891,1,'The believers are only those who believe in Allah and His Messenger then they doubt not and struggle hard with their wealth and their lives in the way of Allah; they are the truthful ones.',NULL,49,15),
 (13892,2,'Only those are Believers who have believed in Allah and His Messenger, and have never since doubted, but have striven with their belongings and their persons in the Cause of Allah: Such are the sincere ones.',NULL,49,15),
 (13893,3,'The (true) believers are those only who believe in Allah and His messenger and afterward doubt not, but strive with their wealth and their lives for the cause of Allah. Such are the sincere.',NULL,49,15),
 (13894,1,'Say: Do you apprise Allah of your religion, and Allah knows what is in the heavens and what is in the earth; and Allah is Cognizant of all things.',NULL,49,16),
 (13895,2,'Say: "What! Will ye instruct Allah about your religion? But Allah knows all that is in the heavens and on earth: He has full knowledge of all things.',NULL,49,16),
 (13896,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Would ye teach Allah your religion, when Allah knoweth all that is in the heavens and all that is in the earth, and Allah is Aware of all things?',NULL,49,16),
 (13897,1,'They think that they lay you under an obligation by becoming Muslims. Say: Lay me not under obligation by your Islam: rather Allah lays you under an obligation by guiding you to the faith if you are truthful.',NULL,49,17),
 (13898,2,'They impress on thee as a favour that they have embraced Islam. Say, "Count not your Islam as a favour upon me: Nay, Allah has conferred a favour upon you that He has guided you to the faith, if ye be true and sincere.',NULL,49,17),
 (13899,3,'They make it a favour unto thee (Muhammad) that they have surrendered (unto Him). Say: Deem not your Surrender a favour unto me; but Allah doth confer a favour on you, inasmuch as He hath led you to the Faith, if ye are earnest.',NULL,49,17),
 (13900,1,'Surely Allah knows the unseen things of the heavens and the earth; and Allah sees what you do.',NULL,49,18),
 (13901,2,'"Verily Allah knows the secrets of the heavens and the earth: and Allah Sees well all that ye do."',NULL,49,18),
 (13902,3,'Lo! Allah knoweth the Unseen of the heavens and the earth. And Allah is Seer of what ye do.',NULL,49,18),
 (13903,1,'Qaf. I swear by the glorious Quran (that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah)',NULL,50,1),
 (13904,2,'Qaf: By the Glorious Qur''an (Thou art Allah''s Messenger).',NULL,50,1),
 (13905,3,'Qaf. By the Glorious Qur''an,',NULL,50,1),
 (13906,1,'Nay! they wonder that there has come to them a warner from among themselves, so the unbelievers say: This is a wonderful thing:',NULL,50,2),
 (13907,2,'But they wonder that there has come to them a Warner from among themselves. So the Unbelievers say: "This is a wonderful thing!',NULL,50,2),
 (13908,3,'Nay, but they marvel that a warner of their own hath come unto them; and the disbelievers say: This is a strange thing:',NULL,50,2),
 (13909,1,'What! when we are dead and have become dust? That is afar (from probable) return.',NULL,50,3),
 (13910,2,'"What! When we die and become dust, (shall we live again?) That is a (sort of) return far (from our understanding)."',NULL,50,3),
 (13911,3,'When we are dead and have become dust (shall we be brought back again)? That would be a far return!',NULL,50,3),
 (13912,1,'We know indeed what the earth diminishes of them, and with Us is a writing that preserves.',NULL,50,4),
 (13913,2,'We already know how much of them the earth takes away: With Us is a record guarding (the full account).',NULL,50,4),
 (13914,3,'We know that which the earth taketh of them, and with Us is a recording Book.',NULL,50,4),
 (13915,1,'Nay, they rejected the truth when it came to them, so they are (now) in a state of confusion.',NULL,50,5),
 (13916,2,'But they deny the Truth when it comes to them: so they are in a confused state.',NULL,50,5),
 (13917,3,'Nay, but they have denied the truth when it came unto them, therefor they are now in troubled case.',NULL,50,5),
 (13918,1,'Do they not then look up to heaven above them how We have made it and adorned it and it has no gaps?',NULL,50,6),
 (13919,2,'Do they not look at the sky above them?- How We have made it and adorned it, and there are no flaws in it?',NULL,50,6),
 (13920,3,'Have they not then observed the sky above them, how We have constructed it and beautified it, and how there are no rifts therein?',NULL,50,6),
 (13921,1,'And the earth, We have made it plain and cast in it mountains and We have made to grow therein of all beautiful kinds,',NULL,50,7),
 (13922,2,'And the earth- We have spread it out, and set thereon mountains standing firm, and produced therein every kind of beautiful growth (in pairs)-',NULL,50,7),
 (13923,3,'And the earth have We spread out, and have flung firm hills therein, and have caused of every lovely kind to grow thereon,',NULL,50,7),
 (13924,1,'To give sight and as a reminder to every servant who turns frequently (to Allah).',NULL,50,8),
 (13925,2,'To be observed and commemorated by every devotee turning (to Allah).',NULL,50,8),
 (13926,3,'A vision and a reminder for every penitent slave.',NULL,50,8),
 (13927,1,'And We send down from the cloud water abounding in good, then We cause to grow thereby gardens and the grain that is reaped,',NULL,50,9),
 (13928,2,'And We send down from the sky rain charted with blessing, and We produce therewith gardens and Grain for harvests;',NULL,50,9),
 (13929,3,'And We send down from the sky blessed water whereby We give growth unto gardens and the grain of crops,',NULL,50,9),
 (13930,1,'And the tall palm-trees having spadices closely set one above another,',NULL,50,10),
 (13931,2,'And tall (and stately) palm-trees, with shoots of fruit-stalks, piled one over another;-',NULL,50,10),
 (13932,3,'And lofty date-palms with ranged clusters,',NULL,50,10),
 (13933,1,'A sustenance for the servants, and We give life thereby to a dead land; thus is the rising.',NULL,50,11),
 (13934,2,'As sustenance for (Allah''s) Servants;- and We give (new) life therewith to land that is dead: Thus will be the Resurrection.',NULL,50,11),
 (13935,3,'Provision (made) for men; and therewith We quicken a dead land. Even so will be the resurrection of the dead.',NULL,50,11),
 (13936,1,'(Others) before them rejected (prophets): the people of Nuh and the dwellers of Ar-Rass and Samood,',NULL,50,12),
 (13937,2,'Before them was denied (the Hereafter) by the People of Noah, the Companions of the Rass, the Thamud,',NULL,50,12),
 (13938,3,'The folk of Noah denied (the truth) before them, and (so did) the dwellers at Ar-Rass and (the tribe of) Thamud,',NULL,50,12),
 (13939,1,'And Ad and Firon and Lut''s brethren,',NULL,50,13),
 (13940,2,'The ''Ad, Pharaoh, the brethren of Lut,',NULL,50,13),
 (13941,3,'And (the tribe of) A''ad, and Pharaoh, and the brethren of Lot,',NULL,50,13),
 (13942,1,'And the dwellers of the grove and the people of Tuba; all rejected the messengers, so My threat came to pass.',NULL,50,14),
 (13943,2,'The Companions of the Wood, and the People of Tubba''; each one (of them) rejected the messengers, and My warning was duly fulfilled (in them).',NULL,50,14),
 (13944,3,'And the dwellers in the wood, and the folk of Tubb''a: every one denied their messengers, therefor My threat took effect.',NULL,50,14),
 (13945,1,'Were We then fatigued with the first creation? Yet are they in doubt with regard to a new creation.',NULL,50,15),
 (13946,2,'Were We then weary with the first Creation, that they should be in confused doubt about a new Creation?',NULL,50,15),
 (13947,3,'Were We then worn out by the first creation? Yet they are in doubt about a new creation.',NULL,50,15),
 (13948,1,'And certainly We created man, and We know what his mind suggests to him, and We are nearer to him than his life-vein.',NULL,50,16),
 (13949,2,'It was We Who created man, and We know what dark suggestions his soul makes to him: for We are nearer to him than (his) jugular vein.',NULL,50,16),
 (13950,3,'We verily created man and We know what his soul whispereth to him, and We are nearer to him than his jugular vein.',NULL,50,16),
 (13951,1,'When the two receivers receive, sitting on the right and on the left.',NULL,50,17),
 (13952,2,'Behold, two (guardian angels) appointed to learn (his doings) learn (and noted them), one sitting on the right and one on the left.',NULL,50,17),
 (13953,3,'When the two Receivers receive (him), seated on the right hand and on the left,',NULL,50,17),
 (13954,1,'He utters not a word but there is by him a watcher at hand.',NULL,50,18),
 (13955,2,'Not a word does he utter but there is a sentinel by him, ready (to note it).',NULL,50,18),
 (13956,3,'He uttereth no word but there is with him an observer ready.',NULL,50,18),
 (13957,1,'And the stupor of death will come in truth; that is what you were trying to escape.',NULL,50,19),
 (13958,2,'And the stupor of death will bring Truth (before his eyes): "This was the thing which thou wast trying to escape!"',NULL,50,19),
 (13959,3,'And the agony of death cometh in truth. (And it is said unto him): This is that which thou wast wont to shun.',NULL,50,19),
 (13960,1,'And the trumpet shall be blown; that is the day of the threatening.',NULL,50,20),
 (13961,2,'And the Trumpet shall be blown: that will be the Day whereof Warning (had been given).',NULL,50,20),
 (13962,3,'And the trumpet is blown. This is the threatened Day.',NULL,50,20),
 (13963,1,'And every soul shall come, with it a driver and a witness.',NULL,50,21),
 (13964,2,'And there will come forth every soul: with each will be an (angel) to drive, and an (angel) to bear witness.',NULL,50,21),
 (13965,3,'And every soul cometh, along with it a driver and a witness.',NULL,50,21),
 (13966,1,'Certainly you were heedless of it, but now We have removed from you your veil, so your sight today is sharp.',NULL,50,22),
 (13967,2,'(It will be said:) "Thou wast heedless of this; now have We removed thy veil, and sharp is thy sight this Day!"',NULL,50,22),
 (13968,3,'(And unto the evil-doer it is said): Thou wast in heedlessness of this. Now We have removed from thee thy covering, and piercing is thy sight this day.',NULL,50,22),
 (13969,1,'And his companions shall say: This is what is ready with me.',NULL,50,23),
 (13970,2,'And his Companion will say: "Here is (his Record) ready with me!"',NULL,50,23),
 (13971,3,'And (unto the evil-doer) his comrade saith: This is that which I have ready (as testimony).',NULL,50,23),
 (13972,1,'Do cast into hell every ungrateful, rebellious one,',NULL,50,24),
 (13973,2,'(The sentence will be:) "Throw, throw into Hell every contumacious Rejecter (of Allah)!-',NULL,50,24),
 (13974,3,'(And it is said): Do ye twain hurl to hell each rebel ingrate,',NULL,50,24),
 (13975,1,'Forbidder of good, exceeder of limits, doubter,',NULL,50,25),
 (13976,2,'"Who forbade what was good, transgressed all bounds, cast doubts and suspicions;',NULL,50,25),
 (13977,3,'Hinderer of good, transgressor, doubter,',NULL,50,25),
 (13978,1,'Who sets up another god with Allah, so do cast him into severe chastisement.',NULL,50,26),
 (13979,2,'"Who set up another god beside Allah: Throw him into a severe penalty."',NULL,50,26),
 (13980,3,'Who setteth up another god along with Allah. Do ye twain hurl him to the dreadful doom.',NULL,50,26),
 (13981,1,'His companion will say: Our Lord! I did not lead him into inordinacy but he himself was in a great error.',NULL,50,27),
 (13982,2,'His Companion will say: "Our Lord! I did not make him transgress, but he was (himself) far astray."',NULL,50,27),
 (13983,3,'His comrade saith: Our Lord! I did not cause him to rebel, but he was (himself) far gone in error.',NULL,50,27),
 (13984,1,'He will say: Do not quarrel in My presence, and indeed I gave you the threatening beforehand:',NULL,50,28),
 (13985,2,'He will say: "Dispute not with each other in My Presence: I had already in advance sent you Warning.',NULL,50,28),
 (13986,3,'He saith: Contend not in My presence, when I had already proffered unto you the warning.',NULL,50,28),
 (13987,1,'My word shall not be changed, nor am I in the least unjust to the servants.',NULL,50,29),
 (13988,2,'"The Word changes not before Me, and I do not the least injustice to My Servants."',NULL,50,29),
 (13989,3,'The sentence that cometh from Me cannot be changed, and I am in no wise a tyrant unto the slaves.',NULL,50,29),
 (13990,1,'On the day that We will say to hell: Are you filled up? And it will say: Are there any more?',NULL,50,30),
 (13991,2,'One Day We will ask Hell, "Art thou filled to the full?" It will say, "Are there any more (to come)?"',NULL,50,30),
 (13992,3,'On the day when We say unto hell: Art thou filled? and it saith: Can there be more to come?',NULL,50,30),
 (13993,1,'And the garden shall be brought near to those who guard (against evil), not far off:',NULL,50,31),
 (13994,2,'And the Garden will be brought nigh to the Righteous,- no more a thing distant.',NULL,50,31),
 (13995,3,'And the Garden is brought nigh for those who kept from evil, no longer distant.',NULL,50,31),
 (13996,1,'This is what you were promised, (it is) for every one who turns frequently (to Allah), keeps (His limits);',NULL,50,32),
 (13997,2,'(A voice will say:) "This is what was promised for you,- for every one who turned (to Allah) in sincere repentance, who kept (His Law),',NULL,50,32),
 (13998,3,'(And it is said): This is that which ye were promised. (It is) for every penitent and heedful one,',NULL,50,32),
 (13999,1,'Who fears the Beneficent Allah in secret and comes with a penitent heart:',NULL,50,33),
 (14000,2,'"Who feared (Allah) Most Gracious Unseen, and brought a heart turned in devotion (to Him):',NULL,50,33),
 (14001,3,'Who feareth the Beneficent in secret and cometh with a contrite heart.',NULL,50,33),
 (14002,1,'Enter it in peace, that is the day of abiding.',NULL,50,34),
 (14003,2,'"Enter ye therein in Peace and Security; this is a Day of Eternal Life!"',NULL,50,34),
 (14004,3,'Enter it in peace. This is the day of immortality.',NULL,50,34),
 (14005,1,'They have therein what they wish and with Us is more yet.',NULL,50,35),
 (14006,2,'There will be for them therein all that they wish,- and more besides in Our Presence.',NULL,50,35),
 (14007,3,'There they have all that they desire, and there is more with Us.',NULL,50,35),
 (14008,1,'And how many a generation did We destroy before them who were mightier in prowess than they, so they went about and about in the lands. Is there a place of refuge?',NULL,50,36),
 (14009,2,'But how many generations before them did We destroy (for their sins),- stronger in power than they? Then did they wander through the land: was there any place of escape (for them)?',NULL,50,36),
 (14010,3,'And how many a generation We destroyed before them, who were mightier than these in prowess so that they overran the lands! Had they any place of refuge (when the judgment came)?',NULL,50,36),
 (14011,1,'Most surely there is a reminder in this for him who has a heart or he gives ear and is a witness.',NULL,50,37),
 (14012,2,'Verily in this is a Message for any that has a heart and understanding or who gives ear and earnestly witnesses (the truth).',NULL,50,37),
 (14013,3,'Lo! therein verily is a reminder for him who hath a heart, or giveth ear with full intelligence.',NULL,50,37),
 (14014,1,'And certainly We created the heavens and the earth and what is between them in six periods and there touched Us not any fatigue.',NULL,50,38),
 (14015,2,'We created the heavens and the earth and all between them in Six Days, nor did any sense of weariness touch Us.',NULL,50,38),
 (14016,3,'And verily We created the heavens and the earth, and all that is between them, in six Days, and naught of weariness touched Us.',NULL,50,38),
 (14017,1,'Therefore be patient of what they say, and sing the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting.',NULL,50,39),
 (14018,2,'Bear, then, with patience, all that they say, and celebrate the praises of thy Lord, before the rising of the sun and before (its) setting.',NULL,50,39),
 (14019,3,'Therefor (O Muhammad) bear with what they say, and hymn the praise of thy Lord before the rising and before the setting of the sun;',NULL,50,39),
 (14020,1,'And glorify Him in the night and after the prayers.',NULL,50,40),
 (14021,2,'And during part of the night, (also,) celebrate His praises, and (so likewise) after the postures of adoration.',NULL,50,40),
 (14022,3,'And in the night-time hymn His praise, and after the (prescribed) prostrations.',NULL,50,40),
 (14023,1,'And listen on the day when the crier shall cry from a near place',NULL,50,41),
 (14024,2,'And listen for the Day when the Caller will call out from a place quiet near,-',NULL,50,41),
 (14025,3,'And listen on the day when the crier crieth from a near place,',NULL,50,41),
 (14026,1,'The day when they shall hear the cry in truth; that is the day of coming forth.',NULL,50,42),
 (14027,2,'The Day when they will hear a (mighty) Blast in (very) truth: that will be the Day of Resurrection.',NULL,50,42),
 (14028,3,'The day when they will hear the (Awful) Cry in truth. That is the day of coming forth (from the graves).',NULL,50,42),
 (14029,1,'Surely We give life and cause to die, and to Us is the eventual coming;',NULL,50,43),
 (14030,2,'Verily it is We Who give Life and Death; and to Us is the Final Goal-',NULL,50,43),
 (14031,3,'Lo! We it is Who quicken and give death, and unto Us is the journeying.',NULL,50,43),
 (14032,1,'The day on which the earth shall cleave asunder under them, they will make haste; that is a gathering together easy to Us.',NULL,50,44),
 (14033,2,'The Day when the Earth will be rent asunder, from (men) hurrying out: that will be a gathering together,- quite easy for Us.',NULL,50,44),
 (14034,3,'On the day when the earth splitteth asunder from them, hastening forth (they come). That is a gathering easy for Us (to make).',NULL,50,44),
 (14035,1,'We know best what they say, and you are not one to compel them; therefore remind him by means of the Quran who fears My threat.',NULL,50,45),
 (14036,2,'We know best what they say; and thou art not one to overawe them by force. So admonish with the Qur''an such as fear My Warning!',NULL,50,45),
 (14037,3,'We are Best Aware of what they say, and thou (O Muhammad) art in no wise a compeller over them. But warn by the Qur''an him who feareth My threat.',NULL,50,45),
 (14038,1,'I swear by the wind that scatters far and wide,',NULL,51,1),
 (14039,2,'By the (Winds) that scatter broadcast;',NULL,51,1),
 (14040,3,'By those that winnow with a winnowing',NULL,51,1),
 (14041,1,'Then those clouds bearing the load (of minute things in space).',NULL,51,2),
 (14042,2,'And those that lift and bear away heavy weights;',NULL,51,2),
 (14043,3,'And those that bear the burden (of the rain)',NULL,51,2),
 (14044,1,'Then those (ships) that glide easily,',NULL,51,3),
 (14045,2,'And those that flow with ease and gentleness;',NULL,51,3),
 (14046,3,'And those that glide with ease (upon the sea)',NULL,51,3),
 (14047,1,'Then those (angels who) distribute blessings by Our command;',NULL,51,4),
 (14048,2,'And those that distribute and apportion by Command;-',NULL,51,4),
 (14049,3,'And those who distribute (blessings) by command,',NULL,51,4),
 (14050,1,'What you are threatened with is most surely true,',NULL,51,5),
 (14051,2,'Verily that which ye are promised is true;',NULL,51,5),
 (14052,3,'Lo! that wherewith ye are threatened is indeed true,',NULL,51,5),
 (14053,1,'And the judgment must most surely come about.',NULL,51,6),
 (14054,2,'And verily Judgment and Justice must indeed come to pass.',NULL,51,6),
 (14055,3,'And lo! the judgment will indeed befall.',NULL,51,6),
 (14056,1,'I swear by the heaven full of ways.',NULL,51,7),
 (14057,2,'By the Sky with (its) numerous Paths,',NULL,51,7),
 (14058,3,'By the heaven full of paths,',NULL,51,7),
 (14059,1,'Most surely you are at variance with each other in what you say,',NULL,51,8),
 (14060,2,'Truly ye are in a doctrine discordant,',NULL,51,8),
 (14061,3,'Lo! ye, forsooth, are of various opinion (concerning the truth).',NULL,51,8),
 (14062,1,'He is turned away from it who would be turned away.',NULL,51,9),
 (14063,2,'Through which are deluded (away from the Truth) such as would be deluded.',NULL,51,9),
 (14064,3,'He is made to turn away from it who is (himself) averse.',NULL,51,9),
 (14065,1,'Cursed be the liars,',NULL,51,10),
 (14066,2,'Woe to the falsehood-mongers,-',NULL,51,10),
 (14067,3,'Accursed be the conjecturers',NULL,51,10),
 (14068,1,'Who are in a gulf (of ignorance) neglectful;',NULL,51,11),
 (14069,2,'Those who (flounder) heedless in a flood of confusion:',NULL,51,11),
 (14070,3,'Who are careless in an abyss!',NULL,51,11),
 (14071,1,'They ask: When is the day of judgment?',NULL,51,12),
 (14072,2,'They ask, "When will be the Day of Judgment and Justice?"',NULL,51,12),
 (14073,3,'They ask: When is the Day of Judgment?',NULL,51,12),
 (14074,1,'(It is) the day on which they shall be tried at the fire.',NULL,51,13),
 (14075,2,'(It will be) a Day when they will be tried (and tested) over the Fire!',NULL,51,13),
 (14076,3,'(It is) the day when they will be tormented at the Fire,',NULL,51,13),
 (14077,1,'Taste your persecution! this is what you would hasten on.',NULL,51,14),
 (14078,2,'"Taste ye your trial! This is what ye used to ask to be hastened!"',NULL,51,14),
 (14079,3,'(And it will be said unto them): Taste your torment (which ye inflicted). This is what ye sought to hasten.',NULL,51,14),
 (14080,1,'Surely those who guard (against evil) shall be in gardens and fountains.',NULL,51,15),
 (14081,2,'As to the Righteous, they will be in the midst of Gardens and Springs,',NULL,51,15),
 (14082,3,'Lo! those who keep from evil will dwell amid gardens and watersprings,',NULL,51,15),
 (14083,1,'Taking what their Lord gives them; surely they were before that, the doers of good.',NULL,51,16),
 (14084,2,'Taking joy in the things which their Lord gives them, because, before then, they lived a good life.',NULL,51,16),
 (14085,3,'Taking that which their Lord giveth them; for lo! aforetime they were doers of good;',NULL,51,16),
 (14086,1,'They used to sleep but little in the night.',NULL,51,17),
 (14087,2,'They were in the habit of sleeping but little by night,',NULL,51,17),
 (14088,3,'They used to sleep but little of the night,',NULL,51,17),
 (14089,1,'And in the morning they asked forgiveness.',NULL,51,18),
 (14090,2,'And in the hour of early dawn, they (were found) praying for Forgiveness;',NULL,51,18),
 (14091,3,'And ere the dawning of each day would seek forgiveness,',NULL,51,18),
 (14092,1,'And in their property was a portion due to him who begs and to him who is denied (good).',NULL,51,19),
 (14093,2,'And in their wealth and possessions (was remembered) the right of the (needy,) him who asked, and him who (for some reason) was prevented (from asking).',NULL,51,19),
 (14094,3,'And in their wealth the beggar and the outcast had due share.',NULL,51,19),
 (14095,1,'And in the earth there are signs for those who are sure,',NULL,51,20),
 (14096,2,'On the earth are signs for those of assured Faith,',NULL,51,20),
 (14097,3,'And in the earth are portents for those whose faith is sure.',NULL,51,20),
 (14098,1,'And in your own souls (too); will you not then see?',NULL,51,21),
 (14099,2,'As also in your own selves: Will ye not then see?',NULL,51,21),
 (14100,3,'And (also) in yourselves. Can ye then not see?',NULL,51,21),
 (14101,1,'And in the heaven is your sustenance and what you are threatened with.',NULL,51,22),
 (14102,2,'And in heaven is your Sustenance, as (also) that which ye are promised.',NULL,51,22),
 (14103,3,'And in the heaven is your providence and that which ye are promised;',NULL,51,22),
 (14104,1,'And by the Lord of the heavens and the earth! it is most surely the truth, just as you do speak.',NULL,51,23),
 (14105,2,'Then, by the Lord of heaven and earth, this is the very Truth, as much as the fact that ye can speak intelligently to each other.',NULL,51,23),
 (14106,3,'And by the Lord of the heavens and the earth, it is the truth, even as (it is true) that ye speak.',NULL,51,23),
 (14107,1,'Has there come to you information about the honored guests of Ibrahim?',NULL,51,24),
 (14108,2,'Has the story reached thee, of the honoured guests of Abraham?',NULL,51,24),
 (14109,3,'Hath the story of Abraham''s honoured guests reached thee (O Muhammad)?',NULL,51,24),
 (14110,1,'When they entered upon him, they said: Peace. Peace, said he, a strange people.',NULL,51,25),
 (14111,2,'Behold, they entered his presence, and said: "Peace!" He said, "Peace!" (and thought, "These seem) unusual people."',NULL,51,25),
 (14112,3,'When they came in unto him and said: Peace! he answered, Peace! (and thought): Folk unknown (to me).',NULL,51,25),
 (14113,1,'Then he turned aside to his family secretly and brought a fat (roasted) calf,',NULL,51,26),
 (14114,2,'Then he turned quickly to his household, brought out a fatted calf,',NULL,51,26),
 (14115,3,'Then he went apart unto his housefolk so that they brought a fatted calf;',NULL,51,26),
 (14116,1,'So he brought it near them. He said: What! will you not eat?',NULL,51,27),
 (14117,2,'And placed it before them.. he said, "Will ye not eat?"',NULL,51,27),
 (14118,3,'And he set it before them, saying: Will ye not eat?',NULL,51,27),
 (14119,1,'So he conceived in his mind a fear on account of them. They said: Fear not. And they gave him the good news of a boy possessing knowledge.',NULL,51,28),
 (14120,2,'(When they did not eat), He conceived a fear of them. They said, "Fear not," and they gave him glad tidings of a son endowed with knowledge.',NULL,51,28),
 (14121,3,'Then he conceived a fear of them. They said: Fear not! and gave him tidings of (the birth of) a wise son.',NULL,51,28),
 (14122,1,'Then his wife came up in great grief, and she struck her face and said: An old barren woman!',NULL,51,29),
 (14123,2,'But his wife came forward (laughing) aloud: she smote her forehead and said: "A barren old woman!"',NULL,51,29),
 (14124,3,'Then his wife came forward, making moan, and smote her face, and cried: A barren old woman!',NULL,51,29),
 (14125,1,'They said: Thus says your Lord: Surely He is the Wise, the Knowing.',NULL,51,30),
 (14126,2,'They said, "Even so has thy Lord spoken: and He is full of Wisdom and Knowledge."',NULL,51,30),
 (14127,3,'They said: Even so saith thy Lord. Lo! He is the Wise, the Knower.',NULL,51,30),
 (14128,1,'He said: What is your affair then, O messengers!',NULL,51,31),
 (14129,2,'(Abraham) said: "And what, O ye Messengers, is your errand (now)?"',NULL,51,31),
 (14130,3,'(Abraham) said: And (afterward) what is your errand, O ye sent (from Allah)?',NULL,51,31),
 (14131,1,'They said: Surely we are sent to a guilty people,',NULL,51,32),
 (14132,2,'They said, "We have been sent to a people (deep) in sin;-',NULL,51,32),
 (14133,3,'They said: Lo! we are sent unto a guilty folk,',NULL,51,32),
 (14134,1,'That we may send down upon them stone of clay,',NULL,51,33),
 (14135,2,'"To bring on, on them, (a shower of) stones of clay (brimstone),',NULL,51,33),
 (14136,3,'That we may send upon them stones of clay,',NULL,51,33),
 (14137,1,'Sent forth from your Lord for the extravagant.',NULL,51,34),
 (14138,2,'"Marked as from thy Lord for those who trespass beyond bounds."',NULL,51,34),
 (14139,3,'Marked by thy Lord for (the destruction of) the wanton.',NULL,51,34),
 (14140,1,'Then We brought forth such as were therein of the believers.',NULL,51,35),
 (14141,2,'Then We evacuated those of the Believers who were there,',NULL,51,35),
 (14142,3,'Then we brought forth such believers as were there.',NULL,51,35),
 (14143,1,'But We did not find therein save a (single) house of those who submitted (the Muslims).',NULL,51,36),
 (14144,2,'But We found not there any just (Muslim) persons except in one house:',NULL,51,36),
 (14145,3,'But We found there but one house of those surrendered (to Allah).',NULL,51,36),
 (14146,1,'And We left therein a sign for those who fear the painful punishment.',NULL,51,37),
 (14147,2,'And We left there a Sign for such as fear the Grievous Penalty.',NULL,51,37),
 (14148,3,'And We left behind therein a portent for those who fear a painful doom.',NULL,51,37),
 (14149,1,'And in Musa: When We sent him to Firon with clear authority.',NULL,51,38),
 (14150,2,'And in Moses (was another Sign): Behold, We sent him to Pharaoh, with authority manifest.',NULL,51,38),
 (14151,3,'And in Moses (too, there is a portent) when We sent him unto Pharaoh with clear warrant,',NULL,51,38),
 (14152,1,'But he turned away with his forces and said: A magician or a mad man.',NULL,51,39),
 (14153,2,'But (Pharaoh) turned back with his Chiefs, and said, "A sorcerer, or one possessed!"',NULL,51,39),
 (14154,3,'But he withdrew (confiding) in his might, and said: A wizard or a madman.',NULL,51,39),
 (14155,1,'So We seized him and his hosts and hurled them into the sea and he was blamable.',NULL,51,40),
 (14156,2,'So We took him and his forces, and threw them into the sea; and his was the blame.',NULL,51,40),
 (14157,3,'So We seized him and his hosts and flung them in the sea, for he was reprobate.',NULL,51,40),
 (14158,1,'And in Ad: When We sent upon them the destructive wind.',NULL,51,41),
 (14159,2,'And in the ''Ad (people) (was another Sign): Behold, We sent against them the devastating Wind:',NULL,51,41),
 (14160,3,'And in (the tribe of) A''ad (there is a portent) when we sent the fatal wind against them.',NULL,51,41),
 (14161,1,'It did not leave aught on which it blew, but it made it like ashes.',NULL,51,42),
 (14162,2,'It left nothing whatever that it came up against, but reduced it to ruin and rottenness.',NULL,51,42),
 (14163,3,'It spared naught that it reached, but made it (all) as dust.',NULL,51,42),
 (14164,1,'And in Samood: When it was said to them: Enjoy yourselves for a while.',NULL,51,43),
 (14165,2,'And in the Thamud (was another Sign): Behold, they were told, "Enjoy (your brief day) for a little while!"',NULL,51,43),
 (14166,3,'And in (the tribe of) Thamud (there is a portent) when it was told them: Take your ease awhile.',NULL,51,43),
 (14167,1,'But they revolted against the commandment of their Lord, so the rumbling overtook them while they saw.',NULL,51,44),
 (14168,2,'But they insolently defied the Command of their Lord: So the stunning noise (of an earthquake) seized them, even while they were looking on.',NULL,51,44),
 (14169,3,'But they rebelled against their Lord''s decree, and so the thunderbolt overtook them even while they gazed;',NULL,51,44),
 (14170,1,'So they were not able to rise up, nor could they defend themselves-',NULL,51,45),
 (14171,2,'Then they could not even stand (on their feet), nor could they help themselves.',NULL,51,45),
 (14172,3,'And they were unable to rise up, nor could they help themselves.',NULL,51,45),
 (14173,1,'And the people of Nuh before, surely they were a transgressing people.',NULL,51,46),
 (14174,2,'So were the People of Noah before them for they wickedly transgressed.',NULL,51,46),
 (14175,3,'And the folk of Noah aforetime. Lo! they were licentious folk.',NULL,51,46),
 (14176,1,'And the heaven, We raised it high with power, and most surely We are the makers of things ample.',NULL,51,47),
 (14177,2,'With power and skill did We construct the Firmament: for it is We Who create the vastness of pace.',NULL,51,47),
 (14178,3,'We have built the heaven with might, and We it is Who make the vast extent (thereof).',NULL,51,47),
 (14179,1,'And the earth, We have made it a wide extent; how well have We then spread (it) out.',NULL,51,48),
 (14180,2,'And We have spread out the (spacious) earth: How excellently We do spread out!',NULL,51,48),
 (14181,3,'And the earth have We laid out, how gracious is the Spreader (thereof)!',NULL,51,48),
 (14182,1,'And of everything We have created pairs that you may be mindful.',NULL,51,49),
 (14183,2,'And of every thing We have created pairs: That ye may receive instruction.',NULL,51,49),
 (14184,3,'And all things We have created by pairs, that haply ye may reflect.',NULL,51,49),
 (14185,1,'Therefore fly to Allah, surely I am a plain warner to you from Him.',NULL,51,50),
 (14186,2,'Hasten ye then (at once) to Allah: I am from Him a Warner to you, clear and open!',NULL,51,50),
 (14187,3,'Therefor flee unto Allah; lo! I am a plain warner unto you from him.',NULL,51,50),
 (14188,1,'And do not set up with Allah another god: surely I am a plain warner to you from Him.',NULL,51,51),
 (14189,2,'And make not another an object of worship with Allah: I am from Him a Warner to you, clear and open!',NULL,51,51),
 (14190,3,'And set not any other god along with Allah; lo! I am a plain warner unto you from Him.',NULL,51,51),
 (14191,1,'Thus there did not come to those before them a messenger but they said: A magician or a mad man.',NULL,51,52),
 (14192,2,'Similarly, no messenger came to the Peoples before them, but they said (of him) in like manner, "A sorcerer, or one possessed"!',NULL,51,52),
 (14193,3,'Even so there came no messenger unto those before them but they said: A wizard or a madman!',NULL,51,52),
 (14194,1,'Have they charged each other with this? Nay! they are an inordinate people.',NULL,51,53),
 (14195,2,'Is this the legacy they have transmitted, one to another? Nay, they are themselves a people transgressing beyond bounds!',NULL,51,53),
 (14196,3,'Have they handed down (the saying) as an heirloom one unto another? Nay, but they are froward folk.',NULL,51,53),
 (14197,1,'Then turn your back upon them for you are not to blame;',NULL,51,54),
 (14198,2,'So turn away from them: not thine is the blame.',NULL,51,54),
 (14199,3,'So withdraw from them (O Muhammad), for thou art in no wise blameworthy,',NULL,51,54),
 (14200,1,'And continue to remind, for surely the reminder profits the believers.',NULL,51,55),
 (14201,2,'But teach (thy Message) for teaching benefits the Believers.',NULL,51,55),
 (14202,3,'And warn, for warning profiteth believers.',NULL,51,55),
 (14203,1,'And I have not created the jinn and the men except that they should serve Me.',NULL,51,56),
 (14204,2,'I have only created Jinns and men, that they may serve Me.',NULL,51,56),
 (14205,3,'I created the jinn and humankind only that they might worship Me.',NULL,51,56),
 (14206,1,'I do not desire from them any sustenance and I do not desire that they should feed Me.',NULL,51,57),
 (14207,2,'No Sustenance do I require of them, nor do I require that they should feed Me.',NULL,51,57),
 (14208,3,'I seek no livelihood from them, nor do I ask that they should feed Me.',NULL,51,57),
 (14209,1,'Surely Allah is the Bestower of sustenance, the Lord of Power, the Strong.',NULL,51,58),
 (14210,2,'For Allah is He Who gives (all) Sustenance,- Lord of Power,- Steadfast (for ever).',NULL,51,58),
 (14211,3,'Lo! Allah! He it is that giveth livelihood, the Lord of unbreakable might.',NULL,51,58),
 (14212,1,'So surely those who are unjust shall have a portion like the portion of their companions, therefore let them not ask Me to hasten on.',NULL,51,59),
 (14213,2,'For the Wrong-doers, their portion is like unto the portion of their fellows (of earlier generations): then let them not ask Me to hasten (that portion)!',NULL,51,59),
 (14214,3,'And lo! for those who (now) do wrong there is an evil day like unto the evil day (which came for) their likes (of old); so let them not ask Me to hasten on (that day).',NULL,51,59),
 (14215,1,'Therefore woe to those who disbelieve because of their day which they are threatened with.',NULL,51,60),
 (14216,2,'Woe, then, to the Unbelievers, on account of that Day of theirs which they have been promised!',NULL,51,60),
 (14217,3,'And woe unto those who disbelieve, from (that) their day which they are promised.',NULL,51,60),
 (14218,1,'I swear by the Mountain,',NULL,52,1),
 (14219,2,'By the Mount (of Revelation);',NULL,52,1),
 (14220,3,'By the Mount,',NULL,52,1),
 (14221,1,'And the Book written',NULL,52,2),
 (14222,2,'By a Decree inscribed',NULL,52,2),
 (14223,3,'And a Scripture inscribed',NULL,52,2),
 (14224,1,'In an outstretched fine parchment,',NULL,52,3),
 (14225,2,'In a Scroll unfolded;',NULL,52,3),
 (14226,3,'On fine parchment unrolled,',NULL,52,3),
 (14227,1,'And the House (Kaaba) that is visited,',NULL,52,4),
 (14228,2,'By the much-frequented Fane;',NULL,52,4),
 (14229,3,'And the House frequented,',NULL,52,4),
 (14230,1,'And the elevated canopy',NULL,52,5),
 (14231,2,'By the Canopy Raised High;',NULL,52,5),
 (14232,3,'And the roof exalted,',NULL,52,5),
 (14233,1,'And the swollen sea',NULL,52,6),
 (14234,2,'And by the Ocean filled with Swell;-',NULL,52,6),
 (14235,3,'And the sea kept filled,',NULL,52,6),
 (14236,1,'Most surely the punishment of your Lord will come to pass;',NULL,52,7),
 (14237,2,'Verily, the Doom of thy Lord will indeed come to pass;-',NULL,52,7),
 (14238,3,'Lo! the doom of thy Lord will surely come to pass;',NULL,52,7),
 (14239,1,'There shall be none to avert it;',NULL,52,8),
 (14240,2,'There is none can avert it;-',NULL,52,8),
 (14241,3,'There is none that can ward it off.',NULL,52,8),
 (14242,1,'On the day when the heaven shall move from side to side',NULL,52,9),
 (14243,2,'On the Day when the firmament will be in dreadful commotion.',NULL,52,9),
 (14244,3,'On the day when the heaven will heave with (awful) heaving,',NULL,52,9),
 (14245,1,'And the mountains shall pass away passing away (altogether).',NULL,52,10),
 (14246,2,'And the mountains will fly hither and thither.',NULL,52,10),
 (14247,3,'And the mountains move away with (awful) movement,',NULL,52,10),
 (14248,1,'So woe on that day to those who reject (the truth),',NULL,52,11),
 (14249,2,'Then woe that Day to those that treat (Truth) as Falsehood;-',NULL,52,11),
 (14250,3,'Then woe that day unto the deniers',NULL,52,11),
 (14251,1,'Those who sport entering into vain discourses.',NULL,52,12),
 (14252,2,'That play (and paddle) in shallow trifles.',NULL,52,12),
 (14253,3,'Who play in talk of grave matters;',NULL,52,12),
 (14254,1,'The day on which they shall be driven away to the fire of hell with violence.',NULL,52,13),
 (14255,2,'That Day shall they be thrust down to the Fire of Hell, irresistibly.',NULL,52,13),
 (14256,3,'The day when they are thrust with a (disdainful) thrust, into the fire of hell',NULL,52,13),
 (14257,1,'This is the fire which you used to give the lie to.',NULL,52,14),
 (14258,2,'"This:, it will be said, "Is the Fire,- which ye were wont to deny!',NULL,52,14),
 (14259,3,'(And it is said unto them): This is the Fire which ye were wont to deny.',NULL,52,14),
 (14260,1,'Is it magic then or do you not see?',NULL,52,15),
 (14261,2,'"Is this then a fake, or is it ye that do not see?',NULL,52,15),
 (14262,3,'Is this magic, or do ye not see?',NULL,52,15),
 (14263,1,'Enter into it, then bear (it) patiently, or do not bear (it) patiently, it is the same to you; you shall be requited only (for) what you did.',NULL,52,16),
 (14264,2,'"Burn ye therein: the same is it to you whether ye bear it with patience, or not: Ye but receive the recompense of your (own) deeds."',NULL,52,16),
 (14265,3,'Endure the heat thereof, and whether ye are patient of it or impatient of it is all one for you. Ye are only being paid for what ye used to do.',NULL,52,16),
 (14266,1,'Surely those who guard (against evil) shall be in gardens and bliss',NULL,52,17),
 (14267,2,'As to the Righteous, they will be in Gardens, and in Happiness,-',NULL,52,17),
 (14268,3,'Lo! those who kept their duty dwell in gardens and delight,',NULL,52,17),
 (14269,1,'Rejoicing because of what their Lord gave them, and their Lord saved them from the punishment of the burning fire.',NULL,52,18),
 (14270,2,'Enjoying the (Bliss) which their Lord hath bestowed on them, and their Lord shall deliver them from the Penalty of the Fire.',NULL,52,18),
 (14271,3,'Happy because of what their Lord hath given them, and (because) their Lord hath warded off from them the torment of hell-fire.',NULL,52,18),
 (14272,1,'Eat and drink pleasantly for what you did,',NULL,52,19),
 (14273,2,'(To them will be said:) "Eat and drink ye, with profit and health, because of your (good) deeds."',NULL,52,19),
 (14274,3,'(And it is said unto them): Eat and drink in health (as a reward) for what ye used to do,',NULL,52,19),
 (14275,1,'Reclining on thrones set in lines, and We will unite them to large-eyed beautiful ones.',NULL,52,20),
 (14276,2,'They will recline (with ease) on Thrones (of dignity) arranged in ranks; and We shall join them to Companions, with beautiful big and lustrous eyes.',NULL,52,20),
 (14277,3,'Reclining on ranged couches. And we wed them unto fair ones with wide, lovely eyes.',NULL,52,20),
 (14278,1,'And (as for) those who believe and their offspring follow them in faith, We will unite with them their offspring and We will not diminish to them aught of their work; every man is responsible for what he shall have wrought.',NULL,52,21),
 (14279,2,'And those who believe and whose families follow them in Faith,- to them shall We join their families: Nor shall We deprive them (of the fruit) of aught of their works: (Yet) is each individual in pledge for his deeds.',NULL,52,21),
 (14280,3,'And they who believe and whose seed follow them in faith, We cause their seed to join them (there), and We deprive them of nought of their (life''s) work. Every man is a pledge for that which he hath earned.',NULL,52,21),
 (14281,1,'And We will aid them with fruit and flesh such as they desire.',NULL,52,22),
 (14282,2,'And We shall bestow on them, of fruit and meat, anything they shall desire.',NULL,52,22),
 (14283,3,'And We provide them with fruit and meat such as they desire.',NULL,52,22),
 (14284,1,'They shall pass therein from one to another a cup wherein there shall be nothing vain nor any sin.',NULL,52,23),
 (14285,2,'They shall there exchange, one with another, a (loving) cup free of frivolity, free of all taint of ill.',NULL,52,23),
 (14286,3,'There they pass from hand to hand a cup wherein is neither vanity nor cause of sin.',NULL,52,23),
 (14287,1,'And round them shall go boys of theirs as if they were hidden pearls.',NULL,52,24),
 (14288,2,'Round about them will serve, (devoted) to them, young male servants (handsome) as Pearls well-guarded.',NULL,52,24),
 (14289,3,'And there go round, waiting on them menservants of their own, as they were hidden pearls.',NULL,52,24),
 (14290,1,'And some of them shall advance towards others questioning each other.',NULL,52,25),
 (14291,2,'They will advance to each other, engaging in mutual enquiry.',NULL,52,25),
 (14292,3,'And some of them draw near unto others, questioning,',NULL,52,25),
 (14293,1,'Saying: Surely we feared before on account of our families:',NULL,52,26),
 (14294,2,'They will say: "Aforetime, we were not without fear for the sake of our people.',NULL,52,26),
 (14295,3,'Saying: Lo! of old, when we were with our families, we were ever anxious;',NULL,52,26),
 (14296,1,'But Allah has been gracious to us and He has saved us from the punishment of the hot wind:',NULL,52,27),
 (14297,2,'"But Allah has been good to us, and has delivered us from the Penalty of the Scorching Wind.',NULL,52,27),
 (14298,3,'But Allah hath been gracious unto us and hath preserved us from the torment of the breath of Fire.',NULL,52,27),
 (14299,1,'Surely we called upon Him before: Surely He is the Benign, the Merciful.',NULL,52,28),
 (14300,2,'"Truly, we did call unto Him from of old: truly it is He, the Beneficent, the Merciful!"',NULL,52,28),
 (14301,3,'Lo! we used to pray unto Him of old. Lo! He is the Benign, the Merciful.',NULL,52,28),
 (14302,1,'Therefore continue to remind, for by the grace of your Lord, you are not a soothsayer, or a madman.',NULL,52,29),
 (14303,2,'Therefore proclaim thou the praises (of thy Lord): for by the Grace of thy Lord, thou art no (vulgar) soothsayer, nor art thou one possessed.',NULL,52,29),
 (14304,3,'Therefor warn (men, O Muhammad). By the grace of Allah thou art neither soothsayer nor madman.',NULL,52,29),
 (14305,1,'Or do they say: A poet, we wait for him the evil accidents of time.',NULL,52,30),
 (14306,2,'Or do they say:- "A Poet! we await for him some calamity (hatched) by Time!"',NULL,52,30),
 (14307,3,'Or say they: (he is) a poet, (one) for whom we may expect the accident of time?',NULL,52,30),
 (14308,1,'Say: Wait, for surely I too with you am of those who wait.',NULL,52,31),
 (14309,2,'Say thou: "Await ye!- I too will wait along with you!"',NULL,52,31),
 (14310,3,'Say (unto them): Except (your fill)! Lo! I am with you among the expectant.',NULL,52,31),
 (14311,1,'Nay! do their understandings bid them this? Or are they an inordinate people?',NULL,52,32),
 (14312,2,'Is it that their faculties of understanding urge them to this, or are they but a people transgressing beyond bounds?',NULL,52,32),
 (14313,3,'Do their minds command them to do this, or are they an outrageous folk?',NULL,52,32),
 (14314,1,'Or do they say: He has forged it. Nay! they do not believe.',NULL,52,33),
 (14315,2,'Or do they say, "He fabricated the (Message)"? Nay, they have no faith!',NULL,52,33),
 (14316,3,'Or say they: He hath invented it? Nay, but they will not believe!',NULL,52,33),
 (14317,1,'Then let them bring an announcement like it if they are truthful.',NULL,52,34),
 (14318,2,'Let them then produce a recital like unto it,- If (it be) they speak the truth!',NULL,52,34),
 (14319,3,'Then let them produce speech the like thereof, if they are truthful.',NULL,52,34),
 (14320,1,'Or were they created without there being anything, or are they the creators?',NULL,52,35),
 (14321,2,'Were they created of nothing, or were they themselves the creators?',NULL,52,35),
 (14322,3,'Or were they created out of naught? Or are they the creators?',NULL,52,35),
 (14323,1,'Or did they create the heavens and the earth? Nay! they have no certainty.',NULL,52,36),
 (14324,2,'Or did they create the heavens and the earth? Nay, they have no firm belief.',NULL,52,36),
 (14325,3,'Or did they create the heavens and the earth? Nay, but they are sure of nothing!',NULL,52,36),
 (14326,1,'Or have they the treasures of your Lord with them? Or have they been set in absolute authority?',NULL,52,37),
 (14327,2,'Or are the Treasures of thy Lord with them, or are they the managers (of affairs)?',NULL,52,37),
 (14328,3,'Or do they own the treasures of thy Lord? Or have they been given charge (thereof)?',NULL,52,37),
 (14329,1,'Or have they the means by which they listen? Then let their listener bring a clear authority.',NULL,52,38),
 (14330,2,'Or have they a ladder, by which they can (climb up to heaven and) listen (to its secrets)? Then let (such a) listener of theirs produce a manifest proof.',NULL,52,38),
 (14331,3,'Or have they any stairway (unto heaven) by means of which they overhear (decrees). Then let their listener produce some warrant manifest!',NULL,52,38),
 (14332,1,'Or has He daughters while you have sons?',NULL,52,39),
 (14333,2,'Or has He only daughters and ye have sons?',NULL,52,39),
 (14334,3,'Or hath He daughters whereas ye have sons?',NULL,52,39),
 (14335,1,'Or do you ask them for a reward, so that they are overburdened by a debt?',NULL,52,40),
 (14336,2,'Or is it that thou dost ask for a reward, so that they are burdened with a load of debt?-',NULL,52,40),
 (14337,3,'Or askest thou (Muhammad) a fee from them so that they are plunged in debt?',NULL,52,40),
 (14338,1,'Or have they the unseen so that they write (it) down?',NULL,52,41),
 (14339,2,'Or that the Unseen in it their hands, and they write it down?',NULL,52,41),
 (14340,3,'Or possess they the Unseen so that they can write (it) down?',NULL,52,41),
 (14341,1,'Or do they desire a war? But those who disbelieve shall be the vanquished ones in war.',NULL,52,42),
 (14342,2,'Or do they intend a plot (against thee)? But those who defy Allah are themselves involved in a Plot!',NULL,52,42),
 (14343,3,'Or seek they to ensnare (the messenger)? But those who disbelieve, they are the ensnared!',NULL,52,42),
 (14344,1,'Or have they a god other than Allah? Glory be to Allah from what they set up (with Him).',NULL,52,43),
 (14345,2,'Or have they a god other than Allah? Exalted is Allah far above the things they associate with Him!',NULL,52,43),
 (14346,3,'Or have they any god beside Allah? Glorified be Allah from all that they ascribe as partner (unto Him)!',NULL,52,43),
 (14347,1,'And if they should see a portion of the heaven coming down, they would say: Piled up clouds.',NULL,52,44),
 (14348,2,'Were they to see a piece of the sky falling (on them), they would (only) say: "Clouds gathered in heaps!"',NULL,52,44),
 (14349,3,'And if they were to see a fragment of the heaven falling, they would say: A heap of clouds.',NULL,52,44),
 (14350,1,'Leave them then till they meet that day of theirs wherein they shall be made to swoon (with terror):',NULL,52,45),
 (14351,2,'So leave them alone until they encounter that Day of theirs, wherein they shall (perforce) swoon (with terror),-',NULL,52,45),
 (14352,3,'Then let them be (O Muhammad), till they meet their day, in which they will be thunder-stricken,',NULL,52,45),
 (14353,1,'The day on which their struggle shall not avail them aught, nor shall they be helped.',NULL,52,46),
 (14354,2,'The Day when their plotting will avail them nothing and no help shall be given them.',NULL,52,46),
 (14355,3,'A day in which their guile will naught avail them, nor will they be helped.',NULL,52,46),
 (14356,1,'And surely those who are unjust shall have a punishment besides that (in the world), but most of them do not know.',NULL,52,47),
 (14357,2,'And verily, for those who do wrong, there is another punishment besides this: But most of them understand not.',NULL,52,47),
 (14358,3,'And verily, for those who do wrong, there is a punishment beyond that. But most of them know not.',NULL,52,47),
 (14359,1,'And wait patiently for the judgment of your Lord, for surely you are before Our eyes, and sing the praise of your Lord when you rise;',NULL,52,48),
 (14360,2,'Now await in patience the command of thy Lord: for verily thou art in Our eyes: and celebrate the praises of thy Lord the while thou standest forth,',NULL,52,48),
 (14361,3,'So wait patiently (O Muhammad) for thy Lord''s decree, for surely thou art in Our sight; and hymn the praise of thy Lord when thou uprisest,',NULL,52,48),
 (14362,1,'And in the night, give Him glory too, and at the setting of the stars.',NULL,52,49),
 (14363,2,'And for part of the night also praise thou Him,- and at the retreat of the stars!',NULL,52,49),
 (14364,3,'And in the night-time also hymn His praise, and at the setting of the stars.',NULL,52,49),
 (14365,1,'I swear by the star when it goes down.',NULL,53,1),
 (14366,2,'By the Star when it goes down,-',NULL,53,1),
 (14367,3,'By the Star when it setteth,',NULL,53,1),
 (14368,1,'Your companion does not err, nor does he go astray;',NULL,53,2),
 (14369,2,'Your Companion is neither astray nor being misled.',NULL,53,2),
 (14370,3,'Your comrade erreth not, nor is deceived;',NULL,53,2),
 (14371,1,'Nor does he speak out of desire.',NULL,53,3),
 (14372,2,'Nor does he say (aught) of (his own) Desire.',NULL,53,3),
 (14373,3,'Nor doth he speak of (his own) desire.',NULL,53,3),
 (14374,1,'It is naught but revelation that is revealed,',NULL,53,4),
 (14375,2,'It is no less than inspiration sent down to him:',NULL,53,4),
 (14376,3,'It is naught save an inspiration that is inspired,',NULL,53,4),
 (14377,1,'The Lord of Mighty Power has taught him,',NULL,53,5),
 (14378,2,'He was taught by one Mighty in Power,',NULL,53,5),
 (14379,3,'Which one of mighty powers hath taught him,',NULL,53,5),
 (14380,1,'The Lord of Strength; so he attained completion,',NULL,53,6),
 (14381,2,'Endued with Wisdom: for he appeared (in stately form);',NULL,53,6),
 (14382,3,'One vigorous; and he grew clear to view',NULL,53,6),
 (14383,1,'And he is in the highest part of the horizon.',NULL,53,7),
 (14384,2,'While he was in the highest part of the horizon:',NULL,53,7),
 (14385,3,'When he was on the uppermost horizon.',NULL,53,7),
 (14386,1,'Then he drew near, then he bowed',NULL,53,8),
 (14387,2,'Then he approached and came closer,',NULL,53,8),
 (14388,3,'Then he drew nigh and came down',NULL,53,8),
 (14389,1,'So he was the measure of two bows or closer still.',NULL,53,9),
 (14390,2,'And was at a distance of but two bow-lengths or (even) nearer;',NULL,53,9),
 (14391,3,'Till he was (distant) two bows'' length or even nearer,',NULL,53,9),
 (14392,1,'And He revealed to His servant what He revealed.',NULL,53,10),
 (14393,2,'So did (Allah) convey the inspiration to His Servant- (conveyed) what He (meant) to convey.',NULL,53,10),
 (14394,3,'And He revealed unto His slave that which He revealed.',NULL,53,10),
 (14395,1,'The heart was not untrue in (making him see) what he saw.',NULL,53,11),
 (14396,2,'The (Prophet''s) (mind and) heart in no way falsified that which he saw.',NULL,53,11),
 (14397,3,'The heart lied not (in seeing) what it saw.',NULL,53,11),
 (14398,1,'What! do you then dispute with him as to what he saw?',NULL,53,12),
 (14399,2,'Will ye then dispute with him concerning what he saw?',NULL,53,12),
 (14400,3,'Will ye then dispute with him concerning what he seeth?',NULL,53,12),
 (14401,1,'And certainly he saw him in another descent,',NULL,53,13),
 (14402,2,'For indeed he saw him at a second descent,',NULL,53,13),
 (14403,3,'And verily he saw him yet another time',NULL,53,13),
 (14404,1,'At the farthest lote-tree;',NULL,53,14),
 (14405,2,'Near the Lote-tree beyond which none may pass:',NULL,53,14),
 (14406,3,'By the lote-tree of the utmost boundary,',NULL,53,14),
 (14407,1,'Near which is the garden, the place to be resorted to.',NULL,53,15),
 (14408,2,'Near it is the Garden of Abode.',NULL,53,15),
 (14409,3,'Nigh unto which is the Garden of Abode.',NULL,53,15),
 (14410,1,'When that which covers covered the lote-tree;',NULL,53,16),
 (14411,2,'Behold, the Lote-tree was shrouded (in mystery unspeakable!)',NULL,53,16),
 (14412,3,'When that which shroudeth did enshroud the lote-tree,',NULL,53,16),
 (14413,1,'The eye did not turn aside, nor did it exceed the limit.',NULL,53,17),
 (14414,2,'(His) sight never swerved, nor did it go wrong!',NULL,53,17),
 (14415,3,'The eye turned not aside nor yet was overbold.',NULL,53,17),
 (14416,1,'Certainly he saw of the greatest signs of his Lord.',NULL,53,18),
 (14417,2,'For truly did he see, of the Signs of his Lord, the Greatest!',NULL,53,18),
 (14418,3,'Verily he saw one of the greater revelations of his Lord.',NULL,53,18),
 (14419,1,'Have you then considered the Lat and the Uzza,',NULL,53,19),
 (14420,2,'Have ye seen Lat. and ''Uzza,',NULL,53,19),
 (14421,3,'Have ye thought upon Al-Lat and Al-''Uzza',NULL,53,19),
 (14422,1,'And Manat, the third, the last?',NULL,53,20),
 (14423,2,'And another, the third (goddess), Manat?',NULL,53,20),
 (14424,3,'And Manat, the third, the other?',NULL,53,20),
 (14425,1,'What! for you the males and for Him the females!',NULL,53,21),
 (14426,2,'What! for you the male sex, and for Him, the female?',NULL,53,21),
 (14427,3,'Are yours the males and His the females?',NULL,53,21),
 (14428,1,'This indeed is an unjust division!',NULL,53,22),
 (14429,2,'Behold, such would be indeed a division most unfair!',NULL,53,22),
 (14430,3,'That indeed were an unfair division!',NULL,53,22),
 (14431,1,'They are naught but names which you have named, you and your fathers; Allah has not sent for them any authority. They follow naught but conjecture and the low desires which (their) souls incline to; and certainly the guidance has come to them from their Lord.',NULL,53,23),
 (14432,2,'These are nothing but names which ye have devised,- ye and your fathers,- for which Allah has sent down no authority (whatever). They follow nothing but conjecture and what their own souls desire!- Even though there has already come to them Guidance from their Lord!',NULL,53,23),
 (14433,3,'They are but names which ye have named, ye and your fathers, for which Allah hath revealed no warrant. They follow but a guess and that which (they) themselves desire. And now the guidance from their Lord hath come unto them.',NULL,53,23),
 (14434,1,'Or shall man have what he wishes?',NULL,53,24),
 (14435,2,'Nay, shall man have (just) anything he hankers after?',NULL,53,24),
 (14436,3,'Or shall man have what he coveteth?',NULL,53,24),
 (14437,1,'Nay! for Allah is the hereafter and the former (life).',NULL,53,25),
 (14438,2,'But it is to Allah that the End and the Beginning (of all things) belong.',NULL,53,25),
 (14439,3,'But unto Allah belongeth the after (life), and the former.',NULL,53,25),
 (14440,1,'And how many an angel is there in the heavens whose intercession does not avail at all except after Allah has given permission to whom He pleases and chooses.',NULL,53,26),
 (14441,2,'How many-so-ever be the angels in the heavens, their intercession will avail nothing except after Allah has given leave for whom He pleases and that he is acceptable to Him.',NULL,53,26),
 (14442,3,'And how many angels are in the heavens whose intercession availeth naught save after Allah giveth leave to whom He chooseth and accepteth.',NULL,53,26),
 (14443,1,'Most surely they who do not believe in the hereafter name the angels with female names.',NULL,53,27),
 (14444,2,'Those who believe not in the Hereafter, name the angels with female names.',NULL,53,27),
 (14445,3,'Lo! it is those who disbelieve in the Hereafter who name the angels with the names of females.',NULL,53,27),
 (14446,1,'And they have no knowledge of it; they do not follow anything but conjecture, and surely conjecture does not avail against the truth at all.',NULL,53,28),
 (14447,2,'But they have no knowledge therein. They follow nothing but conjecture; and conjecture avails nothing against Truth.',NULL,53,28),
 (14448,3,'And they have no knowledge thereof. They follow but a guess, and lo! a guess can never take the place of the truth.',NULL,53,28),
 (14449,1,'Therefore turn aside from him who turns his back upon Our reminder and does not desire anything but this world''s life.',NULL,53,29),
 (14450,2,'Therefore shun those who turn away from Our Message and desire nothing but the life of this world.',NULL,53,29),
 (14451,3,'Then withdraw (O Muhammad) from him who fleeth from Our remembrance and desireth but the life of the world.',NULL,53,29),
 (14452,1,'That is their goal of knowledge; surely your Lord knows best him who goes astray from His path and He knows best him who follows the right direction.',NULL,53,30),
 (14453,2,'That is as far as knowledge will reach them. Verily thy Lord knoweth best those who stray from His Path, and He knoweth best those who receive guidance.',NULL,53,30),
 (14454,3,'Such is their sum of knowledge. Lo! thy Lord is Best Aware of him who strayeth, and He is Best Aware of him whom goeth right.',NULL,53,30),
 (14455,1,'And Allah''s is what is in the heavens and what is in the earth, that He may reward those who do evil according to what they do, and (that) He may reward those who do good with goodness.',NULL,53,31),
 (14456,2,'Yea, to Allah belongs all that is in the heavens and on earth: so that He rewards those who do evil, according to their deeds, and He rewards those who do good, with what is best.',NULL,53,31),
 (14457,3,'And unto Allah belongeth whatsoever is in the heavens and whatsoever is in the earth, that He may reward those who do evil with that which they have done, and reward those who do good with goodness.',NULL,53,31),
 (14458,1,'Those who keep aloof from the great sins and the indecencies but the passing idea; surely your Lord is liberal in forgiving. He knows you best when He brings you forth from the earth and when you are embryos in the wombs of your mothers; therefore do not attribute purity to your souls; He knows him best who guards (against evil).',NULL,53,32),
 (14459,2,'Those who avoid great sins and shameful deeds, only (falling into) small faults,- verily thy Lord is ample in forgiveness. He knows you well when He brings you out of the earth, And when ye are hidden in your mothers'' wombs. Therefore justify not yourselves: He knows best who it is that guards against evil.',NULL,53,32),
 (14460,3,'Those who avoid enormities of sin and abominations, save the unwilled offences - (for them) lo! thy Lord is of vast mercy. He is Best Aware of you (from the time) when He created you from the earth, and when ye were hidden in the bellies of your mothers. Therefor ascribe not purity unto yourselves. He is Best Aware of him who wardeth off (evil).',NULL,53,32),
 (14461,1,'Have you then seen him who turns his back?',NULL,53,33),
 (14462,2,'Seest thou one who turns back,',NULL,53,33),
 (14463,3,'Didst thou (O Muhammad) observe him who turned away,',NULL,53,33),
 (14464,1,'And gives a little and (then) withholds.',NULL,53,34),
 (14465,2,'Gives a little, then hardens (his heart)?',NULL,53,34),
 (14466,3,'And gave a little, then was grudging?',NULL,53,34),
 (14467,1,'Has he the knowledge of the unseen so that he can see?',NULL,53,35),
 (14468,2,'What! Has he knowledge of the Unseen so that he can see?',NULL,53,35),
 (14469,3,'Hath he knowledge of the Unseen so that he seeth?',NULL,53,35),
 (14470,1,'Or, has he not been informed of what is in the scriptures of Musa?',NULL,53,36),
 (14471,2,'Nay, is he not acquainted with what is in the Books of Moses-',NULL,53,36),
 (14472,3,'Or hath he not had news of what is in the books of Moses',NULL,53,36),
 (14473,1,'And (of) Ibrahim who fulfilled (the commandments):',NULL,53,37),
 (14474,2,'And of Abraham who fulfilled his engagements?-',NULL,53,37),
 (14475,3,'And Abraham who paid his debt:',NULL,53,37),
 (14476,1,'That no bearer of burden shall bear the burden of another-',NULL,53,38),
 (14477,2,'Namely, that no bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another;',NULL,53,38),
 (14478,3,'That no laden one shall bear another''s load,',NULL,53,38),
 (14479,1,'And that man shall have nothing but what he strives for-',NULL,53,39),
 (14480,2,'That man can have nothing but what he strives for;',NULL,53,39),
 (14481,3,'And that man hath only that for which he maketh effort,',NULL,53,39),
 (14482,1,'And that his striving shall soon be seen-',NULL,53,40),
 (14483,2,'That (the fruit of) his striving will soon come in sight:',NULL,53,40),
 (14484,3,'And that his effort will be seen.',NULL,53,40),
 (14485,1,'Then shall he be rewarded for it with the fullest reward-',NULL,53,41),
 (14486,2,'Then will he be rewarded with a reward complete;',NULL,53,41),
 (14487,3,'And afterward he will be repaid for it with fullest payment;',NULL,53,41),
 (14488,1,'And that to your Lord is the goal-',NULL,53,42),
 (14489,2,'That to thy Lord is the final Goal;',NULL,53,42),
 (14490,3,'And that thy Lord, He is the goal;',NULL,53,42),
 (14491,1,'And that He it is Who makes (men) laugh and makes (them) weep;',NULL,53,43),
 (14492,2,'That it is He Who granteth Laughter and Tears;',NULL,53,43),
 (14493,3,'And that He it is who maketh laugh, and maketh weep,',NULL,53,43),
 (14494,1,'And that He it is Who causes death and gives life-',NULL,53,44),
 (14495,2,'That it is He Who granteth Death and Life;',NULL,53,44),
 (14496,3,'And that He it is Who giveth death and giveth life;',NULL,53,44),
 (14497,1,'And that He created pairs, the male and the female',NULL,53,45),
 (14498,2,'That He did create in pairs,- male and female,',NULL,53,45),
 (14499,3,'And that He createth the two spouses, the male and the female,',NULL,53,45),
 (14500,1,'From the small seed when it is adapted',NULL,53,46),
 (14501,2,'From a seed when lodged (in its place);',NULL,53,46),
 (14502,3,'From a drop (of seed) when it is poured forth;',NULL,53,46),
 (14503,1,'And that on Him is the bringing forth a second time;',NULL,53,47),
 (14504,2,'That He hath promised a Second Creation (Raising of the Dead);',NULL,53,47),
 (14505,3,'And that He hath ordained the second bringing forth;',NULL,53,47),
 (14506,1,'And that He it is Who enriches and gives to hold;',NULL,53,48),
 (14507,2,'That it is He Who giveth wealth and satisfaction;',NULL,53,48),
 (14508,3,'And that He it is Who enricheth and contenteth;',NULL,53,48),
 (14509,1,'And that He is the Lord of the Sirius;',NULL,53,49),
 (14510,2,'That He is the Lord of Sirius (the Mighty Star);',NULL,53,49),
 (14511,3,'And that He it is Who is the Lord of Sirius;',NULL,53,49),
 (14512,1,'And that He did destroy the Ad of old',NULL,53,50),
 (14513,2,'And that it is He Who destroyed the (powerful) ancient ''Ad (people),',NULL,53,50),
 (14514,3,'And that He destroyed the former (tribe of) A''ad,',NULL,53,50),
 (14515,1,'And Samood, so He spared not',NULL,53,51),
 (14516,2,'And the Thamud nor gave them a lease of perpetual life.',NULL,53,51),
 (14517,3,'And (the tribe of) Thamud He spared not;',NULL,53,51),
 (14518,1,'And the people of Nuh before; surely they were most unjust and inordinate;',NULL,53,52),
 (14519,2,'And before them, the people of Noah, for that they were (all) most unjust and most insolent transgressors,',NULL,53,52),
 (14520,3,'And the folk of Noah aforetime, Lo! they were more unjust and more rebellious;',NULL,53,52),
 (14521,1,'And the overthrown cities did He overthrow,',NULL,53,53),
 (14522,2,'And He destroyed the Overthrown Cities (of Sodom and Gomorrah).',NULL,53,53),
 (14523,3,'And Al-Mu''tafikah He destroyed',NULL,53,53),
 (14524,1,'So there covered them that which covered.',NULL,53,54),
 (14525,2,'So that (ruins unknown) have covered them up.',NULL,53,54),
 (14526,3,'So that there covered them that which did cover.',NULL,53,54),
 (14527,1,'Which of your Lord''s benefits will you then dispute about?',NULL,53,55),
 (14528,2,'Then which of the gifts of thy Lord, (O man,) wilt thou dispute about?',NULL,53,55),
 (14529,3,'Concerning which then, of the bounties of thy Lord, canst thou dispute?',NULL,53,55),
 (14530,1,'This is a warner of the warners of old.',NULL,53,56),
 (14531,2,'This is a Warner, of the (series of) Warners of old!',NULL,53,56),
 (14532,3,'This is a warner of the warners of old.',NULL,53,56),
 (14533,1,'The near event draws nigh.',NULL,53,57),
 (14534,2,'The (Judgment) ever approaching draws nigh:',NULL,53,57),
 (14535,3,'The threatened Hour is nigh.',NULL,53,57),
 (14536,1,'There shall be none besides Allah to remove it.',NULL,53,58),
 (14537,2,'No (soul) but Allah can lay it bare.',NULL,53,58),
 (14538,3,'None beside Allah can disclose it.',NULL,53,58),
 (14539,1,'Do you then wonder at this announcement?',NULL,53,59),
 (14540,2,'Do ye then wonder at this recital?',NULL,53,59),
 (14541,3,'Marvel ye then at this statement,',NULL,53,59),
 (14542,1,'And will you laugh and not weep?',NULL,53,60),
 (14543,2,'And will ye laugh and not weep,-',NULL,53,60),
 (14544,3,'And laugh and not weep,',NULL,53,60),
 (14545,1,'While you are indulging in varieties.',NULL,53,61),
 (14546,2,'Wasting your time in vanities?',NULL,53,61),
 (14547,3,'While ye amuse yourselves?',NULL,53,61),
 (14548,1,'So make obeisance to Allah and serve (Him).',NULL,53,62),
 (14549,2,'But fall ye down in prostration to Allah, and adore (Him)!',NULL,53,62),
 (14550,3,'Rather prostrate yourselves before Allah and serve Him.',NULL,53,62),
 (14551,1,'The hour drew nigh and the moon did rend asunder.',NULL,54,1),
 (14552,2,'The Hour (of Judgment) is nigh, and the moon is cleft asunder.',NULL,54,1),
 (14553,3,'The hour drew nigh and the moon was rent in twain.',NULL,54,1),
 (14554,1,'And if they see a miracle they turn aside and say: Transient magic.',NULL,54,2),
 (14555,2,'But if they see a Sign, they turn away, and say, "This is (but) transient magic."',NULL,54,2),
 (14556,3,'And if they behold a portent they turn away and say: Prolonged illusion.',NULL,54,2),
 (14557,1,'And they call (it) a lie, and follow their low desires; and every affair has its appointed term.',NULL,54,3),
 (14558,2,'They reject (the warning) and follow their (own) lusts but every matter has its appointed time.',NULL,54,3),
 (14559,3,'They denied (the Truth) and followed their own lusts. Yet everything will come to a decision',NULL,54,3),
 (14560,1,'And certainly some narratives have come to them wherein is prevention--',NULL,54,4),
 (14561,2,'There have already come to them Recitals wherein there is (enough) to check (them),',NULL,54,4),
 (14562,3,'And surely there hath come unto them news whereof the purport should deter,',NULL,54,4),
 (14563,1,'Consummate wisdom-- but warnings do not avail;',NULL,54,5),
 (14564,2,'Mature wisdom;- but (the preaching of) Warners profits them not.',NULL,54,5),
 (14565,3,'Effective wisdom; but warnings avail not.',NULL,54,5),
 (14566,1,'So turn (your) back on them (for) the day when the inviter shall invite them to a hard task,',NULL,54,6),
 (14567,2,'Therefore, (O Prophet,) turn away from them. The Day that the Caller will call (them) to a terrible affair,',NULL,54,6),
 (14568,3,'So withdraw from them (O Muhammad) on the day when the Summoner summoneth unto a painful thing.',NULL,54,6),
 (14569,1,'Their eyes cast down, going forth from their graves as if they were scattered locusts,',NULL,54,7),
 (14570,2,'They will come forth,- their eyes humbled - from (their) graves, (torpid) like locusts scattered abroad,',NULL,54,7),
 (14571,3,'With downcast eyes, they come forth from the graves as they were locusts spread abroad,',NULL,54,7),
 (14572,1,'Hastening to the inviter. The unbelievers shall say: This is a hard day.',NULL,54,8),
 (14573,2,'Hastening, with eyes transfixed, towards the Caller!- "Hard is this Day!", the Unbelievers will say.',NULL,54,8),
 (14574,3,'Hastening toward the summoner; the disbelievers say: This is a hard day.',NULL,54,8),
 (14575,1,'Before them the people of Nuh rejected, so they rejected Our servant and called (him) mad, and he was driven away.',NULL,54,9),
 (14576,2,'Before them the People of Noah rejected (their messenger): they rejected Our servant, and said, "Here is one possessed!", and he was driven out.',NULL,54,9),
 (14577,3,'The folk of Noah denied before them, yea, they denied Our slave and said: A madman; and he was repulsed.',NULL,54,9),
 (14578,1,'Therefore he called upon his Lord: I am overcome, come Thou then to help.',NULL,54,10),
 (14579,2,'Then he called on his Lord: "I am one overcome: do Thou then help (me)!"',NULL,54,10),
 (14580,3,'So he cried unto his Lord, saying: I am vanquished, so give help.',NULL,54,10),
 (14581,1,'So We opened the gates of the cloud with water pouring',NULL,54,11),
 (14582,2,'So We opened the gates of heaven, with water pouring forth.',NULL,54,11),
 (14583,3,'Then opened We the gates of heaven with pouring water',NULL,54,11),
 (14584,1,'And We made water to flow forth in the land in springs, so the water gathered together according to a measure already ordained.',NULL,54,12),
 (14585,2,'And We caused the earth to gush forth with springs, so the waters met (and rose) to the extent decreed.',NULL,54,12),
 (14586,3,'And caused the earth to gush forth springs, so that the waters met for a predestined purpose.',NULL,54,12),
 (14587,1,'And We bore him on that which was made of planks and nails',NULL,54,13),
 (14588,2,'But We bore him on an (Ark) made of broad planks and caulked with palm-fibre:',NULL,54,13),
 (14589,3,'And We carried him upon a thing of planks and nails,',NULL,54,13),
 (14590,1,'Sailing, before Our eyes, a reward for him who was denied.',NULL,54,14),
 (14591,2,'She floats under our eyes (and care): a recompense to one who had been rejected (with scorn)!',NULL,54,14),
 (14592,3,'That ran (upon the waters) in Our sight, as a reward for him who was rejected.',NULL,54,14),
 (14593,1,'And certainly We left it as a sign, but is there anyone who',NULL,54,15),
 (14594,2,'And We have left this as a Sign (for all time): then is there any that will receive admonition?',NULL,54,15),
 (14595,3,'And verily We left it as a token; but is there any that remembereth?',NULL,54,15),
 (14596,1,'How (great) was then My punishment and My warning!',NULL,54,16),
 (14597,2,'But how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning?',NULL,54,16),
 (14598,3,'Then see how (dreadful) was My punishment after My warnings!',NULL,54,16),
 (14599,1,'And certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance, but is there anyone who will mind?',NULL,54,17),
 (14600,2,'And We have indeed made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition?',NULL,54,17),
 (14601,3,'And in truth We have made the Qur''an easy to remember; but is there any that remembereth?',NULL,54,17),
 (14602,1,'Ad treated (the truth) as a lie, so how (great) was My punishment and My warning!',NULL,54,18),
 (14603,2,'The ''Ad (people) (too) rejected (Truth): then how terrible was My Penalty and My Warning?',NULL,54,18),
 (14604,3,'(The tribe of) A''ad rejected warnings. Then how (dreadful) was My punishment after My warnings.',NULL,54,18),
 (14605,1,'Surely We sent on them a tornado in a day of bitter ill-luck',NULL,54,19),
 (14606,2,'For We sent against them a furious wind, on a Day of violent Disaster,',NULL,54,19),
 (14607,3,'Lo! We let loose on them a raging wind on a day of constant calamity,',NULL,54,19),
 (14608,1,'Tearing men away as if they were the trunks of palm-trees torn up.',NULL,54,20),
 (14609,2,'Plucking out men as if they were roots of palm-trees torn up (from the ground).',NULL,54,20),
 (14610,3,'Sweeping men away as though they were uprooted trunks of palm-trees.',NULL,54,20),
 (14611,1,'How (great) was then My punishment and My warning!',NULL,54,21),
 (14612,2,'Yea, how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning!',NULL,54,21),
 (14613,3,'Then see how (dreadful) was My punishment after My warnings!',NULL,54,21),
 (14614,1,'And certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance, but is there anyone who will mind?',NULL,54,22),
 (14615,2,'But We have indeed made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition?',NULL,54,22),
 (14616,3,'And in truth We have made the Qur''an easy to remember; but is there any that remembereth?',NULL,54,22),
 (14617,1,'Samood rejected the warning.',NULL,54,23),
 (14618,2,'The Thamud (also) rejected (their) Warners.',NULL,54,23),
 (14619,3,'(The tribe of) Thamud rejected warnings',NULL,54,23),
 (14620,1,'So they said: What! a single mortal from among us! Shall we follow him? Most surely we shall in that case be in sure error and distress:',NULL,54,24),
 (14621,2,'For they said: "What! a man! a Solitary one from among ourselves! shall we follow such a one? Truly should we then be straying in mind, and mad!',NULL,54,24),
 (14622,3,'For they said; Is it a mortal man, alone among us, that we are to follow? Then indeed we should fall into error and madness.',NULL,54,24),
 (14623,1,'Has the reminder been made to light upon him from among us? Nay! he is an insolent liar!',NULL,54,25),
 (14624,2,'"Is it that the Message is sent to him, of all people amongst us? Nay, he is a liar, an insolent one!"',NULL,54,25),
 (14625,3,'Hath the remembrance been given unto him alone among us? Nay, but he is a rash liar.',NULL,54,25),
 (14626,1,'Tomorrow shall they know who is the liar, the insolent one.',NULL,54,26),
 (14627,2,'Ah! they will know on the morrow, which is the liar, the insolent one!',NULL,54,26),
 (14628,3,'(Unto their warner it was said): To-morrow they will know who is the rash liar.',NULL,54,26),
 (14629,1,'Surely We are going to send the she-camel as a trial for them; therefore watch them and have patience.',NULL,54,27),
 (14630,2,'For We will send the she-camel by way of trial for them. So watch them, (O Salih), and possess thyself in patience!',NULL,54,27),
