 (14634,3,'And inform them that the water is to be shared between (her and) them. Every drinking will be witnessed.',NULL,54,28),
 (14635,1,'But they called their companion, so he took (the sword) and slew (her).',NULL,54,29),
 (14636,2,'But they called to their companion, and he took a sword in hand, and hamstrung (her).',NULL,54,29),
 (14637,3,'But they call their comrade and he took and hamstrung (her).',NULL,54,29),
 (14638,1,'How (great) was then My punishment and My warning!',NULL,54,30),
 (14639,2,'Ah! how (terrible) was My Penalty and My Warning!',NULL,54,30),
 (14640,3,'Then see how (dreadful) was My punishment after My warnings!',NULL,54,30),
 (14641,1,'Surely We sent upon them a single cry, so they were like the dry fragments of trees which the maker of an enclosure collects.',NULL,54,31),
 (14642,2,'For We sent against them a single Mighty Blast, and they became like the dry stubble used by one who pens cattle.',NULL,54,31),
 (14643,3,'Lo! We sent upon them one Shout, and they became as the dry twigs (rejected by) the builder of a cattle-fold.',NULL,54,31),
 (14644,1,'And certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance, but is there anyone who will mind?',NULL,54,32),
 (14645,2,'And We have indeed made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition?',NULL,54,32),
 (14646,3,'And in truth We have made the Qur''an easy to remember; but is there any that remembereth?',NULL,54,32),
 (14647,1,'The people of Lut treated the warning. as a lie.',NULL,54,33),
 (14648,2,'The people of Lut rejected (his) warning.',NULL,54,33),
 (14649,3,'The folk of Lot rejected warnings.',NULL,54,33),
 (14650,1,'Surely We sent upon them a stonestorm, except Lut''s followers; We saved them a little before daybreak,',NULL,54,34),
 (14651,2,'We sent against them a violent Tornado with showers of stones, (which destroyed them), except Lut''s household: them We delivered by early Dawn,-',NULL,54,34),
 (14652,3,'Lo! We sent a storm of stones upon them (all) save the family of Lot, whom We rescued in the last watch of the night,',NULL,54,34),
 (14653,1,'A favor from Us; thus do We reward him who gives thanks.',NULL,54,35),
 (14654,2,'As a Grace from Us: thus do We reward those who give thanks.',NULL,54,35),
 (14655,3,'As grace from Us. Thus We reward him who giveth thanks.',NULL,54,35),
 (14656,1,'And certainly he warned them of Our violent seizure, but they obstinately disputed the warning.',NULL,54,36),
 (14657,2,'And (Lut) did warn them of Our Punishment, but they disputed about the Warning.',NULL,54,36),
 (14658,3,'And he indeed had warned them of Our blow, but they did doubt the warnings.',NULL,54,36),
 (14659,1,'And certainly they endeavored to turn him from his guests, but We blinded their eyes; so taste My chastisement and My warning.',NULL,54,37),
 (14660,2,'And they even sought to snatch away his guests from him, but We blinded their eyes. (They heard:) "Now taste ye My Wrath and My Warning."',NULL,54,37),
 (14661,3,'They even asked of him his guests for an ill purpose. Then We blinded their eyes (and said): Taste now My punishment after My warnings!',NULL,54,37),
 (14662,1,'And certainly a lasting chastisement overtook them in the morning.',NULL,54,38),
 (14663,2,'Early on the morrow an abiding Punishment seized them:',NULL,54,38),
 (14664,3,'And in truth the punishment decreed befell them early in the morning.',NULL,54,38),
 (14665,1,'So taste My chastisement and My warning.',NULL,54,39),
 (14666,2,'"So taste ye My Wrath and My Warning."',NULL,54,39),
 (14667,3,'Now taste My punishment after My warnings!',NULL,54,39),
 (14668,1,'And certainly We have made the Quran easy for remembrance, but is there anyone who will mind?',NULL,54,40),
 (14669,2,'And We have indeed made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember: then is there any that will receive admonition?',NULL,54,40),
 (14670,3,'And in truth We have made the Qur''an easy to remember; but is there any that remembereth?',NULL,54,40),
 (14671,1,'And certainly the warning came to Firon''s people.',NULL,54,41),
 (14672,2,'To the People of Pharaoh, too, aforetime, came Warners (from Allah).',NULL,54,41),
 (14673,3,'And warnings came in truth unto the house of Pharaoh',NULL,54,41),
 (14674,1,'They rejected all Our communications, so We overtook them after the manner of a Mighty, Powerful One.',NULL,54,42),
 (14675,2,'The (people) rejected all Our Signs; but We seized them with such Penalty (as comes) from One Exalted in Power, able to carry out His Will.',NULL,54,42),
 (14676,3,'Who denied Our revelations, every one. Therefore We grasped them with the grasp of the Mighty, the Powerful.',NULL,54,42),
 (14677,1,'Are the unbelievers of yours better than these, or is there an exemption for you in the scriptures?',NULL,54,43),
 (14678,2,'Are your Unbelievers, (O Quraish), better than they? Or have ye an immunity in the Sacred Books?',NULL,54,43),
 (14679,3,'Are your disbelievers better than those, or have ye some immunity in the scriptures?',NULL,54,43),
 (14680,1,'Or do they say: We are a host allied together to help each other?',NULL,54,44),
 (14681,2,'Or do they say: "We acting together can defend ourselves"?',NULL,54,44),
 (14682,3,'Or say they: We are a host victorious?',NULL,54,44),
 (14683,1,'Soon shall the hosts be routed, and they shall turn (their) backs.',NULL,54,45),
 (14684,2,'Soon will their multitude be put to flight, and they will show their backs.',NULL,54,45),
 (14685,3,'The hosts will all be routed and will turn and flee.',NULL,54,45),
 (14686,1,'Nay, the hour is their promised time, and the hour shall be most grievous and bitter.',NULL,54,46),
