 (16266,3,'The day when they come forth from the graves in haste, as racing to a goal,',NULL,70,43),
 (16267,1,'Their eyes cast down; disgrace shall overtake them; that is the day which they were threatened with.',NULL,70,44),
 (16268,2,'Their eyes lowered in dejection,- ignominy covering them (all over)! such is the Day the which they are promised!',NULL,70,44),
 (16269,3,'With eyes aghast, abasement stupefying them: Such is the Day which they are promised.',NULL,70,44),
 (16270,1,'Surely We sent Nuh to his people, saying: Warn your people before there come upon them a painful chastisement.',NULL,71,1),
 (16271,2,'We sent Noah to his People (with the Command): "Do thou warn thy People before there comes to them a grievous Penalty."',NULL,71,1),
 (16272,3,'Lo! We sent Noah unto his people (saying): Warn thy people ere the painful doom come unto them.',NULL,71,1),
 (16273,1,'He said: O my people! Surely I am a plain warner to you:',NULL,71,2),
 (16274,2,'He said: "O my People! I am to you a Warner, clear and open:',NULL,71,2),
 (16275,3,'He said: O my people! Lo! I am a plain warner unto you',NULL,71,2),
 (16276,1,'That you should serve Allah and be careful of (your duty to) Him and obey me:',NULL,71,3),
 (16277,2,'"That ye should worship Allah, fear Him and obey me:',NULL,71,3),
 (16278,3,'(Bidding you): Serve Allah and keep your duty unto Him and obey me,',NULL,71,3),
 (16279,1,'He will forgive you some of your faults and grant you a delay to an appointed term; surely the term of Allah when it comes is not postponed; did you but know!',NULL,71,4),
 (16280,2,'"So He may forgive you your sins and give you respite for a stated Term: for when the Term given by Allah is accomplished, it cannot be put forward: if ye only knew."',NULL,71,4),
 (16281,3,'That He may forgive you somewhat of your sins and respite you to an appointed term. Lo! the term of Allah, when it cometh, cannot be delayed, if ye but knew.',NULL,71,4),
 (16282,1,'He said: O my Lord! surely I have called my people by night and by day!',NULL,71,5),
 (16283,2,'He said: "O my Lord! I have called to my People night and day:',NULL,71,5),
 (16284,3,'He said: My Lord! Lo! I have called unto my people night and day',NULL,71,5),
 (16285,1,'But my call has only made them flee the more:',NULL,71,6),
 (16286,2,'"But my call only increases (their) flight (from the Right).',NULL,71,6),
 (16287,3,'But all my calling doth but add to their repugnance;',NULL,71,6),
 (16288,1,'And whenever I have called them that Thou mayest forgive them, they put their fingers in their ears, cover themselves with their garments, and persist and are puffed up with pride:',NULL,71,7),
 (16289,2,'"And every time I have called to them, that Thou mightest forgive them, they have (only) thrust their fingers into their ears, covered themselves up with their garments, grown obstinate, and given themselves up to arrogance.',NULL,71,7),
 (16290,3,'And lo! whenever I call unto them that Thou mayst pardon them they thrust their fingers in their ears and cover themselves with their garments and persist (in their refusal) and magnify themselves in pride.',NULL,71,7),
 (16291,1,'Then surely I called to them aloud:',NULL,71,8),
 (16292,2,'"So I have called to them aloud;',NULL,71,8),
 (16293,3,'And lo! I have called unto them aloud,',NULL,71,8),
 (16294,1,'Then surely I spoke to them in public and I spoke to them in secret:',NULL,71,9),
 (16295,2,'"Further I have spoken to them in public and secretly in private,',NULL,71,9),
 (16296,3,'And lo! I have made public proclamation unto them, and I have appealed to them in private.',NULL,71,9),
 (16297,1,'Then I said, Ask forgiveness of your Lord, surely He is the most Forgiving:',NULL,71,10),
 (16298,2,'"Saying, ''Ask forgiveness from your Lord; for He is Oft-Forgiving;',NULL,71,10),
 (16299,3,'And I have said: Seek pardon of your Lord. Lo! He was ever Forgiving.',NULL,71,10),
 (16300,1,'He will send down upon you the cloud, pouring down abundance of rain:',NULL,71,11),
 (16301,2,'"''He will send rain to you in abundance;',NULL,71,11),
 (16302,3,'He will let loose the sky for you in plenteous rain,',NULL,71,11),
 (16303,1,'And help you with wealth and sons, and make for you gardens, and make for you rivers.',NULL,71,12),
 (16304,2,'"''Give you increase in wealth and sons; and bestow on you gardens and bestow on you rivers (of flowing water).',NULL,71,12),
 (16305,3,'And will help you with wealth and sons, and will assign unto you Gardens and will assign unto you rivers.',NULL,71,12),
 (16306,1,'What is the matter with you that you fear not the greatness of Allah?',NULL,71,13),
 (16307,2,'"''What is the matter with you, that ye place not your hope for kindness and long-suffering in Allah,-',NULL,71,13),
 (16308,3,'What aileth you that ye hope not toward Allah for dignity',NULL,71,13),
 (16309,1,'And indeed He has created you through various grades:',NULL,71,14),
 (16310,2,'"''Seeing that it is He that has created you in diverse stages?',NULL,71,14),
 (16311,3,'When He created you by (divers) stages?',NULL,71,14),
 (16312,1,'Do you not see how Allah has created the seven heavens ,~ one above another,',NULL,71,15),
 (16313,2,'"''See ye not how Allah has created the seven heavens one above another,',NULL,71,15),
 (16314,3,'See ye not how Allah hath created seven heavens in harmony,',NULL,71,15),
 (16315,1,'And made the moon therein a light, and made the sun a lamp?',NULL,71,16),
 (16316,2,'"''And made the moon a light in their midst, and made the sun as a (Glorious) Lamp?',NULL,71,16),
 (16317,3,'And hath made the moon a light therein, and made the sun a lamp?',NULL,71,16),
 (16318,1,'And Allah has made you grow out of the earth as a growth:',NULL,71,17),
 (16319,2,'"''And Allah has produced you from the earth growing (gradually),',NULL,71,17),
 (16320,3,'And Allah hath caused you to grow as a growth from the earth,',NULL,71,17),
 (16321,1,'Then He returns you to it, then will He bring you forth a (new) bringing forth:',NULL,71,18),
 (16322,2,'"''And in the End He will return you into the (earth), and raise you forth (again at the Resurrection)?',NULL,71,18),
 (16323,3,'And afterward He maketh you return thereto, and He will bring you forth again, a (new) forthbringing.',NULL,71,18),
 (16324,1,'And Allah has made for you the earth a wide expanse,',NULL,71,19),
 (16325,2,'"''And Allah has made the earth for you as a carpet (spread out),',NULL,71,19),
 (16326,3,'And Allah hath made the earth a wide expanse for you',NULL,71,19),
 (16327,1,'That you may go along therein in wide paths.',NULL,71,20),
 (16328,2,'"''That ye may go about therein, in spacious roads.''"',NULL,71,20),
 (16329,3,'That ye may thread the valley-ways thereof.',NULL,71,20),
 (16330,1,'Nuh said: My Lord! surely they have disobeyed me and followed him whose wealth and children have added to him nothing but loss.',NULL,71,21),
 (16331,2,'Noah said: "O my Lord! They have disobeyed me, but they follow (men) whose wealth and children give them no increase but only Loss.',NULL,71,21),
 (16332,3,'Noah said: My Lord! Lo! they have disobeyed me and followed one whose wealth and children increase him in naught save ruin;',NULL,71,21),
 (16333,1,'And they have planned a very great plan.',NULL,71,22),
 (16334,2,'"And they have devised a tremendous Plot.',NULL,71,22),
 (16335,3,'And they have plotted a mighty plot,',NULL,71,22),
 (16336,1,'And they say: By no means leave your gods, nor leave Wadd, nor Suwa; nor Yaghus, and Yauq and Nasr.',NULL,71,23),
 (16337,2,'"And they have said (to each other), ''Abandon not your gods: Abandon neither Wadd nor Suwa'', neither Yaguth nor Ya''uq, nor Nasr'';-',NULL,71,23),
 (16338,3,'And they have said: Forsake not your gods. Forsake not Wadd, nor Suwa'', nor Yaghuth and Ya''uq and Nasr.',NULL,71,23),
 (16339,1,'And indeed they have led astray many, and do not increase the unjust in aught but error.',NULL,71,24),
 (16340,2,'"They have already misled many; and grant Thou no increase to the wrong-doers but in straying (from their mark)."',NULL,71,24),
 (16341,3,'And they have led many astray, and Thou increasest the wrong-doers in naught save error.',NULL,71,24),
 (16342,1,'Because of their wrongs they were drowned, then made to enter fire, so they did not find any helpers besides Allah.',NULL,71,25),
 (16343,2,'Because of their sins they were drowned (in the flood), and were made to enter the Fire (of Punishment): and they found- in lieu of Allah- none to help them.',NULL,71,25),
 (16344,3,'Because of their sins they were drowned, then made to enter a Fire. And they found they had no helpers in place of Allah.',NULL,71,25),
 (16345,1,'And Nuh said: My Lord! leave not upon the land any dweller from among the unbelievers:',NULL,71,26),
 (16346,2,'And Noah, said: "O my Lord! Leave not of the Unbelievers, a single one on earth!',NULL,71,26),
 (16347,3,'And Noah said: My Lord! Leave not one of the disbelievers in the land.',NULL,71,26),
 (16348,1,'For surely if Thou leave them they will lead astray Thy servants, and will not beget any but immoral, ungrateful (children)',NULL,71,27),
 (16349,2,'"For, if Thou dost leave (any of) them, they will but mislead Thy devotees, and they will breed none but wicked ungrateful ones.',NULL,71,27),
 (16350,3,'If Thou shouldst leave them, they will mislead Thy slaves and will beget none save lewd ingrates.',NULL,71,27),
 (16351,1,'My Lord! forgive me and my parents and him who enters my house believing, and the believing men and the believing women; and do not increase the unjust in aught but destruction!',NULL,71,28),
 (16352,2,'"O my Lord! Forgive me, my parents, all who enter my house in Faith, and (all) believing men and believing women: and to the wrong-doers grant Thou no increase but in perdition!"',NULL,71,28),
 (16353,3,'My Lord! Forgive me and my parents and him who entereth my house believing, and believing men and believing women, and increase not the wrong-doers in aught save ruin.',NULL,71,28),
 (16354,1,'Say: It has been revealed to me that a party of the jinn listened, and they said: Surely we have heard a wonderful Quran,',NULL,72,1),
 (16355,2,'Say: It has been revealed to me that a company of Jinns listened (to the Qur''an). They said, ''We have really heard a wonderful Recital!',NULL,72,1),
 (16356,3,'Say (O Muhammad): It is revealed unto me that a company of the Jinn gave ear, and they said: Lo! we have heard a marvellous Qur''an,',NULL,72,1),
 (16357,1,'Guiding to the right way, so we believe in it, and we will not set up any one with our Lord:',NULL,72,2),
 (16358,2,'''It gives guidance to the Right, and we have believed therein: we shall not join (in worship) any (gods) with our Lord.',NULL,72,2),
 (16359,3,'Which guideth unto righteousness, so we believe in it and we ascribe no partner unto our Lord.',NULL,72,2),
 (16360,1,'And that He-- exalted be the majesty of our Lord-- has not taken a consort, nor a son:',NULL,72,3),
 (16361,2,'''And Exalted is the Majesty of our Lord: He has taken neither a wife nor a son.',NULL,72,3),
 (16362,3,'And (we believe) that He - exalted be the glory of our Lord! - hath taken neither wife nor son,',NULL,72,3),
 (16363,1,'And that the foolish amongst us used to forge extravagant things against Allah:',NULL,72,4),
 (16364,2,'''There were some foolish ones among us, who used to utter extravagant lies against Allah;',NULL,72,4),
 (16365,3,'And that the foolish one among us used to speak concerning Allah an atrocious lie.',NULL,72,4),
 (16366,1,'And that we thought that men and jinn did not utter a lie against Allah:',NULL,72,5),
 (16367,2,'''But we do think that no man or spirit should say aught that untrue against Allah.',NULL,72,5),
 (16368,3,'And lo! we had supposed that humankind and jinn would not speak a lie concerning Allah -',NULL,72,5),
 (16369,1,'And that persons from among men used to seek refuge with persons from among jinn, so they increased them in wrongdoing:',NULL,72,6),
 (16370,2,'''True, there were persons among mankind who took shelter with persons among the Jinns, but they increased them in folly.',NULL,72,6),
 (16371,3,'And indeed (O Muhammad) individuals of humankind used to invoke the protection of individuals of the jinn, so that they increased them in revolt against Allah);',NULL,72,6),
 (16372,1,'And that they thought as you think, that Allah would not raise anyone:',NULL,72,7),
 (16373,2,'''And they (came to) think as ye thought, that Allah would not raise up any one (to Judgment).',NULL,72,7),
 (16374,3,'And indeed they supposed, even as ye suppose, that Allah would not raise anyone (from the dead) -',NULL,72,7),
 (16375,1,'And that we sought to reach heaven, but we found it filled with strong guards and flaming stars.',NULL,72,8),
 (16376,2,'''And we pried into the secrets of heaven; but we found it filled with stern guards and flaming fires.',NULL,72,8),
 (16377,3,'And (the Jinn who had listened to the Qur''an said): We had sought the heaven but had found it filled with strong warders and meteors.',NULL,72,8),
 (16378,1,'And that we used to sit in some of the sitting-places thereof to steal a hearing, but he who would (try to) listen now would find a flame lying in wait for him:',NULL,72,9),
 (16379,2,'''We used, indeed, to sit there in (hidden) stations, to (steal) a hearing; but any who listen now will find a flaming fire watching him in ambush.',NULL,72,9),
 (16380,3,'And we used to sit on places (high) therein to listen. But he who listeneth now findeth a flame in wait for him;',NULL,72,9),
 (16381,1,'And that we know not whether evil is meant for those who are on earth or whether their Lord means to bring them good:',NULL,72,10),
 (16382,2,'''And we understand not whether ill is intended to those on earth, or whether their Lord (really) intends to guide them to right conduct.',NULL,72,10),
 (16383,3,'And we know not whether harm is boded unto all who are in the earth, or whether their Lord intendeth guidance for them.',NULL,72,10),
 (16384,1,'And that some of us are good and others of us are below that: we are sects following different ways:',NULL,72,11),
 (16385,2,'''There are among us some that are righteous, and some the contrary: we follow divergent paths.',NULL,72,11),
 (16386,3,'And among us there are righteous folk and among us there are far from that. We are sects having different rules.',NULL,72,11),
 (16387,1,'And that we know that we cannot escape Allah in the earth, nor can we escape Him by flight:',NULL,72,12),
 (16388,2,'''But we think that we can by no means frustrate Allah throughout the earth, nor can we frustrate Him by flight.',NULL,72,12),
 (16389,3,'And we know that we cannot escape from Allah in the earth, nor can we escape by flight.',NULL,72,12),
 (16390,1,'And that when we heard the guidance, we believed in it; so whoever believes in his Lord, he should neither fear loss nor being overtaken (by disgrace):',NULL,72,13),
 (16391,2,'''And as for us, since we have listened to the Guidance, we have accepted it: and any who believes in his Lord has no fear, either of a short (account) or of any injustice.',NULL,72,13),
 (16392,3,'And when we heard the guidance, we believed therein, and whoso believeth in his Lord, he feareth neither loss nor oppression.',NULL,72,13),
 (16393,1,'And that some of us are those who submit, and some of us are the deviators; so whoever submits, these aim at the right way:',NULL,72,14),
 (16394,2,'''Amongst us are some that submit their wills (to Allah), and some that swerve from justice. Now those who submit their wills - they have sought out (the path) of right conduct:',NULL,72,14),
 (16395,3,'And there are among us some who have surrendered (to Allah) and there are among us some who are unjust. And whoso hath surrendered to Allah, such have taken the right path purposefully.',NULL,72,14),
 (16396,1,'And as to the deviators, they are fuel of hell:',NULL,72,15),
 (16397,2,'''But those who swerve,- they are (but) fuel for Hell-fire''-',NULL,72,15),
 (16398,3,'And as for those who are unjust, they are firewood for hell.',NULL,72,15),
 (16399,1,'And that if they should keep to the (right) way, We would certainly give them to drink of abundant water,',NULL,72,16),
 (16400,2,'(And Allah''s Message is): "If they (the Pagans) had (only) remained on the (right) Way, We should certainly have bestowed on them Rain in abundance.',NULL,72,16),
 (16401,3,'If they (the idolaters) tread the right path, We shall give them to drink of water in abundance',NULL,72,16),
 (16402,1,'So that We might try them with respect to it; and whoever turns aside from the reminder of his Lord, He will make him enter into an afflicting chastisement:',NULL,72,17),
 (16403,2,'"That We might try them by that (means). But if any turns away from the remembrance of his Lord, He will cause him to undergo a severe Penalty.',NULL,72,17),
 (16404,3,'That We may test them thereby, and whoso turneth away from the remembrance of his Lord; He will thrust him into ever-growing torment.',NULL,72,17),
 (16405,1,'And that the mosques are Allah''s, therefore call not upon any one with Allah:',NULL,72,18),
 (16406,2,'"And the places of worship are for Allah (alone): So invoke not any one along with Allah;',NULL,72,18),
 (16407,3,'And the places of worship are only for Allah, so pray not unto anyone along with Allah.',NULL,72,18),
 (16408,1,'And that when the servant of Allah stood up calling upon Him, they wellnigh crowded him (to death).',NULL,72,19),
 (16409,2,'"Yet when the Devotee of Allah stands forth to invoke Him, they just make round him a dense crowd."',NULL,72,19),
 (16410,3,'And when the slave of Allah stood up in prayer to Him, they crowded on him, almost stifling.',NULL,72,19),
 (16411,1,'Say: I only call upon my Lord, and I do not associate any one with Him.',NULL,72,20),
 (16412,2,'Say: "I do no more than invoke my Lord, and I join not with Him any (false god)."',NULL,72,20),
 (16413,3,'Say (unto them, O Muhammad): I pray unto Allah only, and ascribe unto Him no partner.',NULL,72,20),
 (16414,1,'Say: I do not control for you evil or good.',NULL,72,21),
 (16415,2,'Say: "It is not in my power to cause you harm, or to bring you to right conduct."',NULL,72,21),
 (16416,3,'Say: Lo! I control not hurt nor benefit for you.',NULL,72,21),
 (16417,1,'Say: Surely no one can protect me against Allah, nor can I find besides Him any place of refuge:',NULL,72,22),
 (16418,2,'Say: "No one can deliver me from Allah (If I were to disobey Him), nor should I find refuge except in Him,',NULL,72,22),
 (16419,3,'Say: Lo! none can protect me from Allah, nor can I find any refuge beside Him',NULL,72,22),
 (16420,1,'(It is) only a delivering (of communications) from Allah and His messages; and whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger surely he shall have the fire of hell to abide therein for a long time.',NULL,72,23),
 (16421,2,'"Unless I proclaim what I receive from Allah and His Messages: for any that disobey Allah and His Messenger,- for them is Hell: they shall dwell therein for ever."',NULL,72,23),
 (16422,3,'(Mine is) but conveyance (of the Truth) from Allah, and His messages; and whoso disobeyeth Allah and His messenger, lo! his is fire of hell, wherein such dwell for ever.',NULL,72,23),
 (16423,1,'Until when they see what they are threatened with, then shall they know who is weaker in helpers and fewer in number.',NULL,72,24),
 (16424,2,'At length, when they see (with their own eyes) that which they are promised,- then will they know who it is that is weakest in (his) helper and least important in point of numbers.',NULL,72,24),
 (16425,3,'Till (the day) when they shall behold that which they are promised (they may doubt); but then they will know (for certain) who is weaker in allies and less in multitude.',NULL,72,24),
 (16426,1,'Say: I do not know whether that with which you are threatened be nigh or whether my Lord will appoint for it a term:',NULL,72,25),
 (16427,2,'Say: "I know not whether the (Punishment) which ye are promised is near, or whether my Lord will appoint for it a distant term.',NULL,72,25),
 (16428,3,'Say (O Muhammad, unto the disbelievers): I know not whether that which ye are promised is nigh, or if my Lord hath set a distant term for it.',NULL,72,25),
 (16429,1,'The Knower of the unseen! so He does not reveal His secrets to any,',NULL,72,26),
 (16430,2,'"He (alone) knows the Unseen, nor does He make any one acquainted with His Mysteries,-',NULL,72,26),
 (16431,3,'(He is) the Knower of the Unseen, and He revealeth unto none His secret,',NULL,72,26),
 (16432,1,'Except to him whom He chooses as a messenger; for surely He makes a guard to march before him and after him,',NULL,72,27),
 (16433,2,'"Except a messenger whom He has chosen: and then He makes a band of watchers march before him and behind him,',NULL,72,27),
 (16434,3,'Save unto every messenger whom He hath chosen, and then He maketh a guard to go before him and a guard behind him',NULL,72,27),
 (16435,1,'So that He may know that they have truly delivered the messages of their Lord, and He encompasses what is with them and He records the number of all things.',NULL,72,28),
 (16436,2,'"That He may know that they have (truly) brought and delivered the Messages of their Lord: and He surrounds (all the mysteries) that are with them, and takes account of every single thing."',NULL,72,28),
 (16437,3,'That He may know that they have indeed conveyed the messages of their Lord. He surroundeth all their doings, and He keepeth count of all things.',NULL,72,28),
 (16438,1,'O you who have wrapped up in your garments!',NULL,73,1),
 (16439,2,'O thou folded in garments!',NULL,73,1),
 (16440,3,'O thou wrapped up in thy raiment!',NULL,73,1),
 (16441,1,'Rise to pray in the night except a little,',NULL,73,2),
 (16442,2,'Stand (to prayer) by night, but not all night,-',NULL,73,2),
 (16443,3,'Keep vigil the night long, save a little -',NULL,73,2),
 (16444,1,'Half of it, or lessen it a little,',NULL,73,3),
 (16445,2,'Half of it,- or a little less,',NULL,73,3),
 (16446,3,'A half thereof, or abate a little thereof',NULL,73,3),
 (16447,1,'Or add to it, and recite the Quran as it ought to be recited.',NULL,73,4),
 (16448,2,'Or a little more; and recite the Qur''an in slow, measured rhythmic tones.',NULL,73,4),
 (16449,3,'Or add (a little) thereto - and chant the Qur''an in measure,',NULL,73,4),
 (16450,1,'Surely We will make to light upon you a weighty Word.',NULL,73,5),
 (16451,2,'Soon shall We send down to thee a weighty Message.',NULL,73,5),
 (16452,3,'For we shall charge thee with a word of weight.',NULL,73,5),
 (16453,1,'Surely the rising by night is the firmest way to tread and the best corrective of speech.',NULL,73,6),
 (16454,2,'Truly the rising by night is most potent for governing (the soul), and most suitable for (framing) the Word (of Prayer and Praise).',NULL,73,6),
 (16455,3,'Lo! the vigil of the night is (a time) when impression is more keen and speech more certain.',NULL,73,6),
 (16456,1,'Surely you have in the day time a long occupation.',NULL,73,7),
 (16457,2,'True, there is for thee by day prolonged occupation with ordinary duties:',NULL,73,7),
 (16458,3,'Lo! thou hast by day a chain of business.',NULL,73,7),
 (16459,1,'And remember the name of your Lord and devote yourself to Him with (exclusive) devotion.',NULL,73,8),
 (16460,2,'But keep in remembrance the name of thy Lord and devote thyself to Him whole-heartedly.',NULL,73,8),
 (16461,3,'So remember the name of thy Lord and devote thyself with a complete devotion -',NULL,73,8),
 (16462,1,'The Lord of the East and the West-- there is no god but He-- therefore take Him for a protector.',NULL,73,9),
 (16463,2,'(He is) Lord of the East and the West: there is no god but He: take Him therefore for (thy) Disposer of Affairs.',NULL,73,9),
 (16464,3,'Lord of the East and the West; there is no Allah save Him; so choose thou Him alone for thy defender -',NULL,73,9),
 (16465,1,'And bear patiently what they say and avoid them with a becoming avoidance.',NULL,73,10),
 (16466,2,'And have patience with what they say, and leave them with noble (dignity).',NULL,73,10),
 (16467,3,'And bear with patience what they utter, and part from them with a fair leave-taking.',NULL,73,10),
 (16468,1,'And leave Me and the rejecters, the possessors of ease and plenty, and respite them a little.',NULL,73,11),
 (16469,2,'And leave Me (alone to deal with) those in possession of the good things of life, who (yet) deny the Truth; and bear with them for a little while.',NULL,73,11),
 (16470,3,'Leave Me to deal with the deniers, lords of ease and comfort (in this life); and do thou respite them awhile.',NULL,73,11),
 (16471,1,'Surely with Us are heavy fetters and a flaming fire,',NULL,73,12),
 (16472,2,'With Us are Fetters (to bind them), and a Fire (to burn them),',NULL,73,12),
 (16473,3,'Lo! with Us are heavy fetters and a raging fire,',NULL,73,12),
 (16474,1,'And food that chokes and a painful punishment,',NULL,73,13),
 (16475,2,'And a Food that chokes, and a Penalty Grievous.',NULL,73,13),
 (16476,3,'And food which choketh (the partaker), and a painful doom',NULL,73,13),
 (16477,1,'On the day when the earth and the mountains shall quake and the mountains shall become (as) heaps of sand let loose.',NULL,73,14),
 (16478,2,'One Day the earth and the mountains will be in violent commotion. And the mountains will be as a heap of sand poured out and flowing down.',NULL,73,14),
 (16479,3,'On the day when the earth and the hills rock, and the hills become a heap of running sand.',NULL,73,14),
 (16480,1,'Surely We have sent to you a Messenger, a witness against you, as We sent a messenger to Firon.',NULL,73,15),
 (16481,2,'We have sent to you, (O men!) a messenger, to be a witness concerning you, even as We sent a messenger to Pharaoh.',NULL,73,15),
 (16482,3,'Lo! We have sent unto you a messenger as witness against you, even as We sent unto Pharaoh a messenger.',NULL,73,15),
 (16483,1,'But Firon disobeyed the messenger, so We laid on him a violent hold.',NULL,73,16),
 (16484,2,'But Pharaoh disobeyed the messenger; so We seized him with a heavy Punishment.',NULL,73,16),
 (16485,3,'But Pharaoh rebelled against the messenger, whereupon We seized him with no gentle grip.',NULL,73,16),
 (16486,1,'How, then, will you guard yourselves, if you disbelieve, on the day which shall make children grey-headed?',NULL,73,17),
 (16487,2,'Then how shall ye, if ye deny (Allah), guard yourselves against a Day that will make children hoary-headed?-',NULL,73,17),
 (16488,3,'Then how, if ye disbelieve, will ye protect yourselves upon the day which will turn children grey,',NULL,73,17),
 (16489,1,'The heaven shall rend asunder thereby; His promise is ever brought to fulfillment.',NULL,73,18),
 (16490,2,'Whereon the sky will be cleft asunder? His Promise needs must be accomplished.',NULL,73,18),
 (16491,3,'The very heaven being then rent asunder. His promise is to be fulfilled.',NULL,73,18),
 (16492,1,'Surely this is a reminder, then let him, who will take the way to his Lord.',NULL,73,19),
 (16493,2,'Verily this is an Admonition: therefore, whoso will, let him take a (straight) path to his Lord!',NULL,73,19),
 (16494,3,'Lo! This is a Reminder. Let him who will, then, choose a way unto his Lord.',NULL,73,19),
 (16495,1,'Surely your Lord knows that you pass in prayer nearly two-thirds of the night, and (sometimes) half of it, and (sometimes) a third of it, and (also) a party of those with you; and Allah measures the night and the day. He knows that you are not able to do it, so He has turned to you (mercifully), therefore read what is easy of the Quran. He knows that there must be among you sick, and others who travel in the land seeking of the bounty of Allah, and others who fight in Allah''s way, therefore read as much of it as is easy (to you), and keep up prayer and pay the poor-rate and offer to Allah a goodly gift, and whatever of good you send on beforehand for yourselves, you will find it with Allah; that is best and greatest in reward; and ask forgiveness of Allah; surely Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,73,20),
 (16496,2,'Thy Lord doth know that thou standest forth (to prayer) nigh two-thirds of the night, or half the night, or a third of the night, and so doth a party of those with thee. But Allah doth appoint night and day in due measure He knoweth that ye are unable to keep count thereof. So He hath turned to you (in mercy): read ye, therefore, of the Qur''an as much as may be easy for you. He knoweth that there may be (some) among you in ill-health; others travelling through the land, seeking of Allah''s bounty; yet others fighting in Allah''s Cause, read ye, therefore, as much of the Qur''an as may be easy (for you); and establish regular Prayer and give regular Charity; and loan to Allah a Beautiful Loan. And whatever good ye send forth for your souls ye shall find it in Allah''s Presence,- yea, better and greater, in Reward and seek ye the Grace of Allah: for Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful.',NULL,73,20),
 (16497,3,'Lo! thy Lord knoweth how thou keepest vigil sometimes nearly two-thirds of the night, or (sometimes) half or a third thereof, as do a party of those with thee. Allah measureth the night and the day. He knoweth that ye count it not, and turneth unto you in mercy. Recite, then, of the Qur''an that which is easy for you. He knoweth that there are sick folk among you, while others travel in the land in search of Allah''s bounty, and others (still) are fighting for the cause of Allah. So recite of it that which is easy (for you), and establish worship and pay the poor-due, and (so) lend unto Allah a goodly loan. Whatsoever good ye send before you for your souls, ye will find it with Allah, better and greater in the recompense. And seek forgiveness of Allah. Lo! Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.',NULL,73,20),
 (16498,1,'O you who are clothed!',NULL,74,1),
 (16499,2,'O thou wrapped up (in the mantle)!',NULL,74,1),
 (16500,3,'O thou enveloped in thy cloak,',NULL,74,1),
