 (16759,1,'But called the truth a lie and turned back,',NULL,75,32),
 (16760,2,'But on the contrary, he rejected Truth and turned away!',NULL,75,32),
 (16761,3,'But he denied and flouted.',NULL,75,32),
 (16762,1,'Then he went to his followers, walking away in haughtiness.',NULL,75,33),
 (16763,2,'Then did he stalk to his family in full conceit!',NULL,75,33),
 (16764,3,'Then went he to his folk with glee.',NULL,75,33),
 (16765,1,'Nearer to you (is destruction) and nearer,',NULL,75,34),
 (16766,2,'Woe to thee, (O men!), yea, woe!',NULL,75,34),
 (16767,3,'Nearer unto thee and nearer,',NULL,75,34),
 (16768,1,'Again (consider how) nearer to you and nearer.',NULL,75,35),
 (16769,2,'Again, Woe to thee, (O men!), yea, woe!',NULL,75,35),
 (16770,3,'Again nearer unto thee and nearer (is the doom).',NULL,75,35),
 (16771,1,'Does man think that he is to be left to wander without an aim?',NULL,75,36),
 (16772,2,'Does man think that he will be left uncontrolled, (without purpose)?',NULL,75,36),
 (16773,3,'Thinketh man that he is to be left aimless?',NULL,75,36),
 (16774,1,'Was he not a small seed in the seminal elements,',NULL,75,37),
 (16775,2,'Was he not a drop of sperm emitted (in lowly form)?',NULL,75,37),
 (16776,3,'Was he not a drop of fluid which gushed forth?',NULL,75,37),
 (16777,1,'Then he was a clot of blood, so He created (him) then made (him) perfect.',NULL,75,38),
 (16778,2,'Then did he become a leech-like clot; then did (Allah) make and fashion (him) in due proportion.',NULL,75,38),
 (16779,3,'Then he became a clot; then (Allah) shaped and fashioned',NULL,75,38),
 (16780,1,'Then He made of him two kinds, the male and the female.',NULL,75,39),
 (16781,2,'And of him He made two sexes, male and female.',NULL,75,39),
 (16782,3,'And made of him a pair, the male and female.',NULL,75,39),
 (16783,1,'Is not He able to give life to the dead?',NULL,75,40),
 (16784,2,'Has not He, (the same), the power to give life to the dead?',NULL,75,40),
 (16785,3,'Is not He (Who doeth so) Able to bring the dead to life?',NULL,75,40),
 (16786,1,'There surely came over man a period of time when he was a thing not worth mentioning.',NULL,76,1),
 (16787,2,'Has there not been over Man a long period of Time, when he was nothing - (not even) mentioned?',NULL,76,1),
 (16788,3,'Hath there come upon man (ever) any period of time in which he was a thing unremembered?',NULL,76,1),
 (16789,1,'Surely We have created man from a small life-germ uniting (itself): We mean to try him, so We have made him hearing, seeing.',NULL,76,2),
 (16790,2,'Verily We created Man from a drop of mingled sperm, in order to try him: So We gave him (the gifts), of Hearing and Sight.',NULL,76,2),
 (16791,3,'Lo! We create man from a drop of thickened fluid to test him; so We make him hearing, knowing.',NULL,76,2),
 (16792,1,'Surely We have shown him the way: he may be thankful or unthankful.',NULL,76,3),
 (16793,2,'We showed him the Way: whether he be grateful or ungrateful (rests on his will).',NULL,76,3),
 (16794,3,'Lo! We have shown him the way, whether he be grateful or disbelieving.',NULL,76,3),
 (16795,1,'Surely We have prepared for the unbelievers chains and shackles and a burning fire.',NULL,76,4),
 (16796,2,'For the Rejecters we have prepared chains, yokes, and a blazing Fire.',NULL,76,4),
 (16797,3,'Lo! We have prepared for disbelievers manacles and carcans and a raging fire.',NULL,76,4),
 (16798,1,'Surely the righteous shall drink of a cup the admixture of which is camphor',NULL,76,5),
 (16799,2,'As to the Righteous, they shall drink of a Cup (of Wine) mixed with Kafur,-',NULL,76,5),
 (16800,3,'Lo! the righteous shall drink of a cup whereof the mixture is of Kafur,',NULL,76,5),
 (16801,1,'A fountain from which the servants of Allah shall drink; they make it to flow a (goodly) flowing forth.',NULL,76,6),
 (16802,2,'A Fountain where the Devotees of Allah do drink, making it flow in unstinted abundance.',NULL,76,6),
 (16803,3,'A spring wherefrom the slaves of Allah drink, making it gush forth abundantly,',NULL,76,6),
 (16804,1,'They fulfill vows and fear a day the evil of which shall be spreading far and wide.',NULL,76,7),
 (16805,2,'They perform (their) vows, and they fear a Day whose evil flies far and wide.',NULL,76,7),
 (16806,3,'(Because) they perform the vow and fear a day whereof the evil is wide-spreading,',NULL,76,7),
 (16807,1,'And they give food out of love for Him to the poor and the orphan and the captive:',NULL,76,8),
 (16808,2,'And they feed, for the love of Allah, the indigent, the orphan, and the captive,-',NULL,76,8),
 (16809,3,'And feed with food the needy wretch, the orphan and the prisoner, for love of Him,',NULL,76,8),
 (16810,1,'We only feed you for Allah''s sake; we desire from you neither reward nor thanks:',NULL,76,9),
 (16811,2,'(Saying),"We feed you for the sake of Allah alone: no reward do we desire from you, nor thanks.',NULL,76,9),
 (16812,3,'(Saying): We feed you, for the sake of Allah only. We wish for no reward nor thanks from you;',NULL,76,9),
 (16813,1,'Surely we fear from our Lord a stern, distressful day.',NULL,76,10),
 (16814,2,'"We only fear a Day of distressful Wrath from the side of our Lord."',NULL,76,10),
 (16815,3,'Lo! we fear from our Lord a day of frowning and of fate.',NULL,76,10),
 (16816,1,'Therefore Allah win guard them from the evil of that day and cause them to meet with ease and happiness;',NULL,76,11),
 (16817,2,'But Allah will deliver them from the evil of that Day, and will shed over them a Light of Beauty and (blissful) Joy.',NULL,76,11),
 (16818,3,'Therefor Allah hath warded off from them the evil of that day, and hath made them find brightness and joy;',NULL,76,11),
 (16819,1,'And reward them, because they were patient, with garden and silk,',NULL,76,12),
 (16820,2,'And because they were patient and constant, He will reward them with a Garden and (garments of) silk.',NULL,76,12),
 (16821,3,'And hath awarded them for all that they endured, a Garden and silk attire;',NULL,76,12),
 (16822,1,'Reclining therein on raised couches, they shall find therein neither (the severe heat of) the sun nor intense cold.',NULL,76,13),
 (16823,2,'Reclining in the (Garden) on raised thrones, they will see there neither the sun''s (excessive heat) nor (the moon''s) excessive cold.',NULL,76,13),
 (16824,3,'Reclining therein upon couches, they will find there neither (heat of) a sun nor bitter cold.',NULL,76,13),
 (16825,1,'And close down upon them (shall be) its shadows, and its fruits shall be made near (to them), being easy to reach.',NULL,76,14),
 (16826,2,'And the shades of the (Garden) will come low over them, and the bunches (of fruit), there, will hang low in humility.',NULL,76,14),
 (16827,3,'The shade thereof is close upon them and the clustered fruits thereof bow down.',NULL,76,14),
 (16828,1,'And there shall be made to go round about them vessels of silver and goblets which are of glass,',NULL,76,15),
 (16829,2,'And amongst them will be passed round vessels of silver and goblets of crystal,-',NULL,76,15),
 (16830,3,'Goblets of silver are brought round for them, and beakers (as) of glass',NULL,76,15),
 (16831,1,'(Transparent as) glass, made of silver; they have measured them according to a measure.',NULL,76,16),
 (16832,2,'Crystal-clear, made of silver: they will determine the measure thereof (according to their wishes).',NULL,76,16),
 (16833,3,'(Bright as) glass but (made) of silver, which they (themselves) have measured to the measure (of their deeds).',NULL,76,16),
 (16834,1,'And they shall be made to drink therein a cup the admixture of which shall be ginger,',NULL,76,17),
 (16835,2,'And they will be given to drink there of a Cup (of Wine) mixed with Zanjabil,-',NULL,76,17),
 (16836,3,'There are they watered with a cup whereof the mixture is of Zanjabil,',NULL,76,17),
 (16837,1,'(Of) a fountain therein which is named Salsabil.',NULL,76,18),
 (16838,2,'A fountain there, called Salsabil.',NULL,76,18),
 (16839,3,'(The water of) a spring therein, named Salsabil.',NULL,76,18),
 (16840,1,'And round about them shall go youths never altering in age; when you see them you will think them to be scattered pearls.',NULL,76,19),
 (16841,2,'And round about them will (serve) youths of perpetual (freshness): If thou seest them, thou wouldst think them scattered Pearls.',NULL,76,19),
 (16842,3,'There wait on them immortal youths, whom, when thou seest, thou wouldst take for scattered pearls.',NULL,76,19),
 (16843,1,'And when you see there, you shall see blessings and a great kingdom.',NULL,76,20),
 (16844,2,'And when thou lookest, it is there thou wilt see a Bliss and a Realm Magnificent.',NULL,76,20),
 (16845,3,'When thou seest, thou wilt see there bliss and high estate.',NULL,76,20),
 (16846,1,'Upon them shall be garments of fine green silk and thick silk interwoven with gold, and they shall be adorned with bracelets of silver, and their Lord shall make them drink a pure drink.',NULL,76,21),
 (16847,2,'Upon them will be green Garments of fine silk and heavy brocade, and they will be adorned with Bracelets of silver; and their Lord will give to them to drink of a Wine Pure and Holy.',NULL,76,21),
 (16848,3,'Their raiment will be fine green silk and gold embroidery. Bracelets of silver will they wear. Their Lord will slake their thirst with a pure drink.',NULL,76,21),
 (16849,1,'Surely this is a reward for you, and your striving shall be recompensed.',NULL,76,22),
 (16850,2,'"Verily this is a Reward for you, and your Endeavour is accepted and recognised."',NULL,76,22),
 (16851,3,'(And it will be said unto them): Lo! this is a reward for you. Your endeavour (upon earth) hath found acceptance.',NULL,76,22),
 (16852,1,'Surely We Ourselves have revealed the Quran to you revealing (it) in portions.',NULL,76,23),
 (16853,2,'It is We Who have sent down the Qur''an to thee by stages.',NULL,76,23),
 (16854,3,'Lo! We, even We, have revealed unto thee the Qur''an, a revelation;',NULL,76,23),
 (16855,1,'Therefore wait patiently for the command of your Lord, and obey not from among them a sinner or an ungrateful one.',NULL,76,24),
 (16856,2,'Therefore be patient with constancy to the Command of thy Lord, and hearken not to the sinner or the ingrate among them.',NULL,76,24),
 (16857,3,'So submit patiently to thy Lord''s command, and obey not of them any guilty one or disbeliever.',NULL,76,24),
 (16858,1,'And glorify the name of your Lord morning and evening.',NULL,76,25),
 (16859,2,'And celebrate the name or thy Lord morning and evening,',NULL,76,25),
 (16860,3,'Remember the name of thy Lord at morn and evening.',NULL,76,25),
 (16861,1,'And during part of the night adore Him, and give glory to Him (a) long (part of the) night.',NULL,76,26),
 (16862,2,'And part of the night, prostrate thyself to Him; and glorify Him a long night through.',NULL,76,26),
 (16863,3,'And worship Him (a portion) of the night. And glorify Him through the livelong night.',NULL,76,26),
 (16864,1,'Surely these love the transitory and neglect a grievous day before them.',NULL,76,27),
 (16865,2,'As to these, they love the fleeting life, and put away behind them a Day (that will be) hard.',NULL,76,27),
 (16866,3,'Lo! these love fleeting life, and put behind them (the remembrance of) a grievous day.',NULL,76,27),
 (16867,1,'We created them and made firm their make, and when We please We will bring in their place the likes of them by a change.',NULL,76,28),
 (16868,2,'It is We Who created them, and We have made their joints strong; but, when We will, We can substitute the like of them by a complete change.',NULL,76,28),
 (16869,3,'We, even We, created them, and strengthened their frame. And when We will, We can replace them, bringing others like them in their stead.',NULL,76,28),
 (16870,1,'Surely this is a reminder, so whoever pleases takes to his Lord a way.',NULL,76,29),
 (16871,2,'This is an admonition: Whosoever will, let him take a (straight) Path to his Lord.',NULL,76,29),
 (16872,3,'Lo! this is an Admonishment, that whosoever will may choose a way unto his Lord.',NULL,76,29),
 (16873,1,'And you do not please except that Allah please, surely Allah is Knowing, Wise;',NULL,76,30),
 (16874,2,'But ye will not, except as Allah wills; for Allah is full of Knowledge and Wisdom.',NULL,76,30),
 (16875,3,'Yet ye will not, unless Allah willeth. Lo! Allah is Knower, Wise.',NULL,76,30),
 (16876,1,'He makes whom He pleases to enter into His mercy; and (as for) the unjust, He has prepared for them a painful chastisement.',NULL,76,31),
 (16877,2,'He will admit to His Mercy whom He will; But the wrong-doers,- for them has He prepared a grievous Penalty.',NULL,76,31),
 (16878,3,'He maketh whom He will to enter His mercy, and for evil-doers hath prepared a painful doom.',NULL,76,31),
 (16879,1,'I swear by the emissary winds, sent one after another (for men''s benefit),',NULL,77,1),
 (16880,2,'By the (Winds) sent forth one after another (to man''s profit);',NULL,77,1),
 (16881,3,'By the emissary winds, (sent) one after another',NULL,77,1),
 (16882,1,'By the raging hurricanes,',NULL,77,2),
 (16883,2,'Which then blow violently in tempestuous Gusts,',NULL,77,2),
 (16884,3,'By the raging hurricanes,',NULL,77,2),
 (16885,1,'Which scatter clouds to their destined places,',NULL,77,3),
 (16886,2,'And scatter (things) far and wide;',NULL,77,3),
 (16887,3,'By those which cause earth''s vegetation to revive;',NULL,77,3),
 (16888,1,'Then separate them one from another,',NULL,77,4),
 (16889,2,'Then separate them, one from another,',NULL,77,4),
 (16890,3,'By those who winnow with a winnowing,',NULL,77,4),
 (16891,1,'Then I swear by the angels who bring down the revelation,',NULL,77,5),
 (16892,2,'Then spread abroad a Message,',NULL,77,5),
 (16893,3,'By those who bring down the Reminder,',NULL,77,5),
 (16894,1,'To clear or to warn.',NULL,77,6),
 (16895,2,'Whether of Justification or of Warning;-',NULL,77,6),
 (16896,3,'To excuse or to warn,',NULL,77,6),
 (16897,1,'Most surely what you are threatened with must come to pass.',NULL,77,7),
 (16898,2,'Assuredly, what ye are promised must come to pass.',NULL,77,7),
 (16899,3,'Surely that which ye are promised will befall.',NULL,77,7),
 (16900,1,'So when the stars are made to lose their light,',NULL,77,8),
 (16901,2,'Then when the stars become dim;',NULL,77,8),
 (16902,3,'So when the stars are put out,',NULL,77,8),
 (16903,1,'And when the heaven is rent asunder,',NULL,77,9),
 (16904,2,'When the heaven is cleft asunder;',NULL,77,9),
 (16905,3,'And when the sky is riven asunder,',NULL,77,9),
 (16906,1,'And when the mountains are carried away as dust,',NULL,77,10),
 (16907,2,'When the mountains are scattered (to the winds) as dust;',NULL,77,10),
 (16908,3,'And when the mountains are blown away,',NULL,77,10),
 (16909,1,'And when the messengers are gathered at their appointed time',NULL,77,11),
 (16910,2,'And when the messengers are (all) appointed a time (to collect);-',NULL,77,11),
 (16911,3,'And when the messengers are brought unto their time appointed -',NULL,77,11),
 (16912,1,'To what day is the doom fixed?',NULL,77,12),
 (16913,2,'For what Day are these (portents) deferred?',NULL,77,12),
 (16914,3,'For what day is the time appointed?',NULL,77,12),
 (16915,1,'To the day of decision.',NULL,77,13),
 (16916,2,'For the Day of Sorting out.',NULL,77,13),
 (16917,3,'For the Day of Decision.',NULL,77,13),
 (16918,1,'And what will make you comprehend what the day of decision is?',NULL,77,14),
 (16919,2,'And what will explain to thee what is the Day of Sorting out?',NULL,77,14),
 (16920,3,'And what will convey unto thee what the Day of Decision is! -',NULL,77,14),
 (16921,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,15),
 (16922,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,15),
 (16923,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,15),
 (16924,1,'Did We not destroy the former generations?',NULL,77,16),
 (16925,2,'Did We not destroy the men of old (for their evil)?',NULL,77,16),
 (16926,3,'Destroyed We not the former folk,',NULL,77,16),
 (16927,1,'Then did We follow them up with later ones.',NULL,77,17),
 (16928,2,'So shall We make later (generations) follow them.',NULL,77,17),
 (16929,3,'Then caused the latter folk to follow after?',NULL,77,17),
 (16930,1,'Even thus shall We deal with the guilty.',NULL,77,18),
 (16931,2,'Thus do We deal with men of sin.',NULL,77,18),
 (16932,3,'Thus deal We ever with the guilty.',NULL,77,18),
 (16933,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,19),
 (16934,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,19),
 (16935,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,19),
 (16936,1,'Did We not create you from contemptible water?',NULL,77,20),
 (16937,2,'Have We not created you from a fluid (held) despicable?-',NULL,77,20),
 (16938,3,'Did We not create you from a base fluid',NULL,77,20),
 (16939,1,'Then We placed it in a secure resting-place,',NULL,77,21),
 (16940,2,'The which We placed in a place of rest, firmly fixed,',NULL,77,21),
 (16941,3,'Which We laid up in a safe abode',NULL,77,21),
 (16942,1,'Till an appointed term,',NULL,77,22),
 (16943,2,'For a period (of gestation), determined (according to need)?',NULL,77,22),
 (16944,3,'For a known term?',NULL,77,22),
 (16945,1,'So We proportion it-- how well are We at proportioning (things).',NULL,77,23),
 (16946,2,'For We do determine (according to need); for We are the best to determine (things).',NULL,77,23),
 (16947,3,'Thus We arranged. How excellent is Our arranging!',NULL,77,23),
 (16948,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,24),
 (16949,2,'Ah woe, that Day! to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,24),
 (16950,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,24),
 (16951,1,'Have We not made the earth to draw together to itself,',NULL,77,25),
 (16952,2,'Have We not made the earth (as a place) to draw together.',NULL,77,25),
 (16953,3,'Have We not made the earth a receptacle',NULL,77,25),
 (16954,1,'The living and the dead,',NULL,77,26),
 (16955,2,'The living and the dead,',NULL,77,26),
 (16956,3,'Both for the living and the dead,',NULL,77,26),
 (16957,1,'And made therein lofty mountains, and given you to drink of sweet water?',NULL,77,27),
 (16958,2,'And made therein mountains standing firm, lofty (in stature); and provided for you water sweet (and wholesome)?',NULL,77,27),
 (16959,3,'And placed therein high mountains and given you to drink sweet water therein?',NULL,77,27),
 (16960,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,28),
 (16961,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,28),
 (16962,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,28),
 (16963,1,'Walk on to that which you called a lie.',NULL,77,29),
 (16964,2,'(It will be said:) "Depart ye to that which ye used to reject as false!',NULL,77,29),
 (16965,3,'(It will be said unto them:) Depart unto that (doom) which ye used to deny;',NULL,77,29),
 (16966,1,'Walk on to the covering having three branches,',NULL,77,30),
 (16967,2,'"Depart ye to a Shadow (of smoke ascending) in three columns,',NULL,77,30),
 (16968,3,'Depart unto the shadow falling threefold,',NULL,77,30),
 (16969,1,'Neither having the coolness of the shade nor availing against the flame.',NULL,77,31),
 (16970,2,'"(Which yields) no shade of coolness, and is of no use against the fierce Blaze.',NULL,77,31),
 (16971,3,'(Which yet is) no relief nor shelter from the flame.',NULL,77,31),
 (16972,1,'Surely it sends up sparks like palaces,',NULL,77,32),
 (16973,2,'"Indeed it throws about sparks (huge) as Forts,',NULL,77,32),
 (16974,3,'Lo! it throweth up sparks like the castles,',NULL,77,32),
 (16975,1,'As if they were tawny camels.',NULL,77,33),
 (16976,2,'"As if there were (a string of) yellow camels (marching swiftly)."',NULL,77,33),
 (16977,3,'(Or) as it might be camels of bright yellow hue.',NULL,77,33),
 (16978,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,34),
 (16979,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,34),
 (16980,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,34),
 (16981,1,'This is the day on which they shall not speak,',NULL,77,35),
 (16982,2,'That will be a Day when they shall not be able to speak.',NULL,77,35),
 (16983,3,'This is a day wherein they speak not,',NULL,77,35),
 (16984,1,'And permission shall not be given to them so that they should offer excuses.',NULL,77,36),
 (16985,2,'Nor will it be open to them to put forth pleas.',NULL,77,36),
 (16986,3,'Nor are they suffered to put forth excuses.',NULL,77,36),
 (16987,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,37),
 (16988,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,37),
 (16989,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,37),
 (16990,1,'This is the day of decision: We have gathered you and those of yore.',NULL,77,38),
 (16991,2,'That will be a Day of Sorting out! We shall gather you together and those before (you)!',NULL,77,38),
 (16992,3,'This is the Day of Decision, We have brought you and the men of old together.',NULL,77,38),
 (16993,1,'So if you have a plan, plan against Me (now).',NULL,77,39),
 (16994,2,'Now, if ye have a trick (or plot), use it against Me!',NULL,77,39),
 (16995,3,'If now ye have any wit, outwit Me.',NULL,77,39),
 (16996,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,40),
 (16997,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,40),
 (16998,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,40),
 (16999,1,'Surely those who guard (against evil) shall be amid shades and fountains,',NULL,77,41),
 (17000,2,'As to the Righteous, they shall be amidst (cool) shades and springs (of water).',NULL,77,41),
 (17001,3,'Lo! those who kept their duty are amid shade and fountains,',NULL,77,41),
 (17002,1,'And fruits such as they desire.',NULL,77,42),
 (17003,2,'And (they shall have) fruits,- all they desire.',NULL,77,42),
 (17004,3,'And fruits such as they desire.',NULL,77,42),
 (17005,1,'Eat and drink pleasantly because of what you did.',NULL,77,43),
 (17006,2,'"Eat ye and drink ye to your heart''s content: for that ye worked (Righteousness).',NULL,77,43),
 (17007,3,'(Unto them it is said:) Eat, drink and welcome, O ye blessed, in return for what ye did.',NULL,77,43),
 (17008,1,'Surely thus do We reward the doers of good.',NULL,77,44),
 (17009,2,'Thus do We certainly reward the Doers of Good.',NULL,77,44),
 (17010,3,'Thus do We reward the good.',NULL,77,44),
 (17011,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,45),
 (17012,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,45),
 (17013,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,45),
 (17014,1,'Eat and enjoy yourselves for a little; surely you are guilty.',NULL,77,46),
 (17015,2,'(O ye unjust!) Eat ye and enjoy yourselves (but) a little while, for that ye are Sinners.',NULL,77,46),
 (17016,3,'Eat and take your ease (on earth) a little. Lo! ye are guilty.',NULL,77,46),
 (17017,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,47),
 (17018,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,47),
 (17019,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,47),
 (17020,1,'And where it is said to them: Bow down, they do not bow down.',NULL,77,48),
 (17021,2,'And when it is said to them, "Prostrate yourselves!" they do not so.',NULL,77,48),
 (17022,3,'When it is said unto them: Bow down, they bow not down!',NULL,77,48),
 (17023,1,'Woe on that day to the rejecters.',NULL,77,49),
 (17024,2,'Ah woe, that Day, to the Rejecters of Truth!',NULL,77,49),
 (17025,3,'Woe unto the repudiators on that day!',NULL,77,49),
 (17026,1,'In what announcement, then, after it, will they believe?',NULL,77,50),
