 (18539,2,'Then, shall ye be questioned that Day about the joy (ye indulged in!).',NULL,102,8),
 (18540,3,'Then, on that day, ye will be asked concerning pleasure.',NULL,102,8),
 (18541,1,'I swear by the time,',NULL,103,1),
 (18542,2,'By (the Token of) Time (through the ages),',NULL,103,1),
 (18543,3,'By the declining day,',NULL,103,1),
 (18544,1,'Most surely man is in loss,',NULL,103,2),
 (18545,2,'Verily Man is in loss,',NULL,103,2),
 (18546,3,'Lo! man is a state of loss,',NULL,103,2),
 (18547,1,'Except those who believe and do good, and enjoin on each other truth, and enjoin on each other patience.',NULL,103,3),
 (18548,2,'Except such as have Faith, and do righteous deeds, and (join together) in the mutual teaching of Truth, and of Patience and Constancy.',NULL,103,3),
 (18549,3,'Save those who believe and do good works, and exhort one another to truth and exhort one another to endurance.',NULL,103,3),
 (18550,1,'Woe to every slanderer, defamer,',NULL,104,1),
 (18551,2,'Woe to every (kind of) scandal-monger and-backbiter,',NULL,104,1),
 (18552,3,'Woe unto every slandering traducer,',NULL,104,1),
 (18553,1,'Who amasses wealth and considers it a provision (against mishap);',NULL,104,2),
 (18554,2,'Who pileth up wealth and layeth it by,',NULL,104,2),
 (18555,3,'Who hath gathered wealth (of this world) and arranged it.',NULL,104,2),
 (18556,1,'He thinks that his wealth will make him immortal.',NULL,104,3),
 (18557,2,'Thinking that his wealth would make him last for ever!',NULL,104,3),
 (18558,3,'He thinketh that his wealth will render him immortal.',NULL,104,3),
 (18559,1,'Nay! he shall most certainly be hurled into the crushing disaster,',NULL,104,4),
 (18560,2,'By no means! He will be sure to be thrown into That which Breaks to Pieces,',NULL,104,4),
 (18561,3,'Nay, but verily he will be flung to the Consuming One.',NULL,104,4),
 (18562,1,'And what will make you realize what the crushing disaster is?',NULL,104,5),
 (18563,2,'And what will explain to thee That which Breaks to Pieces?',NULL,104,5),
 (18564,3,'Ah, what will convey unto thee what the Consuming One is!',NULL,104,5),
 (18565,1,'It is the fire kindled by Allah,',NULL,104,6),
 (18566,2,'(It is) the Fire of (the Wrath of) Allah kindled (to a blaze),',NULL,104,6),
 (18567,3,'(It is) the fire of Allah, kindled,',NULL,104,6),
 (18568,1,'Which rises above the hearts.',NULL,104,7),
 (18569,2,'The which doth mount (Right) to the Hearts:',NULL,104,7),
 (18570,3,'Which leapeth up over the hearts (of men).',NULL,104,7),
 (18571,1,'Surely it shall be closed over upon them,',NULL,104,8),
 (18572,2,'It shall be made into a vault over them,',NULL,104,8),
 (18573,3,'Lo! it is closed in on them',NULL,104,8),
 (18574,1,'In extended columns.',NULL,104,9),
 (18575,2,'In columns outstretched.',NULL,104,9),
 (18576,3,'In outstretched columns.',NULL,104,9),
 (18577,1,'Have you not considered how your Lord dealt with the possessors of the elephant?',NULL,105,1),
 (18578,2,'Seest thou not how thy Lord dealt with the Companions of the Elephant?',NULL,105,1),
 (18579,3,'Hast thou not seen how thy Lord dealt with the owners of the Elephant?',NULL,105,1),
 (18580,1,'Did He not cause their war to end in confusion,',NULL,105,2),
 (18581,2,'Did He not make their treacherous plan go astray?',NULL,105,2),
 (18582,3,'Did He not bring their stratagem to naught,',NULL,105,2),
 (18583,1,'And send down (to prey) upon them birds in flocks,',NULL,105,3),
 (18584,2,'And He sent against them Flights of Birds,',NULL,105,3),
 (18585,3,'And send against them swarms of flying creatures,',NULL,105,3),
 (18586,1,'Casting against them stones of baked clay,',NULL,105,4),
 (18587,2,'Striking them with stones of baked clay.',NULL,105,4),
 (18588,3,'Which pelted them with stones of baked clay,',NULL,105,4),
 (18589,1,'So He rendered them like straw eaten up?',NULL,105,5),
 (18590,2,'Then did He make them like an empty field of stalks and straw, (of which the corn) has been eaten up.',NULL,105,5),
 (18591,3,'And made them like green crops devoured (by cattle)?',NULL,105,5),
 (18592,1,'For the protection of the Qureaish--',NULL,106,1),
 (18593,2,'For the covenants (of security and safeguard enjoyed) by the Quraish,',NULL,106,1),
 (18594,3,'For the taming of Qureysh.',NULL,106,1),
 (18595,1,'Their protection during their trading caravans in the winter and the summer--',NULL,106,2),
 (18596,2,'Their covenants (covering) journeys by winter and summer,-',NULL,106,2),
 (18597,3,'For their taming (We cause) the caravans to set forth in winter and summer.',NULL,106,2),
 (18598,1,'So let them serve the Lord of this House',NULL,106,3),
 (18599,2,'Let them adore the Lord of this House,',NULL,106,3),
 (18600,3,'So let them worship the Lord of this House,',NULL,106,3),
 (18601,1,'Who feeds them against hunger and gives them security against fear.',NULL,106,4),
 (18602,2,'Who provides them with food against hunger, and with security against fear (of danger).',NULL,106,4),
 (18603,3,'Who hath fed them against hunger and hath made them safe from fear.',NULL,106,4),
 (18604,1,'Have you considered him who calls the judgment a lie?',NULL,107,1),
 (18605,2,'Seest thou one who denies the Judgment (to come)?',NULL,107,1),
 (18606,3,'Hast thou observed him who belieth religion?',NULL,107,1),
 (18607,1,'That is the one who treats the orphan with harshness,',NULL,107,2),
 (18608,2,'Then such is the (man) who repulses the orphan (with harshness),',NULL,107,2),
 (18609,3,'That is he who repelleth the orphan,',NULL,107,2),
 (18610,1,'And does not urge (others) to feed the poor.',NULL,107,3),
 (18611,2,'And encourages not the feeding of the indigent.',NULL,107,3),
 (18612,3,'And urgeth not the feeding of the needy.',NULL,107,3),
 (18613,1,'So woe to the praying ones,',NULL,107,4),
 (18614,2,'So woe to the worshippers',NULL,107,4),
 (18615,3,'Ah, woe unto worshippers',NULL,107,4),
 (18616,1,'Who are unmindful of their prayers,',NULL,107,5),
 (18617,2,'Who are neglectful of their prayers,',NULL,107,5),
 (18618,3,'Who are heedless of their prayer;',NULL,107,5),
 (18619,1,'Who do (good) to be seen,',NULL,107,6),
 (18620,2,'Those who (want but) to be seen (of men),',NULL,107,6),
 (18621,3,'Who would be seen (at worship)',NULL,107,6),
 (18622,1,'And withhold the necessaries of life.',NULL,107,7),
 (18623,2,'But refuse (to supply) (even) neighbourly needs.',NULL,107,7),
 (18624,3,'Yet refuse small kindnesses!',NULL,107,7),
 (18625,1,'Surely We have given you Kausar,',NULL,108,1),
 (18626,2,'To thee have We granted the Fount (of Abundance).',NULL,108,1),
 (18627,3,'Lo! We have given thee Abundance;',NULL,108,1),
 (18628,1,'Therefore pray to your Lord and make a sacrifice.',NULL,108,2),
 (18629,2,'Therefore to thy Lord turn in Prayer and Sacrifice.',NULL,108,2),
 (18630,3,'So pray unto thy Lord, and sacrifice.',NULL,108,2),
 (18631,1,'Surely your enemy is the one who shall be without posterity,',NULL,108,3),
 (18632,2,'For he who hateth thee, he will be cut off (from Future Hope).',NULL,108,3),
 (18633,3,'Lo! it is thy insulter (and not thou) who is without posterity.',NULL,108,3),
 (18634,1,'Say: O unbelievers!',NULL,109,1),
 (18635,2,'Say : O ye that reject Faith!',NULL,109,1),
 (18636,3,'Say: O disbelievers!',NULL,109,1),
 (18637,1,'I do not serve that which you serve,',NULL,109,2),
 (18638,2,'I worship not that which ye worship,',NULL,109,2),
 (18639,3,'I worship not that which ye worship;',NULL,109,2),
 (18640,1,'Nor do you serve Him Whom I serve:',NULL,109,3),
 (18641,2,'Nor will ye worship that which I worship.',NULL,109,3),
 (18642,3,'Nor worship ye that which I worship.',NULL,109,3),
 (18643,1,'Nor am I going to serve that which you serve,',NULL,109,4),
 (18644,2,'And I will not worship that which ye have been wont to worship,',NULL,109,4),
 (18645,3,'And I shall not worship that which ye worship.',NULL,109,4),
 (18646,1,'Nor are you going to serve Him Whom I serve:',NULL,109,5),
 (18647,2,'Nor will ye worship that which I worship.',NULL,109,5),
 (18648,3,'Nor will ye worship that which I worship.',NULL,109,5),
 (18649,1,'You shall have your religion and I shall have my religion.',NULL,109,6),
 (18650,2,'To you be your Way, and to me mine.',NULL,109,6),
 (18651,3,'Unto you your religion, and unto me my religion.',NULL,109,6),
 (18652,1,'When there comes the help of Allah and the victory,',NULL,110,1),
 (18653,2,'When comes the Help of Allah, and Victory,',NULL,110,1),
 (18654,3,'When Allah''s succour and the triumph cometh',NULL,110,1),
 (18655,1,'And you see men entering the religion of Allah in companies,',NULL,110,2),
 (18656,2,'And thou dost see the people enter Allah''s Religion in crowds,',NULL,110,2),
 (18657,3,'And thou seest mankind entering the religion of Allah in troops,',NULL,110,2),
 (18658,1,'Then celebrate the praise of your Lord, and ask His forgiveness; surely He is oft-returning (to mercy).',NULL,110,3),
 (18659,2,'Celebrate the praises of thy Lord, and pray for His Forgiveness: For He is Oft-Returning (in Grace and Mercy).',NULL,110,3),
 (18660,3,'Then hymn the praises of thy Lord, and seek forgiveness of Him. Lo! He is ever ready to show mercy.',NULL,110,3),
 (18661,1,'Perdition overtake both hands of Abu Lahab, and he will perish.',NULL,111,1),
 (18662,2,'Perish the hands of the Father of Flame! Perish he!',NULL,111,1),
 (18663,3,'The power of Abu Lahab will perish, and he will perish.',NULL,111,1),
 (18664,1,'His wealth and what he earns will not avail him.',NULL,111,2),
 (18665,2,'No profit to him from all his wealth, and all his gains!',NULL,111,2),
 (18666,3,'His wealth and gains will not exempt him.',NULL,111,2),
 (18667,1,'He shall soon burn in fire that flames,',NULL,111,3),
 (18668,2,'Burnt soon will he be in a Fire of Blazing Flame!',NULL,111,3),
 (18669,3,'He will be plunged in flaming Fire,',NULL,111,3),
 (18670,1,'And his wife, the bearer of fuel,',NULL,111,4),
 (18671,2,'His wife shall carry the (crackling) wood - As fuel!-',NULL,111,4),
 (18672,3,'And his wife, the wood-carrier,',NULL,111,4),
 (18673,1,'Upon her neck a halter of strongly twisted rope.',NULL,111,5),
 (18674,2,'A twisted rope of palm-leaf fibre round her (own) neck!',NULL,111,5),
 (18675,3,'Will have upon her neck a halter of palm-fibre.',NULL,111,5),
 (18676,1,'Say: He, Allah, is One.',NULL,112,1),
 (18677,2,'Say: He is Allah, the One and Only;',NULL,112,1),
 (18678,3,'Say: He is Allah, the One!',NULL,112,1),
 (18679,1,'Allah is He on Whom all depend.',NULL,112,2),
 (18680,2,'Allah, the Eternal, Absolute;',NULL,112,2),
 (18681,3,'Allah, the eternally Besought of all!',NULL,112,2),
 (18682,1,'He begets not, nor is He begotten.',NULL,112,3),
 (18683,2,'He begetteth not, nor is He begotten;',NULL,112,3),
 (18684,3,'He begetteth not nor was begotten.',NULL,112,3),
 (18685,1,'And none is like Him.',NULL,112,4),
 (18686,2,'And there is none like unto Him.',NULL,112,4),
 (18687,3,'And there is none comparable unto Him.',NULL,112,4),
 (18688,1,'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the dawn,',NULL,113,1),
 (18689,2,'Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the Dawn',NULL,113,1),
